antang = (t:n) (w:grain/corn) (d:threshed grain kept as food; in everyday speech husked rice) (e:~ lei dingin Josef' kiangah) (r:1.41.57/1.41.49) (q:draft)
bawlkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/restore/repair/remake) (d:make again, put right what was spoiled) (e:a ngeina bangin Jerusalem ~ uh hi) (b:bawl) (r:16.3.8/19.28.5) (q:draft)
bilvang = (t:n) (w:loop/eyelet) (d:loop made on the edge of a curtain to take a clasp; bil ear with vang hole) (e:puan khat tungah ~ sawmnga bawlin) (r:2.36.12/2.26.5) (q:draft)
