etteh = (t:n) (w:example/model/pattern) (d:something looked at to copy or to take warning from; et look with teh compare) (e:midangte’ ~ dingin ka bawl ding hi) (r:26.14.8/52.1.7) (q:draft)
giahna = (t:n) (w:lodging place/camp/resting place) (d:place where one stops for the night) (e:Lampi-ah a ~ khatah) (b:giah) (r:2.4.24/1.43.21) (q:draft)
honsak = (t:v) (w:open/open for) (d:open something for someone or cause it to open; hon with sak) (e:Topa Pasian in ka bil hong ~ a) (b:hon) (r:23.50.5/42.24.45) (q:draft)
hukna = (t:n) (w:lewdness/lust/sexual immorality) (d:shameless sexual desire or behaviour) (e:na ~ leh na paktatna hangin) (b:huk) (r:26.23.35/45.13.13) (q:draft)
hukna = (t:n) (w:cover/covering) (d:thing that covers or closes an opening; han hukna suang, the stone that closes a tomb) (e:han ~ suang a likkhiat khit ciangin) (r:40.28.2/1.29.2) (q:draft)
innlamte = (t:n) (w:builders) (d:those who build houses, plural) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ tungah pia uh hi) (b:innlam) (r:14.34.11/12.22.6) (q:draft)
kampaute = (t:n) (w:words/sayings/speech) (d:plural, the things a person says) (e:ka ~ hong ngai in) (b:kampau) (r:19.54.2/9.17.31) (q:draft)
keugaw = (t:v) (w:dry up/wither/be parched) (d:become completely dry; also describes waterless land) (e:guah a khaktan ciangin leitung ~ a) (r:18.12.15/38.9.11) (q:draft)
khakcip = (t:v) (w:shut up/close up/block/hem in) (d:shut tightly or completely so that nothing passes) (e:ni sagih sung inn ~ ding hi) (b:khak) (r:3.14.38/14.32.3) (q:draft)
khusak = (t:v) (w:put on the head/crown) (d:put a hat or crown on someone's head; causative with sak) (e:ling tawh kigaan lukhu a ~ uh hi) (r:41.15.17/19.21.3) (q:draft)
khutsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the hand/in the hand of) (d:khutsung with the place marker a: in the hand or palm, held by) (e:a ~ om suang khat tawh) (b:khutsung) (r:4.35.17/19.127.4) (q:draft)
kiasak = (t:v) (w:cause to fall/bring down/send down/drop) (d:kia fall with causative sak) (e:kumpi tokhom tung pan ~ a) (b:kia) (r:42.1.52/2.9.18) (q:draft)
kihaltum = (t:v) (w:be burned up/be set on fire/be consumed) (d:passive, be completely burned) (e:amaute mei tawh ~ siang hi) (b:haltum) (r:10.23.7/24.49.2) (q:draft)
