kikhui = (t:v) (w:be sewn/be stitched/be embroidered) (d:passive of khui sew; phim tawh kikhui, worked with a needle, embroidered; kikhui tuah, sewn together) (e:phim tawh ~-in a kizem kawnggak khat) (b:khui) (r:2.28.39/2.36.11) (q:draft)
kikumin = (t:v) (w:confer/discuss/consult together) (d:connective form of kikum, usually thu kikumin, having talked a matter over) (e:a nasemte tawh thu ~) (b:kikum) (r:12.6.8/10.3.17) (q:draft)
kilawh = (t:v) (w:spread) (d:of a skin disease, spread to other parts of the body) (e:mun khat bekah omin a ~ kei leh) (r:3.13.23/3.13.32) (q:draft)
kilawh = (t:v) (w:be picked/be gleaned) (d:of fruit, be gathered; kilawh kik, be gone over again, gleaned) (e:a sanghte a ~ kik bangin) (r:24.6.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimatsak = (t:v) (w:fasten together/join/couple) (d:kimat hold to each other with sak cause: join things so that they hold together, as curtains with clasps) (e:puante khat leh khat ~ hi) (b:kimat) (r:2.36.13/2.26.11) (q:draft)
kinek = (t:v) (w:be eaten) (d:passive of ne eat, in the form used before bang, leh and nouns) (e:A ni thum ni-in a ~ peuhmah leh) (b:nek) (r:3.19.7/5.12.22) (q:draft)
kinek = (t:v) (w:devour one another/eat each other) (d:reciprocal of ne eat) (e:na kipeh, na ~ uh leh) (b:nek) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kingaknate = (t:n) (w:stands/supports/bases) (d:plural of kingakna, a thing that something rests on; in the verses the movable stands under the temple basins and the base of a table) (e:tuikuang a ~ le tuate tungah) (b:kingakna) (r:14.4.14/24.27.19) (q:draft)
kingen = (t:v) (w:be asked/be requested/be demanded) (d:passive of ngen ask; hong kingen, asked leave of me; a kingen thungetna, the prayer that is offered) (e:ama' tungah a ~ zahzah) (b:ngen) (r:2.21.30/9.20.28) (q:draft)
kiniamkhiatte = (t:n) (w:the humble/the lowly) (d:plural of kiniamkhiat, those who humble themselves) (e:a ~ tungah maipha pia hi) (b:kiniamkhiat) (r:20.3.34/42.18.14) (q:draft)
