kiteeng = (t:v) (w:marry/be married) (d:of a man and a woman, live together as husband and wife; with tawh, marry someone) (e:numei dang tawh a ~ peuhmah in) (b:teeng) (r:41.10.11/40.19.10) (q:draft)
kithatlum = (t:v) (w:be slain/be killed/be slaughtered) (d:passive of thatlum, kill outright) (e:Mun citeng-ah mi ~ ding a) (b:thatlum) (r:26.6.7/24.11.19) (q:draft)
kiute = (t:n) (w:corners/angles) (d:plural of kiu corner) (e:Biakbuk nung lam ~’ adingin) (b:kiu) (r:2.26.23/2.36.28) (q:draft)
kiute = (t:n) (w:those who knock) (d:kiu knock with plural te; a kiute, the ones who knock at a door) (e:A ~ khempeuh ading kongkhak) (b:kiu) (r:40.7.8/42.11.10) (q:draft)
kizemin = (t:v) (w:be adorned/be dressed/be decorated) (d:connective form of kizem, adorning oneself or being adorned with fine clothes, gold or jewels) (e:kumpi puan tawh ~ om uh hi) (b:kizem) (r:11.22.10/19.45.9) (q:draft)
