khangkhangin = (t:v) (w:grow/keep growing) (d:khang grow doubled for continuing action, with the linking suffix in) (e:Tua singkung pen ~ gol semsema) (r:27.4.11/27.4.20) (q:draft)
khapi = (t:n) (w:moon) (d:kha moon with pi great: the moon as a heavenly body) (e:hun ciamteh nadingin ~ na bawl a) (b:kha) (r:19.104.19/19.72.7) (q:draft)
khawlcip = (t:v) (w:stand still/stop completely/come to a standstill) (d:khawl stop, rest with cip firmly) (e:tuipi ~ thei lo a) (b:khawl) (r:23.57.20/15.4.24) (q:draft)
khempeuha = (t:det) (w:every/all) (d:khempeuh with the ending a, in or of: mun khempeuha is in every place, everywhere) (e:Mun ~ om Jew mite lakah) (b:khempeuh) (r:44.24.5/9.14.47) (q:draft)
kholsa = (t:n) (w:stores/treasure/what is stored up) (d:khol store with sa already done: things that have been laid up) (e:a ngahsa uh leh a ~ uh na tampite) (b:khol) (r:23.15.7/18.20.26) (q:draft)
kholsa = (t:adv) (w:beforehand/in advance/already) (d:follows a verb: done or made ready ahead of time, as kigelh kholsa written beforehand and kiseh kholsa determined beforehand; kholsa-a om is be prepared) (e:a kiseh ~ bang a) (r:27.11.36/40.26.24) (q:draft)
khuapihte = (t:n) (w:townspeople/citizens/fellow townsmen) (d:plural; after the name of a town, the people of that town) (e:Samaria ~ in Pasian’ thu a mang uh a) (b:khuapih) (r:44.8.14/42.11.30) (q:draft)
khuisa = (t:v) (w:sigh/groan) (d:breathe out deeply in grief or strong feeling) (e:Vantung ento-in ~ a) (r:41.7.34/23.24.7) (q:draft)
khumzaw = (t:adj) (w:sweeter/more delightful) (d:khum sweet with zaw more) (e:khuaizu sangin ka kam-ah ~ hi) (b:khum) (r:19.119.103/22.1.2) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (t:n) (w:palm/open hand) (d:the flat inner side of the hand; khutpeek zan is hold out the hands) (e:ka ~ sungah nang kong gelh khinzo a) (r:23.49.16/45.10.21) (q:draft)
khutpeek = (t:n) (w:handbreadth) (d:the width of a hand used as a measure) (e:A sahna in ~ mai cia ahi hi) (r:11.7.26) (q:draft)
kiangpan = (t:prep) (w:from) (d:from a person, from someone's presence; kiang with pan, more often written kiang panin) (e:Pasian ~ hong kipia Kha i ngah zo hi) (r:46.2.12/18.3.19) (q:draft)
kibatna = (t:n) (w:likeness/resemblance/similarity) (d:how one thing is like another, or what two have in common) (e:mi bawlsiapa a ~ uh khat om hi) (b:kibat) (r:20.29.13/50.2.7) (q:draft)
kibotkhia = (t:v) (w:be uprooted/be pulled up/be torn out) (d:ki with botkhia pull out) (e:a suan loh kung khempeuh ~ ding hi) (b:botkhia) (r:40.15.13/20.2.22) (q:draft)
kihalna = (t:n) (w:burning/place of burning) (d:kihal be burned with na: the burning of something; kihalna mun is the place where it is burned, the hearth of an altar) (e:ganhing ~ mun in tong li sang ding a) (b:kihal) (r:26.43.15/4.19.6) (q:draft)
kihalna = (t:n) (w:distance/gap/space between) (d:the space kept between two things) (e:tong tulnih bang ~ om ding hi) (r:6.3.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
