kiseelin = (t:v) (w:be hidden/hide oneself/be concealed) (d:kiseel with the linking in; meel kiseelin, in disguise) (e:theihna sum a om khempeuh ~ om hi) (b:kiseel) (r:51.2.3/14.18.29) (q:draft)
kiseelin = (t:v) (w:quarrel/dispute/contend) (d:with tawh, quarrelling with someone) (e:Mite Moses tawh ~) (b:kiseel) (r:4.20.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiseelte = (t:n) (w:hidden things/those hidden/hidden treasures) (d:kiseel be hidden with te plural) (e:leh sehnel sunga na manpha ~ ngah uh hi) (b:kiseel) (r:5.33.19/42.12.2) (q:draft)
kisiansuahin = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be purified/be cleansed) (d:kisiansuah with the linking in) (e:Mi tampite ~ a hoih leh a hoih lo) (b:kisiansuah) (r:27.12.10/47.7.1) (q:draft)
kisimkhawm = (t:v) (w:be counted together/be numbered among) (d:kisim be counted with khawm, together; with tawh or lakah for the group) (e:sawltak sawm-le-khatte tawh a ~ hi) (b:kisim) (r:44.1.26/4.2.33) (q:draft)
kisimmawhna = (t:n) (w:insult/scorn/contempt/disrespect) (d:the act of despising or insulting one another, or of being scorned by others) (e:kitotna leh ~ bei ding hi) (b:kisimmawh) (r:20.22.10/19.69.19) (q:draft)
kisimte = (t:n) (w:those counted/those numbered) (d:kisim with plural -te, the ones who were counted in a census) (e:amau sung pan a ~ in) (b:kisim) (r:4.26.62/4.1.22) (q:draft)
kisimte = (t:n) (w:things read/what was read) (d:kisim with plural -te, the words that were read out from a book) (e:laibu sunga thu ~ lim takin ngai) (b:kisim) (r:16.8.3) (q:draft)
kisingkhia = (t:v) (w:be shaken off/be shaken out) (d:passive ki- form of singkhia, shake something out or off; also said of the earth shaken from its place) (e:kauphe bangin kei hong ~ hi) (b:singkhia) (r:19.109.23/16.5.13) (q:draft)
kisugawp = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be destroyed/be oppressed) (d:passive ki- form of sugawp, crush) (e:kulh kongpi gei-ah amaute ~ a) (b:sugawp) (r:18.5.4/5.28.33) (q:draft)
kisukha = (t:v) (w:have to do with/associate with/come into contact with) (d:touch or affect one another; with tawh, to have dealings with someone, and of a dead body, to come into contact with it) (e:a gamta mite tawh ~ vet kei un) (b:sukha) (r:49.5.7/4.5.2) (q:draft)
kisukham = (t:v) (w:be broken/be smashed/be crushed) (d:passive ki- form of sukham, break in pieces, said mostly of a clay pot) (e:a kihuanna leibeel ~ ding hi) (b:sukham) (r:3.6.28/24.19.11) (q:draft)
kisuksiatsak = (t:v) (w:be destroyed/be demolished/be ruined) (d:passive ki- form of suksiatsak, destroy) (e:a innte uh ~ ding hi) (b:suksiatsak) (r:36.1.13/24.4.20) (q:draft)
kiteen = (t:v) (w:marry/be married) (d:short form of kiteeng, written with an apostrophe before a suffix or a following word: kiteen’na, marriage, kiteen’sak, give in marriage) (e:kipina, ~’na om lo ding hi) (b:teen) (r:40.22.30/42.20.34) (q:draft)
kiteen = (t:v) (w:dwell/be lived in) (d:in kiteen’na mun, a place that is lived in, an abode) (e:Daii tak-a a ~’na mun) (b:teen) (r:23.33.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kithawhkiksak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised from the dead/be resurrected) (d:passive ki- form of thawhkiksak, raise up again) (e:sihna panin amah a ~ ciangin) (r:43.2.22/46.15.43) (q:draft)
kithehthangna = (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion/place of scattering) (d:kithehthang with -na; before mun, gam or minamte it means where they were scattered) (e:a ~ mun khempeuh panin) (b:kithehthang) (r:24.40.12/26.29.13) (q:draft)
kituiphum = (t:v) (w:be baptized) (d:passive ki- form of tuiphum, baptize, literally immerse in water) (e:Jesuh zong a ~ hi) (b:tuiphum) (r:42.3.21/40.3.16) (q:draft)
kizeem = (t:v) (w:be dressed/be adorned/adorn oneself/be decorated) (d:ki- form of zeem, of a person dressed in fine clothes or a thing decorated with something) (e:puan hoih tawh ~ a) (b:zeem) (r:42.7.25/66.21.19) (q:draft)
kizelthang = (t:v) (w:spread out/be scattered/spread abroad) (d:of peoples or descendants spreading over the earth in every direction) (e:tung panin leitungah minamte ~ hi) (r:1.10.32/1.28.14) (q:draft)
kizemte = (t:adj) (w:embroidered/decorated/carved) (d:kizem with plural -te, said of several decorated things, as embroidered cloth or carved work) (e:saihadial puan ~ tawh na puankhai kibawl) (b:kizem) (r:26.27.7/19.74.6) (q:draft)
kizutna = (t:n) (w:overlay/coating/plaster) (d:kizut with -na, what is smeared or laid on a surface: the plaster of a wall, or the metal overlay of the top of a post) (e:a khuamlu zepnate a ~ zong ngun) (b:kizut) (r:2.38.17/3.14.41) (q:draft)
koihcip = (t:v) (w:isolate/shut up/keep shut away) (d:koih, put, with cip, tightly closed: put away and keep closed in; also of keeping the hand held back in the fold of the garment) (e:ni sagih sung ~ ding hi) (b:koih) (r:3.13.50/19.74.11) (q:draft)
koimahah = (t:adv) (w:anywhere/nowhere) (d:koimah with the place marker ah; used with a negative verb: not anywhere, nowhere) (e:inn panin ~ a paikhia kei hi) (b:koimah) (r:42.1.24/18.34.22) (q:draft)
kuampi = (t:n) (w:valley/great valley) (d:kuam, valley, with -pi, great: a large or deep valley) (e:a kikalah ~ om ding hi) (b:kuam) (r:38.14.4/26.37.1) (q:draft)
kuampi = (t:n) (w:abyss/bottomless pit) (d:the deep pit in which Satan is shut up) (e:~ sungah a khiatsuk khit ciangin) (b:kuam) (r:66.20.3/66.20.1) (q:draft)
kuangdaite = (t:n) (w:plates/dishes) (d:kuangdai with plural -te, the flat dishes of the table in the tabernacle) (e:tua tungah a ~, paknamtui pakante) (b:kuangdai) (r:4.4.7/2.37.16) (q:draft)
kuangin = (t:v) (w:burn/blaze/break out) (d:kuang, burn with flame, with the linking suffix -in) (e:meivak bangin ~ a taang hi) (b:kuang) (r:43.5.35/2.22.6) (q:draft)
kungah = (t:adv) (w:on the bush/on the plant/from the tree) (d:kung, tree or plant, with the place marker ah; follows the name of the plant) (e:Thangling ~ theigah kilo thei hiam) (b:kung) (r:40.7.16/42.6.44) (q:draft)
kungah = (t:adv) (w:to the uprights/on the frame) (d:kung in the sense of the upright frame of a stand, with the place marker ah) (e:a khawkte a ~ kibulh a) (b:kung) (r:11.7.28/11.7.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
laa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkey/ass/mule) (d:laa van vawhsak means saddle the donkey) (e:Kei adingin ~ van hong vawhsak un) (r:11.13.27/19.32.9) (q:draft)
lahtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to show/can show) (d:lah, show, with theih, be able; lahtheih nadingin means so that one may show) (e:ama tungah migitna ka ~ nadingin) (b:lah) (r:10.9.1/45.9.22) (q:draft)
laidal = (t:n) (w:scroll/writing tablet/sheet) (d:a sheet or surface to write on; a scroll when it is rolled up) (e:Zekhariah in zong ~ khat ngen a) (r:42.1.63/23.34.4) (q:draft)
lal = (t:v) (w:migrate/move/wander/sojourn) (d:move from one place to live in another; lal-a om, to live as a sojourner away from home) (e:Amaute nisuahna lamah ~ uh a) (r:1.11.2/60.1.17) (q:draft)
lampha = (t:v) (w:rebuild/build up/restore) (d:build again what was ruined, from lam, build) (e:tang lai-a a siasate ~ ding uh) (r:23.61.4/12.14.22) (q:draft)
lamsangah = (t:prep) (w:as regards/concerning/in respect of/according to) (d:lamsang, side or aspect, with ah; after a noun it means in the matter of) (e:Ci-le-sa ~ Israelte na en ta un) (b:lamsang) (r:46.10.18/47.11.6) (q:draft)
lawkite = (t:n) (w:pagans/heathens/unbelievers) (d:lawki with plural -te, people who do not worship God, those outside the faith) (e:~ nangawn a gamtat lohte) (b:lawki) (r:46.5.1/30.7.17) (q:draft)
lawngin = (t:v) (w:touch) (d:lawng, touch, with the linking suffix -in, touching and then doing the next action) (e:a khut tawh ~ a damsak hi) (b:lawng) (r:42.22.51/11.19.5) (q:draft)
lawnna = (t:n) (w:touching/touch/contact) (d:the act of touching, from lawng, touch; misi luang lawnna is contact with a dead body) (e:Misi luang ~ hangin ka nin uh) (b:lawn) (r:4.9.7/42.8.47) (q:draft)
leengmang = (t:v) (w:fly away/fly off) (d:leeng, fly, with mang, out of sight) (e:muvanlai bangin thakhatin ~ thei hi) (r:20.23.5/24.4.25) (q:draft)
leengto = (t:v) (w:fly up/soar/rise up) (d:leeng, fly, with to, upward) (e:muvanlai bangin kha tawh ~-in) (b:leeng) (r:23.40.31/26.10.15) (q:draft)
leipa = (t:n) (w:buyer) (d:lei, buy, with -pa, marking a man: the man who buys) (e:Van ~ in van zuakpa kiangah) (r:20.20.14/3.25.30) (q:draft)
leite = (t:n) (w:buyers) (d:lei, buy, with plural -te: those who buy) (e:sunga sumzuakte leh sum ~ khempeuh hawlkhia) (r:41.11.15/44.7.9) (q:draft)
leite = (t:n) (w:tongues) (d:lei, tongue, with plural -te) (e:amau ~ in namsau hiamte ahi hi) (r:19.57.4) (q:draft)
leitungmi = (t:n) (w:earthly person/man of the earth/worldly person/mortal) (d:leitung, earth, with mi, person: a human being of this world, as against vantungmi, a heavenly one) (e:~’ lim i neih mah bangin) (b:leitung) (r:46.15.49/46.3.19) (q:draft)
lelhna = (t:n) (w:defeat) (d:lelhna thuak means suffer defeat, be defeated) (e:~ na thuak ding uh hi) (b:lelh) (r:3.26.17/2.32.18) (q:draft)
lelte = (t:adj) (w:mere/merely/only) (d:lel, only or merely, with plural -te: those that are nothing more than what is said, as mihing ahi lelte, mere humans) (e:Mihing ahi ~ in kei bang hong cih) (b:lel) (r:19.56.4/47.10.4) (q:draft)
linglawng = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be startled/be troubled) (d:be shaken with fear; with sak, to terrify or trouble someone) (e:amaute lau-in ~ gawp uh a) (r:42.24.37/27.7.15) (q:draft)
lona = (t:n) (d:lo, not, with -na: the state or place of not being or not doing; a kilang lona-ah, where it does not show, means in secret or aside) (e:a kilang ~-ah paipih a) (b:lo) (r:44.23.19/40.6.4) (q:draft)
lozaw = (t:adv) (w:less/even less) (d:lo, not, with the comparative zaw: more so not; a gina lozaw, less good, inferior; kilawm lozaw, even less fitting) (e:pawlpi dangte sangin bangah a gina ~) (b:lo) (r:47.12.13/20.19.10) (q:draft)
luituite = (t:n) (w:streams/brooks/springs) (d:luitui with plural -te, the running waters of streams) (e:kei’ suah hunin ~ om nai lo hi) (b:luitui) (r:20.8.24/19.78.44) (q:draft)
lukham = (t:n) (w:pillow/cushion) (d:what the head is laid on in sleep, from lu, head) (e:gunkuang tawlam ~ tungah a ihmu hi) (r:41.4.38/1.28.18) (q:draft)
lumsak = (t:v) (w:make lie down/lay down) (d:lum, lie down, with the causative sak) (e:Lo nona-ah keimah hong ~ a) (b:lum) (r:19.23.2/10.8.2) (q:draft)
lungdamzaw = (t:adj) (w:happier/more joyful) (d:lungdam with the comparative zaw; as a command, rejoice rather) (e:a ~ ding hi ci-in ka um) (b:lungdam) (r:46.7.40/42.10.20) (q:draft)
lunggulhin = (t:v) (w:desire/long for/set the mind on) (d:lunggulh with the linking suffix -in, longing for something) (e:atung lam nate bek ~ om un) (b:lunggulh) (r:51.3.2/18.7.2) (q:draft)
lungham = (t:v) (w:be angry/be furious/be enraged) (d:a strong word for anger, used beside heh; lungham mahmahna, great wrath) (e:a tawp dongin ~ den ding) (r:24.3.5/23.8.21) (q:draft)
lungkimhuai = (t:adj) (w:pleasing/acceptable/satisfying) (d:lungkim, be satisfied, with huai, worthy of: such as pleases; with lo, displeasing) (e:mai-ah a ~ hi ding hi) (r:39.3.4/1.38.10) (q:draft)
lungnem = (t:adj) (w:meek/gentle/humble) (d:of a soft and mild heart, from lung, heart, and nem, soft) (e:A ~ mite in Pasian’ ciamsa leitang) (r:40.5.5/4.12.3) (q:draft)
masakna = (t:n) (w:first) (d:masak, do first, with -na: the place or occasion where something was first done, translated first or at first) (e:Ka min ka teen’sak ~ Shiloh khua-ah) (b:masak) (r:24.7.12/43.10.40) (q:draft)
mau = (t:v) (w:mourn/wail/lament) (d:in the pair a kap a mau, weeping and mourning) (e:a kap a ~ om kei un) (r:16.8.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
mau = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:rush/papyrus/reed) (d:a plant of wet ground, named together with grass and reeds) (e:lopa, pumpeng leh ~ po ding hi) (r:23.35.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
mau = (t:pron) (w:they/them/their) (d:second part of amau written as two words, a mau; whether English has they, them or their depends on the place in the sentence) (e:a ~ khut tawh a bawlnate) (r:66.9.20/43.6.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
mavan = (t:v) (w:prosper/succeed/go well) (d:short form of mavang, written mavan’ with an apostrophe before a following word or suffix; mavan’na is success) (e:gal dona bangci ~’ hiam cih) (r:10.11.7/14.24.20) (q:draft)
mawhsaknate = (t:n) (w:accusations/charges) (d:mawhsakna with plural -te) (e:A ~ uh amau’ thukham ngeina tawh) (b:mawhsakna) (r:44.23.29/44.25.11) (q:draft)
meibung = (t:n) (w:oven) (d:a closed fireplace for baking bread, from mei, fire) (e:nupi sawm in ~ khat sungah) (r:3.26.26/3.2.4) (q:draft)
meivakkhuamte = (t:n) (w:lampstands) (d:meivakkhuam with plural -te) (e:kham citak ~ leh a meivakte) (b:meivakkhuam) (r:14.4.20/11.7.49) (q:draft)
mialin = (t:v) (w:be dark/become dark/grow dark) (d:mial, dark, with the linking suffix -in: being or becoming dark, followed by another verb) (e:ni hong ~, kha, sisan hong bang) (b:mial) (r:29.2.31/19.35.6) (q:draft)
mialna = (t:n) (w:darkness/dark place) (d:mial, dark, with -na; mialna mun is a dark place) (e:tua ~ pen nasia mahmah ding hi) (b:mial) (r:40.6.23/23.45.3) (q:draft)
miphakte = (t:n) (w:lepers/people with leprosy) (d:miphak with plural -te) (e:~ in damna a ngah kik uh hi) (b:miphak) (r:40.11.5/40.10.8) (q:draft)
mittawpa = (t:n) (w:blind man) (d:mittaw, blind, with -pa, marking a man) (e:Amaute in ~ sam uh a) (b:mittaw) (r:41.10.49/43.9.13) (q:draft)
momai = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (e:aktui tangin ~ a pia ding) (r:42.11.12/66.9.5) (q:draft)
moman = (t:n) (w:bride-price/dowry) (d:the price paid to the father of a bride, from mo, bride, and man, price) (e:kumpipa in ~ deih lo hi) (r:9.18.25/2.22.16) (q:draft)
mualbo = (t:n) (w:hill/hilltop/knoll) (d:a hill or rise of ground, used after the name of the hill, as Ofel mualbo, the hill of Ophel) (e:Ofel ~-ah teeng uh a) (r:16.11.21/16.3.27) (q:draft)
mualtungte = (t:n) (w:mountains/hills) (d:mualtung with plural -te) (e:mihonpi lungdam bangin ~ ah gamlumna) (b:mualtung) (r:23.13.4/26.35.12) (q:draft)
mutheite = (t:n) (w:seers/those who see) (d:muthei, able to see, with plural -te; thu mutheite are those who see or discern things, the seers) (e:nomau’ lutang ahi thu ~ khuhcip hi) (b:muthei) (r:23.29.10/20.8.9) (q:draft)
namgimtui = (t:n) (w:oil/lamp oil) (d:oil burned in a lamp) (e:~ a pua kei uh hi) (r:40.25.3/40.25.8) (q:draft)
nangzo = (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:nang, resist, with zo, be able: be able to withstand; mostly used with a negative) (e:a galte uh ~ nawn lo uh hi) (b:nang) (r:7.2.14/6.23.9) (q:draft)
nard = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:nard/spikenard) (d:a fragrant plant and the costly perfume made from it, a loanword) (e:henna leh ~ sing namtuite a po hi) (r:22.4.13/41.14.3) (q:draft)
nawtkhia = (t:v) (w:push out/drive out/thrust out/depose) (d:nawt, push, with khia, out) (e:a hon lak panin na ~ uh hi) (b:nawt) (r:26.34.21/23.22.19) (q:draft)
nektawm = (t:n) (w:food/something to eat) (d:what there is to eat; nektawm ding nei lo, having nothing to eat) (e:a gilo mi in ~ ding nei loin) (r:20.13.25/20.12.9) (q:draft)
nene = (t:v) (w:eat/devour/keep eating) (d:ne, eat or drink, said twice for repeated or continued action: eat again and again, eat as a habit) (e:Esau’ sa matsa ~ ahih manin) (r:1.25.28/27.7.7) (q:draft)
nengniamin = (t:v) (w:oppress) (d:nengniam, oppress, with the linking suffix -in) (e:mi zawngte ~, mi cimawhte a sugawp) (b:nengniam) (r:30.4.1/36.3.1) (q:draft)
ngaihsunkha = (t:v) (w:think/suppose/imagine) (d:ngaihsun, think, with kha: come to think so, often of a mistaken idea) (e:Pasian a kikhemzo dingin ~ kei un) (r:48.6.7/19.50.21) (q:draft)
ngap = (t:v) (w:dare/venture) (d:na ngap nak leh, if you dare) (e:Na ~ nak leh na minthan’ nading) (r:18.40.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngap = (t:v) (w:ford/wade across/cross) (d:cross water on foot, as at a ford; ka ngap zo kei hi, I could not get across) (e:amaute in ngahmun ~ uh hi) (r:10.19.18/26.47.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
nialte = (t:n) (w:those who deny/those who reject/rebels/the disobedient) (d:nial, deny or refuse, with plural -te; thu nialte are those who refuse to obey or believe) (e:Mite mai-ah hong ~ Pasian’ vantungmite mai-ah) (b:nial) (r:42.12.9/45.13.2) (q:draft)
niamin = (t:adv) (w:low) (d:niam, low, with -in; a niamin kikoih, be put low, be humbled) (e:Mite a ~ kikoih suak a) (b:niam) (r:23.5.15/23.2.17) (q:draft)
ninin = (t:adv) (w:unclean/as unclean/impure) (d:nin, unclean, with -in: in an unclean state; a ninin ngaihsun, regard as unclean) (e:ni sagih sung a ~ om ding) (b:nin) (r:3.15.19/44.10.15) (q:draft)
ninneng = (t:n) (w:speck/mote/bit of dust) (d:a tiny bit of dirt; ninneng tang, a single speck) (e:na u na nau’ mit sunga ~ tang) (r:40.7.3/40.7.5) (q:draft)
nungtakik = (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life/revive) (d:nungta, live, with kik, again; with sak, raise to life again) (e:a sih hangin a ~ ding hi) (b:nungta) (r:43.11.25/18.14.7) (q:draft)
oksak = (t:v) (w:put around the neck/hang on) (d:ok, wear around the neck, with the causative sak: put a chain or necklace on someone) (e:a ngawng-ah kham khainiang khat ~ hi) (b:ok) (r:1.41.42/26.16.11) (q:draft)
omkhawmte = (t:n) (w:companions/those who are with) (d:omkhawm, be together, with plural -te: those who are with someone) (e:amah tawh a ~ a lusu uh hi) (b:omkhawm) (r:42.9.32/44.20.34) (q:draft)
omteng = (t:n) (w:all that is/everything in/all who are) (d:om, be, with teng, all: all that there is in a place, all who are there) (e:a gam sunga ~ ka suksiat ciangin) (b:om) (r:26.32.15/1.7.23) (q:draft)
omzaw = (t:v) (w:be rather/be instead) (d:om be, live, with zaw rather: be or live in one way rather than another) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh a kidimin ~ un) (b:om) (r:49.5.18/24.7.24) (q:draft)
omzaw = (t:v) (w:be more) (d:there is more of something, used with sangin than) (e:mihaite a dingin lametna ~ lai hi) (b:om) (r:20.26.12/13.24.4) (q:draft)
