sincip = (t:v) (w:cover over/seal off/shut in) (d:sin, cover, with cip, tightly: close over so that nothing shows or gets out) (e:suangtumpi tawh a hong ~ uh hi) (b:sin) (r:25.3.53/18.9.7) (q:draft)
singin = (t:v) (w:shaking/shaking out) (d:sing, shake, with in linking to the next verb; lu singin is shaking the head, puan singin is shaking out the garment) (e:a lu uh ~ zahpihbawl uh a) (r:41.15.29/16.5.13) (q:draft)
singliim = (t:n) (w:shade of a tree/shady tree) (d:sing, tree, with liim, shade; in Jeremiah for the spreading trees under which idols were worshipped) (e:~ nuai khempeuhah numei paktat bangin) (r:24.3.6/24.2.20) (q:draft)
sotto = (t:v) (w:lengthen/extend/prolong) (d:make longer in time; hun sotto is put off, delay; also go on further) (e:ci-in a hun ~ kei in) (r:20.3.28/40.6.27) (q:draft)
suahsakna = (t:n) (w:making/turning into/causing) (d:the act or place of making something become or come out; sal suahsakna is sending into exile) (e:Tui, leenggahzu a ~ Galilee gam Kana) (b:suahsak) (r:43.4.46/23.27.8) (q:draft)
suakkha = (t:v) (w:become/turn out to be/end up as) (d:suak, become, with kha, happen to: come to be something without meaning to) (e:kuama ten lohna gam simtham na ~ ding) (r:24.6.8/58.12.16) (q:draft)
suanpa = (t:n) (w:planter/the one who plants) (d:suan, plant, with pa marking a male person) (e:Keimah in a ~ ka hi hi) (b:suan) (r:46.3.6/46.3.7) (q:draft)
suanpa = (t:n) (w:son/male descendant) (d:suan, descendant, with pa marking a male; used in the title Son of David) (e:~ aw, kei hong hehpih in) (b:suan) (r:42.18.39) (q:draft)
sumang = (t:v) (w:destroy/demolish/do away with) (d:make something disappear completely) (e:a vekpi-in ~ un) (r:24.50.21/4.33.52) (q:draft)
sumbawlna = (t:n) (w:trade/commerce/business) (d:sum bawl, make money, with na: trading, and the place of trade) (e:Na ~ teng uh maimang khinta hi) (b:sumbawl) (r:23.23.10/23.23.17) (q:draft)
sunglamah = (t:adv) (w:inside/inwardly/toward the inside) (d:sunglam, the inner side, with the place marker ah) (e:a nunglam uh a ~ om hi) (b:sunglam) (r:14.4.4/45.2.29) (q:draft)
sungsuk = (t:v) (w:pour out/pour down) (d:sung, pour, with suk, downward; in the Bible of pouring out anger on someone) (e:tungah na hehna ~ in) (r:24.10.25/19.69.24) (q:draft)
sutpi = (t:n) (w:main post/pillar/cornerstone) (d:the chief post that holds up a house; in the Bible for a pillar, a cornerstone and a firm foundation) (e:tua inn ~ pen Jesuh mahmah ahi hi) (r:49.2.20/66.3.12) (q:draft)
taangkhiasak = (t:v) (w:shine out/give out light/radiate) (d:taangkhia, shine out, with sak, cause) (e:kha in zong khuavak ~ lo ding hi) (b:taangkhia) (r:23.13.10/58.1.3) (q:draft)
taangkhiasak = (t:v) (w:stretch out/put forth) (d:of the hand, khut taangkhiasak: reach out the hand to strike) (e:ka khutte ka ~ kei hi) (r:9.26.23/9.22.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
taangmi = (t:n) (w:ambassador/envoy/messenger) (d:a person sent to speak for a king or for another) (e:kumpi ~ dingin a puak) (r:24.29.3/49.6.20) (q:draft)
taangzaw = (t:adj) (w:brighter) (d:taang, shine, with zaw, more) (e:sun sangin a ~ khuavak khat) (b:taang) (r:44.26.13/18.11.17) (q:draft)
taanna = (t:n) (w:loss/losing) (d:taan, lose or be deprived of, with na; lawm taanna is losing a friend) (e:bawngno milim a ~ hangun) (b:taan) (r:28.10.5/20.17.9) (q:draft)
