khiim = (t:v) (w:charm/enchant) (d:bring a snake under control by a spell) (e:Phuisamna tawh gulpi a ~ thei) (r:18.3.8/21.10.11) (q:draft)
khinmang = (t:adv) (w:completely/entirely/utterly) (d:placed after a verb: the action takes in the whole and nothing is left over) (e:namsau tawh that ~ uh hi) (r:6.11.11/45.13.9) (q:draft)
khinte = (t:n) (d:those who have already done the action; khin already, joined to the verb before it, with the plural te: a thokik khinte, those who have risen again) (e:Sihna panin a thokik ~ ahih manin) (b:khin) (r:42.20.36/51.3.1) (q:draft)
khitlam = (t:n) (d:the fact that an action is finished; khit finish with lam, placed after a verb and before a word of seeing or knowing: a sih khitlam a mu, see that she has died) (e:a sih ~ a muh uh ciangin) (r:44.5.10/9.14.3) (q:draft)
khohsa = (t:adj) (w:invited) (d:khoh invite, with sa for a completed action; a khohsa mite, those who have been invited) (e:a ~ mite a sam dingin) (b:khoh) (r:40.22.3/42.14.17) (q:draft)
kholte = (t:n) (w:things stored up/stores) (d:khol store with the plural te: the things that have been stored) (e:tu ni donga a ~ Babilon ah) (b:khol) (r:12.20.17) (q:draft)
kholte = (t:n) (w:those who store/those who gather in) (d:khol store with the plural te: the people who have gathered and stored the crop) (e:a ~ in ne-in Topa phat ding) (b:khol) (r:23.62.9) (q:draft)
khotakin = (t:adv) (w:firmly/fast/steadfastly) (d:kho strong with takin; used with len hold: hold firmly) (e:upna thu ~ lenin ka zokhin hi) (b:kho) (r:55.4.7/58.2.1) (q:draft)
khuacing = (t:n) (w:guard/town guard/watch) (d:khua town with cing guard: one who keeps watch over a town or a post) (e:~ mite in Jonathan leh a galhiam) (r:9.14.12/16.7.3) (q:draft)
khuankhuan = (t:adv) (w:roaming about/prowling) (d:found only after vak go about: vak khuankhuan, prowl around) (e:khua sungah vak ~ uh hi) (r:19.59.6/19.59.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuasikmul = (t:n) (w:body hair/gooseflesh) (d:the hair of the body that rises with fear or cold; khuasikmul suak, the hair stands on end) (e:ka ~ hong suaksak hi) (r:18.4.15/19.119.120) (q:draft)
khuat = (t:v) (w:dig up/paw/scratch) (d:scrape at the ground with the feet or hands, or dig something out of it) (e:a khe-un lei ~ uh a) (r:18.39.21/24.13.7) (q:draft)
khuazang = (t:n) (w:whole town/whole city) (d:all the people of a town taken together) (e:Jerusalem ~ gamlumin a om uh) (r:44.21.31/44.13.44) (q:draft)
khulna = (t:n) (w:being thrown in/casting in) (d:khul throw into a fire, with the noun suffix na; khulna thuak, be thrown into the fire) (e:hell meikuang sungah ~ thuak thei ding hi) (b:khul) (r:40.5.22/40.18.9) (q:draft)
khumzangah = (t:n) (w:on the roof/in the vault) (d:khumzang roof or vault, with the place marker ah) (e:galvilpa kulh kongpi ~ paito a) (b:khumzang) (r:10.18.24/18.22.14) (q:draft)
khusa-in = (t:v) (w:wearing on the head/with on the head) (d:khu put on the head, with sa for a completed action and the linking ending in: having something on the head, a hat or ashes) (e:silhsa leh lukhu ~ hencip uh a) (r:27.3.21/24.2.37) (q:draft)
khusakin = (t:v) (w:putting on the head of/crowning) (d:khusak put something on the head of another person, with the linking ending in) (e:kumpi lukhu amah ~ Vashti’ taangin) (b:khusak) (r:17.2.17/9.17.38) (q:draft)
khutlum = (t:n) (w:hand/hands) (d:the hand as that which kills or does violence; after a possessive, with in or tawh: at the hands of) (e:kote’ ~-in na si ding hi) (r:24.11.21/24.19.7) (q:draft)
khutzaw = (t:adj) (w:with a withered hand/paralysed) (d:khut hand with zaw weak: having a weak or withered hand; khutzaw khezaw, weak in hand and foot, paralysed) (e:Jesuh in ~ mipa kiangah) (b:khut) (r:41.3.3/44.8.7) (q:draft)
kiamkiam = (t:v) (w:keep going down/recede steadily) (d:kiam decrease, repeated to show that it goes on little by little) (e:leitung panin tuite ~ hi) (r:1.8.3/1.8.5) (q:draft)
kiamsak = (t:v) (w:reduce/decrease/diminish) (d:kiam become less, with the causative sak: make less, or let become fewer) (e:a man na ~ ding uh hi) (b:kiam) (r:3.25.16/19.107.38) (q:draft)
kiamsuk = (t:v) (w:sink/go down/subside) (d:kiam go down, with suk downward) (e:leitung khempeuh khang toin ~ ding hi) (b:kiam) (r:30.8.8/30.9.5) (q:draft)
kiatin = (t:v) (w:scraping/shaving) (d:kiat scrape or shave, with the linking ending in; of scraping the walls of a house and of shaving the hair) (e:amah in a mul ~ a puan) (b:kiat) (r:1.41.14/3.14.43) (q:draft)
kibalnen = (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be cut in pieces) (d:passive ki with balnen break in pieces; often followed by gawp, violently) (e:Josef ~ gawp a hihna) (b:balnen) (r:1.37.33/27.3.29) (q:draft)
kibalzan = (t:v) (w:be torn to pieces/be torn) (d:passive ki with balzan tear apart; of a person or animal torn by a wild beast) (e:amah ~ khin taktak hi) (b:balzan) (r:1.44.28/2.22.13) (q:draft)
kibuan = (t:v) (w:be raped/be violated/be mistreated) (d:be seized and used with violence; said of women when a city is taken) (e:numeite zong ~ ding hi) (r:38.14.2/24.13.22) (q:draft)
kibuasa = (t:adj) (w:shed/poured out) (d:kibua be poured out, with sa for a completed action; said of blood) (e:a ~, kiciamna si ahi hi) (b:kibua) (r:41.14.24/42.11.50) (q:draft)
kibuluh = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ransacked) (d:passive ki with buluh plunder) (e:No hong buluhte ~ ding a) (b:buluh) (r:24.30.16/31.1.6) (q:draft)
kiciamte = (t:n) (w:those who swear/those under oath) (d:kiciam swear with the plural te) (e:Vantung gam tawh a ~ in) (b:kiciam) (r:40.23.22/44.23.13) (q:draft)
kiciamzo = (t:v) (w:have sworn) (d:kiciam swear, with zo for an action already carried out) (e:pasian ahi lopite peuh tawh ~ uh hi) (b:kiciam) (r:24.5.7/6.9.19) (q:draft)
kiciangto = (t:v) (w:be piled up/be built up high) (d:kiciang be built up in courses, with to upward; of waters heaped up and of walls rising to the sky) (e:Na nak ging tawh tuite ~ a) (b:kiciang) (r:2.15.8/5.9.1) (q:draft)
kicil = (t:v) (w:be trodden/be trampled/be threshed) (d:passive ki with cil tread out; of grapes in a winepress and of grain on a threshing floor) (e:buhcilna tawh ~ lo a) (r:23.28.27/66.14.20) (q:draft)
kicingta = (t:v) (w:be complete now/be fulfilled) (d:kicing complete, with ta showing that the state has now been reached; a hun kicingta, the time is ripe) (e:keima lungdamna ~ hi) (b:kicing) (r:43.3.29/27.11.13) (q:draft)
kicipna = (t:n) (w:gap/breach) (d:in kulh a kicipna mun, the place where a wall is broken through and has to be closed up; built on kicip with the noun suffix na) (e:kulh a ~ munah a ding zo ding) (r:26.22.30/26.13.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidawh = (t:v) (w:be pulled out/be drawn out) (d:passive ki with dawh pull out; kidawh khiatsak, have something pulled out and taken away) (e:na lupna nangawn hong ~ khiatsak ding hi) (b:dawh) (r:20.22.27/15.6.11) (q:draft)
kidawh = (t:v) (w:be set/be planted) (d:in so kidawh, of spikes or pitfalls set in a path beside snares) (e:thang kisiahin so ~ a) (r:20.22.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kidiahin = (t:v) (w:wallowing/soaked/steeped) (d:kidiah be dipped or soaked, with the linking ending in; of lying soaked in blood, or of being steeped in drink) (e:ama sisan sungah Amasa ~ om hi) (b:kidiah) (r:10.20.12/34.1.10) (q:draft)
kidik = (t:v) (w:sob/mourn/weep bitterly) (d:weep with heavy sobs; used together with kap weep) (e:bang hangin kapin ka ~ hiam) (r:19.42.9/24.13.17) (q:draft)
kidikdik = (t:v) (w:keep sobbing/go on mourning) (d:kidik sob, repeated to show that the weeping goes on) (e:kunin ka ~ hi) (r:19.35.14/19.43.2) (q:draft)
kidoksa = (t:adj) (w:drawn/unsheathed) (d:kidok be drawn out, with sa for a completed action; of a sword out of its sheath) (e:a ~ namsau khat omin) (r:13.21.16/23.21.15) (q:draft)
kidon = (t:v) (w:care for oneself/heed one another) (d:don care for, with ki, which turns the action on oneself or on each other; note bek a kidon, who care only for yourselves; kidon lohna, not heeding one another) (e:tuute don loin note bek a ~) (b:don) (r:26.34.10/20.18.19) (q:draft)
kidot = (t:v) (w:be asked/be questioned) (d:passive ki with dot ask) (e:Tua bangin a ~ ciangin siampite in) (b:dot) (r:37.2.12/44.22.24) (q:draft)
kidot = (t:v) (w:ask one another) (d:dot ask, with ki in the sense of each other) (e:Note khatlekhat na ~ uh) (b:dot) (r:43.16.19) (q:draft)
kidotna = (t:n) (w:questioning/controversy/dispute) (d:kidot ask one another, with the noun suffix na; thu kidotna, debate over questions) (e:Judah ngeina thu leh thu ~ khempeuh) (b:kidot) (r:44.26.3/55.2.23) (q:draft)
kigawivui = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be ground) (d:passive ki with gawivui crush fine; of fresh heads of grain) (e:phawk nadingin a ~ an pawlkhat) (b:gawivui) (r:3.2.16/3.2.14) (q:draft)
kiguaihna = (t:n) (w:hire/earnings) (d:in a kiguaihna sum, the money a prostitute is paid for hiring out the body) (e:A paktatnu a ~ sum ahi a) (b:guaihna) (r:5.23.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihah = (t:v) (w:be tended/be pruned/be dressed) (d:of vines; a kihah lo leenggui is a vine left untended) (e:a ~ lo leengguite panin zong) (b:hah) (r:3.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihah = (t:v) (w:be forced/be compelled) (d:in kihah piak, of drink pressed on a guest) (e:zu nekna zia pen ~ piak cih) (b:hah) (r:17.1.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kihalsan = (t:adj) (w:glowing/red-hot/burnished) (d:kihal be burned, with san red: heated in the fire until it glows; said of bronze) (e:sumngo ~ tawh a kibang khe) (b:kihal) (r:66.2.18/26.1.27) (q:draft)
kihansuah = (t:v) (w:encourage one another/exhort one another) (d:hansuah urge on, with ki in the sense of each other) (e:khat leh khat ~ un la) (b:hansuah) (r:52.5.11/58.3.13) (q:draft)
kihawlkhiatna = (t:n) (w:being driven out/expulsion) (d:kihawlkhiat be driven out, with the noun suffix na; before a noun of place, the place from which or to which one was driven) (e:Hih mipa a ~ thu Jesuh in) (b:kihawlkhiat) (r:43.9.35/42.11.24) (q:draft)
kihawmsak = (t:v) (w:be distributed/be divided out/be sent out) (d:passive ki with hawmsak distribute; of land shared out by lot and of letters sent round) (e:a gamh uh ~ ding hi) (b:hawmsak) (r:4.26.56/17.8.10) (q:draft)
kiheihei = (t:v) (w:turn to and fro/keep turning) (d:hei turn with ki, turn oneself, repeated to show that the action goes on; of a door on its hinges) (e:mi thadahpa a lupna tungah ~ hi) (r:20.26.14) (q:draft)
kihencip = (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied up) (d:passive ki with hencip bind fast; in Job 5:16 of the unjust being silenced) (e:Amaute lah ~ lo a) (b:hencip) (r:27.3.25/18.5.16) (q:draft)
kihoho = (t:v) (w:converse/talk together/commune) (d:talk with one another at length, the word repeated for an action that goes on; in Psalm 77:6 of communing with the own heart) (e:Kamkhum tawh i ~ ngei hi) (r:19.55.14/19.77.6) (q:draft)
kihongsa = (t:adj) (w:open/opened) (d:kihong be opened, with sa for a completed action; a kihongsa hankhuk, an open grave) (e:a ~ hankhuk tawh kibang hi) (b:kihong) (r:19.5.9/45.3.13) (q:draft)
kihuansa = (t:adj) (w:boiled/cooked) (d:kihuan be cooked, with sa for a completed action; in Ezekiel 27:18 said of iron, apparently worked or wrought) (e:Siampipa in a ~ tuutal liang) (b:kihuan) (r:4.6.19/26.27.18) (q:draft)
kihuauna = (t:n) (w:whispering) (d:kihuau whisper to one another, with the noun suffix na) (e:mi tampi’ ~ ka za hi) (b:kihuau) (r:19.31.13/10.12.19) (q:draft)
kikaih = (t:v) (w:be pulled/be drawn) (d:passive ki with kaih pull, used before another word: kikaih khiat, be pulled off; kikaih khop, be gathered together) (e:Mihonte a ~ khop ding ciangin) (b:kaih) (r:4.10.7/5.25.10) (q:draft)
kikak = (t:v) (w:be apart/be separate) (d:of two frames, apparently stand apart at the bottom while joined at the top; the NIV has double) (e:Tuate a bul lam-ah ~ a) (r:2.36.29/2.26.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikan = (t:v) (w:be investigated/be searched/be examined) (d:passive of kan, search, with the prefix ki: a matter is looked into) (e:ama thu a ~ khit ciangin) (b:kan) (r:44.25.26/15.4.19) (q:draft)
kikan = (t:v) (w:be stretched/be fastened) (d:found in a kikan'na khau, the cords by which a tent is stretched and held) (e:a ~’na khau khempeuh kitat khin hi) (r:24.10.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikawi = (t:v) (w:embrace/hug each other) (d:kawi, embrace, with the prefix ki, each other) (e:~ hun om a) (b:kawi) (r:21.3.5) (q:draft)
kikawi = (t:v) (w:be driven about/drift) (d:with heihei, be carried round and round, of a ship at sea; kawi, go around, with the prefix ki) (e:tuipi sungah ka ~ heihei lai takun) (b:kawi) (r:44.27.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikekin = (t:v) (w:be torn/be split) (d:kikek, be torn, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; kikekin phelnih a suak, was torn in two) (e:a taw dongin ~ phelnih a kisuah hi) (r:41.15.38/40.27.51) (q:draft)
kikhaina = (t:n) (w:hanging/being hung/crucifixion) (d:kikhai, be hung up, with the noun suffix na; a kikhaina mun, the place where he was hung) (e:Jesuh a ~ mun pen Jerusalem khuapi) (b:kikhai) (r:43.19.20/48.3.13) (q:draft)
kikhamval = (t:v) (w:be left over/remain over) (d:of food that is more than people could eat; a kikhamval, what is left after all have eaten their fill) (e:a ~ anlum le ngasa khawm uh a) (b:khamval) (r:41.6.43/42.9.17) (q:draft)
kikhapna = (t:n) (w:bargain/wager/pledge) (d:an agreement in which each side pledges something; khapna, pledge, with the prefix ki, each other) (e:ka topa tawh ~ khat bawl un) (b:khapna) (r:12.18.23) (q:draft)
kikhawlpa = (t:n) (w:friend/companion) (d:kikhawl, keep company, with pa marking a man: a man who keeps company with someone, used with tawh) (e:nangmah a hong zahtakte tawh a ~ ka hi hi) (b:kikhawl) (r:19.119.63/42.7.34) (q:draft)
kikhawmtuah = (t:v) (w:gather together/assemble/unite) (d:come together in one place or as one group, also to join against someone) (e:ka paang a beng dingin hong ~ uh hi) (r:18.16.10/16.8.1) (q:draft)
kikhelkik = (t:v) (w:be changed/be revoked/turn back) (d:kikhel, change, with kik, back or again: of a decree or a word, be altered or revoked; of people, turn from their ways) (e:a hawmkhiatsa thupiakna ~ thei lo hi) (b:kikhel) (r:27.6.15/66.9.20) (q:draft)
kikhemin = (t:v) (w:be deceived/be enticed/deceive oneself) (d:kikhem with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; nang leh nang kikhemin, deceiving yourself) (e:Nang leh nang ~) (b:kikhem) (r:24.37.9/5.11.16) (q:draft)
kikhentan = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be parted/be divided) (d:of flowing water, be stopped and separated) (e:Jordan a galkah ciangin Jordan tuite ~ hi) (r:6.4.7) (q:draft)
kikhenthangte = (t:n) (w:scattered people/exiles/outcasts) (d:kikhenthang, be scattered, with plural te: those who have been scattered) (e:Israel a ~ a kaikhawm Topa Pasian in) (b:kikhenthang) (r:23.56.8/23.11.12) (q:draft)
kikhep = (t:v) (w:be folded/fold) (d:be folded over double, of cloth; also of the leaves of a folding door) (e:a ~ ciangin a dung khap khat) (b:khep) (r:2.39.9/11.6.34) (q:draft)
kikhial = (t:v) (w:be a mistake/be done in error/err) (d:khial, be wrong, with the prefix ki: something is done wrongly without intending it) (e:a ~ hi kha ding hi) (b:khial) (r:1.43.12/4.15.24) (q:draft)
kikhiam = (t:v) (w:be reduced/be lessened/be diminished) (d:passive of khiam, reduce) (e:nangma sehna zah panin ~ ding hi) (b:khiam) (r:3.27.18/2.5.11) (q:draft)
kikhihnate = (t:n) (w:bonds/bindings/chains) (d:kikhihna with plural te: the things by which someone is bound) (e:amah a ~ a khut panin tolhkhia hi) (b:kikhihna) (r:7.15.14/19.116.16) (q:draft)
kikhualna = (t:n) (w:sake/benefit/regard) (d:khualna, regard, with the prefix ki: regard for oneself or care shown for someone; keimah ka kikhualna, for my own sake) (e:Keimah ka ~, keimah ka kingaihsutna-in) (b:khualna) (r:23.48.11/47.4.15) (q:draft)
kikhuang = (t:v) (w:stretch oneself out/lie stretched over) (d:lay oneself at full length upon someone, used with tungah) (e:paito-in ama tungah ~ hi) (r:12.4.35/12.4.34) (q:draft)
kikhulna = (t:n) (w:being thrown into fire/burning) (d:kikhul, be thrown into fire, with the noun suffix na; kat a kikhulna meiphualpi, the fiery lake where sulfur burns) (e:meikuang sungah ~ a thuak ding uh hi) (b:kikhul) (r:40.5.22/66.20.10) (q:draft)
kikihta = (t:v) (w:be feared/be dreaded) (d:passive of kihta, fear, with the prefix ki) (e:a nai a gamla ah a ~ mite) (b:kihta) (r:23.18.7) (q:draft)
kikipsaksa = (t:adj) (w:established/prescribed/ordained) (d:kikipsak, be established, with the completive suffix sa: already laid down; a kikipsaksa bangin, as it is prescribed) (e:a ~ bangin buk pawi bawl uh a) (b:kikipsak) (r:15.3.4/14.2.4) (q:draft)
kikoihte = (t:n) (w:things put/things stored) (d:kikoih, be put or kept, with plural te: the things that were placed or stored, as in sum kikoihte, the money that was put there) (e:mun sunga sum ~ leh) (b:kikoih) (r:23.45.3/1.43.18) (q:draft)
kikop = (t:v) (w:be allied/join with/be together with) (d:be joined with someone as a pair, used with tawh; kop, pair, with the prefix ki) (e:Siriate pen Efraim mite tawh ~) (b:kop) (r:23.7.2/12.18.25) (q:draft)
kikopa = (t:n) (w:one who cries out/one calling) (d:kiko, cry out, with pa marking a man: the man who is calling) (e:Gampa lakah a ~’ aw in) (b:kiko) (r:41.1.3/40.3.3) (q:draft)
kilaih = (t:v) (w:be replaced/be exchanged/alternate) (d:passive of laih, replace: one thing is put in the place of another; kilaih sak, take in turn) (e:anlum a lum lai tawh a ~ pah ding) (b:laih) (r:9.21.6/13.24.6) (q:draft)
kilakin = (t:v) (w:show/appear/present oneself) (d:kilak, show or appear, with the linking ending in; khat leh khat tungah kilakin, showing to one another) (e:tungah itna leh hehpihna ~) (b:kilak) (r:38.7.9/9.1.22) (q:draft)
kilamdangin = (t:adv) (w:differently/distinctly/with a distinction) (d:kilamdang, differ from one another, with the ending in: so as to be different) (e:Israel mite a ~ Topa in bawl hi) (b:kilamdang) (r:2.11.7/46.14.7) (q:draft)
kilamin = (t:v) (w:be built/be built up) (d:kilam, be built, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Tua inn pen suang lianpite tawh ~) (b:kilam) (r:15.5.8/42.21.5) (q:draft)
kilamto = (t:v) (w:be raised/be lifted up/be upraised) (d:passive of lamto, lift up; of a hand held up, also of trees standing high) (e:ama khut ~ lai hi) (b:lamto) (r:23.9.12/23.2.13) (q:draft)
kilangkhia = (t:v) (w:be revealed/come to light/be shown) (d:kilang, appear, with khia, out; kilangkhia sak, bring to light, uncover) (e:thuman i hihna hong ~ sak zo hi) (b:kilang) (r:24.51.10/24.49.10) (q:draft)
kilangsakin = (t:v) (w:reveal/show/make known) (d:kilangsak, reveal, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:ama minthan’na ~ a nungzuite in) (b:kilangsak) (r:43.2.11/45.3.7) (q:draft)
kilehngat = (t:v) (w:turn away from/be opposed to/be contrary) (d:face the opposite way from someone or something, used with tawh) (e:Topa tawh a lungsim a ~ mi in) (r:24.17.5/48.3.21) (q:draft)
kilelsak = (t:v) (w:let oneself be defeated/pretend to be beaten) (d:lel, be defeated, with the prefix ki and causative sak; with khem, deceive: act as if beaten) (e:amau mai-ah ~ khem uh a) (b:lelsak) (r:6.8.15/6.8.20) (q:draft)
kilemkik = (t:v) (w:be reconciled/be at peace again) (d:kilem, be at peace, with kik, again or back; used with tawh) (e:amah tawh ~ theih nading hong omsak) (b:kilem) (r:51.1.20/45.5.1) (q:draft)
kilemlohna = (t:n) (w:hostility/enmity/discord) (d:the state of not being at peace with one another; kilemlohna bawl, rebel) (e:Khazih in singlamteh hangin ~ thatin) (r:49.2.16/58.3.16) (q:draft)
kilote = (t:n) (w:those called/those named) (d:kilo, be called or named, with plural te: those whose names are given, those called by a name) (e:keima min tawh a ~ khempeuh) (b:kilo) (r:23.43.6/13.9.9) (q:draft)
kiluah = (t:v) (w:be inherited/be passed down) (d:passive of luah, inherit: property comes down from parents or from one generation to the next) (e:pate tung panin a ~ hi a) (b:luah) (r:20.19.14/26.44.28) (q:draft)
kiluhgawp = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be ravaged/be sacked) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action) (e:Khaldea gam ~ ding a) (b:kiluh) (r:24.50.10/26.36.35) (q:draft)
kimah = (t:prep) (w:around/round about) (d:kim, surroundings, with the place marker ah, placed after a noun) (e:biakna tau ~ na theh ding hi) (b:kim) (r:2.29.20/11.11.24) (q:draft)
kimai = (t:v) (w:face each other/face) (d:mai, face, with the prefix ki, each other; found with ngat, turn toward, or tuah, meet) (e:khat leh khat ~ tuah ni) (b:mai) (r:14.25.17/1.30.40) (q:draft)
kimaisakna = (t:n) (w:forgiveness) (d:kimaisak, be forgiven, with the noun suffix na; mawhna kimaisakna, forgiveness of sins) (e:mawhna ~ thu nomau kiangah hong kihilh) (b:kimaisak) (r:44.13.38/44.5.31) (q:draft)
kimaituah = (t:v) (w:face each other/meet face to face/confront) (d:stand face to face with someone, as opponents in battle or in court) (e:khat leh khat gal sungah ~ uh hi) (r:14.25.21/44.25.16) (q:draft)
kimakna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:makna, divorce, with the prefix ki; kimakna lai, certificate of divorce) (e:Moses in ~ lai gelhsakin masak thei hi) (b:makna) (r:41.10.4/23.50.1) (q:draft)
kimasa = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:of a woman who has been sent away by her husband; kima, divorced, with the completive suffix sa) (e:Meigong numei, a ~ numei, a kininsaksa numei) (b:kima) (r:3.21.14/26.44.22) (q:draft)
kimawlna = (t:n) (w:game/contest/sport) (d:kimawl, play, with the noun suffix na: a contest in which athletes compete) (e:~ sungah a kihel mi khempeuh in) (b:kimawl) (r:46.9.25/55.2.5) (q:draft)
kimuhmawh = (t:v) (w:overlook/turn a blind eye/ignore) (d:with bawl, do: act as if one had not seen a wrong) (e:tuapa ~ bawlin amah a thah kei uh leh) (r:3.20.4/20.10.10) (q:draft)
kinaipen = (t:adj) (w:nearest/closest) (d:kinai, be near, with pen, most; used with tawh for the place it is nearest to) (e:a kithat mipa tawh a ~ khuapi upate) (b:kinai) (r:5.21.6/5.21.3) (q:draft)
kinilhna = (t:n) (w:anointing) (d:kinilh, be anointed, with the noun suffix na; sathau kinilhna, anointing with oil) (e:amau’ sathau ~ in amau’ khang tawntungin) (b:kinilh) (r:2.40.15/13.14.8) (q:draft)
kinim = (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:of cloth, coloured; puan kinim, coloured garments) (e:a kinusia puan ~ a kizemte) (r:7.5.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kininsaksa = (t:adj) (w:defiled) (d:kininsak, be made unclean, with the completive suffix sa; of a woman who has been defiled) (e:numei paktat ahih kei leh a ~ numei) (b:kininsak) (r:3.21.7/3.21.14) (q:draft)
kinna = (t:n) (w:zeal/concern/eagerness) (d:kin, care about or be eager, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ puan tawh kitun ding hi) (b:kin) (r:23.59.17/50.4.10) (q:draft)
kinotkhia = (t:v) (w:be driven out/be driven away/be routed) (d:passive of notkhia, drive away) (e:Egypt gam panin amaute ~ a) (b:notkhia) (r:2.12.39/9.7.10) (q:draft)
kinsak = (t:v) (w:move/remove/shift) (d:kin, move, with causative sak: make something change its place) (e:mual ~ zawh nading upna) (b:kin) (r:46.13.2) (q:draft)
kinsak = (t:v) (w:make heed/cause to care about) (d:kin, heed or care about, with causative sak; hong kinsak kei in, do not let me give my attention to) (e:kei hong ~ kei in la) (b:kin) (r:19.119.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuaisiah = (t:v) (w:be subdued/be subjugated/be brought low) (d:passive of nuaisiah, subdue; a kinuaisiah mite, those who are cast down) (e:Tua bangin Filistia mite ~ hi) (b:nuaisiah) (r:13.20.4/47.7.6) (q:draft)
kinusiat = (t:v) (w:be left/be deserted/lie desolate) (d:form of kinusia, be left or deserted, used before words such as sung and dong) (e:leitang a ~ sung khempeuh) (b:kinusia) (r:14.36.21/23.30.17) (q:draft)
kipaidak = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast aside/be left lying) (d:be thrown away and left lying in the open, of an unwanted child or of dead bodies) (e:gamlakah nang hong ~ lel hi) (b:paidak) (r:26.16.5/66.11.8) (q:draft)
kipaihkhiat = (t:v) (w:be thrown out/be cast away/be dropped) (d:passive of paihkhiat, throw away; form used before words such as ciangin, ding and theih) (e:A hoih lo teng a ~ theih nadingin) (b:paihkhiat) (r:30.9.9/44.7.21) (q:draft)
kipaipihna = (t:n) (w:being brought/being taken) (d:kipaipih, be brought or taken, with the noun suffix na; salin kipaipihna, being led away as captives) (e:salin ~ a thuak ding uh hi) (b:kipaipih) (r:42.21.24/15.6.3) (q:draft)
kipaisak = (t:v) (w:be sent/be allowed to go) (d:passive of paisak, send or let go) (e:Topa’ omna-ah amaute bek ~ hi) (b:paisak) (r:26.40.46/17.3.12) (q:draft)
kipaithang = (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown down and left lying about) (e:misi luang ~ ding a) (r:24.9.22/26.6.4) (q:draft)
kipalsat = (t:v) (w:be broken/be violated/be transgressed) (d:passive of palsat, break a law or an agreement) (e:Topa aw, na thu ~ khin ahih ciangin) (b:palsat) (r:19.119.126/23.33.8) (q:draft)
kipankhia = (t:v) (w:come out from/proceed from/begin) (d:kipan, begin, with khia, out: start out from a place or source, used with panin) (e:lungsim panin hong ~ hi a) (b:kipan) (r:40.15.18/66.4.5) (q:draft)
kipau = (t:v) (w:speak to one another/be spoken) (d:pau, speak, with the prefix ki: speak with each other; kipau thei lo, that cannot be put into words) (e:thuman thutak kam ~ un) (b:pau) (r:38.8.16/45.8.26) (q:draft)
kipawlpihte = (t:n) (w:allies/friends/associates) (d:kipawlpih, be allied with, with plural te: those who are joined with someone) (e:hih mite pen Abram’ ~ ahi hi) (r:1.14.13/25.1.19) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:be grafted/be grafted in) (d:passive of peh, graft: a branch is joined onto another tree) (e:Eite tawh hong ~ theih nadingin) (b:peh) (r:45.11.19/45.11.24) (q:draft)
kipeh = (t:v) (w:bite each other) (d:with khat leh khat, one another; said of people who attack each other) (e:khat leh khat na ~, na kinek uh leh) (r:48.5.15) (q:draft)
kipelhin = (t:v) (w:escape/be free from/avoid) (d:kipelh, be free from, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; used with tawh for the thing escaped) (e:upna hangin sihna tawh ~ a kilato hi) (b:kipelh) (r:58.11.5/61.1.4) (q:draft)
kiphawkin = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be realised) (d:kiphawk, be remembered or noticed, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:hih nite ~ a kitan’ nading) (b:kiphawk) (r:17.9.28/41.14.9) (q:draft)
kiphawkmawh = (t:v) (w:overlook/pretend not to notice/hold back) (d:with bawl, do: act as if one had not noticed a wrong, let it pass) (e:mi’ hong hehsaknate ~ bawlna in minthan’na hi) (r:20.19.11/26.24.14) (q:draft)
kiphelkham = (t:v) (w:be split apart/split open) (d:passive of phelkham, split open; said of the ground or the earth) (e:amau’ nuai-ah lei ~ hi) (b:phelkham) (r:4.16.31/23.24.19) (q:draft)
kiphen = (t:v) (w:be opened) (d:passive of phen, open; said of a book or scroll) (e:Laibute zong ~ uh hi) (b:phen) (r:66.20.12/27.7.10) (q:draft)
kiphitsan = (t:v) (w:be hissed at/be scorned/be scoffed at) (d:passive of phitsan, hiss or scoff at; simmawhna tawh a kiphitsan, an object of scorn) (e:simmawhna tawh a ~ den ding gam) (b:phitsan) (r:24.18.16/24.51.37) (q:draft)
kiphunsan = (t:v) (w:grumble against each other/complain against each other) (d:phunsan, grumble against, with the prefix ki, each other) (e:Note khatlekhat ~ kei un) (b:phunsan) (r:43.6.43/59.5.9) (q:draft)
kipiaknate = (t:n) (w:things given/gifts/what was given) (d:kipiak, be given, with the noun suffix na and plural te: gifts offered to God, or with thu, the commands given to someone) (e:letsong tampi a ~ a gen uh ciangin) (b:kipiak) (r:42.21.5/2.34.34) (q:draft)
kipiaksa = (t:adj) (w:given/commanded) (d:kipiak, be given, with the completive suffix sa; thu a kipiaksa bangin, as was commanded) (e:tawntung dingin thu a ~ mah bangin) (b:kipiak) (r:3.6.22/19.122.3) (q:draft)
kipian = (t:v) (w:be created/be made) (d:found in kipian'sak, be created: pian, come into being, with the prefix ki and causative sak) (e:Khazih in leitung a ~’sak ma-in) (b:pian) (r:60.1.20/1.2.4) (q:draft)
kipsaknate = (t:n) (w:supports/stays) (d:kipsakna with plural te: the parts that hold something firm, as the supports of a stand) (e:a ~ leh a khawkte tungah) (b:kipsakna) (r:11.7.36/11.7.35) (q:draft)
kiptak = (t:adj) (w:firm/secure/steadfast) (d:kip, firm, with tak, truly: really firm, genuine; also used as an adverb, firmly) (e:~ khotakin i letkip ding kisam hi) (b:kip) (r:58.2.1/60.1.7) (q:draft)
kisaite = (t:n) (w:matters concerning/things relating to) (d:kisai, concern, with plural te; tawh kisaite, the things that concern or have to do with) (e:ka bawlsate tawh ~-ah thu hong pia ding) (b:kisai) (r:23.45.11/4.30.12) (q:draft)
kisamin = (t:v) (w:call to each other/be called) (d:kisam, be called, with the linking ending in; khat leh khat kisamin, calling to one another) (e:Amaute khat leh khat ~) (b:kisam) (r:23.6.3/66.17.14) (q:draft)
kisamsak = (t:v) (w:let be lacking/leave wanting/lose) (d:kisam, lack, with causative sak; found with lo or kei: let nothing be lacking, lose none) (e:amaute in bangmah ~ lo uh hi) (b:kisam) (r:11.4.27/43.17.12) (q:draft)
kisatgawp = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck hard/strike one another) (d:kisat, be beaten, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action; amau le amau kisatgawp, strike each other down) (e:mihon mai-ah hong ~ hi) (b:kisat) (r:44.16.37/7.7.22) (q:draft)
kisatkham = (t:v) (w:be smashed/be broken down/be broken open) (d:passive of satkham, smash by striking) (e:paknamtui taute ~ ding hi) (b:satkham) (r:26.6.4/34.2.6) (q:draft)
kisatnim = (t:v) (w:be crushed/be bruised) (d:be beaten down and crushed by blows) (e:eite’ mawhna hangin amah ~ hi) (r:23.53.5/23.53.10) (q:draft)
kiselin = (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/quarrel) (d:kisel, argue, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb; used with tawh, with) (e:Jew mite tawh thu ~ a zogawp hi) (b:kisel) (r:44.18.28/4.20.3) (q:draft)
kiselin = (t:v) (w:disguise/hide) (d:with mel, appearance: hiding what one looks like, disguising oneself) (e:na mel ~ Jeroboam’ zi na hih lam) (r:11.14.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisemsakte = (t:n) (w:forced labourers/those made to work) (d:kisemsak, be made to work, with plural te; aana tawh na a kisemsakte, those who are made to work by force) (e:aana tawh na a ~ a uk ahi hi) (b:kisemsak) (r:10.20.24/14.10.18) (q:draft)
kisepna = (t:n) (w:work/doing/being done) (d:kisep, be done or worked on, with the noun suffix na: the carrying out of a work or of deeds) (e:Pasian’ inn a ~ khawl hi) (b:kisep) (r:15.4.24/26.9.4) (q:draft)
kisialna = (t:n) (w:lying/being laid) (d:kisial, lie or be laid down, with the noun suffix na; a kisialna mun, the place where he was laid) (e:amah a ~ mun hong en un) (b:kisial) (r:40.28.6/43.20.12) (q:draft)
kisiangsaksa = (t:adj) (w:refined/purified) (d:kisiangsak, be purified, with the completive suffix sa; of silver and gold that has been refined) (e:a ~ ngun talen tulsagih) (b:kisiangsak) (r:13.29.4/13.28.18) (q:draft)
kisilhsak = (t:v) (w:be clothed/be robed/clothe oneself) (d:silhsak, clothe, with the prefix ki: have a garment put on) (e:kumpipuan ~ a, thahatna tawh kidim hi) (b:silhsak) (r:19.93.1) (q:draft)
kisimin = (t:v) (w:be read) (d:kisim, be read, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Lai Siangtho Nipi ni simin ~) (b:kisim) (r:44.15.21) (q:draft)
kisimin = (t:v) (w:be attacked/be invaded) (d:passive of sim, attack, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:Nang hong ~ hong kilak ni ciangin) (r:26.26.15) (q:draft)
kisinsak = (t:v) (w:train/teach/be trained) (d:kisin, learn or practise, with causative sak: make someone or something learn; also of a person who has been given training) (e:zuauthu gen dingin ~ uh a) (b:kisin) (r:24.9.5/27.1.4) (q:draft)
kisu = (t:v) (w:be struck/be touched) (d:passive of su, touch or strike; with kha: be struck or touched by something, as by the heat of the sun) (e:tawh a ~ kha nawn kei ding uh hi) (b:su) (r:66.7.16) (q:draft)
kisu = (t:v) (w:wrong each other/harm each other) (d:su, harm, with the prefix ki, each other; with khatlekhat, one another) (e:Note khatlekhat ~-in) (b:su) (r:46.6.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisu = (t:v) (w:be pounded/be crushed) (d:passive of su, pound; sum sunga a kisu, what is pounded in a mortar) (e:sum sunga a ~ gawp bangin) (b:su) (r:23.41.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuahin = (t:v) (w:become/be made into/be divided into) (d:kisuah, be made into, with the linking ending in; after a number of parts: forming that many groups) (e:Gam khat peuhpeuh phelnih ~ kido le-uh) (b:kisuah) (r:41.3.24/7.9.34) (q:draft)
kisuai = (t:v) (w:be portrayed/be drawn/be engraved) (d:of figures and pictures, be drawn or worked on a surface) (e:mangkawlsing lim a ~ hi) (r:24.52.22/26.8.10) (q:draft)
kisuanin = (t:v) (w:carry on the shoulder/take up/shoulder) (d:kisuan, put a load on one's own shoulder, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:ka liangko-ah van ~ ka paikhia hi) (b:kisuan) (r:26.12.7/40.16.24) (q:draft)
kisukkhak = (t:v) (w:be touched/come into contact/be harmed) (d:passive of sukkhak, touch; used with tawh for the thing touched; of a person, have a hand laid on him) (e:misi tawh a ~ manin mi nin) (b:sukkhak) (r:37.2.13/6.2.19) (q:draft)
kisusiacip = (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be laid desolate) (d:kisusia, be destroyed, with cip marking that it is done completely) (e:Tu-in na innte ~ ding hi) (b:kisusia) (r:40.23.38/34.1.15) (q:draft)
kisusiamang = (t:v) (w:be completely destroyed/be wiped out) (d:passive of susiamang, destroy completely) (e:Tua khuapi ~ ding a) (b:susiamang) (r:24.49.2/3.27.29) (q:draft)
kisutuah = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:of people, come together in one place) (e:nasem ding bekin tua lai-ah ~ uh hi) (r:16.5.16/26.33.31) (q:draft)
kitamkham = (t:v) (w:be shattered/be broken to pieces/crumble) (d:be broken apart, of mountains, of nations crushing one another and of the heart) (e:taanglai mualliante ~ a) (b:tamkham) (r:35.3.6/24.23.9) (q:draft)
kitamte = (t:n) (w:broken ones/broken pieces) (d:kitam be broken with the plural te, those that are broken; lungsim kitamte are the brokenhearted and beelpei kitamte are potsherds) (e:Amah in lungsim ~ damsak a) (b:kitam) (r:19.147.3/18.41.30) (q:draft)
kitamzante = (t:n) (w:broken ones/shattered ones) (d:kitamzan with the plural te; lungsim kitamzante are the brokenhearted) (e:Lungsim ~ kiangah Topa om a) (b:kitamzan) (r:19.34.18/23.61.1) (q:draft)
kitanna = (t:n) (w:being cut off/being broken off) (d:kitan be broken or cut off with the noun suffix na; lu kitanna is beheading) (e:lu ~ a thuak mite) (b:kitan) (r:66.20.4/27.7.20) (q:draft)
kitansak = (t:v) (w:break/cut/cut off) (d:kitan be broken or cut off with sak, cause, make something break, or of a navel cord, have it cut) (e:taamtaak singte ~ a) (b:kitan) (r:19.29.5/26.16.4) (q:draft)
kitawphah = (t:adj) (w:rocky) (d:used with suang stone, suang kitawphah leilak is rocky ground, where rock lies under a thin layer of soil) (e:Suang ~ leilak a tu khaicite) (r:40.13.20/41.4.16) (q:draft)
kitelin = (t:adv) (w:clearly/distinctly/plainly) (d:kitel be clear with the ending in) (e:a cihnopna a ~ gen uh a) (b:kitel) (r:16.8.8/46.14.8) (q:draft)
kitengin = (t:v) (w:intermarrying/marrying) (d:kiteng marry with the linking ending in, used with tawh, with) (e:a gamta mite tawh ~ kizom kik ding) (b:kiteng) (r:15.9.14/6.23.12) (q:draft)
kitenna = (t:n) (w:marriage/intermarriage) (d:kiten marry with the noun suffix na; kitenna bawl and kitenna nei are to marry) (e:Kote tawh ~ hong bawl un) (b:kiten) (r:1.34.9/42.20.34) (q:draft)
kithahlup = (t:v) (w:be slaughtered/be killed/be cut down) (d:of many people, be killed and laid low) (e:mi khempeuh a ~ khit nadingin) (b:thahlup) (r:31.1.9/24.25.34) (q:draft)
kithang = (t:v) (w:be reported/be widely known/spread) (d:of fame or news, be heard of everywhere) (e:mi khempeuhte lakah ~ ahih ciangin) (r:45.16.19/26.16.14) (q:draft)
kithangsak = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be made famous/be glorified) (d:of God or his name, be made great and known everywhere) (e:leitungah ka min hong ~ hi) (b:thangsak) (r:19.46.10/19.47.9) (q:draft)
kitheikim = (t:v) (w:be known to all/be well known/be seen by all) (d:thei know with kim all, be known or seen by everyone) (e:mite’ lakah a ~ mi khat) (b:theikim) (r:20.31.23/42.17.24) (q:draft)
kithosak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised up) (d:be raised to life from death) (e:sihna panin a ~ Jesuh Khrih) (b:thosak) (r:55.2.8/42.24.6) (q:draft)
kithukhat = (t:v) (w:conspire/plot together/be of one mind) (d:thu khat one matter with ki, agree together on one plan, in these verses against someone) (e:siat nading geelin ~ uh hi) (b:thukhat) (r:19.83.5/19.2.1) (q:draft)
