luisa = (t:adj) (w:old/long-standing/outdated) (d:lui old with sa, which marks a state already reached; a luisa is what has grown old, and of a disease chronic) (e:a om ~ phak natna hi) (b:lui) (r:3.13.11/58.8.13) (q:draft)
lumkhawmsa = (t:adj) (w:having slept with) (d:lumkhawm lie with, with sa marking a completed act; before a noun, who has slept with someone) (e:pasal tawh a ~ numei peuhmah) (b:lumkhawm) (r:4.31.17/28.3.1) (q:draft)
lungdamkoh = (t:v) (w:give thanks/thank) (d:lungdam joy with koh express; lungdamkoh nading is thanksgiving and lungdamkoh piakna a thank offering) (e:Pasian’ tungah ~ nading zong) (r:47.9.12/19.107.22) (q:draft)
lungdamsakte = (t:n) (w:those who please) (d:lungdamsak make glad with te, the people who do so; amah a lungdamsakte is those who please him) (e:amah a ~ tungah pilna) (b:lungdamsak) (r:21.2.26) (q:draft)
lunggulhte = (t:n) (w:lovers) (d:lunggulh desire with te, those whom one desires; na lunggulhte is your lovers) (e:nang in na ~ tungah letsong) (b:lunggulh) (r:26.16.33) (q:draft)
lunggulhte = (t:n) (w:those who desire) (d:lunggulh desire with te, the people who long for something) (e:Siah a ~ tuancil in la) (b:lunggulh) (r:19.68.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
lunghihmawhpih = (t:v) (w:be concerned about/worry about/be afraid of) (d:lunghihmawh worry with pih, which adds the person or thing one is troubled about) (e:amah bek mah in note hong ~ hi) (b:lunghihmawh) (r:50.2.20/24.10.2) (q:draft)
lungkhauhin = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/hard-hearted) (d:lungkhauh with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:ka tapa uh ~ lehdo thei a) (b:lungkhauh) (r:5.21.20/27.5.20) (q:draft)
lungmuanhuai = (t:adj) (w:safe/secure/reassuring) (d:giving peace of mind, free from danger; lungmuang at ease with huai, which marks what causes or deserves a feeling) (e:ka lampi ~ sak hi) (r:10.22.33/9.20.21) (q:draft)
lungsi = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be dismayed/falter) (d:literally the heart dies, lung heart with si die; said of sudden fear or loss of courage) (e:~ lo, lungkia lo ding hi) (r:23.42.4/1.42.28) (q:draft)
lungsimtak = (t:n) (w:sincerity/whole heart/good faith) (d:lungsim heart, mind with tak true; lungsimtak tawh is sincerely, wholeheartedly) (e:~ tawh zui ahih manin) (b:lungsim) (r:6.14.14/42.8.15) (q:draft)
lungso = (t:adj) (w:furious/enraged/wrathful) (d:very angry, literally the heart is hot, lung heart with so be hot) (e:~ sa-in hong thuhilh kei in) (r:19.6.1/44.7.54) (q:draft)
lungtaii = (t:adj) (w:cheerful/joyful/glad) (d:glad at heart, lung heart with taii bright, cheerful; lungtaii takin is joyfully, and in Amos 5:18 it stands opposite lungzin) (e:~ takin tai ding a kipan) (r:19.19.5/30.5.18) (q:draft)
lungtomna = (t:n) (w:quick temper/hot temper/impatience) (d:lungtom short-tempered with the noun suffix na; set against lungduaina patience) (e:~ in kitotna piangsak a) (b:lungtom) (r:20.15.18/20.14.29) (q:draft)
lupnate = (t:n) (w:beds/couches/bedding) (d:lupna bed with plural te) (e:kham leh ngun kibawl ~ kikoih hi) (b:lupna) (r:17.1.6/10.17.28) (q:draft)
lutkhawm = (t:v) (w:enter together/go in with) (d:lut enter with khawm together) (e:biakna innpi sungah a ~ hi) (b:lut) (r:44.3.8/40.25.10) (q:draft)
lutthei = (t:v) (w:can enter/be able to enter) (d:lut enter with thei be able) (e:tua khuapi sungah ~ ding uh hi) (b:lut) (r:66.21.27/40.7.21) (q:draft)
luttheih = (t:v) (w:be able to enter) (d:the form of lutthei used before nading; luttheih nading is so that one may enter, the right to enter) (e:Tua vokte sungah a ~ nadingun) (b:lutthei) (r:42.8.32/58.10.19) (q:draft)
maanin = (t:adv) (w:rightly/justly/uprightly/truly) (d:maan true, right with in) (e:thu a ~ ka khen ding hi) (b:maan) (r:19.75.2/20.4.27) (q:draft)
madawk = (t:adj) (w:foremost/at the front) (d:being at the front or the nearest edge; a madawk teng is the foremost part, in Numbers the outskirts of the camp as seen from a height) (e:amaute a ~ teng bek na mu ding) (r:4.23.13/4.22.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
madawkin = (t:adv) (w:forward/in front/at the front) (d:madawk foremost with in; hong madawkin is coming forward) (e:a ~ Uriah koih inla) (b:madawk) (r:10.11.15/11.22.21) (q:draft)
madawkte = (t:n) (w:front ranks/those in front/vanguard) (d:madawk foremost with plural te; the front part of an army, set against nungdalte the rear) (e:A ~ in a haltum thei meikuang) (b:madawk) (r:29.2.3/29.2.20) (q:draft)
maitaina = (t:n) (w:cheerfulness/cheerful look/brightness) (d:maitai cheerful, bright of face with the noun suffix na; in Amos 5:20 brightness as opposed to gloom) (e:~ in lung nuamsak a) (b:maitai) (r:20.15.30/30.5.20) (q:draft)
maitangte = (t:n) (w:faces) (d:maitang face with plural te) (e:a ~ uh meikuang bang ding hi) (b:maitang) (r:23.13.8/26.10.22) (q:draft)
maksa = (t:adj) (w:divorced) (d:ma divorce in its form mak, with sa marking a completed act; a maksa numei is a divorced woman; not the word mak son-in-law) (e:a pasal in a ~ numei) (r:3.21.7/40.5.32) (q:draft)
maleep = (t:n) (w:deposit/pledge/guarantee) (d:something given in advance as assurance that the rest will follow; in the verses said of the Holy Spirit) (e:eite luahna ~ ahi hi) (r:49.1.14/47.5.5) (q:draft)
malkhat = (t:n) (w:one item/one word) (d:mal a single item with khat one; malkhat khit malkhat is one item after another, where the English has rule on rule or precept upon precept) (e:~ khit ~, gualkhat khit gualkhat) (r:23.28.10/23.28.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
mana = (t:n) (w:manna) (d:the food God gave Israel in the wilderness) (e:~ koihna kham beel tawh) (r:58.9.4) (q:draft)
mana = (t:conj) (w:because/because of) (d:man reason with a; follows the clause that gives the reason, like manin) (e:midangte sangin ka pil zawk ~) (b:man) (r:27.2.30/48.5.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
mangman = (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:one who has dreams and tells them; mang dream with man get, catch; mangman pa is the dreamer) (e:~ khat ahi zongin hong khangin) (r:5.13.1/1.37.19) (q:draft)
mangmuh = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:what is seen as in a dream, a prophetic vision; mang dream with muh, the form of mu see) (e:ka ~ masak sunga ka muh mipa) (b:mangmu) (r:27.9.21/9.3.1) (q:draft)
mangngilhna = (t:n) (w:forgetting/forgetfulness/oblivion) (d:mangngilh forget with the noun suffix na; mangngilhna gam is the land of oblivion) (e:~ gam sungah na hotkhiat huhna) (b:mangngilh) (r:19.88.12/24.3.21) (q:draft)
mangsakte = (t:n) (w:those who lose) (d:mangsak cause to be lost, lose, with te, the people who do so) (e:hangah a nuntakna a ~ in) (b:mangsak) (r:42.9.24/40.16.25) (q:draft)
mannop = (t:v) (w:be willing to listen/be willing to obey) (d:man, the form of mang obey, with nop want; in the verses always with kei, refuse to listen) (e:thu nangawn a ~ kei leh) (r:40.18.17/42.16.31) (q:draft)
mapaisak = (t:v) (w:send ahead/send on before) (d:mapai go ahead with sak cause) (e:ama mai-ah a ~ hi) (b:mapai) (r:42.10.1/41.6.45) (q:draft)
mapekin = (t:conj) (w:before/even before) (d:placed after a verb, already before something happened; ma before with pek and in) (e:mual neute a kibawl ~) (r:20.8.25/45.5.13) (q:draft)
masapa = (t:n) (w:first one/first man) (d:masa first with pa marking a man; a gen masapa is the first to speak) (e:a gen ~ pau loin om ta hen) (b:masa) (r:46.14.30/20.18.17) (q:draft)
matin = (t:adv) (w:as captive/captured) (d:mat seize with in, in the state of being seized; gal matin is taken captive in war) (e:a tanute gal ~) (b:mat) (r:4.21.29/24.30.16) (q:draft)
mawhmaisak = (t:v) (w:forgive/pardon) (d:forgive sins, mawhmai with sak; mawhmaisak nadingin biakna is a sin offering) (e:leitungah ~ theih nading thu nei hi) (b:mawhmai) (r:41.2.10/58.10.8) (q:draft)
meikatna = (t:n) (w:burning/fire/blaze) (d:meikat be on fire with the noun suffix na) (e:tua khua ~ pan a pusuak meikhu) (r:66.18.18/29.2.30) (q:draft)
meikuangte = (t:n) (w:flames) (d:meikuang flame with plural te) (e:a ~ in nang hong kangtum lo ding) (b:meikuang) (r:23.43.2/19.104.4) (q:draft)
meimatumte = (t:n) (w:boils) (d:meimatum boil, a swollen sore, with plural te) (e:a nasia ~ tawh na khukte) (b:meimatum) (r:5.28.35/5.28.27) (q:draft)
melhoihin = (t:adj) (w:beautiful/lovely) (d:melhoih with the linking ending in, used when another descriptive word or verb follows; a melhoihin bawl is make beautiful) (e:Rachel ~ ngaihbaang hi) (b:melhoih) (r:1.29.17/26.31.9) (q:draft)
menzipa = (t:n) (w:governor/ruler/tetrarch) (d:menzi governor with pa marking a man; used of Felix the Roman governor and of Herod the tetrarch) (e:~ kiangah a lai puak uh pia-in) (b:menzi) (r:44.23.33/42.3.19) (q:draft)
metkhia = (t:v) (w:shave off/cut off) (d:met shave with khia out, off) (e:a khamul zong ~ ding hi) (b:met) (r:23.7.20/3.14.9) (q:draft)
metsak = (t:v) (w:shave/have shaved) (d:met shave with sak; shave the hair of another person or have it shaved off) (e:a khamul uh ~ a) (b:met) (r:13.19.4/7.16.19) (q:draft)
migit = (t:v) (w:show favor/be gracious/be kind) (d:the form of migi kind used before hangin and nading; be kind or gracious to someone) (e:Mi gilote tungah na ~ hangin) (b:migi) (r:23.26.10/16.1.11) (q:draft)
mihaipi = (t:n) (w:great fool/fool/stupid person) (d:mihai fool with pi great) (e:a tawpna-ah ~ a suak ding hi) (b:mihai) (r:24.17.11/18.18.3) (q:draft)
mihaupa = (t:n) (w:rich man) (d:mihau rich person with pa marking a man) (e:~ pen amah pil kisa a) (b:mihau) (r:20.28.11/20.13.8) (q:draft)
miksite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ants) (d:miksi ant with plural te) (e:~ kiangah pai in la) (r:20.6.6/20.30.25) (q:draft)
milimin = (t:n) (w:into an idol/as an idol) (d:milim idol, image with the marker in; milimin bawl is make something into an idol) (e:Amau’ ngunte ~ bawl uh a) (b:milim) (r:28.13.2/24.10.3) (q:draft)
minamdangte = (t:n) (w:other nations/nations/foreign peoples) (d:minamdang foreigner, another people, with plural te) (e:~ lakah nong thehthang khin hi) (b:minamdang) (r:19.44.11/26.36.23) (q:draft)
minthannate = (t:n) (w:glories/glory/splendor) (d:minthanna glory with plural te) (e:a ~ uh lopa pak tawh kibang hi) (b:minthanna) (r:60.1.24/19.145.12) (q:draft)
mipite = (t:n) (w:people/crowds/multitude) (d:mipi the public, the mass of people, with plural te) (e:~ in Jesuh a sawlkhia uh hi) (b:mipi) (r:41.5.17/23.5.14) (q:draft)
misiate = (t:n) (w:bad people/the evil/the wicked) (d:misia bad person with plural te; set against mihoihte good people) (e:mihoihte le ~ tungah a kibangin) (b:misia) (r:40.5.45/21.9.2) (q:draft)
mithahna = (t:n) (w:murder/killing/bloodshed) (d:mithah kill a person with the noun suffix na) (e:Zuauna leh ~ tawh a kidim khuapi) (r:34.3.1/40.15.19) (q:draft)
mitin = (t:n) (w:with the eyes/with one's own eyes) (d:mit eye with the marker in, showing the eye as the means of seeing) (e:Ka ~ ka mu zo hi) (b:mit) (r:42.2.32/1.45.12) (q:draft)
mitkhu = (t:n) (w:eyelid) (d:mit eye with khu cover; mitkhu mul, the hair of it, stands for the eyebrows in Leviticus 14:9) (e:i ~ a kawt theih nadingin) (r:24.9.18/3.14.9) (q:draft)
mitkhute = (t:n) (w:eyelids) (d:mitkhu eyelid with plural te) (e:ka ~ ka kikhupsak kei ding hi) (b:mitkhu) (r:19.132.1/18.16.16) (q:draft)
mizuaute = (t:n) (w:liars) (d:mi person with zuau lie and plural te, people who tell lies) (e:~ leh mikhemte kiang panin) (r:19.120.2/20.13.2) (q:draft)
mongteep = (t:n) (w:hem/edge/fringe) (d:the border at the lower edge of a garment; puan mongteep is the edge of a cloak) (e:a puan ~ a lawngsim hi) (r:40.9.20/42.8.44) (q:draft)
mothakte = (t:n) (w:brides) (d:mothak bride, mo bride with thak new, and plural te) (e:zi nei thakte leh ~’ awte) (b:mothak) (r:24.33.11/24.7.34) (q:draft)
mualin = (t:adj) (w:faded/dim) (d:said of a spot on the skin that has grown faint, in mualin om be faded; not the word mual mountain) (e:~ a om leh) (r:3.13.21/3.13.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
mualpi = (t:n) (w:great mountain/mountain) (d:mual mountain with pi great) (e:~ banga lian a) (b:mual) (r:24.51.25/66.8.8) (q:draft)
mualtan = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:viper/snake) (d:a poisonous snake; in the verses always in the address translated brood of vipers) (e:No ~’ suante aw) (r:40.12.34/40.3.7) (q:draft)
muantaak = (t:adj) (w:trustworthy/reliable) (d:worthy of trust, muan trust with taak worthy) (e:a thupiaknate ~ mahmah hi) (r:19.111.7/66.22.6) (q:draft)
muante = (t:n) (w:trusted ones/trusted friends) (d:muan trust with plural te, the people one relies on; lawm muante is trusted friends) (e:Na lawm ~ in nang hong khem uh a) (b:muan) (r:24.38.22/18.12.20) (q:draft)
muhkhak = (t:v) (w:see/catch sight of) (d:the form of muhkha used before ciangin and ding; mu see with kha, which marks that the act happens to reach its object) (e:note hong ~ uh ciangin) (r:26.5.14/47.3.13) (q:draft)
muhtangpi = (t:n) (w:full view/plain sight) (d:after a possessive, before the very eyes of someone, in full view; muhtang with pi) (e:amaute’ ~ mahin vanah Jesuh kilato a) (r:44.1.9/40.17.2) (q:draft)
muktu = (t:v) (w:stumble) (d:in the verses said of the oxen that drew the cart with the ark) (e:bawngtalte ~ ahih manin) (r:13.13.9/10.6.6) (q:draft)
muna = (t:n) (w:place) (d:mun place with the linking a, of or at the place; hih lai muna thungetna is the prayer offered in this place) (e:hih lai ~ thungetna na bil hong ngat in) (b:mun) (r:14.6.40/15.1.4) (q:draft)
mupi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:vulture/kite) (d:a large bird of prey in the lists of unclean birds, named beside the eagle; the English versions have vulture in Leviticus and kite in Deuteronomy) (e:muvanlai, ~, luimu) (r:3.11.13/5.14.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
musi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:hawk) (d:a bird of prey in the lists of unclean birds) (e:vatawt, ~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.16/5.14.15) (q:draft)
mutgawp = (t:v) (w:blow violently/blow hard) (d:mut blow with gawp, which marks violent or thorough action; said of a storm wind) (e:huihpi hat in ~ ding hi) (b:mut) (r:26.13.11/18.27.23) (q:draft)
mutkhia = (t:v) (w:blow away/carry off) (d:mut blow with khia out, away; said of wind) (e:huih in amaute ~ ding a) (b:mut) (r:23.41.16/23.57.13) (q:draft)
nadingah = (t:ppm) (d:nading, which turns a verb into its place or purpose, with the place marker ah; pai nadingah is to where someone is going, on his way) (e:a pai ~ pai hi) (b:nading) (r:1.25.34/1.18.33) (q:draft)
nahoih = (t:n) (w:good thing/good things) (d:na thing with hoih good) (e:a gilkialte ~ tawh vah sak hi) (b:hoih) (r:19.107.9/10.7.28) (q:draft)
naisan = (t:n) (w:gore) (d:found only in the pair sisan naisan, the blood in which a newborn child lies; the meaning of naisan by itself is not clear) (e:sisan ~ lak-a na kitomtom) (r:26.16.6/26.16.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
naizaw = (t:adj) (w:nearer/closer) (d:nai near with zaw more; of time and of kinship) (e:kei sangin a ~ tanau khat) (b:nai) (r:8.3.12/45.13.11) (q:draft)
nakah = (t:n) (w:in the nose/in the nostrils) (d:nak nose, nostril with the place marker ah) (e:na ~ nakpheh hong bulhin) (b:nak) (r:12.19.28/18.27.3) (q:draft)
namcin = (t:adj) (w:every kind of/all kinds of) (d:nam kind with cin every, placed after the noun; thupha namcin, every blessing, is the greeting in a letter) (e:singgah lim ~ i kong gei-ah) (r:22.7.13/15.5.7) (q:draft)
namsak = (t:v) (w:let kiss/allow to kiss) (d:nam kiss with sak let, cause; in the verses of a parting kiss; not the word nam kind) (e:kam vaikhakin hong ~ phot in) (b:nam) (r:11.19.20/1.31.28) (q:draft)
nasiat = (t:adj) (w:severe/intense/great) (d:the form of nasia severe used before ma-in and lam; a nasiat ma-in is before it grows severe) (e:a ~ ma-in kitot khawl pak in) (b:nasia) (r:20.17.14/18.2.13) (q:draft)
naugil = (t:n) (w:womb) (d:nau child with gil belly) (e:~ khakcip ding ka hi hiam) (r:23.66.9/18.3.10) (q:draft)
naupaiite = (t:n) (w:pregnant women) (d:naupaii be with child, with plural te, those who are pregnant) (e:~ le naungek neite a dingin) (b:naupaii) (r:40.24.19/42.21.23) (q:draft)
nautum = (t:n) (w:youngest/youngest child) (d:the last-born of the brothers; a nautum pen is the youngest) (e:David in a ~ pen ahi hi) (r:9.17.14/9.16.11) (q:draft)
nbsp = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word, the HTML entity nbsp left in the Bible text)
nehin = (t:v) (w:come near/approach/step forward) (d:neh come near with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows; mai lam nehin pai is step forward) (e:mai lam ~ hong pai uh hi) (b:neh) (r:4.12.5/43.19.3) (q:draft)
neihlam = (t:n) (d:the fact that someone has something; neih, the form of nei have, with lam, which turns the clause into the thing known or seen) (e:theihna na ~ ka thei hi) (r:27.5.14/43.19.10) (q:draft)
neihlelam = (t:n) (w:wealth/possessions/property) (e:a inn dimin ~ ka pia hi) (r:20.8.21/21.5.19) (q:draft)
neihsunte = (t:n) (w:only possessions/the little one has) (d:neihsun the only one that a person has, with plural te) (e:Mi tagahte’ la ~ guksak uh a) (b:neihsun) (r:18.24.3/37.1.9) (q:draft)
neikha = (t:v) (w:have/have a share in) (d:nei have with kha, which marks that the act reaches its object; in the verses always negated, not have at all, and ngaihsutin neikha lo is not even have in mind) (e:nuntakna ~ het lo uh hi) (r:49.4.18/19.101.4) (q:draft)
neikhin = (t:v) (w:already have/have already) (d:nei have with khin already) (e:thukimna ~ uh ahih manin) (b:nei) (r:43.9.22/42.19.25) (q:draft)
neizo = (t:v) (w:be able to have/manage to have/have obtained) (d:nei have with zo, which marks ability or completion; thu neizo lo is have no force) (e:ka deih zahzah zong ka ~ hi) (b:nei) (r:21.2.8/35.1.4) (q:draft)
nekha = (t:v) (w:eat/get to eat) (d:ne eat with kha, which marks that the act reaches its object, eat any of something; na nekha kei ding is you will not get to eat it) (e:nang in na ~ kei ding hi) (r:12.7.19/3.23.29) (q:draft)
nekloh = (t:v) (w:not eat) (d:nek, the form of ne eat, with loh, the form of lo not; nekloh nading is so as not to eat) (e:I ~ hangin siatna om tuan lo a) (r:46.8.8/44.23.14) (q:draft)
nemang = (t:v) (w:devour/eat up/consume) (d:ne eat with mang gone, eat until nothing is left) (e:kauphe in ~ ding hi) (r:5.28.38/3.26.38) (q:draft)
nemin = (t:adj) (w:gentle/soft/mild) (d:nem soft with the linking ending in, used when another word follows; lungsim nemin is being gentle and kam nemin with gentle words) (e:Kam ~ dawnna in hehna damsak a) (b:nem) (r:20.15.1/56.3.2) (q:draft)
nengniamsak = (t:v) (w:let oppress/allow to oppress) (d:nengniam, oppress, with the causative sak; let one person oppress another, mostly negated) (e:amaute kuamah ~ lo hi) (b:nengniam) (r:13.16.21/19.119.122) (q:draft)
nethei = (t:v) (w:can eat/may eat) (d:ne, eat, with thei, be able or be allowed to) (e:singkung khempeuh na ~ ding hi) (b:ne) (r:1.2.16/58.5.12) (q:draft)
neupente = (t:n) (w:the smallest/the least/the lowliest) (d:neupen, smallest, with the plural te; those who are smallest or lowest of all) (e:a ~ nangawn kumpi a suaksak thei) (b:neupen) (r:27.4.17/23.60.22) (q:draft)
ngahnop = (t:v) (w:want to get/wish to receive) (d:ngah, get, with nop, want; found before man, because, as in sum ngahnop manin, because of wanting money) (e:sum ~ manin mi khat in) (r:18.17.5/42.6.18) (q:draft)
ngaihmuang = (t:adj) (w:secure/at ease/carefree) (d:without fear or worry; ngaihmuang takin is securely, in peace) (e:~ taka a om gam) (r:24.49.31/24.43.12) (q:draft)
ngaihnop = (t:v) (w:want to listen/be willing to hear) (d:ngaih, listen, with nop, want; mi’ ngaihnop dingin pau is speak so that people like to listen, and ngaihnop-huai is pleasant to listen to) (e:na thugen uh hong ~ kei leh) (r:40.10.14/51.4.6) (q:draft)
ngaihsutzaw = (t:v) (w:consider more/regard more highly) (d:ngaihsut, consider, with zaw, more; thupi ngaihsutzaw is consider more important, value above another) (e:midangte thupi ~ un) (b:ngaihsut) (r:50.2.3/18.34.19) (q:draft)
ngakngak = (t:v) (w:keep waiting for/wait and wait) (d:ngak, wait, doubled to show that the waiting goes on) (e:hun ding a ~ mi khat ahi hi) (r:42.2.25/39.3.1) (q:draft)
ngasak = (t:v) (w:make face/turn toward/lay on) (d:nga, face or be turned toward, with the causative sak; make a thing face a direction, and of hands, lay them on) (e:lu tungah amau’ khut ~ inla) (b:nga) (r:3.24.14/1.30.40) (q:draft)
ngatna = (t:n) (w:direction faced/facing) (d:ngat, face or turn toward, with the noun suffix na; the side or direction toward which a thing is turned) (e:Na ~ san peuhpeuh vat gawp in) (b:ngat) (r:26.21.16/26.47.1) (q:draft)
ngeipa = (t:n) (d:ngei, have done or been before, with pa, the male one; after a verb or descriptive word, the man who did so or was so before, as in a mittaw ngeipa, the man who had been blind) (e:a mittaw ~ sam kik uh a) (b:ngei) (r:43.9.24/19.27.9) (q:draft)
ngek = (t:adj) (w:tender/delicate/tiny) (d:small and soft like a newborn; a no ngek is a tender young one and a ngek pen is the least or smallest) (e:A mel hoih, a ~ dikdek) (r:24.6.2/1.33.13) (q:draft)
ngeksuak = (t:adj) (w:tender/delicate/gentle) (d:of a person who is soft and refined, not used to hardship) (e:Note lakah a ~, a cithei pen mipa) (r:5.28.54/5.28.57) (q:draft)
ngeungau = (t:adv) (w:deeply/utterly) (d:descriptive word that strengthens what goes before, of deep longing and of thick darkness) (e:sih ding lunggulh ~ napi) (r:18.3.21/23.8.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngik = (t:v) (w:growl/roar) (d:of a lion over its prey, and of an enemy likened to one) (e:a sa nek ding a ~ ciangin) (r:23.31.4/23.5.30) (q:draft)
ngimnasa = (t:n) (w:what was purposed/set purpose) (d:ngimna, purpose, with sa, already done; what someone has purposed beforehand, mostly as ngimnasa bangin, as purposed) (e:ka ~ bangin kip ding hi) (b:ngimna) (r:23.14.24/60.1.2) (q:draft)
ngingei = (t:adv) (w:thoroughly/utterly/fully) (d:placed after a verb or descriptive word to strengthen it) (e:kei nong paatsak ~ a) (r:18.16.7/18.16.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngolhna = (t:n) (w:fasting/going without) (d:in an ngolhna, going without food, fasting) (e:An ~ hangin ka khukte zaw a) (r:19.109.24/19.69.10) (q:draft)
nialzo = (t:v) (w:be able to contradict/refute) (d:nial, dispute, with zo, be able; negated, not able to contradict) (e:note’ thugen hong ~ loin) (b:nial) (r:42.21.15) (q:draft)
nialzo = (t:v) (w:have rejected) (d:nial, reject, with zo marking the act as done) (e:na muan mite ka ~ hi) (b:nial) (r:24.2.37/24.7.29) (q:draft)
niamsakna = (t:n) (w:humiliation/being brought low) (d:niamsak, make low, with the noun suffix na; niamsakna a thuak mite are those who are bowed down) (e:~ a thuak mite sangto sak a) (b:niamsak) (r:19.146.8/19.145.14) (q:draft)
nikten = (t:n) (w:clothing/garments) (d:found in the pair nikten puansilh, clothes of every kind) (e:annek tuidawn, ~ puansilh i neih nakleh) (r:54.6.8/18.27.16) (q:draft)
nilhsa = (t:adj) (w:anointed) (d:nilh, anoint, with sa, already done; sathau nilhsa is one who has been anointed with oil) (e:sathau ~ na hi uh a) (b:nilh) (r:62.2.20/14.22.7) (q:draft)
ninbulom = (t:n) (w:filth/rubbish/refuse) (d:a compound of nin, dirt; dirt or rubbish that is thrown out) (e:~ bang lel ka hita hi) (r:18.30.19/34.3.6) (q:draft)
ninsakin = (t:v) (w:defiling/making unclean) (d:ninsak, defile, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb) (e:ka biakinn ~, ka min siangtho daisak) (b:ninsak) (r:3.20.3/15.9.10) (q:draft)
nipsak = (t:v) (w:soften/soak/drench) (d:nip with the causative sak; make ground soft and wet through) (e:guahtui tawh na ~ a) (b:nip) (r:19.65.10/23.34.7) (q:draft)
nisuah = (t:n) (w:sunrise) (d:ni, sun, with suah, come out; the time when the sun rises, set against nitum, sunset) (e:~ leh nitum kikal nai sawm) (r:43.11.9/41.16.2) (q:draft)
nomsak = (t:v) (w:moisten/wet/make damp) (d:nom with the causative sak; of dew wetting branches and of clouds filled with moisture) (e:daitui in a ~ tawntung singkung) (b:nom) (r:18.29.19/18.37.11) (q:draft)
nona = (t:n) (d:no, young or tender, with the noun suffix na; in lo nona, a place of fresh young grass, green pasture or grassland) (e:Lo ~-ah keimah hong lumsak a) (b:no) (r:19.23.2/24.9.10) (q:draft)
noptatna = (t:n) (w:indulgence/dissipation/wild living) (d:noptat with the noun suffix na; living for pleasure without restraint; noptatna khamna, the holding back of it, is self-control) (e:a kihhuai ~ ah gamta-in) (b:noptat) (r:65.1.7/61.1.6) (q:draft)
noptuak = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/comfortable/agreeable) (d:of land or a place that is good to be in) (e:a leitang ~ sa hi) (r:1.49.15/19.65.12) (q:draft)
nuaimang = (t:v) (w:destroy utterly/wipe out/annihilate) (e:leitung panin ~ gawp in) (r:25.3.66/24.51.3) (q:draft)
nuainungte = (t:adj) (w:lower) (d:nuainung, lower, with the plural te; tuikhuk nuainungte, the lower springs, set against tungnungte, the upper ones) (e:tuikhuk tungnungte leh tuikhuk ~ a pia) (b:nuainung) (r:7.1.15/6.15.19) (q:draft)
nuampa = (t:n) (w:one who wants to) (d:nuam, want, with pa, the male one; after a verb, the man who wants to do it) (e:an la ~ na hi hi) (b:nuam) (r:42.19.21/43.7.4) (q:draft)
nuamsakin = (t:v) (w:gladdening/cheering/making merry) (d:nuamsak, gladden, with the linking ending in; lung nuamsakin om is enjoy oneself) (e:zu nekna tawh ka lung ~) (b:nuamsak) (r:21.2.3/7.19.22) (q:draft)
nuihsatna = (t:n) (w:mockery/scorn/ridicule) (d:nuihsat, laugh at, with the noun suffix na) (e:amau’ hong ~ leh hong simmawhnate panin) (b:nuihsat) (r:19.119.22/19.89.50) (q:draft)
nulsak = (t:v) (w:wipe/wipe away/wipe dry) (d:nul, wipe, with sak, do it for another) (e:a sam tawh a ~ hi) (b:nul) (r:43.12.3/66.21.4) (q:draft)
nungkin = (t:v) (w:go backward/shrink back/turn back) (d:draw back instead of going forward, set against mainawt, go forward) (e:mainawt loin a ~ zaw uh hi) (r:24.7.24/58.10.39) (q:draft)
nungzangah = (t:adv) (w:on the back) (d:nungzang, the back of a person or animal, with the place marker ah) (e:mihaite’ ~ ciangduai kinga hi) (b:nungzang) (r:20.10.13/27.7.6) (q:draft)
nuta = (t:n) (w:mother and young/mother and child) (d:nu, mother, with ta, child; a mother together with her young, as in la nuta, a donkey and her colt) (e:la ~ thakhatin na mu ding uh) (b:nu) (r:40.21.2/40.21.7) (q:draft)
olno = (t:adj) (w:easy) (d:ol, easy, with no; found as olno takin, easily, with little effort) (e:thungaihsun theite in ~ takin ngah thei) (b:ol) (r:20.14.6/27.11.17) (q:draft)
olsak = (t:v) (w:make common/make plentiful) (d:ol, easy, with the causative sak; make a thing easy to get, as common as stones) (e:suang bangin ngun ~ a) (b:ol) (r:11.10.27/14.1.15) (q:draft)
omden = (t:v) (w:remain/continue/stay on) (d:om, be, with den, continually; go on being so) (e:Tua bangin ~ hi) (r:4.9.16/1.7.17) (q:draft)
omkhit = (t:v) (w:have been/have stayed) (d:om, be or stay, with khit, finished; mostly as omkhit ciangin, after being or staying) (e:kha thum ka ~ uh ciangin) (r:44.28.11/46.15.46) (q:draft)
ommuang = (t:adj) (w:harmless/unsuspecting) (d:of a person or animal that is quietly minding its own business and expects no harm) (e:ui ~ khat a bil-a kaihsak) (r:20.26.17/20.1.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
omto = (t:v) (w:be up above/rise above/stay on) (d:om, be, with to, up or onward; be high above a thing, and of time, go on being in a place) (e:Mual liante tungah tui ~ lai a) (b:om) (r:1.7.20/27.1.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
omziate = (t:n) (w:ways/conditions/features) (d:omzia, how a person or thing is, with the plural te; of a person, his ways, and of a land, what it is like) (e:a leitang ~ hong gelhin) (b:omzia) (r:6.18.4/14.27.7) (q:draft)
omzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand/be able to be/can remain) (d:om, be, with zo, be able) (e:Topa’ mai-ah kua ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:om) (r:9.6.20/18.4.17) (q:draft)
otsan = (t:v) (w:shout to/call out to/shout after) (d:ot, shout, with san, toward a person) (e:vantungmi in kei hong ~ a) (b:ot) (r:38.6.8/7.18.23) (q:draft)
paaimang = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast off/abandon) (d:paai, throw, with mang, away or lost) (e:ka luahsa mite ka ~ ta hi) (r:24.12.7/24.7.29) (q:draft)
paidak = (t:v) (w:forsake/abandon/cast off) (e:ama luahte ~ lo ding hi) (r:19.94.14/28.11.8) (q:draft)
paihna = (t:n) (w:throwing/casting down) (d:paih, a form of paai, throw, with the noun suffix na; the act of throwing or casting down, and before a noun the place where a thing was thrown) (e:luang khempeuh a ~ tuikhuk pen) (b:paih) (r:24.41.9/14.25.8) (q:draft)
paikhiate = (t:n) (w:things that come out) (d:paikhia, come out, with the plural te; a paikhiate, the things that come out) (e:Kam sung pan a ~ in) (b:paikhia) (r:40.15.18/41.7.20) (q:draft)
painopna = (t:n) (w:wish to go/place one wants to go) (d:painop, want to go, with the noun suffix na; the wish to go, and the place where one wants to go) (e:na ~ peuhpeuhah na pai thei hi) (b:painop) (r:24.40.4/44.7.23) (q:draft)
paipihpa = (t:n) (w:the one who led/he who brought) (d:paipih, take along or lead, with pa, the male one; said of God who led his people) (e:gamlak nawkin ama mite a ~ tungah) (b:paipih) (r:19.136.16/5.8.15) (q:draft)
paisakna = (t:n) (w:sending) (d:paisak, send or let go, with the noun suffix na; the act of sending) (e:a Tapa a hong ~ thu) (b:paisak) (r:62.4.14/16.2.5) (q:draft)
paisuksak = (t:v) (w:let go down/make go down/bring down) (d:paisuk, go down, with the causative sak) (e:zang gamah ~ lo uh hi) (b:paisuk) (r:7.1.34/11.2.6) (q:draft)
paitawm = (t:v) (w:come on one's own/come of one's own accord) (d:pai, go or come, with tawm, by oneself; come without being sent by another) (e:ama thu tawh hong ~ leh) (r:43.5.43/43.8.42) (q:draft)
pakkual = (t:n) (w:wreath/garland) (d:pak, flower, with kual, ring; a ring of flowers, in the verses a carved or cast ornament) (e:a pang ciatah ~ om hi) (r:11.7.30/11.7.36) (q:draft)
pakna = (t:n) (d:pak, quickly or for a short while, with the noun suffix na; after a verb it names the doing of it quickly or briefly, as in hauh pakna, getting rich quickly, and ten’ pakna, staying for a while) (e:Ol tak-a hauh ~ in kiam kik) (b:pak) (r:20.13.11/24.35.7) (q:draft)
pakpak = (t:adv) (w:quickly/easily/readily) (d:pak, quickly, doubled; placed after a verb, be quick to do it, as in heh pakpak, be easily angered) (e:heh ~ lo, mite’ mawhna ciamteh lo) (r:46.13.5/45.3.15) (q:draft)
pakpalh = (t:n) (w:open flower/blossom/flower in bloom) (d:pak, flower, with palh, open out) (e:umgah le ~ lim kigelh hi) (r:11.6.18/18.14.2) (q:draft)
palhin = (t:v) (w:blooming/blossoming) (d:palh, open out in bloom, with the linking ending in) (e:Israel ~ dawnkhia ding a) (b:palh) (r:23.27.6/19.90.6) (q:draft)
palhkhia = (t:v) (w:blossom/bloom/burst into bloom) (d:palh, open out in bloom, with khia, out) (e:sehnel gam lungdamin ~ ding hi) (b:palh) (r:23.35.1/23.35.2) (q:draft)
palhngulh = (t:v) (w:be unfaithful to/commit adultery against) (d:break faith with a husband or wife by going with another) (e:a pasal a ~ ahi hi) (r:41.10.12/4.5.12) (q:draft)
palte = (t:n) (w:firstfruits/first ripe ones) (d:the first of a crop to ripen, with the plural te; leenggah a palte, the first ripe grapes) (e:leenggah a ~ a min hun) (r:4.13.20/4.18.12) (q:draft)
pangkhat = (t:n) (w:one side) (d:pang, side, with khat, one; set against pang langkhat, the other side) (e:a ~ lama om nisuh kung) (r:26.41.19/2.26.27) (q:draft)
pangsimte = (t:n) (w:men in ambush/ambushers) (d:pangsim, ambush, with the plural te; a pangsimte, those who lie in ambush) (e:a ~ amau’ nungah om hi) (b:pangsim) (r:14.13.13/7.20.36) (q:draft)
patpuan = (t:n) (w:linen/cotton cloth) (d:pat, cotton, with puan, cloth; the Bible uses it where English has linen) (e:~ dialkaih khat na lei khit ciangin) (r:24.13.1/23.19.9) (q:draft)
patsa = (t:adj) (w:begun/already started) (d:pat, begin, with sa, already done; a patsa, what has been begun) (e:na ~ uh thu a bei dongin) (b:pat) (r:47.8.11/17.9.23) (q:draft)
paukhialhna = (t:n) (w:blasphemy) (d:pau, speak, with khialh, go wrong, and the noun suffix na; wrong speaking, in the verses speaking against God) (e:Pasian tungah ~ min a dim) (r:66.17.3/40.26.65) (q:draft)
paukhiat = (t:v) (w:utter/speak out/say aloud) (d:form of paukhia, speak out, used before words such as ma-in and ciangin) (e:paunak thuhilhnate a ~ ciangin) (b:paukhia) (r:20.26.9/19.139.4) (q:draft)
paukhiatna = (t:n) (w:utterance/speaking) (d:paukhiat, speak out, with the noun suffix na; the act of speaking a word aloud) (e:A kilawm hun-a kammal khat ~ in) (b:paukhiat) (r:20.25.11/5.5.26) (q:draft)
paupeng = (t:adj) (w:stubborn/obstinate/contentious) (d:of people who will not listen or give way) (e:a lungsim uh khauhin ~ uh hi) (r:26.2.4/45.2.8) (q:draft)
pautheih = (t:v) (w:be able to speak/can speak) (d:form of pauthei, be able to speak, used before words such as ding, nading and hangin) (e:pau lamdang na ~ ding uh) (b:pauthei) (r:46.14.5/46.13.1) (q:draft)
pawipi = (t:n) (w:great feast/banquet) (d:pawi, festival or feast, with pi, great) (e:Mi khat in ~ kham a) (b:pawi) (r:42.14.16/20.17.1) (q:draft)
pawlbawl = (t:v) (w:welcome/accept/take in) (d:pawl, group or companion, with bawl, make; receive a person into one's company or service) (e:Upna neu mite ~ unla) (b:pawl) (r:45.14.1/9.14.52) (q:draft)
pawlpawlte = (t:n) (w:all kinds/various groups) (d:pawlpawl, group by group, with the plural te; the various groups of people or kinds of a thing) (e:leitungah mi a ~ in tuipi lian) (b:pawlpawl) (r:42.21.25/49.6.18) (q:draft)
peemin = (t:v) (w:sojourning/residing as a foreigner) (d:peem, live in a place as an incomer, with the linking ending in) (e:Note lakah khualmi khat hong ~) (b:peem) (r:4.9.14/7.19.1) (q:draft)
peeng = (t:n) (w:twin) (d:two born together; sakhi peeng, twin gazelles, and Ta Peeng, the Twin Sons, the figurehead of a ship) (e:a takhawm helhel sakhi ~) (r:22.7.3/44.28.11) (q:draft)
pekpak = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word used with tuk, fall: dropping down limp, as people who faint in the streets) (e:kongzing tengah a tuk ~ uh hi) (r:25.2.12/25.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
pelhthei = (t:v) (w:be able to escape/can avoid/elude) (d:pelh, avoid or escape, with thei, be able) (e:a nih vei mahin na ~ hi) (b:pelh) (r:9.18.11/21.7.26) (q:draft)
pengin = (t:v) (w:being exempt/being off duty) (d:peng, be free of a duty, with the linking ending in) (e:nasep dangte panin ~ biakinn deite sungah) (b:peng) (r:13.9.33/12.11.5) (q:draft)
pengpelep = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:night hawk/screech owl) (d:an unclean bird in the food laws, in the place where English versions have night hawk or screech owl) (e:kalaoh-vasa, ~, vatawt, musi nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.16/5.14.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
petin = (t:v) (w:biting) (d:pet, bite, with the linking ending in) (e:sakol’ khetul ~ a tuangpa nungkiat hi) (b:pet) (r:1.49.17) (q:draft)
petin = (t:adv) (d:in tu pet petin, at this very moment, now at last; pet marks the exact time) (e:Tu pet ~ hih in keima guhte) (r:1.2.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
pettan = (t:v) (w:bite off/gnaw off) (d:pet, bite, with tan, cut through; a pettan kauphe, the cutting locust, is one of the kinds of locust named in Joel) (e:A ~ kauphete’ nek bang teng) (r:29.1.4/29.2.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
peuhin = (t:det) (w:any/whatever) (d:peuh, any or whatever, with the marker in; cikmah peuhin, at any time, and a ut bang peuhin, in whatever way he wants) (e:A ut bang ~ gamta ding a) (b:peuh) (r:27.11.28/41.14.7) (q:draft)
phabel = (t:adj) (w:best/finest/most honoured) (d:pha, good, with bel, most; tutna phabel, the best seat or place of honour) (e:pawikhamna sungah tutna ~ a deih uh hi) (r:41.12.39/40.23.6) (q:draft)
phaikungte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:reeds) (d:phaikung, a reed that grows at the edge of water, with the plural te) (e:amah in ~ lakah a lawh mu a) (r:2.2.5/2.2.3) (q:draft)
phapen = (t:adv) (w:most/most of all/especially) (d:placed after a verb, to the highest degree; thupha ngah phapen, most blessed) (e:lak pan thupha ngah ~ hi ta hen) (r:7.5.24/46.14.1) (q:draft)
phatphat = (t:v) (w:keep praising/praise again and again) (d:phat, praise, doubled to show that the praising goes on) (e:a tawntungin nangma min ka ~ ding hi) (r:19.145.2/19.145.1) (q:draft)
phawktel = (t:v) (w:realise/perceive/understand clearly) (d:phawk, be aware, with tel, understand clearly) (e:Pasian a vangliat mahmahna limtakin ~ in) (r:18.36.22/13.14.2) (q:draft)
phelkek = (t:v) (w:tear down/demolish/pull down) (d:phel, take apart, with kek, tear; of a building or altar) (e:a biakinn a ~ uh hi) (r:12.11.18/18.12.14) (q:draft)
