Zanglei = (t:n) (w:plain) (d:zanglei, plain or lowland, capitalised as the name of a region, the Plain of the Jordan valley and the coastal plain of Philistia) (e:Negeb gam, leh ~ zong) (b:zanglei) (r:5.34.3/26.25.16) (q:draft)
aai = (t:n) (w:lot) (d:spelling of ai, a lot cast to decide something; aai saan is cast lots) (e:note adingin ~ ka saan ding hi) (b:ai) (r:6.18.6/6.18.10) (q:draft)
ahilh = (t:v) (w:teach/taught) (d:hilh, teach, written together with the preceding a, the third person marker; usually written a hilh) (e:thunget nading ~ mah bangin) (b:hilh) (r:42.11.1/56.1.11) (q:draft)
ahipa = (t:n) (w:the one who is/he who is) (d:ahi, is, with pa, the male one; closes a describing phrase, Pasian ahipa the one who is God) (e:amah bek Pasian ~ tungah) (b:ahi) (r:19.136.4/23.57.15) (q:draft)
ahoihte = (t:n) (w:good ones/good things) (d:ahoih, that which is good, with the plural suffix te; gamtatna ahoihte is good deeds) (e:gamtatna ~ ah lungsim utna nei-in) (b:ahoih) (r:56.2.14/3.27.10) (q:draft)
aisanin = (t:adv) (w:by divination/by fortune-telling) (d:aisan, divination, with the suffix in, by means of) (e:~ ama tote ading summeet ngah thei) (b:aisan) (r:44.16.16/28.4.12) (q:draft)
alui = (t:adj) (w:old) (d:lui, old, with the prefix a, that which is old, the old one; paired with athak, the new) (e:a gah ~ leh athak) (b:lui) (r:22.7.13/3.26.10) (q:draft)
amai = (t:n) (w:his face/its front) (d:mai, face or front, written together with a, his, her or its; amai ah is in front of him or them) (e:~ lei ngatin kumpipa zahtakna bawl hi) (b:mai) (r:10.24.20/3.16.14) (q:draft)
ameet = (t:n) (w:interest/usury) (d:meet, interest on a loan, written together with a, its; ameet la is take interest) (e:Leiba ~ kilakna phiat ni) (b:meet) (r:16.5.10/3.25.36) (q:draft)
amethist = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:amethyst) (e:agate suang leh ~ suang ahi hi) (r:2.39.12/66.21.20) (q:draft)
amethyst = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:amethyst) (e:agate suang, le ~ suang ahi hi) (r:2.39.12/66.21.20) (q:draft)
amuh = (t:v) (w:see/saw/find) (d:muh, see or find, written together with the preceding a, the third person marker; usually written a muh) (e:tua mipa in ~ ciangin) (b:muh) (r:10.20.12/9.28.21) (q:draft)
aneu = (t:adj) (w:small) (d:neu, small, with the prefix a, that which is small, the small one; alian aneu is great and small alike) (e:ganhing alian ~, sim zawh loh-a a tam) (b:neu) (r:19.104.25/19.115.13) (q:draft)
angah = (t:adv) (w:in the arms/at the bosom/in the lap) (d:ang, bosom or lap, with the marker ah, in or at) (e:Naomi in naungeek la-in a ~ tawi a) (b:ang) (r:8.4.16/41.9.36) (q:draft)
angkawm = (t:n) (w:adultery/adulterer) (d:unfaithfulness to a husband or wife, or one guilty of it; angkawm ahi is commits adultery) (e:a kiteengte in ~ ahi uh hi) (r:40.19.9/24.9.2) (q:draft)
angvanin = (t:v) (w:being partial to/favoring/taking the side of) (d:angvan, show partiality or favor, with the linking suffix in) (e:Mi mawhte ~ diksak ding hoih lo a) (b:angvan) (r:20.18.5/19.89.17) (q:draft)
anlumte = (t:n) (w:loaves/bread) (d:anlum, loaf of bread, with the plural suffix te) (e:hih ~ pen siampite bek in) (b:anlum) (r:41.2.26/41.6.41) (q:draft)
anneng = (t:n) (w:crumbs/scraps) (d:an, food, with neng, small bits; bits of food that fall from the table) (e:uite in tate ~ kiate sabuai nuai-ah) (r:41.7.28/40.15.27) (q:draft)
ansite = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:ansi, chaff, the empty husks of grain, with the plural suffix te) (e:huih letkhiat ~ tawh kibangsak in) (b:ansi) (r:19.35.5/40.3.12) (q:draft)
antak = (t:n) (w:solid food) (d:an, food, with tak, real or solid; contrasted with nawi, milk) (e:Note in ~ nezo nai lo) (b:an) (r:46.3.2/58.5.12) (q:draft)
apawlpawlte = (t:n) (w:all kinds/various kinds) (d:pawl, group or kind, doubled, with the prefix a and the plural suffix te; follows a noun, every kind of it, ahoih na apawlpawlte is every good work) (e:kha la leh phatna la ~ tawh) (b:apawlpawl) (r:49.5.19/55.3.16) (q:draft)
apkik = (t:v) (w:hand back/give back/return) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with kik, back) (e:kiang mahah na ~ kei ding uh hi) (b:ap) (r:5.23.15/9.30.15) (q:draft)
athak = (t:adj) (w:new) (d:thak, new, with the prefix a, that which is new, the new one; paired with alui, the old) (e:kikheel a, ~ a piang zo hi) (b:thak) (r:47.5.17/22.7.13) (q:draft)
athau = (t:n) (w:fat/its fat) (d:thau, fat, written together with a, its; the fat of an offering) (e:thunuam-a biakna sisan leh ~ a piapa in) (b:thau) (r:3.7.33/3.7.30) (q:draft)
atkhiat = (t:v) (w:cut off) (d:at, cut, with khiat, off or away; the form of atkhia used before sak, manin and similar words) (e:Saul’ puanmong a ~ manin) (b:atkhia) (r:9.24.5/2.4.25) (q:draft)
atsat = (t:v) (w:cut through/sever) (d:compound of at, cut; zagui atsat is cut the sinew of the leg, hamstring a horse) (e:leengkai sakol khempeuh a zagui ~ a) (r:10.8.4/13.18.4) (q:draft)
atuamin = (t:adv) (w:separately/apart/in various ways) (d:atuam, separate or different, with the adverb ending in; doubled as atuam atuamin, each separately, in various ways) (e:nungzuite ~ a khen khit ciangin) (b:atuam) (r:44.19.9/58.1.1) (q:draft)
atuamtuam = (t:adj) (w:various/different/of different kinds) (d:tuamtuam with a before it, each one different from the other) (e:~ thupha a ngah ciat uh hi) (b:tuamtuam) (r:46.7.7/60.4.10) (q:draft)
awkin = (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught/be trapped) (d:form of awk, be caught in a snare, with the linking suffix in) (e:amaute ~ kiman ding hi) (b:awk) (r:23.8.15/23.28.13) (q:draft)
awmdalna = (t:n) (w:breastplate) (d:awmdal, chest covering, with the noun suffix na: armour worn over the chest) (e:dikna ~ na bulh un la) (b:awmdal) (r:49.6.14/66.9.9) (q:draft)
awmgak = (t:n) (w:sash/chest band) (d:awm, chest, with gak, tie: a band tied round the chest) (e:a awm-ah kham ~ gakin) (r:66.15.6/66.1.13) (q:draft)
awngah = (t:adj) (w:open/empty) (d:awng, empty or open, with the place marker ah; mun awngah is in the open place, the public square of a town) (e:khua laizang mun ~ khawmin) (b:awng) (r:5.13.16/14.29.4) (q:draft)
awnggawp = (t:v) (w:shout/clamour/cry out loudly) (d:awng, shout, with gawp, which shows that it is done with force) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi) (b:awng) (r:44.17.7/44.19.32) (q:draft)
awngkekgawp = (t:v) (w:shout furiously/yell/roar) (d:awngkek, shout aloud, with gawp, which shows that it is done with force; of an angry crowd) (e:Mihonte hehlua-in ~ uh a) (b:awngkek) (r:44.22.23/44.19.28) (q:draft)
azu = (t:n) (w:appeal) (d:used with khan: azu khan is to appeal a case to a higher judge; also written as one word, azukhan) (e:kiangah ~ ka khan ding hi) (r:44.25.11/44.26.32) (q:draft)
azukhan = (t:v) (w:appeal/make an appeal) (d:take a case to a higher judge, as Paul appealed to Caesar; also written azu khan) (e:kumpi lianpa kiangah ~ nuam ahih ciangin) (r:44.25.25/44.28.19) (q:draft)
bah = (t:v) (w:be exhausted/be faint/be worn out) (d:have no strength left; with gawp, utterly exhausted) (e:dahin husamin ka ~ gawp hi) (r:25.2.11/24.48.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
bah = (t:v) (w:put to the mouth/feed) (d:lift food to the mouth) (e:a kam ah an a ~ tohkik ding) (r:20.19.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
