kuankhiasak = (t:v) (w:send out/march out) (d:kuankhia set out, with the causative sak: make soldiers go out to war) (e:galkap tul khat ~ a) (b:kuankhia) (r:30.5.3) (q:draft)
kuansakin = (t:v) (w:sending out/sending) (d:kuansak send out, with the linking ending in, sending out and then doing the next action) (e:a galkapte ~ tua mi thatte) (b:kuansak) (r:40.22.7/26.32.3) (q:draft)
kuasak = (t:v) (w:make pound/make burn) (d:said with dip, the heart: make the heart pound or burn with strong feeling) (e:huihpi in ka dip hong ~ a) (r:18.37.1/42.24.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuateng = (t:pron) (w:who/which ones) (d:kua who with teng all: which persons out of a group) (e:~ in ama thu um ding a) (b:kua) (r:43.6.64/46.11.19) (q:draft)
kulhzangah = (t:n) (w:on the wall/on top of the wall) (d:kulhzang top of the wall, with the place marker ah) (e:Israel kumpipa ~ a pai laitakin) (b:kulhzang) (r:12.6.26/16.12.31) (q:draft)
kumminte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:cumin) (d:kummin cumin, with the plural te, the cumin seeds) (e:~ molhtum tawh kisat hi) (b:kummin) (r:23.28.27) (q:draft)
kumnga = (t:n) (w:five years) (d:kum year and nga five written as one word; in a count of years it follows leh, as in kum sawmnih leh kumnga, twenty-five years) (e:kum sawmnih leh ~ pan a tungsiah) (r:4.8.24/23.38.5) (q:draft)
kumsuka = (t:v) (w:coming down/descending/bending down) (d:kumsuk come down, with the linking a before the next verb) (e:Mi khat tungah Kha Siangtho hong ~) (b:kumsuk) (r:43.1.33/42.24.12) (q:draft)
kut = (t:v) (w:nag/press/groan) (d:apparently the form of ku, howl or growl, used before ciangin and before a noun: of a person, keep on at someone with words, or groan aloud) (e:nakpi takin a ~ ciangin) (b:ku) (r:7.16.16/26.26.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
laamte = (t:n) (w:dancers/those who dance) (d:laam dance, with the plural te; a laamte, the ones who are dancing) (e:a ~ lak panin a zi dingun) (b:laam) (r:7.21.23/22.6.13) (q:draft)
lahsate = (t:n) (w:things shown/what was shown) (d:lahsa shown, with the plural te) (e:kong ~ khempeuh tawh kituakin) (b:lahsa) (r:2.25.9/19.78.11) (q:draft)
laiah = (t:adv) (w:there/at that place) (d:lai place with the place marker ah, in tua laiah, there; more often written lai-ah) (e:tua ~ va si ni) (r:24.8.14/24.42.14) (q:draft)
laihilhte = (t:n) (w:teachers) (d:laihilh teacher, with the plural te) (e:A om khempeuh in ~ ahi uh hiam) (b:laihilh) (r:46.12.29/46.12.28) (q:draft)
laitaka = (t:adv) (w:at the time/at that very time/while) (d:laitak, the very time or point, with the linking a that joins it to the following word; zan laitaka, in the night) (e:tua ~ a om Khaldea galkapte) (b:laitak) (r:24.41.3/46.7.24) (q:draft)
laizanga = (t:prep) (w:in the midst of/among/in the middle) (d:laizang midst, with the linking a before om, be: that is in the middle, that is among) (e:A ~ om inndei sung a teh ciangin) (b:laizang) (r:26.41.2/3.15.31) (q:draft)
laknate = (t:n) (w:taking/takings) (d:lakna taking, with the plural te; sumgolh laknate is the taking of bribes, sakol a laknate the horses he obtained) (e:leh sumgolh ~ deih lo hi) (b:lakna) (r:14.19.7/14.1.16) (q:draft)
lakto = (t:v) (w:raise/lift up/hold up) (d:lak with to, up: hold something up high to be seen, as a banner) (e:mite tungah ka lim ka ~ ding hi) (b:lak) (r:23.49.22/23.13.2) (q:draft)
lamlianpi = (t:n) (w:main road/highway/street) (d:lamlian main road, with pi big; set against lamneu, small path) (e:Nasemte zong ~-ah va pai uh a) (b:lamlian) (r:40.22.10/19.77.19) (q:draft)
lamnop = (t:v) (w:want to build/wish to build) (d:lam build with nop, the form of nuam want; a lamnop khempeuh is all that he wished to build) (e:Solomon in a ~ khempeuh a lamkik hi) (r:11.9.19/11.9.1) (q:draft)
lampialin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/going astray) (d:lampial turn aside, stray, with the linking ending in) (e:Kote khialin ~ ka gitloh tat uh hi) (b:lampial) (r:11.8.47/7.14.8) (q:draft)
lampialte = (t:n) (w:strays/those who go astray) (d:lampial stray, with the plural te; of sheep that have strayed, and of people who have left the right way) (e:A ~ na khiang kei uh a) (b:lampial) (r:26.34.4/66.21.8) (q:draft)
lamsate = (t:n) (w:things built/buildings) (d:lamsa built, with the plural te: what someone has built) (e:keimah in ka ~ ka phelkik a) (b:lamsa) (r:24.45.4/18.20.19) (q:draft)
lamteng = (t:n) (w:whole side/all the part toward) (d:lam side, direction, with teng all: the whole of the side that is named) (e:Tua gam leitaw ~ Efraim) (b:lam) (r:6.17.10) (q:draft)
lamteng = (t:n) (w:possessions/goods) (d:in a neih a lamteng, all that one owns, property and goods) (e:a neih a ~ uh zuak uh a) (r:44.2.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamun = (t:adv) (d:lam way, direction, with un, the ending in as used with a plural subject: in the direction of, in the course of; a nung leh lamun is backwards, an a zonna lamun is while they looked for food) (e:a nung leh ~ pai-in) (b:lam) (r:1.9.23/25.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
langbawl = (t:v) (w:turn against/oppose/be hostile to) (d:lang side with bawl make: set oneself against someone) (e:a gamtatsia mite Topa in a ~ hi) (b:lang) (r:60.3.12/18.19.19) (q:draft)
langbawlna = (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility) (d:langbawl turn against, with the noun suffix na; in Proverbs 28:21 mi langbawlna is taking sides between people, partiality) (e:mawhnei mite’ ~ a thuaknate ngaihsun unla) (b:langbawl) (r:58.12.3/20.28.21) (q:draft)
langneih = (t:v) (w:be against/oppose/take sides) (d:lang side with neih have: take a side about someone, mostly against; na langneih mite is your enemies; in Exodus 23:3 of taking sides over a poor man in a lawsuit) (e:mote in a teeknu uh ~ uh hi) (r:33.7.6/2.23.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
lap = (t:v) (w:overtake/catch up with) (e:Khuamial in no hong ~ loh nadingin) (r:43.12.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
latal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:male donkey) (d:la donkey with tal male; the female is lapi) (e:lapi sawmnih leh ~ sawm la hi) (r:1.32.15/1.12.16) (q:draft)
laukawm = (t:adv) (w:fearfully/afraid/in fear) (d:lau fear with kawm while: being afraid and something else at the same time, as laukawm lingkawmin, fearing and trembling, and laukawm nuamkawmin, afraid yet glad) (e:~ lingkawmin hong pai-in) (r:41.5.33/40.28.8) (q:draft)
lausakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to terrify/succeed in frightening) (d:lausak frighten, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:mite na ~ kha ding hi) (b:lausak) (r:23.47.12/26.32.26) (q:draft)
lawhpi = (t:n) (w:winnowing fork/winnowing fan) (d:the tool held in the hand to winnow grain on the threshing floor) (e:A khut in ~ tawi a) (r:40.3.12/42.3.17) (q:draft)
lawhtak = (t:n) (w:gain/profit/portion) (d:what one really gets out of work or effort) (e:bang ~ ka hi hiam) (r:46.15.32/21.9.9) (q:draft)
lawngpi = (t:n) (w:beam/rod) (d:in siam lawngpi, the beam of a weaver's loom, a picture of a very thick spear shaft) (e:A teibul in siam ~ cia bang hi a) (r:9.17.7/10.21.19) (q:draft)
lawnsakin = (t:v) (w:touching) (d:lawnsak touch, with the linking ending in, touching and then doing the next action) (e:a mipa’ bil ~ a damsak hi) (b:lawnsak) (r:42.22.51/24.1.9) (q:draft)
lawnto = (t:v) (w:throw up/toss up) (d:lawn throw with to, up; paired with lawnsuk, throw down, of being tossed about) (e:huihpi in hong lawnsuk hong ~ hi) (b:lawn) (r:18.30.22/18.2.12) (q:draft)
lawtkhia = (t:v) (w:burst out/bulge out/come out) (d:lawt with khia, out: of a wall that bulges outward, and of the contents of the bowels coming out) (e:namsau dok lo a, a ek ~ hi) (r:7.3.22/23.30.13) (q:draft)
leenmang = (t:v) (w:sweep away/blow away/be swept away) (d:leen, form of leeng fly, with mang, out of sight: of the wind carrying things off, and of what is carried off by it) (e:Huih in ~ khin ahih manin) (r:27.2.35/20.10.25) (q:draft)
lehkaih = (t:v) (w:pull back/draw back/bring back) (d:leh back with kaih pull; often followed by kik, again) (e:a liim kal sawm ~ kik hi) (r:12.20.11/20.24.11) (q:draft)
leikhal = (t:n) (w:clay/clod) (d:dry earth or clay that breaks to pieces easily; apparently lei earth with khal harden) (e:na siksante uh ~ bang hi lel hi) (r:18.13.12/20.12.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
leithuk = (t:n) (w:depths of the earth/deep ground/pit) (d:lei earth with thuk deep; leithuk sung is deep under the ground) (e:~ sung panin nang na pau ding a) (r:23.29.4/18.28.4) (q:draft)
lelhlam = (t:n) (w:defeat/being beaten) (d:lelh be overcome, with lam, the fact or state of: a lelhlam a kitheih ciangin is when he saw that he was beaten) (e:Moab kumpipa in a ~ a kitheih ciangin) (r:12.3.26/13.19.16) (q:draft)
lellelte = (t:adj) (w:mere) (d:lel only, merely, doubled and with the plural te: mihing lellelte is those who are no more than human, mere mortals) (e:Mihing ~ in kei, bang hong cihzo ding) (r:19.56.11/23.51.12) (q:draft)
lelsak = (t:v) (w:condemn/make lose/deny justice) (d:lel lose, with the causative sak: make someone lose his case before the judges) (e:a dikpa khahin a mawhpa ~ a) (b:lel) (r:5.25.1/2.23.6) (q:draft)
liangkote = (t:n) (w:shoulders) (d:liangko shoulder, with the plural te) (e:a ~ kikalah sumngo teikhawh kikhai hi) (b:liangko) (r:9.17.6/26.29.18) (q:draft)
lianpenpa = (t:n) (w:chief/highest) (d:lianpen greatest, with pa marking a man: the man highest in rank, placed after a title, as siampi lianpenpa, chief priest) (e:siampi ~ Seraiah tawh) (b:lianpen) (r:24.52.24/27.1.7) (q:draft)
liatluat = (t:v) (w:be very great/be too great) (d:liat be great with luat too much, the forms used before hang and hangin: so great, so much) (e:na mawhna a ~ hang ahi hi) (r:24.13.22/24.4.30) (q:draft)
liatnate = (t:n) (w:majesty/greatness/splendor) (d:liatna greatness, with the plural te) (e:Pahtawina leh ~ ama mai-ah om a) (b:liatna) (r:19.96.6/13.29.11) (q:draft)
liatsak = (t:v) (w:exalt/make great/magnify) (d:liat be great, with the causative sak) (e:nang ~ ding ka kipan ding hi) (b:liat) (r:6.3.7/13.29.12) (q:draft)
liatsakna = (t:n) (w:exalting/making great) (d:liatsak make great, with the noun suffix na) (e:ama kumpigam a ~ kiphawktel hi) (b:liatsak) (r:10.5.12/13.29.12) (q:draft)
liinglawng = (t:v) (w:tremble/shudder/be terrified) (d:be shaken with fear, also written linglawng; with sak, make others tremble) (e:a lungmuangte aw, ~ un) (r:23.32.11/23.32.10) (q:draft)
lik = (t:v) (w:roll) (d:roll a large stone to a place) (e:suangpeek lian khat ~ a) (r:40.27.60/6.10.18) (q:draft)
likkhiat = (t:v) (w:roll away/roll back/move away) (d:lik roll with khiat, away: roll a heavy stone out of its place) (e:suangpi a ~ khit ciangin a tungah) (b:lik) (r:40.28.2/38.12.3) (q:draft)
limlangte = (t:n) (w:mirrors) (d:limlang mirror, with the plural te; in Job 28:18 of a clear precious stone, crystal) (e:numeite’ ~ panin sumngo tawh kisilna kuang) (b:limlang) (r:2.38.8/18.28.18) (q:draft)
limun = (t:adv) (w:as a sign of/as a token of) (d:lim sign, with un, the ending in as used with a plural subject, after a noun: as a sign or mark of that thing) (e:kei hong zahtakna ~ papite na ding uh hi) (b:lim) (r:18.29.8/33.1.16) (q:draft)
linggawp = (t:v) (w:tremble violently/shake with fear/be terrified) (d:ling, also written liing, tremble, with gawp, severely) (e:Moses zong lau-in ~ a) (r:44.7.32/19.48.6) (q:draft)
lingsakgawp = (t:v) (w:shake violently/terrify) (d:lingsak make tremble, with gawp, severely) (e:Leitung a ~ dingin Topa a kipat ciangin) (b:lingsak) (r:23.2.19/26.30.13) (q:draft)
linlian = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word after a verb or adjective, apparently of something evenly and finely shaped: a pang kikim linlian is with its sides exactly equal, square) (e:Tua khuapi a pang kikim ~ a) (r:66.21.16/22.5.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
lipi = (t:n) (w:lake/pool/pond) (d:a body of standing water; tui lipi is a pool or dammed water, mei lipi the lake of fire) (e:kat leh mei ~ sungah) (r:66.21.8/20.17.14) (q:draft)
lipte = (t:n) (w:scales) (d:lip scale, with the plural te; here the scales on the back of Leviathan) (e:a ~ lum bangin kithuap suk cinten a) (b:lip) (r:18.41.15/18.41.16) (q:draft)
lohpipi = (t:part) (d:lohpi, although not, with pi doubled for emphasis, after a verb: quite against what one wants, ka duh lohpipi in is although I did not want it at all) (e:ka duh ~ in an kha a hong nesak hi) (b:lohpi) (r:25.3.15) (q:draft)
lomkhat = (t:n) (w:one bunch/one lump/one bundle) (d:lom bunch, lump, with khat one) (e:Puknah ~ la unla) (r:2.12.22/45.9.21) (q:draft)
lono = (t:n) (w:pasture/meadow) (d:grassland where cattle feed; lono etlawm is the beauty of the pastures) (e:galte pen ~ etlawm tawh kibang hi) (r:19.37.20/11.4.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
lopen = (t:part) (w:least) (d:negative lo with pen most, after a descriptive word: the one that has least of that quality, as a hat lopen, the weakest, and a gina lopen, the lowliest) (e:Manasseh sungah a hat ~ hi a) (b:lo) (r:7.6.15/26.29.15) (q:draft)
lotte = (t:n) (w:things shot/arrows shot) (d:lot shoot, with the plural te: the ones that are shot, as ka thaltang lotte, the arrows I shoot) (e:ka thaltang ~ va tawm in) (b:lot) (r:9.20.36/38.9.14) (q:draft)
luahkhawm = (t:v) (w:inherit together/share the inheritance) (d:luah inherit with khawm together; a luahkhawm mite is fellow heirs) (e:Isaac tawh gamh ~ thei lo ding uh hi) (b:luah) (r:1.21.10/48.4.30) (q:draft)
luahnate = (t:n) (w:inheritances/territories) (d:luahna inheritance, with the plural te: the shares of land received) (e:aisaanna tawh a hawm khiat uh ~ ahi hi) (b:luahna) (r:6.19.51/4.36.2) (q:draft)
luahnate = (t:n) (w:shovels) (d:in vut luahnate, the tools for taking up ashes from the altar) (e:belte, vut ~, taitehte, kuangte) (r:24.52.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
luatnate = (t:n) (w:excess/great intensity) (d:luatna excess, with the plural te, after a verb: the great degree of it, as hong mudah luatnate, how greatly they hate me) (e:keimah hong mudah ~ ngaihsun in) (b:luatna) (r:19.25.19/47.12.21) (q:draft)
luguh = (t:n) (w:skull) (d:lu head with guh bone) (e:a ~ leh a khete leh a khut peekte) (r:12.9.35/24.2.16) (q:draft)
luipi = (t:n) (w:river/large stream/torrent) (d:lui stream with pi big; Egypt luipi is the Wadi of Egypt) (e:ka tauna in ~ ging bang ahi hi) (b:lui) (r:18.3.24/23.27.12) (q:draft)
luisak = (t:v) (w:make old/make obsolete) (d:lui old, with the causative sak) (e:thuciamna masa a ~ hi) (b:lui) (r:58.8.13) (q:draft)
luisak = (t:v) (w:set before/serve) (d:of food, in hong luisak in, let it be set before you) (e:anlum tawmkhat hong ~ in) (r:9.28.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
luk = (t:v) (w:have sex with) (d:in taw luk, of men forcing sexual intercourse on a man) (e:Ama taw ka ~ theih nadingun) (r:7.19.22/1.19.5) (q:draft)
lukhamin = (t:adv) (w:as a pillow/for a pillow) (d:lukham pillow, with the ending in: used as a pillow) (e:~ a zat suang la-in) (b:lukham) (r:1.28.18/1.28.11) (q:draft)
lumkik = (t:v) (w:lie down again/go back to sleep) (d:lum lie down with kik again) (e:tuate ne-in dawnin ~ hi) (b:lum) (r:11.19.6/9.3.5) (q:draft)
lumta = (t:v) (w:lie/have lain down) (d:lum lie down, with ta showing that the state has now come about) (e:hih lai-ah ~ uh hi) (b:lum) (r:26.32.21) (q:draft)
lumta = (t:v) (w:be warm/have become warm) (d:lum warm, with ta showing that the state has now come about; ka khua lumta is I am warm now) (e:Ah, ka khua ~, mei mu khin ing) (b:lum) (r:23.44.16) (q:draft)
lung-amsak = (t:v) (w:trouble/unsettle/terrify) (d:make the heart, lung, disturbed or afraid, with the causative sak) (e:ahih hangin kei hong ~ kei in) (r:24.17.18/44.15.24) (q:draft)
lunggimpih = (t:v) (w:be anxious for/be distressed for/be in anguish over) (d:lunggim be troubled, with pih, together with or for another person) (e:note ka hong ~ ding hi) (b:lunggim) (r:48.4.19/47.11.29) (q:draft)
lungkiat = (t:v) (w:lose heart/be discouraged/give up) (d:form of lungkia used before nading, loh and ngei) (e:kuamah a ~ loh nadingin) (b:lungkia) (r:52.3.2/42.18.1) (q:draft)
lungkimte = (t:n) (w:those who are satisfied/the complacent) (d:lungkim be satisfied, with the plural te) (e:Nomau tumtakin a ~ aw, linglawng un) (b:lungkim) (r:23.32.11/19.49.13) (q:draft)
lungkipin = (t:adv) (w:steadfastly/firmly/with perseverance) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the adverb ending in) (e:a manin ~ a thuakzawh nadingun) (b:lungkip) (r:56.2.2/46.15.58) (q:draft)
lungkipsak = (t:v) (w:encourage/strengthen/make steadfast) (d:lungkip be steadfast, with the causative sak) (e:nungzuite a ~ uh a) (b:lungkip) (r:44.14.21/44.15.32) (q:draft)
lungmuangsak = (t:v) (w:make secure/keep safe/give confidence) (d:lungmuang secure, with the causative sak) (e:Topa muanna in hong ~ hi) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.29.25/21.7.12) (q:draft)
lungsimin = (t:adv) (w:in spirit/in heart/inwardly) (d:lungsim heart, mind, with the ending in: in or with the heart) (e:ka ~ note tawh ka hong omkhawm a) (b:lungsim) (r:51.2.5/1.43.30) (q:draft)
lute = (t:n) (w:heads) (d:lu head, with the plural te) (e:A ~ tungah kumpilukhu sagih a nei hi) (b:lu) (r:66.12.3/19.24.7) (q:draft)
lutol = (t:n) (w:bald head/bald crown) (d:lu head with tol bald: the bald top of the head, set beside talkolh, the bald forehead) (e:a ~ tung hitaleh a talkolh tung hitaleh) (r:3.13.42/3.13.43) (q:draft)
lutungah = (t:n) (w:on the head/upon the head) (d:lutung top of the head, with the place marker ah) (e:sathau thawl khat la-in ama ~ buak a) (b:lutung) (r:9.10.1/10.13.19) (q:draft)
luum = (t:v) (w:be stirred/be in an uproar) (d:in luum lialua, of a whole town moved and noisy with excitement) (e:a khuazangpi-un ~ lialua uh hi) (r:8.1.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
luum = (t:n) (w:shield) (d:named among the weapons of a rider, with galhiam and tei, spear; apparently a spelling of lum, shield) (e:galhiam, ~ leh teite tee zalzal hi) (r:18.39.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
maavanna = (t:n) (w:success/prosperity) (d:maavang prosper, in the form maavan before the noun suffix na) (e:kote tungah ~ hong pia in) (r:23.26.12/16.1.11) (q:draft)
maikhing = (t:v) (w:look sad/be downcast/be dismayed) (d:mai face with khing: have a sad or fallen face) (e:~ loin bangci om theih ding ka hi hiam) (r:16.2.3/19.40.15) (q:draft)
maikhingsak = (t:v) (w:make downcast/dismay/put to shame) (d:maikhing be downcast, with the causative sak) (e:a maizumna uh tawh ~ in) (b:maikhing) (r:19.70.3/19.40.15) (q:draft)
maimangin = (t:v) (w:perishing/wasting away) (d:maimang perish, with the linking ending in) (e:gitlohna hangin note ~) (b:maimang) (r:26.24.23/46.15.54) (q:draft)
maiphut = (t:v) (w:confront/face/come against) (d:mai face with phut: meet someone head on; of the wind, blow against) (e:huih in hong ~ ahih manin) (r:44.27.4/19.17.13) (q:draft)
maiput = (t:n) (w:look on the face/countenance/expression) (d:mai face with put, bear: the look that the face shows) (e:~ in amau langah teci pang hi) (r:23.3.9/26.27.35) (q:draft)
maitaisak = (t:v) (w:brighten the face/make cheerful) (d:maitai cheerful, with the causative sak) (e:Pilna in mipilte ~ a) (b:maitai) (r:21.8.1/20.15.13) (q:draft)
makaipi = (t:n) (w:chief leader/champion/chief) (d:makai leader with pi great; la makaipi is the chief musician) (e:Heman in la ~ hi a) (b:makai) (r:13.6.33/9.17.23) (q:draft)
malam = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb, apparently for doing something readily or straight off, as na sang malam, you so readily accept) (e:thudang khat na sang ~) (r:48.1.6/21.10.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
malin = (t:adv) (w:one by one/individually/by number) (d:mal a single counted item, with in: taken one at a time, person by person or item by item) (e:a ~ simzawh loh ding siatna tampite) (b:mal) (r:19.40.12/9.10.21) (q:draft)
malzah = (t:n) (w:number/total number/count) (d:mal a counted item with zah amount: how many there are of things counted one by one) (e:a ~ tawh kizui-in) (r:4.15.12/13.9.28) (q:draft)
mamsak = (t:v) (w:straighten/make straight) (d:mam straight, with the causative sak) (e:ama lampi khempeuh ka ~ ding hi) (r:23.45.13/21.7.13) (q:draft)
mangbuhhamte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:barley) (d:mangbuhham barley with plural te, the barley plants) (e:~ a vuih laitak hi a) (b:mangbuhham) (r:2.9.31) (q:draft)
mangbuhmante = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:spelt) (d:plural of mangbuhman, a grain named beside mangbuh wheat and mangbuhham barley) (e:mangbuh leh ~ sia lo hi) (r:2.9.32/23.28.25) (q:draft)
mangliante = (t:n) (w:officials/rulers/governors) (d:plural of manglian, a high official or ruler) (e:tua ~ khempeuh milim apna dingin) (r:27.3.3/23.60.17) (q:draft)
mangthangte = (t:n) (w:the lost/lost ones) (d:mangthang be lost or perish, with plural te: those who are lost) (e:a ~ zong loin, a liamte bawl loin) (b:mangthang) (r:38.11.16/42.19.10) (q:draft)
mankhit = (t:v) (w:finish/have finished) (d:man finish with khit, which marks the action as completed; a mankhit ciangin is when he had finished) (e:A thunget a ~ ciangin a nungzuite khat in) (r:42.11.1/42.11.37) (q:draft)
manlahin = (t:adv) (w:busily/being busy) (d:manlah be busy, with in; manlahin om is to be busy, taken up with one's affairs) (e:hua lai-ah ~ a om kalin) (b:manlah) (r:11.20.40/59.1.11) (q:draft)
manlahpih = (t:v) (w:be busy with/occupy oneself with/devote oneself to) (d:manlah be busy, with pih which adds the thing one is busy with) (e:tua bang thute a ~ loh nadingun) (b:manlah) (r:54.1.4/21.3.10) (q:draft)
manpa = (t:n) (w:catcher/one who catches) (d:man catch with pa, a man: the man who catches an animal in hunting) (e:a ~ in a sisan bua khia-in) (b:man) (r:3.17.13) (q:draft)
manpa = (t:n) (w:dreamer) (d:in mang manpa, the man who has dreams; mang man is to dream a dream) (e:mang ~ ahi zongin kithat ding hi) (b:man) (r:5.13.5/5.13.3) (q:draft)
manpah = (t:v) (w:seize at once/arrest immediately) (d:man seize or arrest, with pah at once) (e:Amaute in tua pa ~ uh a) (r:42.23.26/42.20.19) (q:draft)
manphapen = (t:adj) (w:most precious/most valuable) (d:manpha precious with the superlative pen) (e:na neihsa a ~ bangin na kep ding) (b:manpha) (r:20.4.23/38.2.8) (q:draft)
manzah = (t:n) (w:value/price/worth) (d:man price with zah amount: how much a thing is worth) (e:a ~ ding nangmah in seh inla) (r:3.5.18/3.27.18) (q:draft)
masazaw = (t:adv) (w:first/ahead/before others) (d:masa first with the comparative zaw; placed after a verb: do it first, or before someone else does) (e:numei paktatte lut ~ ding hi) (b:masa) (r:40.21.31/40.6.33) (q:draft)
matut = (t:n) (d:found only in matut zawhna, success, what one has managed to achieve; the meaning of matut by itself is not shown by the verses) (e:Amah in ~ zawhna lianpi a neih lam) (r:9.18.15/23.26.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
mawhmai = (t:n) (w:forgiveness of sin/atonement) (d:mawh sin with mai as in maisak forgive; mawhmai biakna is a sin offering, mawhmai ngahna the gaining of forgiveness) (e:Meihal biakna leh ~ biakna zong) (r:19.40.6/20.16.6) (q:draft)
mawhneipa = (t:n) (w:sinner) (d:mawhnei sinner with pa, a man: the sinner, a sinful man) (e:a kisikkik ~ khat hangin) (b:mawhnei) (r:42.15.10/42.19.7) (q:draft)
mawhpa = (t:n) (w:the guilty/guilty man/wrongdoer) (d:mawh sin or be in the wrong, with pa, a man: the one found guilty, opposite of a dikpa, the one in the right) (e:a dikpa khahin a ~ lelsak a) (b:mawh) (r:5.25.1/11.8.32) (q:draft)
mawhsa = (t:adj) (w:sinful/having sinned) (d:mawh sin with sa, which marks a state already reached: one who has sinned; with tawh also said of unlawful sex with someone) (e:hong paai cil-a kipan a ~ ka hi hi) (b:mawh) (r:19.51.5/26.23.7) (q:draft)
mawkte = (t:n) (d:mawk idly or of itself, with plural te: closes a clause to mean those who do so idly or for no cause, as a ding mawkte, those standing idle) (e:sumbuk ah a ding ~ a muh ciangin) (b:mawk) (r:40.20.3/26.44.31) (q:draft)
mawlpihna = (t:n) (w:making a fool of/making sport of/mocking) (d:mawlpih make sport of, with the noun suffix na: the act of treating someone as a plaything) (e:Nang in kei nong ~ hang ahi hi) (b:mawlpih) (r:4.22.29/2.10.1) (q:draft)
meekin = (t:v) (w:kneading) (d:meek knead, with the linking ending in: kneading, and then) (e:annel ~ silngo sawhloh anlum em a) (b:meek) (r:9.28.24) (q:draft)
meekin = (t:v) (w:squeezing/choking) (d:meek squeeze, with the linking ending in; a gawl meekin is gripping him by the throat) (e:a muh ciangin a gawl ~) (b:meek) (r:40.18.28) (q:draft)
meigongin = (t:adv) (w:as a widow) (d:meigong widow with in; meigongin om is to live as a widow) (e:kum li sung ~ a om ahi hi) (b:meigong) (r:42.2.37/23.47.8) (q:draft)
meihalna = (t:n) (w:burning) (d:mei fire and hal burn with the noun suffix na: a burning with fire, also the burning of offerings) (e:Topa in thukhenna leh ~ tawh) (b:meihal) (r:23.4.3/24.11.17) (q:draft)
meihol = (t:n) (w:charcoal/coal) (d:meihol cih is to make a charcoal fire) (e:~ in mei am ding piangsak a) (r:20.26.21/43.18.18) (q:draft)
meiizun = (t:n) (w:mist/dew/dampness) (d:fine moisture from cloud or night air that wets what it settles on) (e:~ in ka sam kawtsak hi) (r:22.5.2/23.18.4) (q:draft)
melin = (t:adv) (w:by sight/by face/in appearance) (d:mel appearance or face with in: melin thei is know someone by face; after a colour word, of that colour in appearance, as a san melin, reddish) (e:ka ~ hong thei nai lo uh a) (b:mel) (r:48.1.22/3.13.49) (q:draft)
meng = (t:adv) (w:quickly/speedily/in haste) (d:placed after a verb: do it quickly, without delay) (e:Topa aw, hong huh ~ in) (r:19.40.13/19.69.17) (q:draft)
metin = (t:v) (w:shaving/having shaved) (d:met shave, with the linking ending in) (e:a lu ~ a cinte tan ding hi) (b:met) (r:5.21.12/24.41.5) (q:draft)
mettom = (t:v) (w:crop/cut short/shave short) (d:met shave or cut hair with tom short; a sam uh a mettom are those who crop their hair, where the NIV has those in distant places) (e:A sam uh a ~ amaute mun khempeuhah) (r:24.49.32/24.9.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
mialcipsak = (t:v) (w:darken completely/shroud in darkness) (d:mial dark, cip completely and the causative sak: make wholly dark) (e:ka pai nading lampi khua ~ hi) (r:18.19.8/25.2.1) (q:draft)
mialta = (t:v) (w:become dark/be darkened) (d:mial be dark, with ta which marks a change that has now come about; khua hong mialta is it had grown dark) (e:Ni le kha ~ a) (b:mial) (r:29.3.15/43.6.17) (q:draft)
mialzawt = (t:v) (w:grope/feel one's way) (d:mial dark with zawt feel about with the hands: grope as in the dark) (e:suntangpi-in zan bangin ~ uh hi) (r:18.5.14/18.12.25) (q:draft)
mibum = (t:n) (w:sorcery/enchantment/spell) (d:mi person with bum bewitch: casting spells on people; mibum theite are enchanters, mibum siamna is skill in spells) (e:mitphial siamte, ~ theite, le khongkhai siamte) (r:27.2.2/23.47.9) (q:draft)
mibumna = (t:n) (w:sorcery/witchcraft/magic spell) (d:mibum cast spells on people, with the noun suffix na) (e:na ~ le na aisannate ah) (b:mibum) (r:23.47.12/48.5.20) (q:draft)
midangpi = (t:n) (w:stranger/outsider/foreigner) (d:midang other person with the intensive pi: a complete stranger) (e:Ka sanggamte lakah ~ ka suak a) (b:midang) (r:19.69.8/18.19.15) (q:draft)
migina = (t:n) (w:worthy man/man of standing/respectable person) (d:mi person with gina worthy; migina lo is a nobody, a worthless person) (e:nang ~ na hi a) (r:11.1.42/8.2.1) (q:draft)
miginalo = (t:n) (w:worthless person/scoundrel/good-for-nothing) (d:migina worthy person with the negative lo; in Hebrews 5:3 said of a weak, imperfect man) (e:~ pa, a gilo pa, thuzuau genin) (b:migina) (r:20.6.12/50.3.2) (q:draft)
mihingin = (t:adv) (w:as a human/as a man) (d:mihing human with in: in the state of a human being) (e:leitungah ~ i suah laitakin) (b:mihing) (r:54.6.7/58.5.7) (q:draft)
mikhem = (t:v) (w:deceive people/cheat) (d:mi person with khem deceive; mikhem theite and mikhem hatte are deceivers, the treacherous) (e:~ theite aw, note’ tungah bang) (r:19.120.3/24.12.1) (q:draft)
mikhempeuh = (t:pron) (w:everyone/all people/everybody) (d:mi person with khempeuh all, written as one word; usually written mi khempeuh) (e:mi ukte leh ~ tungah) (r:16.4.14/60.2.17) (q:draft)
mikhemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/deceitful people) (d:mikhem deceive people, with plural te: those who deceive) (e:mizuaute leh ~ kiang panin) (b:mikhem) (r:19.120.2/19.55.23) (q:draft)
milianpi = (t:n) (w:great man/very great person/somebody) (d:milian great person with the intensive pi) (e:a neupente ~ suak ding hi) (b:milian) (r:23.60.22/10.23.1) (q:draft)
milmial = (t:adv) (w:dimly/dully/faintly) (d:not clear or bright: of seeing, dimly; after a colour word, dull, as a kang milmial, dull white) (e:a kitel pha loin i mu ~ a) (r:46.13.12/3.13.39) (q:draft)
mimi-in = (t:adv) (w:man by man/person by person/one by one) (d:mi person doubled, with in: each person in turn, like a behbehin clan by clan and a innkuankuanin family by family) (e:ama innkuanpihte a ~ hong paipih a) (r:6.7.18/6.7.14) (q:draft)
minno = (t:n) (w:nickname/other name) (d:min name with no small: a second name by which a person is known) (e:Unau Peeng ~ a nei Thomas) (b:min) (r:43.20.24/43.21.2) (q:draft)
misimna = (t:n) (w:census/numbering/counting of people) (d:mi person and sim count with the noun suffix na) (e:Israel mite ~ bawl-a, amaute na sim ciangin) (r:2.30.12/2.30.13) (q:draft)
misipa = (t:n) (w:dead man) (d:misi dead person with pa, a man: the dead man) (e:~ tho a, thu a gen hi) (b:misi) (r:42.7.15/43.11.39) (q:draft)
mitheek = (t:n) (w:wink/signal with the eye) (d:a sign made with the eye; mitheek pia is to wink at someone) (e:Simon Peter in a ~ tawh amah hopih a) (r:43.13.24/20.6.13) (q:draft)
mitsuanin = (t:adv) (w:with eyes fixed on/looking to) (d:mitsuan fix the eyes on, with in; mitsuanin nei is to keep the eyes fixed on, to hold in view) (e:hong cingtaaksak Jesuh ~ nei ni) (b:mitsuan) (r:58.12.2/19.119.6) (q:draft)
mittawsak = (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:mittaw blind with the causative sak) (e:bilngongsak, musak, ~ ahi hiam) (b:mittaw) (r:2.4.11/23.29.9) (q:draft)
mohin = (t:adv) (w:into cakes/as loaves) (d:moh cake or loaf with in; mohin bawl is make into cakes or loaves) (e:beelin huan uh a, ~ a bawl uh hi) (b:moh) (r:4.11.8/1.18.6) (q:draft)
momaite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (e:Gulpi le ~ na sikgawp nading uh) (b:momai) (r:42.10.19/66.9.3) (q:draft)
muaimuai = (t:adv) (w:in a mass/in swarms/in great numbers) (d:placed after a verb of movement, of a great crowd or swarm moving together) (e:mihonpi hong pai ~ a muh ciangin) (r:43.6.5/29.2.2) (q:draft)
muala = (t:n) (w:on the mountain/of the mountain) (d:mual mountain with the ending a, at or on: Lebanon muala om, that are on Mount Lebanon) (e:Lebanon ~ om taamtak singte) (b:mual) (r:19.104.16/23.33.9) (q:draft)
mualpangah = (t:n) (w:on the hillside/at the hillside) (d:mualpang hillside with the place marker ah) (e:tua nai-a om ~ vok hon tampi) (b:mualpang) (r:41.5.11/10.16.13) (q:draft)
mualvum = (t:n) (w:mountain top/summit/peak) (d:the top of a mountain) (e:Lebanon ~ bangin ahi zongin na hoih hi) (r:24.22.6/2.24.17) (q:draft)
muatgawp = (t:v) (w:rot away/decay completely) (d:muat rot with gawp, done to the point of ruin) (e:amaute’ zung pen ~ ding a) (b:muat) (r:23.5.24/19.83.9) (q:draft)
muatsak = (t:v) (w:rot/cause to rot/make decay) (d:muat rot with the causative sak) (e:a khut leh a khete ~ ta hi) (b:muat) (r:18.18.13/20.14.30) (q:draft)
muhah = (t:adv) (w:in the sight of/before the eyes of) (d:muh see with the place marker ah; mit muhah is before one's eyes, in one's sight) (e:note’ mit ~ a hih bangin) (b:muh) (r:5.1.30/5.29.2) (q:draft)
muhnate = (t:n) (w:visions/things seen/sights) (d:plural of muhna, seeing or what is seen; maang muhnate are visions, zakna muhnate hearing and sight) (e:na maang ~ leh na thugen kholhnate) (b:muhna) (r:26.12.27/23.13.1) (q:draft)
muhthadah = (t:adj) (w:loathsome/detestable/repulsive) (d:hateful to look at; muhthadah sa is to find loathsome, muhthadah huai is repulsive, detestable) (e:a ~ huai khat ka mu hi) (r:24.23.13/5.21.23) (q:draft)
mukah = (t:n) (w:in the mouth/on the lips/in the beak) (d:muk lip, mouth or beak with the place marker ah) (e:a tukkhiat thak khat a ~ petin) (b:muk) (r:1.8.11/18.8.21) (q:draft)
mukhol = (t:v) (w:foresee/see beforehand/look ahead to) (d:mu see with khol in advance) (e:thu David in ~ ahih manin) (r:44.2.31/58.11.26) (q:draft)
munbu = (t:n) (w:hiding place/secret place/hidden place) (d:mun place with bu hide: a place out of sight; munbu-na sungah is in secret) (e:~ kawmah mawhnei lote a that hi) (r:19.10.8/42.11.33) (q:draft)
munteng = (t:n) (w:whole place/all the area) (d:mun place with teng all of: the whole of a place or area; of a text, the whole passage where something is written) (e:Hih ~ pen Israel gam sung panin) (b:mun) (r:26.45.8/42.4.20) (q:draft)
mutin = (t:v) (w:blowing) (d:mut blow, with the linking ending in: of wind blowing, or of blowing a trumpet) (e:peengkul ~ awng unla, va gen un) (b:mut) (r:24.4.5/44.27.40) (q:draft)
nadingte = (t:part) (d:nading, for the purpose of, with plural te: closes a phrase to mean the things that are for or that lead to something, as biak nadingte, things for offering) (e:leenggahzu tawh biak ~ lei nading bekin) (b:nading) (r:15.7.17/19.18.23) (q:draft)
naihuai = (t:adj) (w:close/near/related) (d:nai near with huai: close to one in kinship or friendship; also the close person himself, as i naihuai, our kinsman) (e:na lawm ~ pente uh nangawn in) (r:40.6.3/7.9.3) (q:draft)
nailo = (t:adv) (w:not yet/never yet) (d:nai yet with the negative lo, written as one word after a verb; usually written nai lo) (e:lupkhopna tawh pasal a thei ~ numei) (b:nai) (r:4.31.35/7.11.39) (q:draft)
nakging = (t:n) (w:snorting/snort/blast of the nostrils) (d:nak nose with ging sound: the noise of breath forced through the nostrils) (e:galte’ sakol ~ kiza hi) (r:24.8.16/19.18.15) (q:draft)
naksuk = (t:n) (w:breath/breathing) (d:nak nose or breathe with suk downward; used in the pair naksuk naktoh, breathing down and up, for breath or the power to breathe) (e:~ naktoh akipan na khempeuh hong pia) (b:nak) (r:44.17.25/19.135.17) (q:draft)
nakvang = (t:n) (w:nostril/nostrils) (d:nak nose with vang opening) (e:A ~ panin meikhu pusuak a) (r:10.22.9/23.2.22) (q:draft)
namkimte = (t:n) (w:all nations/all peoples/all kinds) (d:namkim all kinds with plural te; mi namkimte are people of every nation) (e:Mi ~ tungah teci a pan’ nadingin) (b:namkim) (r:40.24.14/27.3.4) (q:draft)
nanna = (t:n) (w:support/prop) (d:nan support with the noun suffix na: a part that holds something up, as the supports of a basin stand or the ledges that carry beams) (e:kiu ciatah a ~ li om ciat a) (b:nan) (r:11.7.34/11.6.6) (q:draft)
nanna = (t:n) (w:resistance/withstanding) (d:nan withstand with the noun suffix na: holding out against something, as against a siege) (e:Jerusalem umcihna na ~ ding uh) (b:nan) (r:14.32.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
nannate = (t:n) (w:supports/props) (d:plural of nanna, a part that holds something up) (e:a kiu lite-ah tuikuangpi ~ om hi) (b:nanna) (r:11.7.30/11.7.34) (q:draft)
nasemkhawm = (t:n) (w:fellow servant/fellow worker) (d:nasem servant or work with khawm together: one who serves alongside another) (e:Pasian sungah ~ khat ihi hi) (b:nasem) (r:48.2.9/66.22.9) (q:draft)
nasempate = (t:n) (w:male servants/menservants) (d:plural of nasempa, a male servant) (e:na tanute, na ~, na nasemnute) (b:nasempa) (r:2.20.10/5.5.14) (q:draft)
nasepin = (t:adv) (w:as work/as occupation) (d:nasep work with in; nasepin nei is have as one's trade or occupation) (e:savunnim ~ a nei Simon) (b:nasep) (r:44.9.43/44.10.6) (q:draft)
nasepsa = (t:n) (w:product of labour/produce/earnings) (d:nasep work with sa, already done: what one has worked for and produced) (e:gahte leh na ~ khempeuh uh) (b:nasep) (r:5.28.33/24.20.5) (q:draft)
nattunin = (t:adv) (w:with a fever/sick with fever) (d:nattun fever with in: being ill with fever) (e:sungnu ~ lupna tungah a lum) (b:nattun) (r:40.8.14/41.1.30) (q:draft)
naupaai = (t:v) (w:be pregnant/become pregnant/conceive) (d:nau child with paai carry in the womb; numei naupaai is a pregnant woman) (e:Ahih hangin tua nu in ~ a) (r:12.4.17/12.15.16) (q:draft)
naupangin = (t:n) (w:child) (d:naupang child with in: in a numei a naupangin, women and children alike; also naupang followed by the subject marker in, written as one word) (e:a numei a ~ susia-in) (b:naupang) (r:17.8.11/11.3.22) (q:draft)
nausuahna = (t:n) (w:childbirth/childbearing/delivery) (d:nausuah give birth with the noun suffix na; nausuahna tutphah is the delivery stool) (e:~ tutphah tungah a tu) (b:nausuah) (r:2.1.16/54.2.15) (q:draft)
nauta = (t:n) (w:pupil of the eye/apple of the eye) (d:found in mit nauta, the pupil of the eye, said of what is guarded as most precious) (e:ama mit ~ bangin amaute kem hi) (r:5.32.10/38.2.8) (q:draft)
nauzawpa = (t:n) (w:younger son/younger brother/the younger) (d:nauzaw the younger with pa, a male) (e:a ~ Efraim’ lutang tungah nga a) (b:nauzaw) (r:1.48.14/42.15.13) (q:draft)
nawhkhia = (t:v) (w:drive out/chase out/expel) (d:nawh drive with khia out) (e:gamah kong ~ ding hi) (b:nawh) (r:24.16.13/5.33.27) (q:draft)
nawksuak = (t:v) (w:break through/press through/contend) (d:nawk push against with suak through: force a way through; upna thu-ah nawksuak is to struggle on for the faith) (e:Ammon mite’ gamgi ~ zo lo uh hi) (r:4.21.24/54.6.12) (q:draft)
nawlkhin = (t:v) (w:reject/refuse/turn away from) (d:push aside a person or his word, have nothing to do with) (e:Migilote in Pasian ~ uh a) (r:18.21.14/44.7.39) (q:draft)
nawng = (t:n) (w:marsh/swamp/mire) (e:~ sunga pumpeng lakah bu hi) (r:18.40.21/26.47.11) (q:draft)
nawngkai = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be disturbed/be hindered) (d:nawngkai sa is feel disturbed or annoyed; nawngkai sak is to trouble, stir up or hinder) (e:thu hilh uh ahih manin ~ a sa uh hi) (r:44.4.2/9.14.6) (q:draft)
nawnlo = (t:adv) (w:no longer/no more/not any more) (d:nawn any longer with the negative lo, written as one word after a verb; usually written nawn lo) (e:piak kikkik ding kisam ~ ding) (b:nawn) (r:58.10.2/24.2.35) (q:draft)
nawnloin = (t:adv) (w:no longer/without any more) (d:nawnlo no longer, with the linking ending in: no longer doing so, and) (e:uh lampi lui zui ~) (b:nawnlo) (r:24.18.15/24.7.6) (q:draft)
neihkhawm = (t:v) (w:share/have together/own jointly) (d:neih have with khawm together) (e:midang tawh na ~ ding hi lo hi) (b:neih) (r:20.5.17/43.17.5) (q:draft)
neihkik = (t:v) (w:have again/take again/regain) (d:neih have with kik again; pasal neihkik is to marry again) (e:a zi in pasal a ~ leh) (b:neih) (r:40.5.32/38.1.17) (q:draft)
neihsak = (t:v) (w:let have/give/provide) (d:neih have with the causative sak: cause or allow someone to have) (e:meihal biakna kote nong ~ kul hi) (b:neih) (r:2.10.25/19.137.9) (q:draft)
neihteng = (t:n) (w:all that one has/everything owned) (d:neih have with teng all of: the whole of what is had, placed after the thing owned) (e:vangliatna le aana a ~ uh) (b:neih) (r:66.17.13/30.5.11) (q:draft)
neklam = (t:n) (w:eating/the fact of eating) (d:nek eat with lam, the fact or manner: that someone eats, as the object of a verb of seeing) (e:an a ~ uh a mukha uh hi) (r:41.7.2/42.11.38) (q:draft)
nekpihin = (t:v) (w:eating with) (d:nekpih eat with, with the linking ending in, eating with someone and then doing the next action) (e:amaute in a pawi an ~) (b:nekpih) (r:4.25.2/38.3.10) (q:draft)
nekzah = (t:n) (w:portion/food allowance/ration) (d:nek eat, with zah amount: the amount that one eats, a share of food) (e:amaute’ ~ ding ciat) (r:42.12.42/2.12.4) (q:draft)
nekzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to eat/can eat) (d:nek eat, with zawh, the form of zo be able used before zah; a nekzawh zahzah is as much as one can eat, to the full) (e:a ~ zahzah uh ne ding uh hi) (r:26.39.20/66.19.21) (q:draft)
nencip = (t:v) (w:weigh down/press down/overwhelm) (d:nen press down, with cip tightly: bear down heavily on someone, said of sin and wickedness) (e:mawhna in a ~ mite) (b:nen) (r:23.1.4/26.33.10) (q:draft)
nenete = (t:n) (w:drinkers/drunkards) (d:nene keep eating or drinking, with the plural te: those who drink habitually; zu nenete is drunkards) (e:Zu ~ tawh kikhawl kei inla) (b:nene) (r:20.23.20/20.23.21) (q:draft)
nenniamnate = (t:n) (w:oppressions/acts of oppression) (d:nenniamna oppression, with the plural te) (e:mi na ~ uh khawl un) (b:nenniamna) (r:26.45.9/5.26.7) (q:draft)
netumin = (t:v) (w:devouring/eating up/consuming) (d:netum devour, with the linking ending in, eating up and then the next action follows) (e:a hut in amah ~ a si hi) (b:netum) (r:44.12.23/10.21.5) (q:draft)
neulua = (t:adj) (w:too small) (d:neu small, with lua too much) (e:note a dingin ~ ahih ciangin) (b:neu) (r:6.17.15/12.6.1) (q:draft)
neuzawte = (t:n) (w:lesser ones/smaller ones/the least) (d:neuzaw smaller, lesser, with the plural te: those who are lesser in rank or strength) (e:a ~ in zakhat val) (b:neuzaw) (r:13.12.14/58.7.7) (q:draft)
ngahkikin = (t:v) (w:getting back/recovering/receiving back) (d:ngahkik get back, with the linking ending in) (e:numeite leh mihingte ~ ciahpih hi) (b:ngahkik) (r:1.14.16/3.25.10) (q:draft)
ngahkikna = (t:n) (w:regaining/recovery) (d:ngahkik get back, with the noun suffix na; a ngahkikna dingin is in order to regain) (e:a kumpi gam a ~ dingin) (b:ngahkik) (r:11.12.21/12.14.28) (q:draft)
ngahtheihna = (t:n) (w:obtaining/means of getting) (d:ngahtheih be able to get, with the noun suffix na; sum ngahtheihna ding is in order to get money) (e:sum ~ ding ngaihsutna bek tawh) (b:ngahtheih) (r:33.3.11) (q:draft)
ngaihbaanna = (t:n) (w:charm/loveliness/attractiveness) (d:ngaihbaang lovely, attractive, with the noun suffix na: the charm of a woman) (e:ama ~ tawh lungdamin) (r:20.5.19/20.31.30) (q:draft)
ngaihsutkhak = (t:v) (w:think/suppose/have in mind) (d:form of ngaihsutkha, happen to think, come to think, used in dependent clauses) (e:ka ~ beek zong ahi lo) (r:24.19.5/47.12.6) (q:draft)
ngaihsuttawm = (t:adj) (w:self-devised/made up/of his own invention) (d:ngaihsut think, with tawm, by oneself: thought up on his own; ngaihsuttawm thu is what someone says on his own authority, not what he was given to say) (e:Ama ~ thu hong gen ding hi lo) (r:43.16.13/24.23.31) (q:draft)
ngaingai = (t:v) (w:keep listening/listen on) (d:ngai listen, said twice for continued action) (e:~ napi-in za thei lo) (r:40.13.13/18.32.11) (q:draft)
ngaklai = (t:v) (w:still wait/wait longer/go on waiting) (d:ngak wait, with lai still, any longer) (e:bang tanvei ~ ding ka hi hiam) (r:19.119.84/12.6.33) (q:draft)
ngakngakna-in = (t:n) (w:long waiting/longing) (d:ngak wait, said twice for continued action, with the noun suffix na and in marking the cause: because of waiting and waiting) (e:Ka Pasian ka ~ ka mitte maang ta hi) (r:19.69.3/19.119.81) (q:draft)
ngakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to wait/manage to wait/wait through) (d:ngak wait, keep watch, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:a khan khit dong ~ ding) (b:ngak) (r:8.1.13/40.26.40) (q:draft)
ngal = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild boar/boar) (e:Gamlak a om ~ in susiagawp a) (r:19.80.13) (q:draft)
ngal = (t:part) (d:placed after kei, not, and before leh, if, to stress the condition: kei ngal leh is unless, if indeed not) (e:thu i muh kei ~ leh) (r:27.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaptan = (t:v) (w:wade through/ford/cross on foot) (d:ngap ford, with tan, cut across: go through water on foot; with sak, lead someone through) (e:a tui kei hong ~ sak hi) (r:26.47.3/26.47.4) (q:draft)
ngaptansak = (t:v) (w:lead through water/make wade through) (d:ngaptan wade through, with sak, cause to: take someone across water on foot) (e:a tui kei hong ~ hi) (b:ngaptan) (r:26.47.3/26.47.4) (q:draft)
ngenpa = (t:n) (w:one who asks/asker) (d:ngen ask, with pa marking a man: the man who asks; khutdawh ngenpa is a beggar) (e:tu-a khutdawh ~ hilo ahi hiam) (b:ngen) (r:43.9.8/43.4.10) (q:draft)
ngensak = (t:v) (w:have someone ask/let ask) (d:ngen ask, with sak, cause or allow: send someone to ask, or allow someone to ask) (e:a damsak nadingin a ~ hi) (b:ngen) (r:42.7.3/26.36.37) (q:draft)
ngentang = (t:adv) (w:only/nothing but/all alike) (d:placed after a list of nouns or qualities: these and nothing else, all of that kind) (e:cinatna leh liamnate ~ ka mu hi) (r:24.6.7/27.1.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngetnate = (t:n) (w:requests/petitions/pleas) (d:ngetna request, with the plural te) (e:ka hong ~ hong phawk in) (b:ngetna) (r:24.18.20/39.1.9) (q:draft)
ngetsakna = (t:n) (w:intercession/prayer for someone) (d:ngetsak pray for, with the noun suffix na; thu ngetsakna is praying on behalf of another) (e:thu ka ~ nangawn) (b:ngetsak) (r:19.109.4/54.4.14) (q:draft)
ngiahon = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wolves/pack of wolves) (d:ngia wolf, with hon, pack or flock) (e:~ lakah tuuno khah bangin) (r:42.10.3/40.10.16) (q:draft)
ngiano = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:little fox/young fox) (d:ngia wolf or fox, with no, young or little) (e:~ hon in a suksiat ma-in) (b:ngia) (r:22.2.15) (q:draft)
ngiingei = (t:adv) (w:utterly/thoroughly) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is carried through completely: balnen ngiingei tear to pieces, paatsak ngiingei wear out utterly, kihelkim ngiingei fully mixed) (e:kei nong paatsak ~ a) (r:18.16.7/19.75.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngongtatnate = (t:n) (w:acts of violence/violent deeds/abuses) (d:ngongtatna violence, with the plural te) (e:khua sungah siatna le ~ om a) (b:ngongtatna) (r:19.55.10/26.45.9) (q:draft)
nialnial = (t:v) (w:keep refusing/keep protesting/go on disputing) (d:nial deny, refuse, dispute, said twice for continued action) (e:bang hangin ~ na hi hiam) (r:18.15.11/18.19.7) (q:draft)
niamkoih = (t:v) (w:bring low/humble/abase) (d:niam low, with koih put: put someone in a low place) (e:Topa in Judah mite ~ hi) (r:14.28.19/7.11.35) (q:draft)
niamsakin = (t:v) (w:lowering/bowing down) (d:niamsak make low, with the linking ending in; vantungte niamsakin is bowing the heavens, where the NIV has parted) (e:vantungte ~ hong paisuk a) (b:niamsak) (r:10.22.10/19.18.9) (q:draft)
niamzaw = (t:adj) (w:lower/inferior) (d:niam low, with zaw more; used with sangin, than) (e:tual sangin ~ hi) (b:niam) (r:26.40.18/18.12.3) (q:draft)
nihnapa = (t:n) (w:the second) (d:nihna second, with pa marking a man: after a name, the second man of that name, as Jeroboam the Second; also the man second in rank) (e:Jeroboam a ~ a tu hi) (b:nihna) (r:12.13.13/16.11.9) (q:draft)
ninsakthei = (t:v) (w:can defile/be able to make unclean) (d:ninsak defile, with thei, be able) (e:hihte in mi ~ hi) (b:ninsak) (r:40.15.18/41.7.15) (q:draft)
nom = (t:n) (w:moisture/dampness) (d:wetness in the soil; in the list of plagues in Deuteronomy 28:22 a nom stands where the NIV has mildew) (e:leisung a ~ tam lo ahih manin) (r:42.8.6/5.28.22) (q:draft)
notkik = (t:v) (w:drive back/push back/force back) (d:not push, with kik back) (e:amaute ka ~ uh hi) (b:not) (r:10.11.23/7.1.34) (q:draft)
nu'ng = (t:part) (w:let us) (d:verb-final word for the first person plural, proposing an action to be done together: let us, we will) (e:Thukhen zumah kikhia ~) (r:23.50.8/23.41.1) (q:draft)
nuamsate = (t:n) (w:happy people/those who live at ease) (d:nuamsa be happy, enjoy, with the plural te: mi nuamsate is people who are happy or blessed, and also people who live in comfort) (e:Amah a bel khempeuh mi ~ ahi hi) (b:nuamsa) (r:19.2.11/42.7.25) (q:draft)
nungdelhsak = (t:v) (w:make pursue/send in pursuit) (d:nungdelh pursue, with sak, cause to: namsau ka nungdelhsak ding is I will make the sword pursue them) (e:namsau ka ~ ding hi) (b:nungdelh) (r:24.49.37/26.12.14) (q:draft)
nungsuk = (t:v) (w:blow down/sweep down) (d:of wind: nung blow, with suk downward; paired with nungto, blow upward) (e:Tuipi tungah huihpi nakpi ~ a) (r:42.8.23/22.4.16) (q:draft)
nungtasakkik = (t:v) (w:revive/bring back to life/make live again) (d:nungtasak make live, with kik again) (e:note kong ~ ding hi) (b:nungtasak) (r:26.37.5/19.85.6) (q:draft)
nungtazo = (t:v) (w:be able to live/survive) (d:nungta live, with zo, be able, manage to) (e:kua ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:nungta) (r:4.24.23/39.3.2) (q:draft)
nupate = (t:n) (w:married couple/husband and wife) (d:nupa couple, with te; tua nupate is that couple, the two of them) (e:Tua ~ tawh a kimu dingin) (b:nupa) (r:44.18.2/40.19.10) (q:draft)
nusiazo = (t:v) (w:have forsaken/have abandoned/have left) (d:nusia leave, forsake, with zo showing that the act has been carried through) (e:Na tate un kei hong ~ uh a) (b:nusia) (r:24.5.7/19.71.11) (q:draft)
nutsiat = (t:v) (w:leave/leave behind/abandon) (d:spelling of nusiat, the form of nusia leave used before ding and khit and to describe a noun) (e:thong sungah khumin a ~ mi khat) (r:44.25.14/44.27.40) (q:draft)
olzaw = (t:adj) (w:easier/more bearable) (d:ol easy, with zaw more; used with sangin, than) (e:van le lei a manthan ding ~ lai hi) (b:ol) (r:42.16.17/40.10.15) (q:draft)
omlaisun = (t:adj) (w:remaining/left over) (d:omlai remain, with sun; a omlaisun teng or a omlaisun khempeuh is all who are still left, the remnant) (e:A ~ teng khatlekhat kisanek un) (r:38.11.9/26.9.8) (q:draft)
ompa = (t:n) (w:he who is/the one who is) (d:om be, with pa marking a man: the one who is in a place or with someone) (e:Vantung-a a ~ aw) (b:om) (r:19.123.1/9.16.19) (q:draft)
omsate = (t:n) (w:existing ones/earlier ones/those already there) (d:omsa already existing, with the plural te; after a noun it describes it, as pawlpi omsate, the churches already there) (e:amah in a ~ tawh a kilamdang mahmahin) (b:omsa) (r:27.7.24/44.15.41) (q:draft)
omzawh = (t:v) (w:have been/have stayed) (d:om be, stay, with zawh, completed: the time that one has spent in a state, followed by a count of days or years) (e:thong sungah a ~ kum sawmthum) (r:12.25.27/26.33.21) (q:draft)
pahpahte = (t:n) (d:pahpah at once, readily, with the plural te, making a noun of the verb phrase before it: those who are quick to do something; a heh pahpahte is those who are quick to anger) (e:A heh ~ in kitotna piangsak a) (b:pahpah) (r:20.29.22/59.2.6) (q:draft)
pahtakhuai = (t:adj) (w:honoured/admirable/worthy of honour) (d:pahtak favour, honour, with huai, worthy of) (e:a deihhuai, le a ~ thute ahi hi) (r:50.4.8/23.43.4) (q:draft)
pahtawihuai = (t:adj) (w:honourable/worthy of honour) (d:pahtawi honour, with huai, worthy of) (e:a sanggamte sangin ~ zaw hi) (r:13.4.9/23.58.13) (q:draft)
paihkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:removing/taking away) (d:paihkhiatsak remove, take away from someone, with the linking ending in) (e:suang lungtang ~ mihing lungtang ka guan ding hi) (b:paihkhiatsak) (r:26.11.19/33.5.10) (q:draft)
paikhiatlam = (t:n) (w:going out/departure/leaving) (d:paikhiat go out, with lam, the fact or manner of: that someone has gone out, the leaving of someone) (e:na ~ mi khempeuh musak in) (r:26.12.3/41.6.33) (q:draft)
pailam = (t:n) (w:coming/going) (d:pai go, come, with lam, the fact of: that someone has come or is coming) (e:Pasian hong ~ na phawk lohna hang ahi hi) (r:42.19.44/8.3.3) (q:draft)
pailet = (t:v) (w:pierce through/pass through/penetrate) (d:pai go, with let through: go right through a body) (e:Thaltang khat in a pumpi ~ a) (r:18.20.25/58.4.12) (q:draft)
painop = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go) (d:pai go, with nop, the form of nuam want used in dependent clauses, as before kei leh and ciangin) (e:Jerusalem-ah a ~ kei leh) (r:38.14.17/26.1.12) (q:draft)
painuam = (t:v) (w:want to go/be willing to go/want to come) (d:pai go, come, with nuam want) (e:kei kiangah nong ~ kei veve uh hi) (r:43.5.40/44.19.30) (q:draft)
paipihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/lead back) (d:paipih take along, lead, with kik back) (e:amaute’ gamah ka ~ ding hi) (b:paipih) (r:26.37.21/24.31.9) (q:draft)
paisanin = (t:v) (w:leaving/going away from/going off) (d:paisan go away from, leave, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute ~ khua sung pan paikhia a) (b:paisan) (r:40.21.17/52.1.10) (q:draft)
paisim = (t:v) (w:go secretly/go in secret) (d:pai go, with sim, secretly, without being seen) (e:Zeisu zong a kilang loin a ~ hi) (r:43.7.10/26.17.15) (q:draft)
paisuakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to get through/be able to carry on) (d:paisuak go right through, go on without stopping, with zo, be able; after another verb, manage to keep on doing it to the end) (e:nangmah in na sem ~ ding hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.18.23/18.19.8) (q:draft)
paitosak = (t:v) (w:bring up/let go up/make go up) (d:paito go up, with sak, cause or allow) (e:Egypt panin kote hong ~ na hi hiam) (b:paito) (r:4.20.5/1.50.5) (q:draft)
palikbute = (t:n) (w:officers/police officers) (d:palik police, a loanword from English, with bu and the plural te; in Acts 16 the officers sent by the Roman magistrates) (e:Rom thukhen uliante in ~ samin) (r:44.16.35/44.16.38) (q:draft)
palsatte = (t:n) (w:transgressors/those who break) (d:palsat transgress, with the plural te: those who break a command; thu palsatte is transgressors) (e:thu ~ na zia ka hilh ding a) (b:palsat) (r:19.51.13/58.2.2) (q:draft)
pammaihsa = (t:v) (w:spare/hold dear/be zealous for) (d:pammaih too precious to lose, with sa feel: be unwilling to lose or give up; pammaihsa loin is without sparing) (e:Amah in amaute ~ ahih manin) (b:pammaih) (r:19.72.14/61.2.5) (q:draft)
pamte = (t:n) (w:neighbours/those around) (d:pam side, vicinity, with the plural te; used in the pairs a veng a pamte and na kiim na pamte, the people living all around) (e:na kiim na ~ uh kiang panin) (b:pam) (r:24.49.5/15.1.6) (q:draft)
pantah = (t:v) (w:bring up/rear/raise/nurture) (d:raise a child or a young animal) (e:A no dang khat ~ leuleu a) (r:26.19.5/49.6.4) (q:draft)
pasalnei = (t:v) (w:take a husband/be married) (d:pasal man, husband, with nei have, said of a woman; paired with zinei, take a wife; pasalnei thak is a bride) (e:zinei ~ cih om lo ding) (r:40.22.30/24.16.9) (q:draft)
pawh = (t:part) (w:if only/oh that) (d:sentence-final word after leng or leh, expressing a strong wish) (e:Vakhu bangin kha nei hi leng ~) (r:19.55.6/19.81.13) (q:draft)
pawina = (t:n) (w:ceremony/observance) (d:pawi festival, with the noun suffix na: the keeping of a feast) (e:hih bangin ~ hih ding uh hi) (b:pawi) (r:2.13.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawina = (t:n) (d:in a pawina leitang, land reckoned by the measure of seed it takes: apparently the area sown with a given amount of seed) (e:mangbuhham beem khat a ~ leitang) (r:3.27.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawlkhatin = (t:adv) (w:as one group/in fellowship/united) (d:pawlkhat one group, with the ending in: being one company with someone, in fellowship; pawlkhatin bawl is make into one) (e:Gentail mite le Jew mite ~ hong bawl) (b:pawlkhat) (r:49.2.14/62.1.3) (q:draft)
pawlpihna = (t:n) (w:siding with/alliance) (d:pawlpih side with, with the noun suffix na: the fact of having taken the side of someone) (e:Jessi’ tapa na ~ thu) (b:pawlpih) (r:9.20.30/11.2.28) (q:draft)
pehkik = (t:v) (w:graft in again/graft back) (d:peh graft, with kik again, back) (e:amau’ mun ngei mahah ~ ding hi) (b:peh) (r:45.11.23/45.11.24) (q:draft)
peite = (t:n) (w:wheels) (d:pei wheel, with the plural te) (e:A ~ pen sakol leengpei bangin kibawl hi) (b:pei) (r:11.7.33/2.14.25) (q:draft)
pekpek = (t:adv) (w:very far/by far/long ago) (d:pek far, said twice for emphasis: after lui old, very long ago, ancient; after a comparative with zaw, far more) (e:Khrih nasem a hoihzaw ~ ka hi hi) (r:47.11.23/13.4.22) (q:draft)
