tawhin = (t:v) (w:kindle/light) (d:tawh, kindle a fire, with the linking ending in; mei tawhin, kindling a fire and then) (e:amah in mei ~ moh a em hi) (b:tawh) (r:23.44.15/26.22.21) (q:draft)
tawldamsak = (t:v) (w:refresh/give rest/ease) (d:tawldam, be rested, with sak, cause) (e:a gim mite ka ~ ding a) (b:tawldam) (r:24.31.25/32.4.6) (q:draft)
tawna = (t:prep) (w:through/by means of) (d:tawn, go by way of, with the ending a; tung tawna, that came through a person, placed before a noun) (e:na nasem kamsangte tung ~ kote zuih dinga) (b:tawn) (r:27.9.10/24.37.2) (q:draft)
tawngnungah = (t:adv) (w:in the innermost part/into the inner part) (d:tawngnung, innermost part, with the place ending ah) (e:thong sung ~ amaute koihin) (b:tawngnung) (r:44.16.24/26.41.3) (q:draft)
tawnna = (t:n) (w:threat/rebuke) (d:tawn, threaten, with the noun ending na) (e:~ tawh mi tulkhat tai-in) (b:tawn) (r:23.30.17/19.38.14) (q:draft)
tawntungnate = (t:n) (d:tawntungna, lasting for ever, with plural te; after a verb it names things that last for ever, as nop tawntungnate, eternal pleasures, and thukhen tawntungnate, eternal judgments) (e:na tak lam ah nop ~ om hi) (b:tawntungna) (r:19.16.11/58.6.1) (q:draft)
tawntungpa = (t:n) (d:tawntung, always, with pa, the man who; after a verb, the man who keeps doing it, as hong nawk tawntungpa, the man who often passes by) (e:hih i lampi hong nawk ~ in) (b:tawntung) (r:12.4.9/66.12.10) (q:draft)
tawntungte = (t:n) (d:tawntung, always, with plural te; after a verb, those who always do it, as Topa a zahtak tawntungte, those who always fear the Lord) (e:Topa a zahtak ~ pen mi nuamsa hi) (b:tawntung) (r:20.28.14/13.28.1) (q:draft)
tawpkhakna = (t:n) (w:end/conclusion/last) (d:the very end of a matter; a tawpkhakna-ah, at last, in the end, and a tawpkhakna kam in, finally) (e:A ~ kam in, note khempeuh) (r:60.3.8/27.5.21) (q:draft)
tawpsak = (t:v) (w:stop/bring to an end/dismiss) (d:tawp, stop, with sak, cause: make work stop, or put someone out of his work) (e:ka nasepna panin hong ~ ding ahih manin) (b:tawp) (r:42.16.3/14.16.5) (q:draft)
tawptawp = (t:v) (w:kiss) (d:tawp, kiss, said twice: kiss again and again) (e:Na muk tawh nong ~ a) (r:22.1.2/22.8.1) (q:draft)
tawte = (t:n) (w:bottoms/depths/beds) (d:plural of taw, bottom; tuipi tawte, the bed of the sea) (e:tuipi ~ kimu a) (b:taw) (r:10.22.16) (q:draft)
tawte = (t:n) (w:the blind) (d:taw, blind, with plural te: a mit a tawte, those whose eyes are blind) (e:a mit a ~, bil nei napi-in) (b:taw) (r:23.43.8) (q:draft)
teekta = (t:adj) (w:old/aged) (d:teek, old, with ta, showing a state now reached: be old by now) (e:Kei ka ~ a, ka zi zong) (b:teek) (r:42.1.18/12.4.14) (q:draft)
teelkhiatna = (t:n) (w:election/choosing/selection) (d:teelkhiat, choose out, with the noun ending na) (e:kei hong ~ thu na thei uh hi) (b:teelkhiat) (r:44.15.7/45.11.28) (q:draft)
tehnate = (t:n) (w:measures/scales/balances) (d:plural of tehna, a thing or standard for measuring length, weight or amount) (e:A man tawikhaina le tawi ~ Topa) (b:tehna) (r:20.16.11/3.19.35) (q:draft)
tehno = (t:n) (w:young leaf/sprout/shoot/blade) (d:teh, leaf, with no, young: the first new leaves of a plant) (e:A ~ na muh uh ciangin khuakhal) (b:teh) (r:42.21.30/41.4.28) (q:draft)
tehzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to measure) (d:teh, measure, with zawh, be able; in the verses always tehzawh loh, that cannot be measured) (e:le ~ lohin sumngo le sik ka koih) (r:13.22.14/11.4.29) (q:draft)
teikhawh = (t:n) (w:javelin) (d:a light throwing spear, named beside teipi, the spear) (e:Namsau, teipi, le ~ tawh kei kiangah) (r:9.17.45/9.17.6) (q:draft)
telkheh = (t:v) (w:make plain/make clear/expose) (d:set a matter out openly so that it is clearly understood) (e:pawlkhatte-ah kong ~ mahmah hi) (r:45.15.15/46.4.5) (q:draft)
telthei = (t:v) (w:be able to understand/can understand) (d:tel, understand, with thei, be able) (e:leh thu ~ ding a kikhawm khempeuh) (b:tel) (r:16.8.2/41.8.17) (q:draft)
ten'pihna = (t:n) (w:marrying/marriage) (d:ten, dwell, with pih, together with, and the noun ending na: the taking of a woman to live with as wife) (e:teng gamdang numeite ~ tawh) (r:15.10.2/16.13.23) (q:draft)
tengsakkik = (t:v) (w:settle again/make dwell again) (d:tengsak, cause to live, with kik, again) (e:puanbuk sungah note kong ~ ding hi) (b:tengsak) (r:28.12.9/26.37.14) (q:draft)
tennasa = (t:n) (w:former dwelling/place once lived in) (d:tenna, dwelling place, with sa, already done: the place where one has lived) (e:Na ~ Zion Mual hong phawk in) (b:tenna) (r:19.74.2/18.18.19) (q:draft)
tentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to dwell/be able to live) (d:ten, dwell, with theih, be able; na tentheih nadingun, so that you may live) (e:sawtveipi na ~ nadingun) (b:ten) (r:24.35.7/5.30.20) (q:draft)
tep = (t:v) (w:sap/drain/consume) (d:in tep tum, use up completely, said of foreigners who eat away a people's strength) (e:a thahatna teng uh ~ tum a) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tep = (t:v) (w:join/couple) (d:in tep nadingin singte, timber for the joists or couplings that hold a building together) (e:~ nadingin singte) (r:14.34.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
thadahna = (t:n) (w:laziness/sloth/idleness) (e:Note khempeuh in ~ nei loin) (b:thadah) (r:58.6.11/20.10.4) (q:draft)
thadimsak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/refresh/invigorate) (d:thadim, be full of strength, with sak, cause) (e:epel gah tawh hong ~ in) (b:thadim) (r:22.2.5/38.9.17) (q:draft)
thagolte = (t:n) (w:giants) (d:plural of thagol, big and strong; mi thagolte, the giants, where the NIV has the name Rapha) (e:mi ~ sung panin apiang ahi hi) (r:10.21.20/13.20.6) (q:draft)
thahatpente = (t:n) (w:the strongest/the mightiest) (d:thahatpen, strongest, with plural te; galkap thahatpente, the best troops) (e:galkap ~ a thaneem ding uh hi) (r:27.11.15/25.1.15) (q:draft)
thahloh = (t:v) (w:not kill) (d:thah, kill, with loh, not; thahloh nading, so as not to kill) (e:mi na ~ nading le nangma khut tawh) (r:9.25.26/11.1.51) (q:draft)
thaksuaksak = (t:v) (w:renew/make new/refresh) (d:thaksuak, become new, with sak, cause) (e:kicing a, nuntakna a ~ hi) (b:thaksuak) (r:19.19.7/26.18.31) (q:draft)
thalawhin = (t:v) (w:work for/earn) (d:thalawh, work to earn something, with the linking ending in: working for it, and so) (e:zi khat ~ na sem a) (b:thalawh) (r:28.12.12/49.4.28) (q:draft)
thalawhna = (t:n) (w:earning/work done to earn) (d:thalawh, work to earn something, with the noun ending na: what one does to earn a thing) (e:~ hangin a ngah hi loin) (b:thalawh) (r:49.2.8/28.12.12) (q:draft)
thalpaih = (t:v) (w:throw down/cast down/hurl) (d:fling away with force, as an army into the sea) (e:San Tuipi sungah a ~ pa tungah) (r:19.136.15/19.17.13) (q:draft)
thalpeu = (t:n) (w:bow) (d:the bow that shoots arrows, from thal bow; thalpeu tel in Hosea 7:16 is a faulty bow) (e:A leii uh ~ bangin zang uh a) (r:24.9.3/28.7.16) (q:draft)
thaltawi = (t:v) (w:wield a bow/handle a bow) (d:thal bow with tawi hold: carry and use a bow; thaltawi siam and thaltawi theite are archers) (e:~ theite va sam un) (r:24.50.29/23.21.17) (q:draft)
thaneemte = (t:n) (w:the weak/weak ones) (d:thaneem weak with the plural te: those who are weak; lungsim thaneemte is weak consciences) (e:mi ~ a hong teel hi) (b:thaneem) (r:46.1.27/9.2.4) (q:draft)
thangna = (t:n) (d:thang, the second part of theh thang scatter abroad and kikhen thang be split apart, with the noun suffix na: theh thangna mun is the place to which people were scattered, kikhen thangna thu the report of being divided) (e:a kitheh ~ mun khempeuh panin) (r:24.40.12/46.11.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
thangsiahin = (t:v) (w:trapping/ensnaring/setting a trap) (d:thangsiah set a trap, with the linking ending in: by setting traps, trapping and then) (e:mite ~ a man uh hi) (b:thangsiah) (r:24.5.26/42.11.54) (q:draft)
thanuam = (t:adj) (w:diligent/eager/willing) (d:glad to work, the opposite of thadah lazy; thanuam takin is eagerly, lungsim thanuam sak is encourage) (e:~ takin nasem hi) (r:20.31.13/44.15.32) (q:draft)
thanuamte = (t:n) (w:the diligent/diligent ones) (d:thanuam diligent with the plural te, set against thadahte the lazy) (e:Mi ~ vanglian a) (b:thanuam) (r:20.12.24/20.12.27) (q:draft)
thatkha = (t:v) (w:kill accidentally/happen to kill) (d:that kill with kha, which shows that the act comes to happen or reaches its object: kill someone without intending it; thatkha lo is did not get to kill) (e:sawm lopi-in mi khatpeuh a ~) (r:4.35.11/5.19.3) (q:draft)
thawhsakkik = (t:v) (w:raise again/raise up/bring back to life) (d:thawhsak cause to rise with kik again: raise someone from death) (e:sihna panin a ~ Lazaras zong) (r:43.12.9/52.1.10) (q:draft)
thawi = (t:v) (w:search/rummage through/ransack) (d:go through a house or belongings looking for something) (e:Ka van khempeuh na ~ khit hangin) (r:1.31.37/11.20.6) (q:draft)
theemsak = (t:v) (w:scorch/blast/wither) (d:theem thin with the causative sak: of the east wind, make ears of grain thin and dried up) (e:nisuahna huih in a ~ a hawm vui) (r:1.41.6/1.41.27) (q:draft)
thehna = (t:n) (w:sprinkling/splashing) (d:theh sprinkle with the noun suffix na: the act of sprinkling blood) (e:sisan tawh ~ a ngah nading) (b:theh) (r:60.1.1/26.43.18) (q:draft)
theihkhiat = (t:v) (w:find out/discover/fathom) (d:theih know with khiat out: come to know by searching, used before a noun or zawh) (e:kuama ~ zawh loh na lian tampi) (b:theih) (r:18.9.10/21.7.29) (q:draft)
theihkhit = (t:v) (w:have come to know/know fully/finish learning) (d:theih know with khit, finished: theihkhit ciangin is after one has come to know, theihkhit phetin as soon as one knows) (e:Keima pianzia ding ka ~ phetin) (r:50.2.23/42.6.40) (q:draft)
theikim = (t:v) (w:all know/know fully) (d:thei know with kim all: said of everyone knowing a thing, or of knowing the whole of it) (e:mi khempeuh in hih thu ~ lo uh hi) (r:46.8.7/44.16.3) (q:draft)
theimoh = (t:n) (w:fig cake/cake of pressed figs) (d:thei fig with moh cake: figs pressed into a lump) (e:~ khat le leenggahkeu bawk nih) (r:9.30.12/9.25.18) (q:draft)
theipah = (t:v) (w:know at once/recognize immediately) (d:thei know with pah at once) (e:Jesuh ahihlam a ~ uh hi) (r:41.6.54/41.2.8) (q:draft)
theipah = (t:v) (w:be able at once) (d:thei can with pah at once, after a verb: khua mukik theipah is was able to see again immediately) (e:amah in khua mukik ~ a) (r:41.10.52) (q:draft)
theipal = (t:n) (w:early fig/first-ripe fig) (d:a fig that is ripe before the main season, from thei fig) (e:tuk tun ma-in a om ~ min tawh) (r:23.28.4/26.27.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
theisakkik = (t:v) (w:make able again/enable again) (d:thei can with the causative sak and kik again, after a verb: pau theisakkik is make able to speak again, khua mu theisakkik make able to see again) (e:kua in khua mu ~ hiam) (r:43.9.21/26.3.27) (q:draft)
theizaw = (t:v) (w:know better/know more) (d:thei know with zaw more) (e:Nangmah in na ~ ding hi) (b:thei) (r:66.7.14) (q:draft)
theizaw = (t:v) (w:be more able) (d:thei can with zaw more, after a verb: able to do it more than others, or all the more able) (e:pau lamdang pau ~ ka hih manin) (b:thei) (r:46.14.18/58.9.14) (q:draft)
thenli = (t:num) (w:forty thousand) (d:then ten thousand with li four; sangkhat leh thenli leh tulli is 144,000) (e:sangkhat leh ~ leh tulli ahi hi) (r:66.7.4/66.14.1) (q:draft)
thokhia = (t:v) (w:get up/rise up) (d:tho rise with khia out: get up out of bed or sleep) (e:cik ciangin ~ ding na hi hiam) (b:tho) (r:20.6.9/42.11.7) (q:draft)
thokikzo = (t:v) (w:be able to rise again/get up again) (d:thokik rise again with zo be able; in the verses always negated, thokikzo nawn lo, never able to rise again) (e:A lupna panin ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:thokik) (r:19.41.8/23.24.20) (q:draft)
thuahte = (t:n) (w:additional gifts/special gifts) (d:thuah in addition with the plural te, in piak thuahte: the things given on top of the tithe) (e:sawm-ah-khat le na piak ~ uh) (b:thuah) (r:5.12.6/5.12.17) (q:draft)
thuakkhak = (t:v) (w:suffer/undergo/incur) (d:form of thuakkha used before ding and loh nading: come to suffer something bad) (e:Pasian’ thukhenna na ~ loh nadingun) (b:thuakkha) (r:59.5.12/61.3.9) (q:draft)
thuapna = (t:n) (w:patch/patching) (d:thuap put on as a further layer, with the noun suffix na: the piece put on, or the act of patching; thuapna puan is the patch) (e:a ~ puanthak in puanlui keeksakin) (b:thuap) (r:41.2.21/42.5.36) (q:draft)
thuciamin = (t:v) (w:promising/vowing) (d:thuciam promise with the linking ending in: making a promise, having promised) (e:Topa aw, ama tungah ~) (b:thuciam) (r:14.6.16/39.2.14) (q:draft)
thugenkholh = (t:n) (w:prophecy/prediction) (d:thu word with genkholh tell beforehand: what is spoken beforehand) (e:Oded’ tapa Azariah’ ~) (r:14.15.8/61.1.21) (q:draft)
thugenpa = (t:n) (w:speaker/the one who speaks) (d:thugen speak with pa marking a man: the man who is speaking or who spoke) (e:Hihnu kiangah ~ nang na hi hiam) (b:thugen) (r:7.13.11/18.36.4) (q:draft)
thuh = (t:v) (w:seal/stamp) (d:press a seal or signet on a document) (e:kumpipa’ minthuhna zungbuh tawh ~ in) (r:17.8.8) (q:draft)
thuh = (t:v) (w:repay/avenge) (d:in thuh kikna, repayment or vengeance; the same as thuhkik pay back a wrong) (e:amaute na ~ kikna hong musak in) (r:24.20.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
thukanin = (t:adv) (w:as spies/as a spy/to spy) (d:thukan spy with the marker in: in the role of spies) (e:tua gam ~ kote hong ngaihsun hi) (b:thukan) (r:1.42.30/6.2.1) (q:draft)
thukhamnate = (t:n) (w:laws/statutes/decrees) (d:thukhamna law with the plural te; paired with thupiaknate, commands) (e:ka thupiaknate leh ka ~ a zui) (b:thukhamna) (r:11.11.34/11.9.6) (q:draft)
thukhauh = (t:adj) (w:harsh/severe/fierce) (d:thu word, matter with khauh hard: stern in what one says or orders; thukhauh pa is a harsh man, a tyrant; in Daniel 2:15 a harsh decree) (e:~ pa’ mat mite kihonkhia zo ding) (r:23.49.24/27.2.15) (q:draft)
thukihilhna = (t:n) (w:discipline/correction/instruction) (d:being taught or corrected, from thuhilh teach, discipline, with ki and the noun suffix na) (e:~ a zui lo mi in) (r:20.13.18/20.15.10) (q:draft)
thukip = (t:n) (w:firm word/sure word/decree) (d:thu word with kip firm: a word or ruling that stands and is not changed) (e:a kikhelkik ngei nawn lo ding ~) (r:23.45.23/19.18.22) (q:draft)
thuknate = (t:n) (w:depths/deeps/deep places) (d:thukna depth with the plural te; lei thuknate is the depths of the earth) (e:Lei ~ aw, awng un) (b:thukna) (r:23.44.23/5.33.13) (q:draft)
thukzawk = (t:adj) (w:deeper) (d:form of thukzaw, deeper, used before kei and leh; a vun sangin a thukzawk leh means if it is deeper than the skin) (e:a vun sangin a ~ kei a) (b:thukzaw) (r:3.13.21/3.13.25) (q:draft)
thumantak = (t:n) (w:honesty/integrity/good faith) (d:thuman right, true with tak real: true uprightness; lungsimtak le thumantak tawh is sincerely and honourably) (e:lungsimtak le ~ mah tawh a gamta) (b:thuman) (r:7.9.16/1.47.29) (q:draft)
thumthum = (t:v) (w:plead/beg earnestly/keep asking) (d:thum beg, doubled to show that the asking is repeated or urgent) (e:A sun a zanin ama tungah a ~) (r:42.18.7/47.8.4) (q:draft)
thumthum = (t:v) (w:moan/coo) (d:of doves, make a low mournful sound) (e:vakhu bangin i ~ hi) (r:23.59.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
thungaihna = (t:n) (w:obedience) (d:thungaih obey, listen with the noun suffix na; in Hebrews 5:7 thungaihna ngah is be heard, receive a hearing) (e:Note ~ in a kicin’ khit ciangin) (b:thungaih) (r:47.10.6/60.1.1) (q:draft)
thupiaksate = (t:n) (w:commands/things commanded/instructions) (d:thupiaksa what has been commanded, with the plural te) (e:Pasian’ nasem Moses’ ~ khempeuh bangin) (b:thupiaksa) (r:13.6.49/54.5.7) (q:draft)
thusimna = (t:n) (w:respect/esteem/regard) (d:thusim be mindful of, with the noun suffix na: the regard shown to someone) (e:mi’ hong ~ deihhuai zaw hi) (b:thusim) (r:20.22.1/60.3.15) (q:draft)
thutakte = (t:n) (w:truths/true things) (d:thutak truth with the plural te, often in the pair thuman thutakte) (e:i zaksa thuman ~) (b:thutak) (r:58.2.1/49.5.9) (q:draft)
thutawpna = (t:n) (w:end/final outcome/destiny/fate) (d:thu matter with tawpna end: how things end for someone) (e:a ~ uh a vekpi-in kibang lel hi) (r:21.9.2/19.73.17) (q:draft)
thutheihte = (t:n) (w:knowledge/things known/learning) (d:thu matter with theih know and the plural te: the things one knows) (e:amau’ ~ haina a suaksak pa) (r:23.44.25/18.15.17) (q:draft)
thuzak = (t:n) (w:news/report/what is heard) (d:thu word with zak hear: the thing heard, a message or news) (e:Mihaite in a ~ peuh um pahpah a) (r:20.14.15/58.4.2) (q:draft)
tokhomah = (t:n) (w:on the throne/to the throne) (d:tokhom throne with the place marker ah) (e:Israel kumpi ~ kong tu a) (b:tokhom) (r:14.6.10/66.3.21) (q:draft)
tolhkhia = (t:v) (w:slip off/drop off/come out) (d:tolh slip out with khia out: of bonds falling from the hands, of bowels coming out of the body) (e:a kikhihnate a khut panin ~ hi) (b:tolh) (r:7.15.14/14.21.19) (q:draft)
tomna = (t:n) (w:shortness/brevity) (d:tom short with the noun suffix na: the fact of being short in time) (e:migilote’ nopsak hun a ~ thu) (b:tom) (r:18.20.5) (q:draft)
tomna = (t:n) (w:nest building) (d:tom gather, in bu tom build a nest, with the noun suffix na; bu a tomna ding is that it should build its nest) (e:mualtungah bu a ~ ding) (b:tom) (r:18.39.27) (q:draft)
tomsak = (t:v) (w:shorten/cut short) (d:tom short with the causative sak) (e:Topa in tua nite a ~ kei leh) (b:tom) (r:41.13.20/19.89.45) (q:draft)
tosak = (t:v) (w:strengthen/make firm) (d:of the bars of a gate: make strong and lasting) (e:na kulh kongpi zawlte ~ a) (r:19.147.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
tosak = (t:v) (w:send up/cause to go up) (d:to upward with the causative sak, after a verb of movement: paikhia tosak is make someone go up out of a place) (e:kote hong paikhia ~ kei in) (b:to) (r:2.33.15) (q:draft)
tuanthu = (t:n) (w:old story/ancient record/tradition) (d:an account handed down from former times; paired with tangthu story as tangthu tuanthu, traditions) (e:Hih pen ~ lui pekpek ahi hi) (r:13.4.22/51.2.8) (q:draft)
tuibuahna = (t:n) (w:drink offering/libation) (d:tuibuah drink offering with the noun suffix na: the pouring out of a drink offering; tuibuahna thawl is a jar for drink offerings) (e:~ dinga kizang keute zong) (b:tuibuah) (r:24.52.19/4.4.7) (q:draft)
tuidawk = (t:n) (w:bay/inlet) (d:tui water with dawk jut out: a part of the sea that reaches into the land) (e:~ le a gei-a leilak mu uh a) (r:44.27.39/6.15.2) (q:draft)
tuihupna = (t:n) (w:sponge) (d:tui water with hup soak up and the noun suffix na: a thing that soaks up liquid) (e:leenggahzu-hau sungah ~ diahin) (r:41.15.36/43.19.29) (q:draft)
tuikhuka = (t:n) (w:at the well/at the spring/in the cistern) (d:tuikhuk well with the marker a, at or of: that is at the well) (e:~ mipa kiangah a tai hi) (b:tuikhuk) (r:1.24.29/23.30.14) (q:draft)
tuikhukpi = (t:n) (w:reservoir/pool/great pool) (d:tuikhuk well, cistern with pi great: a large made pool of water) (e:Gibeon ~ a tun uh ciangin) (b:tuikhuk) (r:24.41.12/21.2.6) (q:draft)
tuilim = (t:n) (w:fresh water/sweet water/sweet drink) (d:tui water with lim tasty: water good to drink, set against tuikha bitter water and tui-al salt water; anlim tuilim is good food and drink) (e:Tui-al in ~ piangsak ngei lo hi) (r:59.3.12/16.8.10) (q:draft)
tuimang = (t:v) (w:melt away/dissolve/waste away) (d:tui water, liquid with mang vanish: turn to liquid and disappear) (e:vantung nate sa lua-in a ~ ding) (r:61.3.12/19.112.10) (q:draft)
tuinakah = (t:n) (w:to the spring/at the spring) (d:tuinak spring with the place marker ah) (e:Tua ciangin ~ amah pai-in) (b:tuinak) (r:12.2.21/18.38.16) (q:draft)
tuipeek = (t:v) (w:swim) (d:tui water with peek swim; tuipeekpa is a swimmer) (e:~ thei khempeuh in teembaw panin) (r:44.27.43/23.25.11) (q:draft)
tuisak = (t:v) (w:melt) (d:tui water, liquid with the causative sak: make ice or metal turn to liquid) (e:Amah in thupia-in tuate ~ hi) (b:tui) (r:19.147.18/26.22.20) (q:draft)
tuithukpite = (t:n) (w:the deeps/great depths/deep waters) (d:tuithukpi the great deep with the plural te: the deep waters of the sea) (e:~ tuibeem-ah a koih hi) (r:19.33.7/23.51.10) (q:draft)
tuithukte = (t:n) (w:deep waters/depths/deeps) (d:tuithuk deep water with the plural te) (e:Nail gun ~ kangcip ding hi) (b:tuithuk) (r:38.10.11/19.69.14) (q:draft)
tulsawmnih = (t:num) (w:twenty thousand) (d:tul thousand with sawmnih twenty) (e:mi ~ ahi hi) (r:10.18.7/10.8.5) (q:draft)
tumasiah = (t:adv) (w:before/formerly/in the past) (d:tuma before now with siah: in the time up to now; tumasiah-a bangin is as before) (e:~-a a leiseek bawlzah mah uh) (r:2.5.8/2.4.10) (q:draft)
tumdang = (t:adj) (w:strange/unusual/extraordinary) (d:different from the ordinary; paired with lamdang, strange, wonderful) (e:a ~ ama nasep sem dingin) (r:23.28.21/23.29.14) (q:draft)
tumkhit = (t:v) (w:have gone in/have entered) (d:tum go in with khit, finished: innsungah a tumkhit ciangin is after he had gone into the house) (e:Innsungah Jesuh a ~ ciangin) (r:41.9.28/41.10.10) (q:draft)
tumkhit = (t:v) (w:have set) (d:of the sun, tum go down with khit, finished: ni a tumkhit ciangin is after sunset) (e:Ni a ~ ciangin) (r:42.4.40) (q:draft)
tumpa = (t:n) (w:striker/the one who struck) (d:tum strike with the fist, with pa marking a man: the man who struck the blow) (e:tua a ~ kithat ding hi) (r:4.35.21/2.21.19) (q:draft)
tumpa = (t:n) (w:trumpeter/player) (d:tum play or sound an instrument, with pa marking a man: peengkul tumpa is the man who sounds the trumpet) (e:Peengkul ~ ahih leh keima kiangah om hi) (b:tum) (r:16.4.18) (q:draft)
tumtakin = (t:adv) (w:complacently/self-contentedly) (d:in nomau’ tumtakin a lungkim, said of women who feel secure and are satisfied with themselves; the part tum is not clear) (e:Nomau’ ~ a lungkim numeite aw) (r:23.32.10/23.32.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
tungkhuhna = (t:n) (w:covering/roof/canopy) (d:tungkhuh cover over with the noun suffix na: what covers something from above) (e:Biakbuk tungah a ~ zal a) (r:2.40.19/11.7.6) (q:draft)
tungsiahte = (t:n) (w:those above/those older) (d:tungsiah upward with the plural te: the people from a stated age upward) (e:Kum sawmguk pan a ~ pen) (b:tungsiah) (r:3.27.7/14.31.17) (q:draft)
tungthama = (t:adj) (w:outward/superficial/on the surface) (d:tungtham surface with the marker a: that is only on the outside; tungthama phatna is flattery, a tungthama kimu nate outward appearances) (e:A ~ kimu nate siksanin) (b:tungtham) (r:43.7.24/20.28.23) (q:draft)
tungto = (t:v) (w:come up/go up/arrive up) (d:tung arrive with to upward: reach a place by going up) (e:Babylon panin hong ~ hi) (b:tung) (r:15.7.6/66.8.4) (q:draft)
tungvat = (t:v) (w:come suddenly/arrive suddenly) (d:tung arrive, come upon, with vat suddenly) (e:amaute tungah siatna hong ~ ding hi) (r:52.5.3/44.2.2) (q:draft)
tunkhitna = (t:n) (w:arrival/having arrived) (d:tunkhit have arrived with the noun suffix na: the fact that someone or something has arrived; tunkhitna thu is the news that one has come) (e:Keilah-ah David a ~ thu) (r:9.23.7/44.21.22) (q:draft)
tunpihin = (t:v) (w:bringing/bringing to/having brought) (d:tunpih bring to a place, with the linking ending in: brought and then) (e:Amah in hih mun hong ~) (b:tunpih) (r:5.26.9/9.31.12) (q:draft)
tunzawh = (t:v) (w:have arrived/manage to reach) (d:tun arrive with zawh, form of zo, finish, be able: tunzawh ni thum ciangin is three days after arriving, tunzawh nading so as to manage to reach) (e:Festas hong ~ ni thum ciangin) (r:44.25.1/44.27.12) (q:draft)
tutnasa = (t:n) (w:place sat on/former seat) (d:tutna seat with sa, already: the thing or place where someone has been sitting) (e:annek sabuai-ah a ~ mun hong zuanin) (b:tutna) (r:43.13.12/3.15.6) (q:draft)
tutphahte = (t:n) (w:seats/benches) (d:tutphah seat with the plural te) (e:vakhu zuakte’ ~ sawnpaih sak hi) (b:tutphah) (r:41.11.15/40.21.12) (q:draft)
tutpih = (t:v) (w:sit with/sit together with) (d:tut sit with pih, together with: a tutpih mite are those who sit with him) (e:An ne-a a ~ mite khat in) (b:tut) (r:42.14.15/44.26.30) (q:draft)
tutu = (t:v) (w:keep sitting/sit on and on) (d:tu sit, doubled to show that the sitting goes on or is habitual) (e:Bang hangin ~ lai i hi hiam) (r:24.8.14/43.9.8) (q:draft)
tuuhonpi = (t:n) (w:great flock/large flock of sheep) (d:tuuhon flock of sheep with pi great) (e:~ bangin Israel mite ka tamsak ding hi) (b:tuuhon) (r:26.36.37/26.36.38) (q:draft)
tuukhumna = (t:n) (w:sheep pen/sheepfold) (d:tuu sheep with khum shut in and the noun suffix na: the place where sheep are shut in) (e:Hih ~ sunga om lo tuute) (r:43.10.16/43.10.1) (q:draft)
tuummang = (t:v) (w:engulf/swallow up/submerge) (d:tuum cover over with mang, out of sight: of water covering something so that it is lost; also sink and be lost in the sea) (e:Tui in amau’ langte ~ khin a) (r:19.106.11/26.27.27) (q:draft)
tuumsak = (t:v) (w:cover/cause to cover/overwhelm) (d:tuum cover over with the causative sak: make water cover and bury someone) (e:tuipi luangsakin amaute ka ~ hi) (b:tuum) (r:6.24.7/2.15.19) (q:draft)
tuununo = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:ewe lamb) (d:tuu sheep with nu female and no young: a young female sheep) (e:Hih na koihtuam ~ sagihte) (r:1.21.29/1.21.28) (q:draft)
uap = (t:v) (w:accompany/attend/escort) (d:go with or go out to someone as a companion, as the friends who attend a bridegroom) (e:amah a ~ dingin tangval sawmthum) (r:7.14.11/40.25.1) (q:draft)
uhteh = (t:part) (d:in le uhteh, also written le-uhteh, placed after a verb: if you do, when you do, said to several people; uh marks the plural and le with teh the condition) (e:Amau gah en le ~) (r:40.7.16/41.11.3) (q:draft)
uihna = (t:n) (w:stench/stink/bad smell) (d:uih stink with the noun suffix na) (e:Paknamtui tangin ~) (b:uih) (r:23.3.24/30.4.10) (q:draft)
uili = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:flea) (e:~ bang lel keimah a that dingin) (r:9.26.20/9.24.14) (q:draft)
uiphuk = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:frog) (e:~ tawh a kibang kha gilo thum) (r:66.16.13/2.8.12) (q:draft)
ukcip = (t:v) (w:subdue/control completely/hold in one's power) (d:uk rule with cip tightly: bring fully under one's rule or power) (e:~ dingin na hanciam uh mite) (b:uk) (r:26.13.20/24.27.8) (q:draft)
ulianin = (t:n) (w:as ruler/as prince/as leader) (d:ulian ruler, official with the marker in: into or in the position of a ruler, after bawl make or koih appoint) (e:Israel-te tungah ~ nang hong koih) (b:ulian) (r:9.25.30/19.113.8) (q:draft)
ulianpi = (t:n) (w:great official/great man/high official) (d:ulian official with pi great: a man of high rank) (e:kumpipa’ maipha a ngah ~ khat ahi hi) (b:ulian) (r:12.5.1/17.9.4) (q:draft)
upapen = (t:adj) (w:eldest/oldest/firstborn) (d:upa elder with pen most: the oldest of the brothers or sons) (e:ama u a ~ Eliab in za hi) (b:upa) (r:9.17.28/9.17.14) (q:draft)
uplahna = (t:n) (w:doubt/unbelief) (d:the state of doubting or not believing, the opposite of upna faith; uplahna lungsim is an unbelieving heart) (e:Note in ~ nei hetloin) (r:40.21.21/41.11.23) (q:draft)
utbang = (t:n) (w:what one wants/own wish/own way) (d:ut wish with bang as: as one likes; a utbang peuhin gamta is do just as he pleases) (e:A ~ peuhin gamta ding a) (r:27.11.28/44.14.16) (q:draft)
utok = (t:n) (w:lobe of the liver) (d:the lobe attached to the liver of a sacrificed animal, in a sin tunga a utok) (e:a sin tunga a ~ le a kal nihte) (r:2.29.13/2.29.22) (q:draft)
uumcip = (t:v) (w:surround/besiege/hem in) (d:uum surround with cip tightly: close in on all sides) (e:Jerusalem khuapi galkapte in a ~) (b:uum) (r:42.21.20/42.19.43) (q:draft)
vaakna = (t:n) (w:feeding/provision of food/sustenance) (d:vaak, feed, with the noun suffix na: the act of feeding or supplying someone with food; vaakna ngah is to be fed, to be filled) (e:amau in ~ a ngah ding uh hi) (b:vaak) (r:40.5.6/11.18.13) (q:draft)
vaaksak = (t:v) (w:light up/give light to/make bright) (d:vaak, be bright, with the causative sak: turn darkness into light, give light to the eyes) (e:ka khuamial na ~ hi) (b:vaak) (r:19.18.28/19.19.8) (q:draft)
vaang = (t:n) (w:might/power/strength) (d:written with a long vowel; the same word as vang, power) (e:na ~ tawh ka dikna kilangsak in) (r:19.54.1/23.36.5) (q:draft)
vakthap = (t:v) (w:wander/roam/go about) (d:go about from place to place; in 2 Thessalonians 3:11 of idle people who go about meddling in the affairs of others) (e:Gamla pekah ka ~ ding a) (r:19.55.7/53.3.11) (q:draft)
valteng = (t:n) (w:rest/remainder/what is left) (d:val, be left over, with teng, all of: all that remains after a part is taken) (e:An tawh biakna a ~ pen) (b:val) (r:3.2.10/27.7.7) (q:draft)
vanglianin = (t:adv) (w:powerfully/mightily/with power) (d:vanglian, mighty, with the ending in: being mighty, in a mighty way) (e:thungetna in nakpi ~ muibun mahmah hi) (b:vanglian) (r:59.5.16/19.112.9) (q:draft)
vanglianpi = (t:n) (w:great power/might/majesty) (d:vanglian, mighty, with pi, great: vanglianpi tawh is with great power; in Hebrews 8:1 the Majesty in heaven) (e:~ tawh Pasian’ Ukna hong tung) (b:vanglian) (r:41.9.1/58.8.1) (q:draft)
vankoihnate = (t:n) (w:storehouses/storerooms/treasuries) (d:vankoihna, storehouse, with the plural te) (e:sathau koihna ding ~ zong a bawl hi) (b:vankoihna) (r:14.32.28/12.18.15) (q:draft)
vatmaipa = (t:n) (w:one who struck down/slayer) (d:vatmai, strike down, with pa, the male one who does it: a vatmaipa is he who struck down) (e:Kumpi liante a ~ tungah) (b:vatmai) (r:19.136.17/19.136.10) (q:draft)
veengah = (t:n) (w:in the quarter/in the neighbourhood) (d:veeng, a quarter or neighbourhood of a town, with the place marker ah, in or to: Naioth veengah is in Naioth, a quarter of Ramah; veeng is the long-vowel spelling of veng) (e:Ramah khua sung Naioth ~ David om hi) (r:9.19.19/9.19.23) (q:draft)
veilama = (t:n) (w:on the left/at the left side) (d:veilam, left side, with the place ending a, at or on: ka veilama is on my left) (e:A ~ omte ne uh a) (b:veilam) (r:23.9.20/41.10.40) (q:draft)
vekun = (t:adv) (w:all/all of them/altogether) (d:used as a vekun, all of them together, with a plural subject) (e:a ~ sal suak khin uh hi) (r:24.13.19/26.39.23) (q:draft)
vengah = (t:n) (w:in the quarter/in the neighbourhood) (d:veng, a quarter or neighbourhood of a town, with the place marker ah, in or to: Naioth vengah is in Naioth, a quarter of Ramah) (e:Ramah khuasung Naioth ~ om uh hi) (b:veng) (r:9.19.22/9.19.19) (q:draft)
vialcip = (t:v) (w:wrap around/wrap up/enfold) (d:vial, bind around, with cip, tightly: wrap closely all round) (e:lopate in ka lu hong ~ hi) (b:vial) (r:32.2.5/18.38.9) (q:draft)
viik = (t:v) (w:brandish/swing/wave) (d:swing a sword or the arm in order to strike; viik suk is swing down) (e:Ka namsau ka ~ ciangin kumpite) (r:26.32.10/23.30.32) (q:draft)
vilpa = (t:n) (w:watchman/sentinel/lookout) (d:vil, watch, with pa, a man who does it; gal vilpa is the man who keeps watch for the enemy) (e:Gal ~ aw, tu zan bangci hiam) (b:vil) (r:23.21.11/23.21.12) (q:draft)
vomin = (t:v) (w:turn black/grow black) (d:vom, black, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb: turning black and then) (e:Ka vun ~ dulhkhia a) (b:vom) (r:18.30.30/66.6.12) (q:draft)
vuak = (t:v) (w:hit/strike/beat) (d:form of vua, strike; in Isaiah 53:4 of one struck by God) (e:Hong ~ hangun ka liam kei a) (b:vua) (r:20.23.35/23.53.4) (q:draft)
vuknelh = (t:v) (w:overwhelm/cover over/surpass/choke) (d:vuk, cover, with nelh, over: cover over completely; in 1 Kings 10:7 wisdom and wealth far exceed the report that was heard, in Matthew 13:22 worries and riches choke the word) (e:in ka zak thute ~ hi) (r:11.10.7/40.13.22) (q:draft)
vulkik = (t:v) (w:wither away/wither) (d:vul, wither, with kik, back: of a plant that has come up, wither and die back) (e:ahih manin a ~ pah hi) (b:vul) (r:42.8.6/18.24.24) (q:draft)
vulsak = (t:v) (w:make wither/blight) (d:vul, wither, with the causative sak: cause plants to wither; mai vulsak is make the face look drawn and gloomy) (e:na mai uh ~ kei un) (b:vul) (r:30.4.9/40.6.16) (q:draft)
zaai = (t:v) (w:spread out/spread wide) (d:of branches, spread out wide; written with a long vowel, the same word as zai, wide) (e:A kung golin a hiangte ~ ahih manin) (r:41.4.32/23.16.8) (q:draft)
zaha = (t:adv) (w:so/such/to that extent) (d:zah, amount, with the linking a, used after hih, tua or bang and before a describing word or a noun: hih zaha tam is so many, bang zaha lian is how great) (e:bang ~ lian kidemna) (b:zah) (r:51.2.1/58.12.1) (q:draft)
zahpihbawl = (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/sneer at/make fun of) (d:zahpih, mock, with bawl, do or treat) (e:Galkapte in zong ~ uh a) (b:zahpih) (r:42.23.36/44.17.32) (q:draft)
zahzahun = (t:adv) (w:as much as/as many as) (d:zahzah, as much as, with the plural ending un, used when the subject is plural: a duh zahzahun is as much as they want) (e:a duh ~ sa ne-in si dawn ding) (b:zahzah) (r:26.39.17/66.19.21) (q:draft)
zakiasak = (t:v) (w:dethrone/depose/remove from office) (d:za, rank or office, with kiasak, cause to fall: bring a ruler down from his position) (e:Amah in kumpite ~ a) (r:18.12.18/14.36.3) (q:draft)
zakkhit = (t:v) (w:have heard/finish hearing) (d:zak, hear, with khit, finished: used before ciangin or phet for after hearing, as soon as one has heard) (e:a cinat a ~ ciangin tua lai-ah) (r:43.11.6/41.4.15) (q:draft)
zalhmai-in = (t:v) (w:level/flatten/make level) (d:zalhmai, make flat and even, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb; zalh is spread flat) (e:leivumte ~, guahtui tawh na nipsak a) (r:19.65.10/23.45.2) (q:draft)
zaliatna = (t:n) (w:high rank/high position/dignity) (d:za, rank, with liatna, greatness: a great office or exalted standing) (e:Amah a ~ panin sukniam ding) (r:19.62.4/27.11.39) (q:draft)
zangkhawm = (t:v) (w:share/use together/have in common) (d:zang, use, with khawm, together) (e:neihsa khempeuh gawmin a ~ uh hi) (b:zang) (r:44.2.44/48.6.6) (q:draft)
zangmang = (t:v) (w:squander/use up/waste) (d:zang, use, with mang, away or lost: use up until it is gone; in Mark 12:40 of consuming the property of widows) (e:numei paktatte tungah ~ khin a) (r:42.15.30/41.12.40) (q:draft)
zangpa = (t:n) (w:user/one who uses) (d:zang, use, with pa, the male one who does it: a zangpa is the one who uses or wields it) (e:Mihai khat kamtai-a a ~ in) (b:zang) (r:20.26.6/23.10.15) (q:draft)
zangthei = (t:v) (w:can use/be able to use) (d:zang, use, with thei, can) (e:a ut bangin ~ nawn loin) (b:zang) (r:46.7.4/54.1.8) (q:draft)
zangzaw = (t:adj) (w:lighter) (d:zang, light in weight, with zaw, more; after sangin, than) (e:a kigawmin husan’ sangin ~ hi) (r:19.62.9) (q:draft)
zangzaw = (t:v) (w:use rather/use instead) (d:zang, use, with zaw, rather: use it for this and not for that) (e:itna tawh khatlekhat kikhualna-in ~ un) (b:zang) (r:48.5.13) (q:draft)
zanihte = (t:num) (w:two hundred) (d:zanih, two hundred, with the plural te, of people: mi zanihte is the two hundred men) (e:A kisam mi ~ Jerusalem panin) (b:zanih) (r:10.15.11/9.30.21) (q:draft)
zanpi = (t:n) (w:night/dead of night) (d:zan, night, with pi, great: zanpi mahin is in the night itself, while it was still night) (e:a nu tawh ~ mahin ding khia) (b:zan) (r:40.2.14/16.2.15) (q:draft)
zapi = (t:adj) (w:wide/spacious/vast) (d:of rooms and of a realm: very wide, of great extent) (e:Amah in gam ~ tak uk ding a) (r:27.11.3/24.22.14) (q:draft)
zasakin = (t:v) (w:report/announce/inform) (d:zasak, make known, with the linking ending in, which joins it to the following verb: thu zasakin is reporting the matter, letting someone hear it) (e:Tua ciangin galvilpa in thu ~) (b:zasak) (r:12.9.18/23.43.9) (q:draft)
zatnate = (t:n) (w:uses/practices) (d:zatna, use, with the plural te: kam kihhuai zatnate is the use of filthy language, tawitehna man lo zatnate the use of false measures) (e:kam kihhuai ~ ahi zongin) (b:zatna) (r:51.3.8/33.6.10) (q:draft)
zawlpeek = (t:n) (w:rim/frame/border) (d:zawl, rim, with peek, flat piece: the flat rim or frame round the top of the table) (e:a ~ gei-ah a kualte om ding hi) (r:2.25.27/2.25.25) (q:draft)
zawnglua = (t:adj) (w:too poor/very poor) (d:zawng, poor, with lua, too or very) (e:~ leuleu leng mi’ na guksakin) (b:zawng) (r:20.30.9/3.27.8) (q:draft)
zeel = (t:v) (w:spread through/fill/pervade) (d:of news or a scent, reach every part of a place; written with a long vowel, the same word as zel) (e:paknamtui in inn sung teng a ~ hi) (r:43.12.3/40.4.24) (q:draft)
zeel = (t:adv) (w:often/repeatedly/regularly) (d:placed after a verb for an action done time after time; written with a long vowel, the same word as zel) (e:an nek ka tang ~ uh hi) (r:40.9.14) (q:draft)
zelzelin = (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly/often) (d:zelzel, repeatedly, with the ending in, placed after a verb) (e:in gam lakah amah lehdo ~) (b:zelzel) (r:19.78.40/19.59.6) (q:draft)
zelzelna = (t:n) (w:frequent occurrence/repeated doing) (d:zelzel, again and again, with the noun suffix na: the fact that something is done or happens many times; na nat mun zelzelna is your frequent illnesses) (e:na nat mun ~ hangin) (b:zelzel) (r:54.5.23/21.7.22) (q:draft)
zepnate = (t:n) (w:ornaments/decorations/overlays) (d:zepna, ornament, with the plural te; khuamlu zepnate are the decorated tops of the posts, overlaid with silver) (e:a khuamlu ~ leh a gaknate) (b:zepna) (r:2.38.19/2.38.28) (q:draft)
ziahziah = (t:adv) (w:freely/generously/liberally) (d:placed after a verb of giving or spending: without holding back) (e:Mi pawlkhat in sum zang ~ napi-in) (r:20.11.24/13.29.9) (q:draft)
ziauziau = (t:adv) (w:readily/lightly/easily) (d:placed after a verb: do something lightly and readily, as changing the mind again and again or bringing out whatever one pleases; exact force not confirmed) (e:na lungsim khel ~ na hi hiam) (r:24.2.36/40.13.52) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziing = (t:n) (w:deep darkness/gloom) (d:paired with khuamial, darkness: khuamial sung leh a ziing sung is darkness and the deepest gloom; written with a long vowel, the same word as zing) (e:khuamial sung leh a ~ sungah tu uh a) (r:19.107.10/19.107.14) (q:draft)
ziing = (t:v) (w:grow dark/be darkened) (d:in khim ziing, darkness falls over a place) (e:na gam khempeuh khim ~ ding hi) (r:26.32.8) (q:draft)
ziinling = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:another spelling of zinling: zin, earthquake, and ling, shake) (e:~ khit ciangin meikuang om a) (r:11.19.12/11.19.11) (q:draft)
zingsol = (t:n) (c:star) (w:morning star) (e:Amaute tungah ~ zong ka pia ding hi) (r:66.2.28/66.22.16) (q:draft)
zinkhia = (t:v) (w:go away on a journey/set out/leave home) (d:zin, travel, with khia, out) (e:Inn panin gamlapi-ah a ~ mipa) (b:zin) (r:20.27.8/40.25.15) (q:draft)
zinlin = (t:n) (w:earthquake) (d:zinling, earthquake, written without the final g and with an apostrophe before ma, before, and before the suffix na) (e:~’ ma kum nih hun laitakin) (r:30.1.1/66.16.18) (q:draft)
zinna = (t:n) (w:journey/travel/travelling) (d:zin, travel, with the noun suffix na; ka zinna khempeuhah is everywhere I travelled) (e:khual gamlapi ~-in paat gawp hi) (b:zin) (r:6.9.13/45.15.18) (q:draft)
zipi = (t:n) (w:wedding/marriage) (d:zi, wife: the taking of a wife; zipi hun is the time of the wedding and zipi pa the bridegroom) (e:Tuuno’ ~ hun a tung zo hi) (b:zi) (r:66.19.7/23.62.5) (q:draft)
zolo = (t:v) (w:cannot/be unable to) (d:zo, be able, with the negative lo, written as one word after a verb: not able to do it) (e:kuamah a damsak ~ zato siam-a kineite) (b:zo) (r:18.13.4/18.12.22) (q:draft)
zomsuak = (t:v) (w:continue/keep on/carry through) (d:zom, continue, with suak, through: go on with something without stopping, carry it through to the end) (e:na ki-itna uh na ~ un) (r:58.13.1/47.8.11) (q:draft)
zomto = (t:v) (w:carry on/continue/keep up) (d:zom, continue, with to, onward: carry on what others began; innkuan zomto is carry on a family line) (e:i pu i pate’ maban ~ vet un) (b:zom) (r:40.23.32/5.25.9) (q:draft)
zongzaw = (t:v) (w:seek rather/seek instead/seek all the more) (d:zong, seek, with zaw, rather or more) (e:midangte’ phattuam nading ~ un) (b:zong) (r:46.10.24/24.38.4) (q:draft)
zontheih = (t:v) (w:be able to seek/can seek) (d:zon, seek, with theih, can, the form used before nading: so that one can seek or find) (e:na min hong ~ nadingin) (b:zon) (r:19.83.16/45.1.20) (q:draft)
zuahzuah = (t:adv) (w:freely/generously/lavishly) (d:placed after a verb of giving or distributing: give out widely without holding back) (e:Amah in hawmkhia ~ a) (r:19.112.9/47.9.9) (q:draft)
zualsak = (t:v) (w:tame/subdue) (d:zual, tame, with the causative sak: make a wild animal tame) (e:kuamah in ~ zo lo) (r:18.39.7/59.3.7) (q:draft)
zuaute = (t:adj) (w:false/lying) (d:zuau, false, with the plural te, placed after a noun: pasian zuaute is false gods, kamsang zuaute is false prophets) (e:tua bangmahin kamsang ~ a pahtakbawl uh hi) (b:zuau) (r:42.6.26/24.14.22) (q:draft)
zuauthute = (t:n) (w:lies/false words/deceptive words) (d:zuauthu, lie, with the plural te) (e:a kicici ~ um kei un) (b:zuauthu) (r:24.7.4/2.5.9) (q:draft)
zuhai = (t:n) (w:drunkard) (d:zu, liquor: one given to heavy drinking; paired with anhai, glutton) (e:amah in anhai ~ ahi hi) (r:5.21.20/42.7.34) (q:draft)
zuihpih = (t:v) (w:follow along with/go along with) (d:zuih, follow, with pih, together with: follow a practice along with others, or go with someone along a path) (e:a phuahtawm ngeinate ~ uh hi) (b:zuih) (r:12.17.19/23.42.16) (q:draft)
zuihsa = (t:v) (w:have followed/have kept) (d:zuih, follow or keep, with sa, already done: what one has already followed or kept) (e:Hihte khempeuh ka ~ ahi hi) (b:zuih) (r:40.19.20/54.4.6) (q:draft)
zuikhin = (t:v) (w:have kept/have fulfilled/keep fully) (d:zui, follow or keep, with khin, completely or already) (e:hih thukhamte khempeuh ka ~ hi) (b:zui) (r:41.10.20/45.13.8) (q:draft)
zuikik = (t:v) (w:go back with/follow back) (d:zui, follow, with kik, back or again: go back with someone; in Daniel 11:20 follow after in turn, succeed) (e:nadingin kei hong ~ in) (b:zui) (r:9.15.30/27.11.20) (q:draft)
zuisuak = (t:v) (w:go on with/keep following/continue in) (d:zui, follow, with suak, through or onward: go along with someone all the way, keep on following) (e:Balaam in Balak’ uliante a ~ hi) (r:4.22.35/59.1.25) (q:draft)
zunek = (t:v) (w:drink liquor/drink wine) (d:form of zune, drink liquor, used before another word: zunek a hatte is those strong at drinking, zunek ding is what is to be drunk) (e:khamtheih ~ a hatte) (b:zune) (r:23.5.22/56.2.3) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:v) (w:take root/be rooted) (d:zung, root, with kha: strike root; also written apart as zung kha) (e:a thuk lamah ~ kikin) (r:12.19.30/49.3.17) (q:draft)
zungkha = (t:n) (w:bitter root) (d:in Hebrews 12:15, zungkha a nei singkung, where the English has a bitter root that grows up; perhaps zung, root, with kha, bitter; not confirmed) (e:~ a nei singkung hong khangin) (r:58.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
AHI = (t:v) (w:is/be) (d:ahi, is, written in capital letters in an inscription or a name set in capitals) (e:NAZARETH KHUAMI ZEISU ~ HI) (r:43.19.19/24.23.6) (q:draft)
