Be-eri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeri) (d:the Hittite father of Judith, and the father of the prophet Hosea) (e:~’ tapa Hosea tungah Topa in) (r:28.1.1/1.26.34) (q:draft)
Beel = (t:n) (w:pot) (d:beel, pot, written with a capital in Beel sekpa, the potter, one who shapes pots) (e:~ sekpa’ innah paisuk in la) (b:beel) (r:24.18.2) (q:draft)
Beel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beeliada) (d:first part of the name Beel-i-ada, Beeliada, a son of David; not a word by itself) (e:Elishama, ~-i-ada, leh Elifelet ahi uh hi) (r:13.14.7) (q:draft)
Beer = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beer) (d:a well where Israel camped in the desert, and a town to which Jotham fled; also written Be-er) (e:Tua lai panin ~ munah pai uh hi) (r:4.21.16/7.9.21) (q:draft)
Beno = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beno) (d:a Levite, descendant of Merari through Jaaziah) (e:sung panin ~, Shoham, Zakkur) (r:13.24.27) (q:draft)
Beon = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beon) (d:a town east of the Jordan in the land asked for by Reuben and Gad) (e:Sebam, Nebo, leh ~) (r:4.32.3) (q:draft)
Beri = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Beri) (d:a descendant of Asher, son of Zophah) (e:Shual, ~, Imrah) (r:13.7.36) (q:draft)
Beth-azmaveth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Beth Azmaveth/Azmaveth) (d:a town near Jerusalem; the NIV has Azmaveth in these verses) (e:~ khuami sawmli-le-nih ahi hi) (r:15.2.24/16.12.29) (q:draft)
Beth-togarmah = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Beth Togarmah) (d:a land in the far north that traded horses and mules with Tyre) (e:~ gam mite in zong na vante) (r:26.27.14/26.38.6) (q:draft)
Bethma-akah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beth Maakah) (d:second part of the name of the town Abel Bethma-akah, Abel Beth Maakah, in the north of Israel) (e:Abel ~ khua ah Sheba pai hi) (r:10.20.14/10.20.15) (q:draft)
Bul = (t:name) (w:Bul) (d:name of the eighth month of the Hebrew year; not the common word bul, base) (e:a kha giatna ahi ~ kha-in) (r:11.6.38) (q:draft)
Ciknawng = (t:n) (w:marsh) (d:ciknawng written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~ om lohna-ah laiphai kungte po thei) (b:ciknawng) (r:18.8.11) (q:draft)
Damaska = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Damascus) (d:the city of Damascus, also written Damaskas; Damaska gam is the land around the city) (e:~ khua mite thazaw uh a) (r:24.49.24/10.8.5) (q:draft)
Dikna = (t:n) (w:righteousness/justice) (d:dikna written with a capital in a line of verse, and as a name of the rider on the white horse, Faithful in the NIV) (e:~ leh Thuman kici hi) (b:dikna) (r:66.19.11/58.1.8) (q:draft)
