amanpha = (t:adj) (w:precious/valuable/costly) (d:manpha, precious, with the prefix a written as one word, placed before the noun) (e:ahoih ~ nate a dimin om hi) (b:manpha) (r:20.24.4/66.18.12) (q:draft)
amin = (t:n) (w:his name/its name) (d:min, name, with the prefix a, his or its, written as one word) (e:~ mah bangin amah zong ahi hi) (b:min) (r:9.25.25) (q:draft)
amsakin = (t:v) (w:make drunk/make dazed) (d:am with sak, cause, and the suffix in: making someone drunk or dazed, said of the cup of ruin; the meaning of am is taken from the NIV drunkenness) (e:hong ~ hong lungkhamsak ding hi) (r:26.23.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
anbuk = (t:n) (w:kitchen/cookhouse) (d:an, food, with buk, hut or shelter: a place where food is cooked) (e:nasemte in a huanna ~ ahi hi) (r:26.46.24) (q:draft)
ancil = (t:v) (w:thresh/tread out grain) (d:an, grain, with cil, tread: tread out grain on the threshing floor) (e:sual tunga ~ bangin) (r:24.51.33) (q:draft)
ancilnate = (t:n) (w:threshing floors) (d:ancilna, threshing floor, with the plural te) (e:a ~ uh luh uh hi) (b:ancilna) (r:9.23.1) (q:draft)
angkawmte = (t:n) (w:adulterers) (d:angkawm, commit adultery, with the plural te: people who commit adultery) (e:mun khempeuhah ~ a dim hi) (b:angkawm) (r:24.23.10) (q:draft)
angtang = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/glory) (e:kote ka ~ ngitnget uh a) (r:19.44.8) (q:draft)
angtanpih = (t:v) (w:be proud of/take pride in/boast of) (d:angtan, the form of angtang, boast, used before a suffix, with pih: be proud of someone or something; also said of the thing one is proud of, Israel-te’ angtanpih, the pride of Israel) (e:note ka hong ~ mahmah hi) (r:50.4.1/19.47.4) (q:draft)
anhaihna = (t:n) (w:sifting of grain/sieve) (d:an, grain, with haih, sift or winnow, and na: the sifting of grain; anhaihna ciang is the tool it is done with, a sieve in the NIV) (e:~ ciang tawh an a kihaih mah bangin) (r:30.9.9) (q:draft)
anhuanpa = (t:n) (w:cook) (d:anhuan, cook food, with -pa, a man: the man who cooks) (e:Tua ciangin Samuel in ~ kiangah) (b:anhuan) (r:9.9.23/9.9.24) (q:draft)
anis = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:dill/anise) (d:a garden herb of which a tenth was given, named with mint and cumin; the English word anise) (e:leengmasel leh ~ leh meh namkim) (r:42.11.42/40.23.23) (q:draft)
ankhing = (t:n) (w:food/grain) (d:food or grain as a thing lent, named beside sumgum, money, in the law against lending at interest; the part khing is not explained by the verse) (e:sumgum hitaleh, ~ hitaleh) (r:5.23.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
ankholna = (t:n) (w:grain storage/storehouse) (d:an, food or grain, with kholna, storing: the storing of grain; ankholna inn is a storehouse or granary) (e:Josef in ~ innte khempeuh hongin) (r:1.41.56) (q:draft)
ankungnote = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:young plants/seedlings) (d:ankung, crop plant, with no, young or small, and the plural te) (e:Tua ~ in zung thuk kha zo lo) (r:41.4.6/40.13.6) (q:draft)
anli = (t:n) (w:self-sown grain) (d:grain that comes up by itself without being sown; anli pote, the things that grow from it) (e:kumin ~ pote na ne ding uh a) (r:23.37.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
anlimnono = (t:n) (w:choice foods/delicacies/presents of food) (d:anlim, tasty food, with nono, said of several things each of that quality: good things to eat, sent to one another as gifts at a feast) (e:~ khat leh khat kikholh ni) (r:17.9.22/17.9.19) (q:draft)
anlui = (t:n) (w:old grain/old crop) (d:an, food or grain, with lui, old: the grain of an earlier harvest, the opposite of anthak, new grain) (e:note in ~ na ne ding uh hi) (r:3.25.22) (q:draft)
anneek = (t:n) (w:eating/meal) (d:an, food, with neek, a form of ne, eat: the eating of food; anneek tuidawn, eating and drinking, and anneek sabuai, a table for meals) (e:note in ~ tuidawn akipan na khempeuh) (r:46.10.31/44.6.2) (q:draft)
annelte = (t:n) (w:flour/fine flour) (d:annel, flour, with the plural te, in a list of goods) (e:a ~ le mangbuhte, a bawngte) (b:annel) (r:66.18.13/13.9.29) (q:draft)
annengte = (t:n) (w:crumbs) (d:anneng, a crumb of food, with the plural te) (e:sabuai tung panin a kia ~) (b:anneng) (r:40.15.27/42.16.21) (q:draft)
anphalte = (t:n) (w:sheaves) (d:bundles of cut grain brought to the threshing floor; plural with te) (e:ancilna phualah ~ kaihkhop bangin) (r:33.4.12) (q:draft)
anphual = (t:n) (w:grain pile/heap of grain) (d:an, grain, with phual, place: the heap of grain at the threshing floor) (e:~ nawl-ah lum dingin pai hi) (r:8.3.7) (q:draft)
anphualte = (t:n) (w:shocks/stacks of grain/grain piles) (d:anphual, a pile of grain, with the plural te: stacked sheaves of cut grain in the field) (e:~ leh ankung ding laite) (b:anphual) (r:7.15.5) (q:draft)
anpia-in = (t:v) (w:serving food/serving at table) (d:an, food, with pia, give, and the suffix in: giving out food, waiting at table) (e:Martha pen ~ a manlah hi) (r:43.12.2/42.22.27) (q:draft)
anpiate = (t:n) (w:cupbearers/servers) (d:an, food, with pia, give, and the plural te: those who serve food and drink at table, cupbearers in the NIV) (e:a ~ leh a puansilhte) (r:14.9.4) (q:draft)
ansangh = (t:n) (w:gleanings/leftover grain) (d:spelling of ansang with a final h: ears of grain left behind the reapers; ansangh tawm, glean) (e:mangbuhham lak khit dong ~ tawm hi) (b:ansang) (r:8.2.23/8.2.7) (q:draft)
ansukna = (t:n) (w:grinding/pounding of grain) (d:an, grain, with suk, pound or crush, and na: the grinding of grain; ansukna ging, the sound of grinding) (e:~ gingte na zak theih phat nawn loh hun) (r:21.12.4) (q:draft)
antangte = (t:n) (w:grain) (d:antang, grain, with the plural te: stores of grain) (e:Faro’ ukna nuai-ah ~ kholin) (b:antang) (r:1.41.35) (q:draft)
anu = (t:n) (w:female) (d:nu, female, with the prefix a written as one word, said of an animal: a female one, the opposite of apa, a male one; tuuno anu, a ewe lamb) (e:kum khat a pha tuuno ~ khat) (b:nu) (r:3.14.10/3.3.6) (q:draft)
anvakna = (t:n) (w:giving of a meal/banquet/feeding) (d:anvak, give food to, with the noun suffix na: the giving of a meal to guests; anvakna pawi, a banquet) (e:Tua bangin ~ pawi na bawl ciangin) (r:42.14.13/42.14.12) (q:draft)
anvui = (t:n) (w:ear of grain/head of grain) (d:an, grain, with vui, ear: grain still in the ear) (e:leh ~ athak a van sungah hong pua hi) (r:12.4.42) (q:draft)
anvuite = (t:n) (w:ears of grain/heads of grain) (d:anvui, ear of grain, with the plural te; the NIV has leftover grain) (e:~ lakah a sang hong tawmsak in) (b:anvui) (r:8.2.2) (q:draft)
apkhawm = (t:v) (w:dedicate together/consecrate together) (d:ap, dedicate, with khawm, together: dedicate or consecrate along with other things or people) (e:kham tawh Topa’ tungah a ~ hi) (b:ap) (r:13.18.11/3.8.30) (q:draft)
apnate = (t:n) (w:those entrusted) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with na and the plural te: here the people into whose hands the money was given) (e:sum a ~ uh tung panin amaute in) (b:ap) (r:12.12.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
appa = (t:n) (w:one who dedicates) (d:ap, dedicate, with -pa, a man: the man who dedicates something) (e:Lo a ~ in a tat nop leh) (b:ap) (r:3.27.19/3.27.15) (q:draft)
apsak = (t:v) (w:have handed over/cause to entrust) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with sak, cause: have something handed over to someone) (e:tua kumpi puante leh sakol ~ in) (b:ap) (r:17.6.9) (q:draft)
apsate = (t:n) (w:dedicated things) (d:apsa, dedicated, with the plural te: the things that someone has dedicated) (e:tapa Joab in a ~ khempeuh zong) (b:apsa) (r:13.26.28) (q:draft)
aptheih = (t:v) (w:be able to hand over/be able to present) (d:ap, hand over or dedicate, with theih, be able, used before nading) (e:Pasian kiangah a ~ nadingin) (b:ap) (r:49.5.26/42.20.20) (q:draft)
atawntungin = (t:adv) (w:forever/for ever) (d:tawntungin, continually, with the prefix a written as one word) (e:zanni, tuni, ~ kikheel loin a om hi) (b:tawntungin) (r:58.13.8/27.6.26) (q:draft)
atkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:cutting off/cut off) (d:at, cut, with khiat, off, sak, do to someone, and the suffix in: cutting a part off a person) (e:na bilte hong ~ na tate hong thahsak) (r:26.23.25) (q:draft)
awh = (t:v) (w:wear around the neck) (d:said of beads or a necklace, khi: khi awh, the necklace that is worn, one jewel of your necklace in the NIV; the meaning of awh alone is not shown by the verse) (e:na khi ~ in ka lungsim hong zo hi) (r:22.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
awkcip = (t:v) (w:be snared/be caught fast/be trapped) (d:awk, be caught, with cip, tightly: be held fast in a trap or snare) (e:amau’ mawhna sungah ~ a) (b:awk) (r:20.29.6) (q:draft)
awklawh = (t:v) (w:be ensnared/get caught) (d:awk, be caught in a snare, with lawh, which shows that this comes on someone as a result of something) (e:note in zong na ~ kha ding uh hi) (r:20.22.25/45.11.9) (q:draft)
awksakna = (t:n) (w:ensnaring/trapping) (d:awksak, ensnare, with the noun suffix na: the act of causing someone to be caught, as the wicked in the work of their own hands) (e:~ tawh amah hong kilang hi) (b:awksak) (r:19.9.16) (q:draft)
awkte = (t:n) (w:those caught/those ensnared) (d:awk, be caught, with the plural te; a awkte, those who are caught in a trap) (e:tua thang ah a ~ tungah) (b:awk) (r:20.22.14) (q:draft)
awnghawh = (t:v) (w:relieve oneself/ease oneself) (d:go aside to empty the bowels, a polite expression) (e:~ nading mun khat na nei ding uh hi) (r:5.23.12/7.3.24) (q:draft)
awngte = (t:adj) (w:empty/deserted) (d:awng, empty, with the plural te; mun awngte, empty places, is used for ruins) (e:mun ~ leh a kim a pamah) (b:awng) (r:14.34.6) (q:draft)
awnsuk = (t:v) (w:tilt down/lean over) (d:awn, lean or tilt, with suk, downward: of a pot, tilt over toward someone) (e:a leilu lam panin hong ~ hi) (b:awn) (r:24.1.13) (q:draft)
azawng = (t:adj) (w:poor) (d:zawng, poor, with the prefix a, written as one word: a poor person, the poor; ahau azawng is rich and poor alike) (e:Tua khua sungah ~ mipil khat om a) (b:zawng) (r:21.9.15/23.24.2) (q:draft)
baa = (t:n) (w:side of the head/temple) (d:in baa sam, the hair that grows at the sides of the head) (e:na ~ samte uh met loin) (r:3.19.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
baak = (t:n) (w:piece/portion) (d:counting word for a piece of meat: sa baak khat, one piece of meat; also written bak) (e:anlum pheng khat, sa ~ khat) (r:10.6.19) (q:draft)
baangin = (t:adj) (w:lovely/attractive) (d:in ngaih baangin, being lovely, said of a person's looks; baang with the linking ending in) (e:Tu-in Josef ngaih ~ a mel hoih hi) (b:baang) (r:1.39.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
baangin = (t:v) (w:turning aside/stopping by) (d:in lam baangin, leaving one's way to call on someone and ask how he is) (e:hong lam ~ dam-le-nat kitheih sakna-in) (r:24.15.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
bahgawp = (t:v) (w:be exhausted/be worn out/faint) (d:bah, be weary, with gawp, utterly: have no strength left, from grief or flight) (e:dahin husamin ka ~ hi) (b:bah) (r:25.2.11/24.48.45) (q:draft)
bahtoh = (t:v) (w:bring up/lift up) (d:lift the hand with food up to the mouth; toh shows upward movement) (e:a kam-ah a ~ ding nangawn gim) (r:20.26.15) (q:draft)
baihte = (t:adj) (w:quick/easy) (d:baih, quick, easy, with the plural te; a heh baihte, those who are quick to get angry, the hot-tempered) (e:a heh ~ khial thei tawntung hi) (b:baih) (r:20.29.22) (q:draft)
bakbak = (t:adv) (w:ravenously/greedily) (d:describes greedy, tearing eating; a ne bakbak, one that devours ravenously, said of a wild animal) (e:a ne ~ keivom hi a) (r:1.49.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
balgawpte = (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:balgawp, tear to pieces, with the plural te: animals that wild beasts have torn) (e:gamsate in a ~ hita leh) (b:balgawp) (r:3.22.8) (q:draft)
balkekna = (t:n) (w:tearing/rending) (d:balkek, tear cloth, with the noun suffix na: the act of tearing one's clothes; a balkekna thu, the news that he had torn them) (e:a puante a ~ thu) (b:balkek) (r:12.5.8) (q:draft)
balkham = (t:v) (w:tear/tear off) (d:bal, tear, with kham: of a lion, tear the arm or the head of its prey) (e:leh a luzang ~ hi) (r:5.33.20) (q:draft)
balkhiat = (t:v) (w:tear away/tear out) (d:form of balkhia used before a following word such as khit) (e:Israel gam a ~ khit ciangin) (b:balkhia) (r:12.17.21) (q:draft)
balnensa-in = (t:adv) (w:broken in pieces/crumbled) (d:balnen, break in pieces, with sa, already done, and the ending in: in the state of having been broken into pieces) (e:helsa leh ~ na paipih ding a) (r:3.6.21) (q:draft)
balnensak = (t:v) (w:tear in pieces for) (d:balnen, break or tear in pieces, with sak: tear prey in pieces for others, as a lion for its mate and cubs) (e:a zi leh a tate’ adingin ~ a) (b:balnen) (r:34.2.12) (q:draft)
baltat = (t:v) (w:tear apart/tear in two/sever) (d:bal, tear, with tat, be severed: tear a thing right through so that the parts come apart) (e:ahih hangin ~ lo ding hi) (r:3.1.17) (q:draft)
balthanggawp = (t:v) (w:tear to pieces/tear apart) (d:balthang, tear apart, with gawp, severely) (e:amaute in Paul ~ kha ding hi) (r:44.23.10/28.13.8) (q:draft)
balzante = (t:n) (w:those torn to pieces/torn animals) (d:balzan, tear to pieces, with the plural te: animals torn by wild beasts) (e:Gamlak ganhingte’ ~ nang' kiangah kong puak kei hi) (b:balzan) (r:1.31.39) (q:draft)
banbulh = (t:n) (w:armlet/bracelet/arm band) (d:ornament worn on the arm, from ban, arm, and bulh, put on) (e:a om a ~ kong la a) (r:10.1.10) (q:draft)
bangcite = (t:pron) (w:who/what kind) (d:bangci, how, with te: what sort of person, which one; a bangcite ahi hiam asks who it is that fits a description) (e:nasem i cih a ~ ahi hiam) (b:bangci) (r:40.24.45/42.12.42) (q:draft)
bangkikin = (t:v) (w:being restored/becoming as before) (d:bangkik with the linking ending in; a ngei bangkikin, becoming again as it was) (e:a ngei ~ amah a siang hi) (b:bangkik) (r:12.5.14/12.5.10) (q:draft)
bangsakin = (t:v) (w:making like/restoring) (d:bangsak, make like, with the linking ending in; a ngei bangsakin, making as it was before) (e:Ammon mite a ngei ~ ka hausakkik ding hi) (b:bangsak) (r:24.49.6/24.48.47) (q:draft)
bangsakkikin = (t:v) (w:restoring) (d:bangsakkik, make as it was before, with the linking ending in) (e:note na ngei uh hong ~) (b:bangsakkik) (r:5.30.3/44.15.16) (q:draft)
bangta = (t:v) (w:have become like/be like now) (d:bang, be like, with ta, which marks a change that has come about) (e:Kote mah na ~ hi) (b:bang) (r:23.14.10/23.1.22) (q:draft)
bangzaha = (t:adv) (w:how/how much) (d:bangzah, how much, with a, placed before a describing word: bangzaha lian, how great) (e:vangliatna ~ lian ahi zongin) (b:bangzah) (r:49.1.19/49.1.18) (q:draft)
bansak = (t:v) (w:cause to reach/let overtake) (d:ban, reach, with sak, cause: make something reach or come upon someone) (e:na hehna so amaute ~ in) (b:ban) (r:19.69.24) (q:draft)
bantan = (t:v) (w:cut off/strike off) (d:of a sword, strike an arm or hand so as to cut it; the second part is tan, cut off) (e:Namsau in a ban ~ hen la) (r:38.11.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
bante = (t:n) (w:arms) (e:A awm leh a ~ ngun tawh kibawl a) (b:ban) (r:27.2.32) (q:draft)
battheih = (t:v) (w:be able to be like/can become like) (d:bat, form of bang, be like, with theih, can; a battheih nading, so that one may be like or become like) (e:mittaw a ~ nadingin) (b:bat) (r:43.9.39/47.11.13) (q:draft)
batzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to reach/attain) (d:bat, reach, with zawh, manage to; with a negative, be beyond one's reach) (e:kei’ ~ ding hi lo hi) (r:21.7.23/19.10.5) (q:draft)
bawhsak = (t:v) (w:pull out/pluck out) (d:bawh, pull up or out, with sak: pull out another person's hair) (e:a sam uh ka ~ gawp hi) (b:bawh) (r:16.13.25) (q:draft)
bawhsat = (t:v) (w:break/snap) (d:break a cord or rope by pulling; bawhsat hak, hard to break) (e:kiheek khauhual ~ hak hi) (r:21.4.12) (q:draft)
bawhsuk = (t:v) (w:crouch down/bow down) (d:of an animal about to give birth, crouch down to the ground; suk shows downward movement) (e:lei-ah a ~ hun thei na hi hiam) (r:18.39.3) (q:draft)
bawlkha = (t:v) (w:make) (d:bawl, make, with kha, happen to; bawlkha kei in, take care not to make) (e:tawh thuciamna ~ kei in) (r:2.34.15/2.34.12) (q:draft)
bawlkhit = (t:v) (w:finish doing/have done) (d:bawl, do or make, with khit, finished; bawlkhit ciangin, after doing) (e:teekteekin a ~ uh ciangin) (r:44.13.29/44.24.18) (q:draft)
bawlkholh = (t:v) (w:prepare/make ready beforehand) (d:form of bawlkhol used before a following word such as khit or sak) (e:mun ka va ~ khit ciangin) (b:bawlkhol) (r:43.14.3/46.2.9) (q:draft)
bawlnopna = (t:n) (w:desire to do/wish to commit) (d:bawl, do, with nop, want, and the noun suffix na; mawh bawlnopna, the desire to do wrong) (e:Mawh ~ lungsim hong neisak kei inla) (r:19.141.4/45.6.22) (q:draft)
bawlpih = (t:v) (w:do together with/join in making) (d:bawl, do or make, with pih, together with someone: take part with others in what they do) (e:si theh biaknate ke’n ~ loin) (b:bawl) (r:19.16.4) (q:draft)
bawlsaksate = (t:n) (w:things done for) (d:bawlsak, do or make for someone, with sa, already done, and the plural te: the things that have been done for someone) (e:na lian hong ~ ngaihsun un) (r:9.12.24) (q:draft)
bawlsiatin = (t:v) (w:mistreated/oppressed) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with the ending in; mi’ bawlsiatin, as ones whom others mistreat) (e:sal suakin mi’ ~ amaute omsak in) (b:bawlsiat) (r:16.4.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawlsiatpa = (t:n) (w:victim/oppressed man) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with pa, a man; a bawlsiatpa, the man who is being mistreated, while the one who mistreats is bawlsiapa) (e:a ~ honkhia-in Iziptpa a that hi) (b:bawlsiat) (r:44.7.24/24.21.12) (q:draft)
bawlsiatte = (t:n) (w:those oppressed/the tormented) (d:bawlsiat, mistreat, with the plural te: those whom someone mistreats or torments) (e:dawimangpa in a ~ khempeuh a damsak hi) (b:bawlsiat) (r:44.10.38/44.5.16) (q:draft)
bawlta = (t:v) (w:make/do) (d:bawl, make or do, with ta, which marks what has now come about) (e:hong ciamnuih ~ uh hi) (b:bawl) (r:18.30.1/19.139.8) (q:draft)
bawlthei = (t:v) (w:can do/be able to perform) (d:bawl, do or make, with thei, be able) (e:hih bangin nalamdang ~ ding ahi hiam) (b:bawl) (r:43.9.16/40.13.54) (q:draft)
bawlthuah = (t:v) (w:keep on holding/do in addition) (d:bawl, do or hold, with thuah, in addition: go on holding a feast for more days) (e:adang ni sagih sung mah ~ uh hi) (r:14.30.23) (q:draft)
bawlung = (t:n) (w:ball) (e:~ bangin hong lawn ding hi) (r:23.22.18) (q:draft)
