beelmang = (t:n) (w:soot/pot black) (d:the black that gathers on a cooking pot; in the verse beauty is smeared with it, that is, made loathsome) (e:Na meel hoihna ~ na kizutnelh hi) (r:26.16.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
beelseekte = (t:n) (w:potters) (e:Hihte in ~ hi a) (b:beelseek) (r:13.4.23) (q:draft)
beemlepang = (t:n) (w:storehouse/barn/provisions) (d:beem le pang written as one word: the bins where grain and food are stored, and so the food kept there) (e:Amaute in ~ zong nei lo napi-in) (r:42.12.24/19.132.15) (q:draft)
beenggawp = (t:v) (w:strike/smite/slap hard) (d:beeng, strike with the hand, with gawp, severely) (e:Pasian in nang hong ~ taktak ding hi) (b:beeng) (r:44.23.3/19.3.7) (q:draft)
beengin = (t:v) (w:beating/striking) (d:beeng, strike, with the linking ending in; awm beengin, beating the breast, a sign of grief) (e:awm ~ a ciah uh hi) (b:beeng) (r:42.23.48/42.18.13) (q:draft)
behlephung = (t:n) (w:descent/lineage/clan and family) (d:beh, clan, le, and, phung, family line, written as one word: the family a person descends from) (e:amau’ ~ a kan thei lo mite) (r:15.2.59/16.7.61) (q:draft)
beikhin = (t:v) (w:be over/be past/be used up) (d:bei, be finished, with khin, already: be completely gone or past) (e:Ka thaneihteng ~ a) (b:bei) (r:27.10.8/58.11.11) (q:draft)
beilawh = (t:v) (w:lose/spend/perish) (d:bei, be finished or used up, with lawh, as a result of something: lose or spend all one has for a thing, or perish because of what has happened) (e:na neih khempeuh na ~ zongin) (r:20.4.7/24.40.15) (q:draft)
beinate = (t:n) (w:costs/expenses) (d:bei, be used up, with the noun suffix na and the plural te; sum beinate, the money spent) (e:hih sum ~ ahih leh kumpi sum) (b:beina) (r:15.6.4) (q:draft)
beisakpa = (t:n) (w:remover/one who puts an end to) (d:beisak, put an end to or let pass, with pa, a man: the man who takes something away, or who lets a time go by) (e:hih mindaina a ~ adingin) (b:beisak) (r:9.17.26/24.46.17) (q:draft)
beisakta = (t:v) (w:put an end to/make cease) (d:beisak, put an end to, with ta, which marks what now comes about) (e:Hih paunak ka ~ ding a) (b:beisak) (r:26.12.23) (q:draft)
beisiangsak = (t:v) (w:wipe out/purge/clear away) (d:beisiang, be completely gone, with sak, cause: remove a thing completely from a place) (e:Jeroboam innkuan ka ~ ding hi) (b:beisiang) (r:11.14.10/14.34.3) (q:draft)
beitumsak = (t:v) (w:consume/destroy completely) (d:beitum, be wholly consumed, with sak, cause; said together with beimangsak, cause to perish) (e:Tua ahih manin Israel ka ~ ding a) (b:beitum) (r:28.5.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
bekbekin = (t:adv) (w:only/solely/nothing but) (d:bekbek, only, with the ending in, placed after the word it limits) (e:a thuman ~ na gamta ding uh hi) (b:bekbek) (r:5.16.20/23.38.16) (q:draft)
bekinah = (t:adv) (w:in only/within just) (d:bekin, only, with the marker ah; nai khat sung bekinah, within just one hour) (e:Nai khat sung ~ thutanna na thuak ta hi) (b:bekin) (r:66.18.10/66.18.17) (q:draft)
bela = (t:part) (w:very/most) (d:bel, which marks the extreme of an order, with a joining it to what follows: a nunung bela piang, born at the very last) (e:khang a nunung ~ piang eite) (b:bel) (r:46.10.11) (q:draft)
bela = (t:v) (w:against/adjoining) (d:bel, cling to or lean on, with a: built against or attached to a wall) (e:biakinn kawm pang ~ kibawl inndei neute) (b:bel) (r:26.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
belawi = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bean) (d:a kind of bean, named among the grains and pulses used for bread) (e:mangbuh, mangbuhham, ~, beli, taang) (r:26.4.9) (q:draft)
belhsak = (t:v) (w:make stick to/cause to cling) (d:belh, cling to, with sak, cause) (e:nangma tungah ka ~ ding hi) (b:belh) (r:26.29.4) (q:draft)
bemeh = (t:n) (w:lentil stew/bean stew) (d:be, bean or lentil, with meh, cooked dish eaten with the staple) (e:Jakob in an leh ~ Esau pia hi) (r:1.25.34) (q:draft)
bengkhia = (t:v) (w:drive away/scare away/chase off) (d:beng with khia, away: drive off birds or animals) (e:amaute a ~ ding mihing om lo ding hi) (b:beng) (r:5.28.26) (q:draft)
bepi = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:bean) (d:a kind of bean, named with lentils among foodstuffs) (e:an, ankan, ~ leh basan) (r:10.17.28) (q:draft)
beril = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:beryl) (d:a precious stone, the English word beryl) (e:a giatna in ~ suangmanpha) (r:66.21.20/2.39.13) (q:draft)
betkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:strike out of/knock out) (d:bet, strike, with khiat, out, and sak: strike a thing so that it drops from the hand) (e:na thaltangte zong kong ~ ding hi) (r:26.39.3) (q:draft)
betkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:striking out of/knocking out) (d:betkhiatsak with the linking ending in) (e:na tawi na thal hong ~) (b:betkhiatsak) (r:26.39.3) (q:draft)
betsan = (t:v) (w:clap at) (d:bet, strike or clap, with san, at someone; khut betsan, clap the hands at someone in scorn) (e:awi-in khut a ~ uh hi) (b:bet) (r:25.2.15) (q:draft)
