buasuk = (t:v) (w:pour down/shower down) (d:bua pour out, with suk downward: pour down from above like rain) (e:vantungte in thumanna ~ ta un) (b:bua) (r:23.45.8) (q:draft)
buhphual = (t:n) (w:threshing floor) (d:buh grain with phual place: the place where grain is threshed and winnowed; in Zechariah 12.6 a place of grain that is on fire, where the NIV has sheaves) (e:ama ~ zap siang ding a) (r:40.3.12/38.12.6) (q:draft)
buhvai = (t:n) (w:chaff) (d:the husks of grain that the wind blows away) (e:huih in ~ a mut bangin) (r:24.13.24) (q:draft)
