bungte = (t:n) (w:bottles/boxes/containers) (d:plural of bung, here a small container: paknamtui bungte are perfume bottles) (e:paknamtui ~ leh a kivom aite) (b:bung) (r:23.3.20) (q:draft)
bunzaw = (t:v) (w:go deeper/affect more) (d:bun go in or take effect, with zaw more: sink in more deeply, said of a rebuke) (e:khatvei taina in ~ hi) (b:bun) (r:20.17.10) (q:draft)
bunzo = (t:v) (w:pierce/penetrate/take effect) (d:bun go in, with zo be able: be able to pierce; in the verse negated, of weapons that cannot pierce at all) (e:thaltangte in zong ~ tuan het lo hi) (b:bun) (r:18.41.26) (q:draft)
buppiak = (t:v) (w:offer/give wholly/surrender) (d:bup whole with piak give: give oneself over completely) (e:na pumpi uh ~ unla) (r:45.6.19) (q:draft)
butsakin = (t:v) (w:put on) (d:butsak put a bracelet or ring on another person, with the linking ending in) (e:tau hong ~ khainiang kong oksak hi) (b:butsak) (r:26.16.11) (q:draft)
ciahkhia = (t:v) (w:leave/go away/depart) (d:ciah go home or return, with khia out: go out and away from a place) (e:lungnuam takin na ~ theita ding uh hi) (b:ciah) (r:44.16.36/26.38.13) (q:draft)
ciahpihna = (t:n) (w:taking back/carrying off) (d:ciahpih take back with one, with the noun suffix na: the act of taking someone away to one's own place) (e:Babilon-ah a ~ thu gen in) (b:ciahpih) (r:26.17.12) (q:draft)
ciahsakin = (t:v) (w:send away/send off/send home) (d:ciahsak send away, with the linking ending in) (e:lampi dangah ~ na suaktasak a) (b:ciahsak) (r:59.2.25/9.9.19) (q:draft)
ciahsakna = (t:n) (w:sending away/dismissal) (d:ciahsak send away, with the noun suffix na; in Isaiah 50.1 of sending away a wife in divorce) (e:Amah ka ~, na nu a kimakna lai) (b:ciahsak) (r:23.50.1) (q:draft)
ciak = (t:v) (w:growl/snarl) (d:the sound made by lion cubs) (e:humpino bangin a ~ lualua ding uh hi) (r:24.51.38) (q:draft)
