ciamkha = (t:v) (w:taste/get a taste of) (d:ciam taste, with kha which shows that the action comes to happen) (e:ka an ~ lo ding uh hi) (r:42.14.24) (q:draft)
ciamkha = (t:v) (w:pledge/promise) (d:ciam promise, with kha: happen to give one's word, in kam ciamkha) (e:a lohsak dingin kam na ~ hiam) (r:20.6.1) (q:draft)
ciamnasa = (t:adj) (w:promised) (d:ciam promise, with na and sa already done: describes what has been promised, here the place the Lord promised) (e:~ munah i paito ding hi) (b:ciamna) (r:4.14.40) (q:draft)
ciamnui = (t:v) (w:joke/jest) (d:speak in fun, not seriously; compare ciamnuih jest) (e:a mak dingte tungah a ~ bang lel hi) (r:1.19.14) (q:draft)
ciamnuihbawl = (t:v) (w:mock/ridicule/make fun of) (d:ciamnuih mockery with bawl make) (e:hong simmawh bawlin hong ~ lel uh hi) (b:ciamnuih) (r:26.36.3/26.36.4) (q:draft)
ciampa = (t:n) (w:promiser/one who promised) (d:ciam promise, with pa marking a man: he who made the promise, said of God) (e:thu a ~ in thumanpa ahi ci-in) (b:ciam) (r:58.11.11/45.4.21) (q:draft)
ciampak = (t:v) (w:vow hastily/promise rashly) (d:ciam promise or vow, with pak quickly: make a vow in haste) (e:tungah thu mawk ~ kei in) (r:21.5.2/21.8.2) (q:draft)
ciamtehsak = (t:v) (w:mark/count against) (d:ciamteh mark or record, with sak: put a mark on someone, or hold a sin on record against someone) (e:Topa in a mawhnate a ~ loh mipa) (b:ciamteh) (r:45.4.8/66.13.16) (q:draft)
ciamtehteh = (t:v) (w:keep remembering/keep on record) (d:ciamteh note or record, with the last syllable repeated for continued action: go on holding in mind) (e:mawhna ~ kei in) (r:23.64.9) (q:draft)
ciangpha = (t:v) (w:rebuild/repair) (d:ciang build up a wall, with pha good: build up again, restore a wall) (e:nadingin Jerusalem kulh ~ ni) (r:16.2.17/14.32.5) (q:draft)
ciangtang = (t:n) (w:shuttle) (d:in siam ciangtang, the shuttle of a weaver's loom) (e:siam ~ sangin manlang zaw a) (r:18.7.6) (q:draft)
ciangto = (t:v) (w:build up/raise) (d:ciang build a wall, with to upward: build a wall up high) (e:a sang mahmahin ~ hi) (b:ciang) (r:14.33.14) (q:draft)
ciantakin = (t:adv) (w:clearly/fully/for certain) (d:cian carefully or clearly, with takin which makes an adverb) (e:hoihsakna thu ~ thei ta uh hen) (b:cian) (r:45.14.5/49.4.30) (q:draft)
ciapna = (t:n) (w:tasting) (d:ciap taste, with the noun suffix na: the act of tasting) (e:hih khuaizu tawmno khat ka ~ hangin) (b:ciap) (r:9.14.29) (q:draft)
ciatte = (t:pron) (w:each of them/each one) (d:ciat each, with the plural ending te: each one of several) (e:a kizompih ~ lamah a kha nihte) (b:ciat) (r:26.1.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
cihkha = (t:v) (w:do to/do anything to) (d:cih do or say, with kha happen to: used with bang or bangmah, do something to someone, usually harm) (e:tua mipa bangmah ~ kei in) (r:40.27.19/33.6.3) (q:draft)
cihmawhnate = (t:n) (w:needs/distresses/hardships) (d:plural of cihmawhna distress or need) (e:buaina, ~ hong tungsak ding hi) (b:cihmawhna) (r:5.28.20/47.8.14) (q:draft)
cihmawk = (t:v) (w:say/happen to say) (d:cih say, with mawk carelessly or without ground: say something that does not hold, as in even if it should say) (e:a ~ hangin pumpi na khat ahihna) (r:46.12.15/46.12.16) (q:draft)
cihnop = (t:v) (w:want to say/mean to say) (d:cih say with nop want, the form of nuam used in dependent clauses) (e:na ~ hangin lungsim a thei Pasian in) (r:20.24.12/42.4.23) (q:draft)
ciimsate = (t:n) (w:the wise/the prudent) (d:ciim, here clear in mind or wise, with sa already and the plural te: people who are already wise) (e:Mi ~ ciimsak semsemin) (r:20.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciingin = (t:v) (w:comb/dress) (d:said of flax thread in anthul khau ciingin, where the NIV has combed flax; with the linking ending in; not the word ciing barren) (e:Anthul khau ~ na a semte) (r:23.19.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciingin = (t:v) (w:keep/store up) (d:keep words in the heart so as to use them; with the linking ending in) (e:Na lungsim uhah ~ zang thei le-uhcin) (r:20.22.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
cikze = (t:v) (w:spare/hold back) (d:in cikze het loin, without holding back at all, without pity) (e:~ het loin note kong sukmang) (r:26.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
cila = (t:adv) (w:at the beginning/at first) (d:cil the early stage or beginning, with the ending a: at the beginning of; cila kipan is from the beginning of) (e:na khempeuh a pian’sak ~ kipan) (b:cil) (r:61.3.4/24.17.12) (q:draft)
cilcil = (t:v) (w:thresh/tread out) (d:cil thresh by treading, repeated to show continuing action: be busy threshing) (e:mangbuh a ~ lai takin a khuadak leh) (r:13.21.20) (q:draft)
ciltangte = (t:n) (w:testicles) (d:plural of ciltang) (e:A ~ a sanim, a kisukham) (b:ciltang) (r:3.22.24) (q:draft)
cilun = (t:conj) (w:when first/at first) (d:cil at first, in the early stage, with the plural ending un: when they first did something) (e:Tua lai-ah a ten ~ amaute in) (b:cil) (r:12.17.25) (q:draft)
cilvui = (t:v) (w:thresh to powder/grind fine) (d:cil thresh or tread, with vui fine as dust: thresh grain until it is crushed) (e:Mi khatpeuh in antang ~ ahi hiam) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimbeng = (t:n) (w:glaze/silver dross) (d:a coating smeared on an earthen pot, where the NIV has silver dross) (e:~ kizut leibel tawh kibang hi) (r:20.26.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
cimitna = (t:n) (w:complete destruction/total ruin) (d:cimit come to a complete end, with the noun suffix na; in siat cimitna, total destruction) (e:siat ~ a pian’ loh nadingin) (r:14.12.12) (q:draft)
cimmai = (t:v) (w:collapse/fall down flat) (d:of a wall: cim fall down, here fall flat to the ground) (e:Khuapikulh ~ ding a, mi khempeuh) (r:6.6.5/6.6.20) (q:draft)
cimsa = (t:adj) (w:fallen/broken down/collapsed) (d:cim fall down or collapse, with sa already done) (e:a ~ kulh khempeuh) (b:cim) (r:14.32.5) (q:draft)
cimsak = (t:v) (w:bring down/make collapse/shake) (d:cim fall down, with the causative sak: cause walls to fall; the NIV has tremble) (e:gin’na in khuapi kulhte ~ ding a) (b:cim) (r:26.26.10) (q:draft)
cimtakin = (t:v) (w:be weary of/be tired of/be fed up with) (d:cimtak be fed up with someone, with the linking ending in) (e:hong ~ hong mudah kha ding hi) (b:cimtak) (r:20.25.17) (q:draft)
cimzan = (t:v) (w:be levelled/collapse completely) (d:of a city: cim fall down, here be brought down flat) (e:a khuapi pen ~ ding hi) (r:23.32.19) (q:draft)
cinghte = (t:n) (w:the generous/those who are kind) (d:cingh generous, with the plural te: those who give freely to the poor) (e:tungah a ~ thupha ngah ahi hi) (b:cingh) (r:20.14.21) (q:draft)
cingkam = (t:n) (w:quiet man/home-loving person) (d:said of Jacob, a peaceful man who stays at home, in contrast to Esau the hunter) (e:inn-ah om hithiatin a ~ khat ahi hi) (r:1.25.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
cingsingte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:almugwood) (d:plural of cingsing, here the logs of almugwood) (e:Tua ciangin kumpipa in ~ Topa’ biakinn) (b:cingsing) (r:11.10.12) (q:draft)
cingtaakna = (t:n) (w:perfection/fullness/maturity) (d:cingtaak perfect or complete, with the noun suffix na) (e:Khrih’ ~ ciang i banto ding hi) (b:cingtaak) (r:49.4.13/58.7.28) (q:draft)
cingteek = (t:n) (w:blight) (d:a disease that withers crops; cingteek sak is strike with blight) (e:~ sakin ka kausansak a) (r:37.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
cinkhit = (t:v) (w:be completed/be over) (d:cin be completed, of a period of time, with khit finished: a cinkhit ciangin is after the time has ended) (e:Kum tulkhat a ~ ciangin) (r:66.20.3/66.11.11) (q:draft)
citakzaw = (t:adj) (w:more faithful/more trustworthy) (d:citak faithful, with zaw more) (e:midang tampi sangin a ~) (b:citak) (r:16.7.2) (q:draft)
citpiak = (t:v) (w:give generously/be generous) (d:cit generous with piak give: give freely to people) (e:Amah in mi ~ ngitngetin) (r:19.37.26) (q:draft)
da = (t:todo) (q:draft, occurs only in aktui da kang in Job 6.6, taken as the white of an egg; the meaning of da by itself cannot be told from the verse)
daanggawp = (t:v) (w:turn pale/turn deathly pale) (d:daang turn pale, with gawp completely) (e:ka mel a ~ hi) (b:daang) (r:27.7.28/29.2.6) (q:draft)
daangsak = (t:v) (w:make pale/let turn pale) (d:daang turn pale, with the causative sak: let the face lose its colour) (e:lungkham lua-in na mel ~ ngeingai zenzen) (b:daang) (r:27.5.10) (q:draft)
daanpiak = (t:v) (w:punish) (d:daan punishment with piak, the form of pia give used before another word; daanpiak ni is the day of punishment) (e:minam khempeuh ~ nadingin a kizan ahi hi) (r:23.14.26/42.21.22) (q:draft)
daantuahna = (t:n) (w:punishment) (d:daantuah meet with punishment, with the noun suffix na: the punishment that someone receives) (e:a ~ uh kibang ding hi) (b:daantuah) (r:26.14.10/26.16.41) (q:draft)
dahzaw = (t:v) (w:grieve more/be sadder) (d:dah mourn or be sad, with zaw more) (e:Jonathan sangin David nakpitakin ~ a) (b:dah) (r:9.20.41) (q:draft)
daigawl = (t:n) (w:fence/hedge/wall) (d:the fence or wall round a vineyard or field) (e:nangmah in a ~ suvang na hi hiam) (r:19.80.12) (q:draft)
daihawh = (t:v) (w:visit the tomb/visit a grave) (d:with hawh visit: go to see a grave, said of the women going to the tomb of Jesus) (e:~ dingin a pai uh hi) (r:40.28.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
daihual = (t:n) (w:boundary/border/limits) (d:the boundary line of a town) (e:ama bukna khuapi ~ pua lamah) (r:4.35.27) (q:draft)
daingo = (t:n) (w:dew) (d:the dew that settles at night; compare daitui dew) (e:Ka lu tungah ~ kia a) (r:22.5.2) (q:draft)
daisaksa = (t:adj) (w:profaned/desecrated) (d:daisak profane, with sa already done: that has been profaned) (e:lakah na ~ uh a lian ka min) (b:daisak) (r:26.36.23) (q:draft)
dakdakin = (t:adv) (w:utterly/completely) (d:dakdak, an intensifier placed after a descriptive word, with the adverb ending in: zaw dakdakin is hanging quite limp) (e:Mi khempeuh’ khut zaw ~) (b:dakdak) (r:26.7.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
dakkhia-in = (t:v) (w:look out/look forth) (d:dak look, with khia out and the linking ending in: looking out from a place) (e:a tutna mun panin amah hong ~) (r:19.33.14) (q:draft)
daldalte = (t:n) (w:glittering things/shining ones) (d:daldal, an intensifier for shining, with the plural te: in a tee daldalte, the things that shone brightly) (e:a tee ~ a mualmang khin zo hi) (b:daldal) (r:25.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
dalnate = (t:n) (w:barriers/limits/boundaries) (d:plural of dalna barrier: things set up to keep people back) (e:Mual kimkotah ~ bawl inla, siangthosak in) (b:dalna) (r:2.19.23) (q:draft)
dalzawh = (t:v) (w:withstand/prevent/ward off) (d:dal block or shield, with zawh be able: be able to stand against or stop something) (e:hong hih nading khempeuh na ~ nadingun) (r:49.6.11/5.28.32) (q:draft)
damlam = (t:n) (w:being healed/healing) (d:dam be healed, with lam: the fact that one has been healed, used with verbs of knowing or feeling) (e:a natna a ~ a kiphawk hi) (r:41.5.29/42.17.15) (q:draft)
damta = (t:v) (w:be healed/be set free) (d:dam be healed, with ta marking a change that has now come about) (e:na natna panin na ~ hi) (b:dam) (r:42.13.12) (q:draft)
damta = (t:v) (w:subside/cool down) (d:of anger: dam with ta, has now died down) (e:na heh hangin na hehna ~ a) (b:dam) (r:23.12.1) (q:draft)
damzaw = (t:v) (w:be better/feel stronger) (d:dam be well, with zaw more: be in better health or strength) (e:ka ci a hong ~ diak hi) (b:dam) (r:27.10.19) (q:draft)
dangate = (t:adj) (w:others/other ones) (d:dang other, with the plural te: the other ones, as in kongpi dangate the other gates) (e:kongpi ~ mah tawh kibang hi) (b:danga) (r:26.40.29/26.40.33) (q:draft)
dangdangin = (t:adv) (w:staggering/reeling) (d:dangdang, an expressive word used after hoi stagger for swaying to and fro, with the adverb ending in) (e:namsau hangin hoi ~ a hailawh ding) (b:dangdang) (r:24.25.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
dantahna = (t:n) (w:punishment/penalty) (d:dantah punish, with the noun suffix na: punishment that falls on someone) (e:nang tungah ~ hong tung lo ding hi) (b:dantah) (r:9.28.10/11.2.33) (q:draft)
dante = (t:n) (w:ways/manners) (d:plural of dan way or manner: nuntak dante is ways of living) (e:na nuntak ~ uh le na gamtatziate) (b:dan) (r:24.26.13) (q:draft)
dante = (t:n) (w:punishments/terrors) (d:plural of dan in the sense of punishment, elsewhere written daan; the NIV has terrors) (e:nangma ~ ka thuak hi) (r:19.88.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapin = (t:v) (w:line/panel) (d:dap line a surface with boards, with the linking ending in) (e:taaksan tawh a innpi kawm ~ kham hoih) (b:dap) (r:14.3.5) (q:draft)
daplan = (t:adj) (w:cunning/crafty/shrewd) (d:of the mind, lungsim daplan: clever in a scheming way) (e:A lungsim ~ lua ahih manin) (r:27.8.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
dapphahte = (t:n) (w:saddle blankets/saddle cloths) (d:dap pad with phah spread and the plural te: cloths spread on the back of a horse for riding) (e:sakol ~ hong pia uh hi) (r:26.27.20) (q:draft)
daptakin = (t:adv) (w:silently/speechlessly/in silence) (d:dap silent or dumbfounded, with takin which makes an adverb: without saying a word, in wonder or dismay) (e:mipa in ~ tua nu na en hi) (b:dap) (r:1.24.21/27.8.27) (q:draft)
daupainate = (t:n) (w:blessings/prosperity/good things) (d:plural of daupaina prosperity) (e:Israelte tungah ka piak ~ khempeuh) (b:daupaina) (r:9.2.32) (q:draft)
dawhkik = (t:v) (w:revoke/withdraw/recall) (d:dawh pull out, with kik back: take back a written order) (e:a laigelhte ~ nadingin lai khat gelhsak in) (b:dawh) (r:17.8.5) (q:draft)
dawhna = (t:n) (w:vat) (d:dawh hold out to receive, with the noun suffix na: in leenggahtui dawhna, the vat that catches the juice of the winepress) (e:leenggahtui ~ dim letin a luang) (b:dawh) (r:29.3.13) (q:draft)
dawksa-in = (t:adj) (w:bared/exposed/uncovered) (d:dawk stick out or show, with sa already done and the linking ending in: with a part of the body left showing) (e:tangguak kheguakin, tawbo ~) (r:23.20.4) (q:draft)
dawksakin = (t:v) (w:stretch out/put out/extend) (d:dawk stick out, with the causative sak and the linking ending in: holding out the tip of a staff) (e:a khut sunga om ciangkhut dawn ~) (b:dawksak) (r:7.6.21) (q:draft)
dawktoh = (t:v) (w:rise up/tower/jut up) (d:dawk jut out, with toh upward: stand up high above the surroundings, said of a mountain) (e:tuipi tungah sangpi-in a ~ bangin) (r:24.46.18) (q:draft)
dawmin = (t:v) (w:deal gently with/treat with care) (d:dawm treat with care, with the linking ending in: gently, considerately) (e:na zite uh ~ na hehpih un) (b:dawm) (r:60.3.7/45.12.10) (q:draft)
dawngdawng = (t:v) (w:keep answering/answer again and again) (d:dawng answer, doubled: go on answering what is asked) (e:hai thudotna ~ lecin, nang zong) (r:20.26.4) (q:draft)
dawngkikin = (t:v) (w:answering/replying) (d:dawngkik answer back, with the linking suffix in: answered and went on to say) (e:a nasempa in Saul ~) (b:dawngkik) (r:9.9.8/11.2.31) (q:draft)
dawnkha = (t:v) (w:get to drink/drink) (d:dawn drink with kha, which shows that the action comes to happen; with kei, never get to drink) (e:a zu na ~ kei ding uh hi) (r:33.6.15/30.5.11) (q:draft)
dawnkhia = (t:v) (w:bud/sprout/put out shoots) (d:dawn, the tip or shoot of a plant, with khia out) (e:Israel palhin ~ ding a) (b:dawn) (r:23.27.6) (q:draft)
dawnngekte = (t:n) (w:shoots/tender shoots) (d:dawnngek, the young tender tip of a branch, with the plural te) (e:a ~ in Gunpi lam zuan hi) (r:19.80.11) (q:draft)
dawnpah = (t:v) (w:answer promptly/reply at once) (d:dawn, the form of dawng answer used before a suffix, with pah at once) (e:A hun mahin ~ theihna lungkimhuai a) (r:20.15.23) (q:draft)
dawnpawlte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:melons) (d:named after cucumbers in the list of the foods of Egypt, where the English has melons; with the plural te) (e:ngasate, tangmaite, ~, lo-uih neute) (r:4.11.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
dawnsim = (t:v) (w:drink secretly/drink in secret) (d:dawn drink with sim secretly; of stolen water in the proverb) (e:Tui ~, khum diak a) (r:20.9.17) (q:draft)
dawntheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to answer/being able to answer) (d:dawn, the form of dawng answer used before a suffix, with theih can and the noun suffix na) (e:thudotna haksa nonote ~) (r:27.5.12/41.12.28) (q:draft)
dawnzum = (t:n) (w:peak/pointed summit) (d:dawn top with zum pointed; a mountain with many peaks is called rugged in the English) (e:aw mual ~ tampi a nei Bashan mual) (r:19.68.15/19.68.16) (q:draft)
dedu = (t:adv) (w:intently/deeply) (d:placed after lungngai think: describes thinking long and hard about something, pondering) (e:nangma thu lungngai ~ ding uh a) (r:23.14.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
deek = (t:v) (w:bargain/barter/haggle) (d:bargain over a thing in order to buy it) (e:lei dingin hong ~ ding a) (r:18.41.6) (q:draft)
deenglum = (t:v) (w:stone to death/stone) (d:with suang tawh, kill by throwing stones; deng throw at, written with a long vowel, with lum, which shows that the blow kills) (e:suang tawh amah ~ ding uh hi) (r:3.20.2/43.8.5) (q:draft)
deidai = (t:adv) (w:very/intensely) (d:placed after kha bitter, to strengthen it: very bitter, as bitter as the venom of snakes) (e:gulgu a khapen zahin kha ~ hi) (r:18.20.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihkik = (t:v) (w:want again/desire again) (d:deih want with kik again) (e:Kumpipa in a ~ kei leh) (b:deih) (r:17.2.14) (q:draft)
deihlam = (t:n) (w:that one wants/the fact of wanting) (d:deih want with lam, which turns the clause into the thing that is known: ka deihlam is that I want) (e:ka ~ hong thei na hih leh) (r:40.25.26/42.19.22) (q:draft)
deihlua = (t:v) (w:want too much/be greedy for/love excessively) (d:deih want with lua too much; with sum, be a lover of money) (e:sum a ~ lo mite hi ding) (b:deih) (r:54.3.3/54.6.10) (q:draft)
deihluat = (t:v) (w:want too much/crave/love excessively) (d:form of deihlua used before leh, in and mahmah and in dependent clauses; also as a noun, craving) (e:hih leitung nate a ~ leh) (b:deihlua) (r:62.2.15/19.106.14) (q:draft)
deihtakin = (t:adv) (w:earnestly/eagerly) (d:deih want with takin, which makes an adverb: with real desire, earnestly) (e:kiangah ~ thu ka ngen hi) (b:deih) (r:27.9.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
deihthuah = (t:v) (w:want more/want in addition) (d:deih want with thuah in addition: desire still more on top of what one has) (e:huaihamin gam a ~ manun) (r:30.1.13/21.6.9) (q:draft)
deihzawkna = (t:n) (w:preference/preferring) (d:deihzaw prefer, in the form deihzawk, with the noun suffix na: liking one more than another) (e:keimah sangin milim a ~ uh hangin) (r:26.6.9/5.21.16) (q:draft)
dekdekte = (t:n) (w:those about to/those on the point of) (d:dekdek almost, about to, with the plural te: a si dekdekte is those who are about to die, the perishing) (e:A si ~, khamtheihzu pia) (b:dekdek) (r:20.31.6) (q:draft)
dekna = (t:n) (w:being about to/being on the point of) (d:dek almost, about to, with the noun suffix na: ka sih dekna is my being close to dying, faint with love in the English) (e:lungzuangin ka sih ~ na gensak un) (b:dek) (r:22.5.8) (q:draft)
demlai = (t:v) (w:still oppose/continue to defy) (d:dem contend with, defy, with lai still: keep on being hostile) (e:kei na hong ~ uhleh) (r:3.26.23/3.26.27) (q:draft)
demna = (t:n) (w:hostility/opposition/rivalry) (d:dem contend with, defy, with the noun suffix na) (e:kei hong ~ uh hangin) (b:dem) (r:3.26.40/50.1.17) (q:draft)
demnopna = (t:n) (w:defiance/obstinacy/rebelliousness) (d:dem defy with nop want to and the noun suffix na: the wish to oppose; demnopna lungsim is a defiant, obstinate heart) (e:~ lungsim nei uh hi) (r:26.3.7/16.9.26) (q:draft)
demte = (t:n) (w:opponents/foes/those who defy) (d:dem contend with, defy, with the plural te: those who set themselves against someone) (e:amah a ~ koihkhong lo a) (b:dem) (r:34.1.2) (q:draft)
dengkhia = (t:v) (w:sweep away/beat down/knock away) (d:deng pelt, strike, with khia out, away; of hail that strikes a shelter and carries it off) (e:na zuau buk uh ~ ding a) (b:deng) (r:23.28.17) (q:draft)
dengnuam = (t:v) (w:want to stone/wish to stone) (d:deng throw at, stone, with nuam want to) (e:manin hong ~ ka hi kei uh a) (r:43.10.33) (q:draft)
dengvui = (t:v) (w:turn to dust/crush to dust) (d:deng throw down, strike, with vui dust as in leivui: break down into dust) (e:hong ~ kik ding na hi hiam) (r:18.10.9) (q:draft)
dengzanin = (t:v) (w:smashing/dashing to pieces) (d:dengzan dash to pieces, with the linking suffix in: smash and go on to the next action) (e:a biakna songte uh ~) (b:dengzan) (r:5.7.5/5.12.3) (q:draft)
denkhap = (t:v) (w:dash down/smash/shatter) (d:throw a thing down so that it breaks, as a potter dashes a pot or as walls are thrown down) (e:beel a ~ bangin leilakah) (r:19.2.9/23.26.5) (q:draft)
densa = (t:adj) (w:long-standing/lasting/perpetual) (d:den always, continually, with sa already done: a sia densa mun is a place that has lain in ruins all along) (e:A sia ~ munah hong) (b:den) (r:19.74.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
deudaute = (t:n) (w:those in procession/those lined up) (d:deudau, in a long row, with the plural te: mihon kigual deudaute is the crowd of people drawn up in line) (e:mihon kigual ~ lakah) (b:deudau) (r:19.45.14/19.45.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
diakah = (t:adv) (w:just/right) (d:diak with the place marker ah; in mai diakah, right in front of, just ahead of) (e:note mai ~ om hi) (b:diak) (r:9.9.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
dialkhipte = (t:n) (w:turbans/headdresses/tiaras) (d:dialkhip, a cloth wound round the head, with the plural te) (e:~ leh kikhuhna puante lakhia ding hi) (b:dialkhip) (r:23.3.23) (q:draft)
didi = (t:adv) (w:gently/steadily) (d:placed after luang flow: describes water running on quietly and steadily) (e:a luang ~ Shiloah tuite nial uh a) (r:23.8.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
dikdekin = (t:adv) (w:thoroughly/completely) (d:dikdek, an intensifier after a descriptive word, with the suffix in; a kaang dikdekin is turned quite white or scorched right through, of blighted crops) (e:a kaang ~ ka bawl hi) (b:dikdek) (r:30.4.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
diklote = (t:n) (w:the unrighteous/wrongdoers/unjust people) (d:dik righteous with lo not and the plural te; used after mi, people) (e:mi ~ tangding mawhna hangin) (r:60.3.18/46.6.9) (q:draft)
diknopna = (t:n) (w:wish to be gracious/desire to show favour) (d:dik gracious, kind, with nop want to and na: ka diknopna mite is the people I wish to be gracious to) (e:Ka ~ mite tungah ka dik ding a) (r:2.33.19) (q:draft)
diksakpa = (t:n) (w:justifier/the one who justifies) (d:diksak justify with pa, marking a man: he who declares righteous, said of God) (e:A ~ in Pasian ahi hi) (b:diksak) (r:45.8.33/45.4.5) (q:draft)
