gilvahte = (t:n) (w:the full/those who are well fed) (d:gilvah be full with plural te, the opposite of gilkialte, the hungry) (e:A ~ in an thalawh uh a) (b:gilvah) (r:9.2.5) (q:draft)
gimbawlin = (t:v) (w:oppress/treat harshly) (d:form of gimbawl, gim suffering with bawl do, with the linking suffix in) (e:Na pa in hong ~ vangik hong suan hi) (r:14.10.4/11.12.4) (q:draft)
