haknawte = (t:n) (w:lead) (d:haknaw lead with plural te, closing a list of metals) (e:dal, leh ~ hong pia uh hi) (b:haknaw) (r:26.27.12) (q:draft)
haksak = (t:v) (w:open/cause to open) (d:hak, of the eyes be open, with the causative sak: open someone's eyes) (e:Pasian in ama mit ~ a) (b:hak) (r:1.21.19) (q:draft)
haksalua = (t:adj) (w:too hard/too difficult) (d:haksa hard with lua, too much) (e:a ~ khat beek om lo hi) (b:haksa) (r:24.32.17/5.17.8) (q:draft)
hakte = (t:n) (w:hard things/secrets/mysteries) (d:hak hard to do with plural te; thu theih hakte, the things that are hard to know, are the secrets or mysteries) (e:Vantung Gam thu theih ~ na theih nadingun) (b:hak) (r:40.13.11/41.4.11) (q:draft)
halpa = (t:n) (w:one who burns/burner) (d:hal burn with pa, the man who does it) (e:Tuate a ~ in ama puante sawpin) (b:hal) (r:3.16.28/26.20.48) (q:draft)
halte = (t:n) (w:those who burn) (d:hal burn with te, the ones who; in the verse those who burned incense) (e:paknamtui a ~ zong hawlkhia hi) (b:hal) (r:12.23.5) (q:draft)
