hoisuk = (t:v) (w:reel/stagger) (d:hoi stagger with suk downward, in the pair hoisuk hoito, reel this way and that) (e:zukham bangin ~ hoito uh a) (b:hoi) (r:19.107.27) (q:draft)
hoito = (t:v) (w:reel/stagger) (d:hoi stagger with to upward, in the pair hoisuk hoito, reel this way and that) (e:zukham bangin hoisuk ~ uh a) (b:hoi) (r:19.107.27) (q:draft)
honkhiat = (t:v) (w:deliver/rescue/save) (d:form of honkhia used before another word such as theih or ding) (e:note hong ~ theih nadingin) (b:honkhia) (r:14.32.14) (q:draft)
honkhiat = (t:v) (w:open/break open) (d:hon open with khiat out, said of opening a seal) (e:khat a ~ ka mu hi) (b:hon) (r:66.6.1) (q:draft)
honkhiate = (t:n) (w:deliverers/saviours) (d:honkhia deliver with plural te: those who deliver) (e:a honkhia ding ~ na puak hi) (b:honkhia) (r:16.9.27) (q:draft)
honsakin = (t:v) (w:opening/opening for) (d:hon open with sak, for someone, and the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:hankhuk hong ~ kong paikhiatpih ciangin) (b:hon) (r:26.37.13/33.2.13) (q:draft)
hontangte = (t:n) (w:band/gang/crowd) (d:hontang with plural te, a whole band of people; migilo hontangte, a band of evildoers) (e:Gilead pen migilo ~’ omna khuapi hi a) (r:28.6.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
hopihpah = (t:v) (w:speak to at once/address immediately) (d:hopih speak to with pah at once) (e:Jesuh in amaute ~ a) (r:40.14.27/41.6.50) (q:draft)
hopihpih = (t:v) (w:speak to repeatedly/keep speaking to) (d:hopih speak to with its last syllable doubled, said of speaking to someone again and again; tam veipi is many times) (e:tam veipi a ~ hi) (b:hopih) (r:24.1.3) (q:draft)
hotte = (t:n) (w:rowers/oarsmen) (d:hot row with plural te: those who row) (e:Nang hong ~ in tuipi thukna gamlapi-ah) (b:hot) (r:26.27.26) (q:draft)
huaihamnate = (t:n) (w:greed/covetous desires) (d:plural of huaihamna: kinds or acts of greed) (e:han’ sanna leh ~ a dim hi) (b:huaihamna) (r:40.23.25/49.5.3) (q:draft)
huainuam = (t:v) (w:want to gather/long to shelter) (d:huai, gather under the wings as a hen covers her chicks, with nuam want) (e:na mite ka ~ tawntung a) (r:40.23.37/42.13.34) (q:draft)
hualin = (t:v) (w:rolling) (d:hual roll with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows: roll a stone, and) (e:suangtum khat ~ a kongvang a hu hi) (r:41.15.46/40.27.60) (q:draft)
huamkha = (t:v) (w:involve/include/take in) (d:huam include with kha reach, touch: take in or affect all of a group) (e:amaute khempeuh ~ ahih manin) (r:4.15.26) (q:draft)
huamkhin = (t:v) (w:include all/cover completely) (d:huam include with khin completely) (e:na khempeuh a ~ hita hi) (b:huam) (r:58.2.8/46.15.27) (q:draft)
huantui = (t:v) (w:smelt/melt out) (d:melt metal out of ore; apparently huan cook, heat with tui liquid) (e:suang sung panin sumsan ~ uh hi) (r:18.28.2) (q:draft)
huathuai = (t:adj) (w:hateful/odious/obnoxious) (d:huat hate with huai worthy of: fit to be hated) (e:Israelte a ~ ahihna zong) (r:9.13.4) (q:draft)
huhsak = (t:v) (w:help/sustain) (d:huh help with sak, cause or let something help a person) (e:kei hong ~ in) (b:huh) (r:19.119.175) (q:draft)
huhthei = (t:v) (w:can help/be able to help/be helpful) (d:huh help with thei can) (e:tua bang a thuakte a hong ~ hi) (b:huh) (r:58.2.18/55.4.11) (q:draft)
hui-ah = (t:adv) (w:along the edge/at the border) (d:follows nawl edge, a nawl hui-ah, said of a crop sown at the edge of a field; hui with the place marker ah, exact meaning of hui not certain) (e:a nawl ~ tuh) (r:23.28.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
huiheek = (t:v) (w:twist/distort/turn upside down) (d:said of the face of the earth being twisted out of shape and ruined; heek is twist) (e:amah in lei maitang ~ gawpin) (r:23.24.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
huihkua = (t:n) (w:storehouse of the wind/wind chamber) (d:huih wind with kua hole, den: the place where the wind is kept) (e:a ~ panin huih a pusuaksak hi) (r:19.135.7/24.10.13) (q:draft)
huknate = (t:n) (w:lewdness/lusts/lewd acts) (d:plural of hukna) (e:Na ~ leh Izipt gam-a kipan) (b:hukna) (r:26.23.27) (q:draft)
hukte = (t:n) (w:ones in heat) (d:huk be in heat with plural te, said of female wild donkeys at mating time) (e:laano ~ na bang zen hi) (b:huk) (r:24.2.24) (q:draft)
humhamin = (t:adv) (w:growling) (d:humham growl with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:~ a sa nek ding uh man uh a) (b:humham) (r:23.5.29) (q:draft)
humna = (t:n) (w:beating/covering) (d:hum cover, press with the hand, with the noun suffix na; dip humna is beating the breast in grief, wailing) (e:kahna, leh dip ~ om hi) (b:hum) (r:17.4.3) (q:draft)
humpinelkaipa = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:lion) (d:humpinelkai lion with pa, the male, paired in the verses with humpinelkaipi lioness) (e:~ bangin kaang to hi) (b:humpinelkai) (r:4.23.24/4.24.9) (q:draft)
humsakin = (t:v) (w:covering/shutting) (d:hum cover with sak cause and the linking ending in: cause the eyes to be covered, and) (e:amah in a mit uh ~) (b:hum) (r:23.44.18) (q:draft)
humsan = (t:v) (w:hide from/cover against) (d:hum cover with san: cover the face so as not to look at someone) (e:a mai uh a ~ mipa bangin) (b:hum) (r:23.53.3) (q:draft)
hunlopi-in = (t:adv) (w:at the wrong time/at any time one likes) (d:hun time with lo not, pi and the ending in: when it is not the proper time) (e:A ~ hong pai leh amah si ding hi) (r:3.16.2) (q:draft)
hunpha = (t:n) (w:opportunity/good chance/privilege) (d:hun time with pha good: a favourable time or chance given to do something) (e:kote tungah ~ hong piaktheih nadingin) (r:51.4.3/50.1.29) (q:draft)
hunpi = (t:n) (w:long time/great while) (d:hun time with pi great: a long period) (e:a hong tung ding ~ khat sung) (b:hun) (r:13.17.17) (q:draft)
hunsau = (t:n) (w:long time) (d:hun time with sau long, the opposite of hun tomno, a short time) (e:~ sungin ahi zongin) (r:44.26.29/27.2.8) (q:draft)
hunsia = (t:n) (w:bad time/evil time/unfavourable time) (d:hun time with sia bad, the opposite of hunhoih) (e:hunhoih ~ cih khen tuan loin) (r:55.4.2/21.9.12) (q:draft)
hupipa = (t:n) (w:protector/defender) (d:hu protect, defend with pi great and pa, a man: the great protector; said of Elijah and Elisha as the defence of Israel, where the NIV has the chariots and horsemen of Israel) (e:Israel mite a ~) (r:12.2.12/12.13.14) (q:draft)
hupna = (t:n) (w:sponge) (d:hup soak up with the noun suffix na; tui hupna, a thing that soaks up liquid, a sponge) (e:tui ~ la-in tuithuk sungah a diah) (b:hup) (r:40.27.48/41.15.36) (q:draft)
husam = (t:v) (w:gasp/pant/be out of breath) (d:hu breath with sam: be short of breath) (e:Zion’ tanu ~ liang-a a kikona aw) (r:24.4.31) (q:draft)
husamin = (t:adv) (w:gasping/breathless) (d:husam gasp with the linking ending in, used when another verb follows) (e:dahin ~ ka bah gawp hi) (b:husam) (r:25.2.11) (q:draft)
husiatna = (t:n) (w:destructive force/fury) (d:paired with vangliatna power in na hehna’ husiatna, apparently the destroying force of anger; siatna is destruction, exact meaning not certain) (e:na hehna’ ~ kua in thei ahi hiam) (r:19.90.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
huthut = (t:adv) (d:follows tau groan, said of stallions neighing with desire, apparently imitating a snorting sound; exact meaning not certain) (e:nehin a tau ~ uh hi) (r:24.5.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
ihihlam = (t:n) (d:i we with hihlam, the fact of being: that we are, followed by thei or kithei know) (e:Pasian tate a it ~ i kithei ding hi) (b:hihlam) (r:62.5.2/45.6.3) (q:draft)
ihsip = (t:v) (w:sleep deeply/be fast asleep) (d:ih sleep with sip: be in deep sleep) (e:Mi a ~ hun zankim laitak) (r:18.4.13) (q:draft)
