kangto = (t:v) (w:rise up/lift up) (d:kang, rise into the air, with to, upward) (e:a leengpeite tawh zong ~ khawm hi) (r:26.1.19) (q:draft)
kangtumsa = (t:adj) (w:burned/burned up) (d:kangtum burn up, with sa, already done) (e:a ~ nin bulomtang panin) (b:kangtum) (r:16.4.2) (q:draft)
kangtumsakin = (t:v) (w:burning up/burning away) (d:kangtumsak burn up, with the connective in; of a refiner burning away dross) (e:A ninte ~, ngunte a siangsakpa bangin) (b:kangtumsak) (r:39.3.3) (q:draft)
kankhiat = (t:v) (w:find out/search out/sound out) (d:form of kankhia used before khit ciangin and similar words) (e:ka pa’ ngaihsutna tawng ka ~ khit ciangin) (b:kankhia) (r:9.20.12) (q:draft)
kansak = (t:v) (w:dry up/make dry) (d:cause water to dry up; also written kangsak) (e:Topa na Pasian un a ~ San Tuipi) (r:6.4.23) (q:draft)
kansak = (t:v) (w:have inquire/have looked into) (d:kan search, ask, with sak, cause: have someone find out about a matter) (e:tua numei’ thu ~ hi) (b:kan) (r:10.11.3) (q:draft)
