kihtakhuaite = (t:adj) (w:fearsome/dreadful/dangerous) (d:kihtakhuai with the plural te, which belongs to the whole phrase: gamsa kihtakhuaite are fierce wild beasts) (e:a that dingin gamsa ~) (b:kihtakhuai) (r:26.14.15) (q:draft)
kihtakin = (t:v) (w:fearing/dreading/in fear of) (d:kihtak fear with the connective in; kihtakin nei is hold in dread) (e:hong kampau ding ~ ka nei) (b:kihtak) (r:18.31.34) (q:draft)
kihtakte = (t:n) (w:things feared/what one fears) (d:kihtak fear with the plural te: the things that someone is afraid of) (e:Amaute’ ~ kihta kei un la) (b:kihtak) (r:23.8.12) (q:draft)
kihualsak = (t:v) (w:roll over/drive over) (d:with sak cause: make the wheel of a threshing cart roll round over the grain) (e:a ~ ciangin amah in) (r:23.28.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
