kikhelsak = (t:v) (w:turn/make change) (d:kikhel, change one's ways, with the causative sak: make someone turn away from a way of life or conduct) (e:panin zong ~ khinzo ding uh hi) (b:kikhel) (r:24.23.22) (q:draft)
kikhennate = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:plural of kikhenna: the groups into which the priests were divided for their service) (e:siampite a pawlpawlin a ~) (b:kikhenna) (r:14.8.14) (q:draft)
kikhensakzo = (t:v) (w:be able to separate/separate) (d:kikhensak, separate, with zo, be able) (e:tawh hong ~ het lo ding hi) (b:kikhensak) (r:45.8.38/45.8.35) (q:draft)
