kikuaitan = (t:v) (w:be broken/be snapped) (d:kuaitan, break in two, with the prefix ki; of a bone or a branch) (e:A guh khat beek a ~ kei ding hi) (b:kuaitan) (r:43.19.36/26.19.12) (q:draft)
kikuaitansa = (t:adj) (w:broken/splintered) (d:kikuaitan, be broken, with sa, already done: that has been broken, of a reed) (e:a ~ pumpeng ciangkhut tawh a kibang) (b:kikuaitan) (r:23.36.6) (q:draft)
kikuan = (t:v) (w:go/go out) (d:kuan, set out for a task, with the prefix ki used without a named subject: people go out to work) (e:nasemin ~ nawn lo hi) (b:kuan) (r:18.24.18) (q:draft)
kikui = (t:v) (w:cut oneself/gash oneself) (d:kui, cut the skin, with the reflexive prefix ki; done to the body as a sign of mourning) (e:a pumpi uh a ~ gawp sa-in) (b:kui) (r:24.41.5) (q:draft)
kikuikham = (t:v) (w:be ripped open/be cut open) (d:said of pregnant women killed in war) (e:a nupi naupaaite uh ~ ding hi) (b:kuikham) (r:28.13.16) (q:draft)
kikunsak = (t:v) (w:be bowed down/be made to stoop) (d:kun, bow or stoop, with the prefix ki and the causative sak) (e:keimah hong ~ a, hong kibokcipsak hi) (r:19.38.6) (q:draft)
kil = (t:adj) (w:wavy/curly) (d:of hair; kil thiuhtheuh describes long hair that falls in waves) (e:A sam sau-in ~ thiuhtheuh a) (r:22.5.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilaakin = (t:v) (w:appear/present oneself) (d:kilaak, show oneself, with the linking ending in) (e:Moab amahmah hong ~) (b:kilaak) (r:23.16.12) (q:draft)
kilahkhiat = (t:v) (w:be revealed/be shown forth) (d:lahkhiat, reveal, with the prefix ki; the form used before ding and hun) (e:upna thu a ~ ding ngakna-in) (b:lahkhiat) (r:48.3.23/45.8.19) (q:draft)
kilahsa = (t:v) (w:appeared/have appeared) (d:kilah, show oneself, with sa for a completed action; a kilahsa bangin, as he had appeared) (e:ama tungah a ~ bangin Solomon tungah) (b:kilah) (r:11.9.2) (q:draft)
kilaigawp = (t:v) (w:struggle together/jostle) (d:kilai, fight with one another, with gawp, roughly or violently) (e:Ama sungah a naute ~ hi) (b:kilai) (r:1.25.22) (q:draft)
kilaithang = (t:v) (w:attack one another/fight one another) (d:with khat leh khat, one another, of people in panic who turn on each other) (e:khat leh khat ~ gawp ding uh hi) (r:38.14.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilakkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:be taken away/be removed) (d:kilakkhiat, be taken away, with sak; of a kingdom taken from a king and of sin removed) (e:Na kumpi gam hong ~ zo hi) (b:kilakkhiat) (r:27.4.31/23.27.9) (q:draft)
kilaklo = (t:v) (w:not be shown/not be given) (d:kilak, be shown, with lo, not, written as one word; of a sign that will not be shown) (e:adang hong ~ ding hi) (b:kilak) (r:40.12.39/40.16.4) (q:draft)
kilaksa = (t:v) (w:shown/have been shown) (d:kilak, be shown, with sa for a completed action; hong kilaksa bangin, as it was shown to you) (e:nang tungah hong ~ bangin kibawl ding hi) (b:kilak) (r:2.27.8) (q:draft)
kilamet = (t:v) (w:expect/hope for) (d:lamet, hope or expect, with the prefix ki) (e:An hau dingin na ~ uh hangin) (b:lamet) (r:37.1.9) (q:draft)
kilamsa = (t:adj) (w:built) (d:kilam, be built, with sa, already done: that was built, placed before the thing built) (e:a ~ inn a lamkik ka hi uh hi) (b:kilam) (r:15.5.11) (q:draft)
kilamsang = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be exalted) (d:lift oneself up high or be lifted up high; the opposite of kiniamkhiat, humble oneself) (e:A kiniamkhiat peuhmah a ~ ding hi) (r:40.23.12) (q:draft)
kilangbawlna = (t:n) (w:opposition/hostility/enmity) (d:langbawlna, opposition, with the prefix ki: being set against one another, or being opposed by others) (e:milim biakna, mi bumna, ~, kitotna) (b:langbawlna) (r:48.5.20/52.2.2) (q:draft)
kilangsakkik = (t:v) (w:make appear again/show again) (d:kilangsak, cause to appear, with kik, again; of Christ shown alive after his death and of his future appearing) (e:Jesuh hong ~ ding hi) (b:kilangsak) (r:54.6.15/44.10.40) (q:draft)
kilatsakna = (t:n) (w:showing/proof) (d:kilatsak, make plain to see, with the noun suffix na; teci kilatsakna, the showing of proof, stands where the English has character) (e:Thuakzawhna in teci ~ a piangsak hi) (b:kilatsak) (r:45.5.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilausak = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be made afraid) (d:lausak, frighten, with the prefix ki) (e:Amaute nakpitakin ~ ding a) (b:lausak) (r:23.44.11) (q:draft)
kilawhgawp = (t:v) (w:break out/spread all over) (d:kilawh, spread, of a skin disease, with gawp, severely: of boils breaking out on people and animals) (e:meimatum piangsakin ~ hi) (b:kilawh) (r:2.9.10/2.9.9) (q:draft)
kilawmzah = (t:n) (w:due amount/as much as is fitting) (d:kilawm, fitting, with zah, amount: as much as one deserves or ought) (e:a theih dingin a ~ a thei nai lo) (r:46.8.2/15.9.13) (q:draft)
kilawng = (t:v) (w:be touched) (d:lawng, touch, with the prefix ki; khut tawh kilawng, be touched with the hand) (e:khut guak tawh amaute ~ ngam lo a) (b:lawng) (r:10.23.6/58.12.18) (q:draft)
kilawnthal = (t:v) (w:be overthrown/be destroyed) (d:lawnthal, overthrow, with the prefix ki; of cities thrown down) (e:Admah le Zeboiim bangin a ~ gawp) (b:lawnthal) (r:5.29.23) (q:draft)
kilawnto-in = (t:v) (w:be thrown up/be tossed up) (d:kilawn, be thrown, with to, up, and the linking ending in; of sailors lifted high by the waves) (e:vanah ~, a thukna-ah kiasuk uh hi) (r:19.107.26) (q:draft)
kilehhek = (t:v) (w:be betrayed/betray one another) (d:lehhek, betray, with the prefix ki: be betrayed, or with khatlekhat, betray each other) (e:Topa Jesuh a ~ ding nitakin) (b:lehhek) (r:46.11.23/40.24.10) (q:draft)
kilehin = (t:v) (w:return/turn back) (d:kileh, turn back, with the linking ending in: going back and then) (e:~ Jordan gunpang ah ding hi) (b:kileh) (r:12.2.13) (q:draft)
kileipa = (t:n) (w:bought slave/one who is bought) (d:kilei, be bought, with pa marking a man: a man bought with money, set beside one born in the household) (e:na sum tawh a ~ hita leh) (b:kilei) (r:1.17.13) (q:draft)
kilemsakkik = (t:v) (w:reconcile/bring back to peace) (d:kilemsak, reconcile, with kik, again; of the one who makes peace between two parties) (e:Pasian le mite a hong ~ thei) (b:kilemsak) (r:54.2.5/39.4.6) (q:draft)
kilemte = (t:adj) (w:at peace/secure) (d:kilem, be at peace, with the plural te; gam kilemte, lands that are at peace) (e:gam ~ nangawn a sim ding hi) (b:kilem) (r:27.11.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilensa-in = (t:v) (w:holding one another/hand in hand) (d:len, hold, with the reciprocal prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; khut kilensa-in, holding hands) (e:a lawmpa tawh khut ~) (r:22.8.5) (q:draft)
kilh = (t:v) (w:nail/fasten) (d:fasten something with nails so that it cannot be moved) (e:sik tawh a ~ uh hi) (r:24.10.4) (q:draft)
kilhcip = (t:v) (w:nail fast/crucify) (d:kilh, nail, with cip, tightly; singlamteh tungah kilhcip is nail to the cross) (e:singlamteh tungah Jesuh ~ uh a) (b:kilh) (r:42.23.33) (q:draft)
kiliatsak = (t:v) (w:exalt oneself/be lifted up) (d:liatsak, make great, with the reflexive prefix ki; of the heart being lifted up over others) (e:ama lungsim a ~ loh nading) (b:liatsak) (r:5.17.19/5.17.20) (q:draft)
kilim = (t:todo) (q:draft, found only in thupha hong kilim piak, be blessed, Deuteronomy 7.14; what kilim adds is not clear)
kilingin = (t:v) (w:tremble/shake) (d:kiling, be shaken, with the linking ending in; of the earth trembling) (e:a et ciangin tua leitung ~) (b:kiling) (r:19.104.31) (q:draft)
kilokhia = (t:v) (w:be designated/be called out) (d:kilo, be named, with khia, out; a minin a kilokhia, singled out by name) (e:a minin a ~ midang omlai hi) (b:kilo) (r:13.16.41/15.10.16) (q:draft)
kilomin = (t:v) (w:huddle together/crowd together) (d:of people gathered close in a heap; compare lom, heap) (e:sawlkawm nuai-ah ~ omkhawm uh hi) (b:lomin) (r:18.30.7) (q:draft)
kilosa = (t:adj) (w:named/specified) (d:kilo, be named, with sa, already done; a min kilosa, whose names have been called) (e:a min ~ hih mite khawmin) (b:kilo) (r:4.1.17) (q:draft)
kiluansakna = (t:n) (w:shedding/flowing) (d:with sisan, blood: sisan kiluansakna is bloodshed, where the English has only blood) (e:Sisan ~, meikatna le meikhu sahpi) (r:44.2.19/29.2.30) (q:draft)
kiluhin = (t:v) (w:be plundered/be looted) (d:kiluh, be plundered, with the linking ending in) (e:inn ~, a zite uh kibuansak ding hi) (b:kiluh) (r:23.13.16) (q:draft)
kilukhuhsa-in = (t:v) (w:with head covered/having covered the head) (d:lu, head, and khuh, cover, with the reflexive prefix ki, sa for a completed action and the linking ending in; a sign of grief or shame) (e:Haman ahih leh ~ a thuum kawmin) (r:17.6.12) (q:draft)
kilumletin = (t:v) (w:be overturned/overturn) (d:kilumlet, be turned over, with the linking ending in; of a tent knocked over) (e:puanbuk ~ lei lakah kiphah hi) (r:7.7.13) (q:draft)
kilunggimsak = (t:v) (w:trouble oneself/make oneself anxious) (d:lunggimsak, make heavy in heart, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Note ~ kei un la) (b:lunggimsak) (r:21.11.10) (q:draft)
kilunggulhna = (t:n) (w:lust/desire for one another) (d:kilunggulh, desire one another, with the noun suffix na; of sexual desire) (e:pasal le pasal ~ ciang dong) (b:kilunggulh) (r:65.1.7/52.4.4) (q:draft)
kilunghimawh = (t:v) (w:worry/be troubled) (d:lunghimawh, worry, with the prefix ki used without a named subject: one has worry or sorrow) (e:Pil semsem lehang ~ semsem a) (b:lunghimawh) (r:21.1.18) (q:draft)
kilungkhamsak = (t:v) (w:distress oneself/be upset) (d:lungkhamsak, make troubled, with the reflexive prefix ki; with kei in, do not let yourself be troubled) (e:Hih thu hangin nangmah ~ kei in) (b:lungkhamsak) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft)
kilungnuamsak = (t:v) (w:comfort oneself/set one's mind at ease) (d:lungnuamsak, make glad or at ease, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Bangbang hitaleh ~ in, ka sanggamnu aw) (b:lungnuamsak) (r:10.13.20) (q:draft)
kilup = (t:v) (w:be lain with) (d:lup, lie down, with the prefix ki; kilup khoppih, be lain with, of sexual intercourse) (e:Hong ~ khoppih lohna mun) (b:lup) (r:24.3.2) (q:draft)
kilutpih = (t:v) (w:be brought in/be taken in) (d:lutpih, bring in, with the prefix ki; of goods carried into a town) (e:khua sungah van hong ~ loh nadingin) (b:lutpih) (r:16.13.19) (q:draft)
kima-sialh = (t:v) (w:boast/brag) (d:boast about oneself; compare kisialh, boast) (e:Zing ciang hun-a ding ~ kei in) (r:20.27.1) (q:draft)
kimaitaisak = (t:v) (w:cheer oneself up/put on a cheerful face) (d:maitaisak, make cheerful, with the reflexive prefix ki) (e:Ka dahnate kimangngilh bawlin ~ ding) (b:maitaisak) (r:18.9.27) (q:draft)
kimaizumsak = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be shamed) (d:maizumsak, put to shame, with the prefix ki) (e:Siatna hun ciangin amaute ~ lo a) (b:maizumsak) (r:19.37.19) (q:draft)
kimamsak = (t:v) (w:be straightened/be made straight) (d:mamsak, straighten, with the prefix ki) (e:A kawisate ~ thei lo a) (b:mamsak) (r:21.1.15) (q:draft)
kimancip = (t:v) (w:be held captive/be seized) (d:mancip, seize and hold fast, with the prefix ki; a kimancip before a noun is captive) (e:A ~ Jerusalem mite aw) (b:mancip) (r:23.52.2) (q:draft)
kimansiang = (t:v) (w:be completed/be finished) (d:kiman, finished, with siang, clean: be wholly finished, of work carried through to the end) (e:nasep khempeuh ~ hi) (b:kiman) (r:14.8.16) (q:draft)
kimap = (t:v) (w:be spared) (d:of a life, be spared, be left alive) (e:na nuntakna hong ~ ding hi) (r:24.38.20/24.38.17) (q:draft)
kimatheih = (t:v) (w:be known beforehand/be foreseen) (d:theih, know, with ma, before, and the prefix ki; a kimatheih lo, that cannot be known in advance) (e:cih a ~ lo mah ahi hi) (r:10.11.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimatsakin = (t:v) (w:fasten together/join) (d:kimatsak, join things so that they hold together, with the linking ending in; of foxes tied tail to tail) (e:a meite leh a meite ~) (b:kimatsak) (r:7.15.4) (q:draft)
kimawksai = (t:v) (w:spring/go off) (d:of a trap, spring shut with nothing in it) (e:thang ~ ahi hiam) (r:30.3.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimawlin = (t:v) (w:play) (d:kimawl, play, with the linking ending in: playing) (e:numei naupang ~ phezaizai ding uh hi) (b:kimawl) (r:38.8.5) (q:draft)
kimawlsak = (t:v) (w:make perform/make play) (d:kimawl, play or perform, with the causative sak: have someone perform or hold a contest before onlookers) (e:Samson a ~ laitakin a en) (b:kimawl) (r:7.16.27/10.2.14) (q:draft)
kimawlte = (t:n) (w:those who play/ones playing) (d:kimawl play, with the plural te: the ones who are playing, here of children) (e:a tu naupang a ~ tawh kibang) (b:kimawl) (r:42.7.32/40.11.16) (q:draft)
kimeeltheih = (t:v) (w:be acquainted/know each other) (d:ki each other, with meel face and theih know: know one another by sight; tawh marks the other person) (e:siampi ukpa tawh ~ a) (r:43.18.15/43.18.16) (q:draft)
kimematna = (t:n) (w:claim/connection/share) (d:kimemat be connected with, with the noun suffix na: something that ties a person to a matter and gives a right in it) (e:bangmah ~ na nei kei uh hi) (r:16.2.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimetcip = (t:v) (w:collapse/sink down/be levelled) (d:said of the age-old hills before God, in parallel with kitamkham crumble; how the word is built is not certain) (e:a om tawntung mualneute ~ hi) (r:35.3.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kimetmai = (t:v) (w:be shaved off/be cut off) (d:of a beard, be shaved clean away; passive ki with met shave) (e:khamul khempeuh ~ hi) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettol = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/be shaved) (d:passive of mettol: of the head, be shaved completely, as a sign of mourning) (e:Dahna limin lu khempeuh ~ a) (b:mettol) (r:23.15.2) (q:draft)
kimettolsak = (t:v) (w:be shaved bald/have the head shaved) (d:kimettol be shaved bald, with sak: have the hair shaved off completely, as a sign of mourning) (e:A sam uh ~ ding a) (b:kimettol) (r:26.7.18) (q:draft)
kiminthan'sak = (t:v) (w:be glorified/be honoured) (d:passive of minthangsak glorify; minthang is shortened to minthan before sak) (e:Ama sungah Pasian a ~ leh) (r:43.13.32/23.61.3) (q:draft)
kimkotteng = (t:adv) (w:all around/on every side) (d:kimkot around with teng all: the whole surrounding of a thing, placed after the thing surrounded) (e:Biakinn ~ a lei kitawito a) (b:kimkot) (r:26.41.8/26.1.4) (q:draft)
kimlaipi = (t:conj) (w:even while/while) (d:kimlai while with the intensive pi: at the very time that something is so) (e:numei nin nei ~ buan uh hi) (b:kimlai) (r:26.22.10) (q:draft)
kimuhpih = (t:v) (w:meet/meet with/come across) (d:kimuh meet, with pih together with; na kimuhpih peuhpeuh, anyone you meet) (e:Na ~ peuhpeuh tungah na pumpi na kipia) (b:kimuh) (r:26.16.25) (q:draft)
kimut = (t:v) (w:be blown/be sounded) (d:passive of mut blow, of a trumpet) (e:Peengkul hong ~ ciangin) (b:mut) (r:23.18.3) (q:draft)
kimute = (t:n) (w:things found/things seen) (d:kimu be seen or found, with the plural te: the things that were found, here the wrongs found in a king) (e:amah a hoih lohna a ~) (b:kimu) (r:14.36.8) (q:draft)
kimuzo = (t:v) (w:be found/can be found) (d:passive of muzo find; kimuzo nawn lo, could no longer be found) (e:Amah ka zonzon hangin ~ nawn lo hi) (b:muzo) (r:19.37.36/20.20.6) (q:draft)
kinaih = (t:v) (w:draw near each other/close in/draw up) (d:ki each other with naih approach: of two armies, come up close to one another for battle) (e:a kido dingin ~ uh hi) (b:naih) (r:9.17.21) (q:draft)
kinaina = (t:n) (w:relationship/kinship/closeness) (d:kinai be near or closely related, with the noun suffix na; tawh marks the other person) (e:amah tawh a ~ zia) (b:kinai) (r:17.8.1) (q:draft)
kinakko = (t:v) (w:shout loudly/cry out) (d:kinak strongly with ko shout: shout hard; with semsem, all the more) (e:ci-in a ~ zaw semsem uh hi) (r:41.15.14/42.18.39) (q:draft)
kinawhsa-in = (t:adv) (w:in haste/hurriedly) (d:kinawh hurry with sa and the adverb ending in: in a hurried state) (e:~ na paikhia kei ding uh hi) (r:23.52.12) (q:draft)
kinawhsak = (t:v) (w:hurry/make haste/hasten) (d:kinawh hurry with sak; va kinawhsak un, go and have them hurry, said of fetching the wailing women quickly) (e:Va ~ un la) (b:kinawh) (r:24.9.18) (q:draft)
kinawtkhia = (t:v) (w:be scoured off/be rubbed off/be removed) (d:passive of nawtkhia, here in the sense rub or scrape out: of the burnt crust in a cooking pot) (e:a kang-op a ~ ngei lo beel) (b:nawtkhia) (r:26.24.6) (q:draft)
kineh = (t:v) (w:come close/go near/keep close) (d:ki with neh press close: get close up to a person or place, with tawh for a person) (e:Tua bang numei tawh ~ kha kei un) (b:neh) (r:20.5.8/44.27.13) (q:draft)
kinehlua = (t:v) (w:be too crowded/press too closely) (d:kineh press close together with lua too much: of a crowd, packed so tight that no one can get through) (e:mihonpi ~ ahih manin) (b:kineh) (r:41.2.4/42.8.19) (q:draft)
kineihnate = (t:n) (w:disputes/lawsuits) (d:plural of kineihna; thu kineihnate are the cases people have against one another) (e:Kei guak in note’ thu ~) (b:kineihna) (r:5.1.12) (q:draft)
kineihpih = (t:v) (w:go to law with/dispute with/confront) (d:in thu kineihpih, have a case against someone in court: kineih as in kineihna dispute, with pih together with) (e:thukhen zumah thu ~ theih hi lo hi) (r:18.9.32) (q:draft)
kinelsak = (t:v) (w:be made smooth/be smoothed) (d:nel fine or smooth with the causative sak and passive ki: of rough ground) (e:a leihumte ~ ding hi) (r:42.3.5) (q:draft)
kinemang = (t:v) (w:be eaten up/be devoured/be destroyed) (d:passive of nemang eat up: of a vineyard left open and grazed bare) (e:ka lakhia ding a, ~ ding hi) (b:nemang) (r:23.5.5) (q:draft)
kinengniamte = (t:n) (w:the oppressed/oppressed people) (d:kinengniam be oppressed, with the plural te: those who are oppressed) (e:Topa in a ~ a dingin) (b:kinengniam) (r:19.103.6/42.4.18) (q:draft)
kinenniam = (t:v) (w:be oppressed/be afflicted) (d:passive of nenniam press down, oppress) (e:Ahih hangin amaute a ~ ciangin) (b:nenniam) (r:2.1.12) (q:draft)
kinetniamna = (t:n) (w:oppression) (d:netniamna oppression with the prefix ki: people oppressing one another, or the state of being oppressed) (e:~ bekbek tawh a kidim hi) (b:netniamna) (r:24.6.6/23.1.17) (q:draft)
kineubawl = (t:v) (w:be degraded/be belittled/be humiliated) (d:passive of neubawl make small: be made little of in the eyes of others) (e:na sanggampa uh a ~ suak ding hi) (r:5.25.3) (q:draft)
kingahsak = (t:v) (w:be given/be granted) (d:passive of ngahsak cause to receive: be made to receive a share) (e:ngahte mah amah zong ~ a) (b:ngahsak) (r:5.33.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingaih = (t:v) (w:love each other/be lovers) (d:form of kingai used as a verbal noun, being in love with someone, with tawh: nang tawh kingaih, to be in love with you) (e:nang tawh ~ nuam mahmah hi) (b:kingai) (r:22.4.10) (q:draft)
kingaihsutna-in = (t:adv) (w:for one's own sake) (d:kingaihsutna, thought or regard for oneself, with in, because of: keimah ka kingaihsutna-in, for my own sake) (e:keimah ka ~ hih bangin kong hih hi) (r:23.48.11) (q:draft)
kingap = (t:v) (w:lean on/rest on) (d:put one's weight on something for support, with tungah on) (e:Nangma tungah amaute hong ~ uh ciangin) (r:26.29.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kingawh = (t:adv) (w:forcibly/by force/violently) (d:ki with ngawh roughly, placed before a verb: kingawh laksak, be taken away by force) (e:na la uh hong ~ laksak ding a) (b:ngawh) (r:5.28.31) (q:draft)
kingensak = (t:v) (w:pray) (d:in thu kingensak in, let prayer be made, let them pray: thu ngen pray, with ki and sak let) (e:nangma tungah thu ~ in) (b:kingen) (r:19.32.6) (q:draft)
kinialin = (t:v) (w:arguing/disputing/debating) (d:kinial argue, with the linking ending in; thu kinialin, arguing over a matter) (e:mite tawh thu ~ a om hi) (b:kinial) (r:44.9.29/55.2.14) (q:draft)
kinialnate = (t:n) (w:arguments/disputes/controversies) (d:plural of kinialna) (e:thu ~ na pelh in) (b:kinialna) (r:55.2.23/54.6.20) (q:draft)
kinilhin = (t:v) (w:being anointed/anointed) (d:kinilh be anointed, with the linking ending in) (e:amaute sathau ~ a kikipsak nading ahi hi) (b:kinilh) (r:2.29.29) (q:draft)
kinilhpa = (t:n) (w:anointed one) (d:kinilh be anointed, with pa for a man: sathau kinilhpa, the one anointed with oil, the Anointed One) (e:sathau ~ thuman lopi-in kithat ding hi) (b:kinilh) (r:27.9.26/27.9.25) (q:draft)
kinilkhia = (t:v) (w:be cast out/be driven away/be exiled) (d:passive of nilkhia cast out; a kinilkhia Israelte, the outcasts of Israel) (e:amah in a ~ Israelte kaikhawm hi) (b:nilkhia) (r:19.147.2) (q:draft)
kinimte = (t:adj) (w:dyed/colourful) (d:kinim dyed with the plural te, of garments: the coloured ones) (e:a kinusia puan ~ Sisera adingin) (b:kinim) (r:7.5.30) (q:draft)
kininsaktawm = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/make oneself unclean) (d:ninsak defile with ki and tawm, by one's own doing: bring uncleanness on oneself) (e:noleno a ~ na hi uh hi) (r:26.20.31/26.22.3) (q:draft)
kinloin = (t:v) (w:neglecting/not caring about) (d:kin heed with lo not and the linking ending in: without care for, neglecting) (e:Pasian’ biakinn ~ i om kei ding hi) (b:kin) (r:16.10.39/50.2.21) (q:draft)
kinolh = (t:v) (w:be rejected/be turned away) (d:passive of nolh reject) (e:a ci mite ~ ding a) (b:nolh) (r:23.42.17) (q:draft)
kinomsak = (t:v) (w:be soothed/be softened/be moistened) (d:passive of nomsak moisten: of wounds, be softened with oil) (e:sathau tawh ~ lo hi) (b:nomsak) (r:23.1.6) (q:draft)
kinophuah = (t:v) (w:name oneself/call oneself/take a name) (d:with min tawh and amahmah, give oneself an added name; phuah is give a name) (e:Israel min tawh amahmah ~ ding hi) (r:23.44.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kinuamsak = (t:v) (w:take heart/cheer up/be comforted) (d:with lung or lungsim heart: nuamsak gladden with ki oneself, cheer oneself, take courage) (e:na lung ~ in) (b:nuamsak) (r:40.9.22/40.9.2) (q:draft)
kinungkiksak = (t:v) (w:be turned back/be driven back) (d:passive of nungkiksak turn back) (e:khempeuh maizumin ~ ta hen) (b:nungkiksak) (r:19.129.5) (q:draft)
kinungsik = (t:v) (w:regret afterwards/be sorry later) (d:nung after with kisik regret: come to regret a thing once it is done) (e:na ~ kha ding hi) (r:20.20.25) (q:draft)
kipaaithang = (t:v) (w:be strewn/be thrown about/lie scattered) (d:of dead bodies, be thrown out and left lying about; also written kipaithang) (e:Jerusalem khua kongzing lakah ~ dinga) (r:24.14.16/24.9.22) (q:draft)
kipah = (t:v) (w:rejoice/be glad) (d:form of kipak rejoice used before endings such as uh and nading) (e:lungdamin na ~ uh hangin) (r:24.50.11/20.23.25) (q:draft)
kipaihna = (t:n) (w:dumping place/throwing away) (d:kipaih be thrown away with the noun suffix na; nin kipaihna phualpi, a heap where rubbish is thrown) (e:nin ~ phualpi suak ding a) (b:kipaih) (r:33.3.12) (q:draft)
kipaii = (t:v) (w:be conceived) (d:passive of paii conceive, of a child) (e:Pasal naungek khat ~ hi) (b:paii) (r:18.3.3/42.2.21) (q:draft)
kipaithangin = (t:v) (w:being strewn/flung about) (d:kipaithang be strewn, with the linking ending in) (e:mun citengah ~ gamdai ding hi) (b:kipaithang) (r:30.8.3) (q:draft)
kipangsak = (t:v) (w:be deployed/be stationed) (d:passive of pangsak post: of soldiers, be drawn up against an enemy) (e:a do dingin amaute ~ hi) (b:pangsak) (r:13.19.11) (q:draft)
kipasalsak = (t:v) (w:be brave/act like men/be courageous) (d:pasal man with ki and sak: make oneself a man, show courage) (e:i Pasian’ khuapite adingin ~ ni) (r:10.10.12) (q:draft)
kipawlpih = (t:v) (w:associate with/ally with/mix with) (d:kipawl associate, with pih together with; a kipawlpih, those one has joined with) (e:A ~ mi namdangte in) (b:kipawl) (r:28.7.9) (q:draft)
kipei = (t:v) (w:whirl/spin/swirl) (d:of a whirlwind, turn round and round; pei is wheel) (e:huihpi nungin pingpei ~ a) (b:pei) (r:34.1.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphatin = (t:v) (w:being praised/praised) (d:kiphat be praised, with the linking ending in) (e:Mipilte ~ kipahtawi a) (b:kiphat) (r:20.12.8) (q:draft)
kiphatphat = (t:v) (w:be praised again and again/be praised continually) (d:passive of phatphat keep praising) (e:nangma nasepnate ~ ding a) (b:phatphat) (r:19.145.4) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (t:v) (w:be quenched/be put out) (d:passive of phelh quench, of a fire) (e:mei a ~ zo kei ding hi) (b:phelh) (r:24.17.27) (q:draft)
kiphelh = (t:v) (w:clear oneself/defend oneself) (d:form of kiphel used before nading: mawhna kiphelh nading, to clear oneself of a charge) (e:tu-ni ka mawhna ~ nading) (b:kiphel) (r:44.22.1) (q:draft)
kiphelin = (t:v) (w:splitting apart/being split) (d:kiphel split apart, with the linking ending in) (e:biakna tau ~ a tunga om vutte) (b:kiphel) (r:11.13.3/11.13.5) (q:draft)
kiphelkek = (t:v) (w:be demolished/be torn down) (d:passive of phelkek tear down, of altars and buildings) (e:Biakna taute ~ ding a) (b:phelkek) (r:26.6.4/41.13.2) (q:draft)
kiphiatsak = (t:v) (w:be blotted out/be wiped out) (d:kiphiat be wiped out with sak: let them be wiped out, here of names in a book) (e:laibu sung panin amaute ~ in la) (b:kiphiat) (r:19.69.28) (q:draft)
kipho = (t:v) (w:be spread out/be exposed/be laid bare) (d:passive of pho spread out: be laid out in the open where all can see) (e:Pasian mai-ah ~ laakin a om hi) (b:pho) (r:58.4.13/24.8.2) (q:draft)
kiphong = (t:v) (w:be awakened/be woken) (d:passive of phong wake) (e:a ihmu kimlai a ~ bang) (b:phong) (r:38.4.1) (q:draft)
kiphop = (t:v) (w:be patched/be mended) (d:passive of phop mend; a kiphop khedap, a patched sandal) (e:a ~ khedapte bulhin) (b:phop) (r:6.9.5) (q:draft)
kiphopte = (t:adj) (w:patched/mended) (d:kiphop be patched, with the plural te: the patched ones, here of wineskins) (e:a kikeek leh a ~ guangin) (b:kiphop) (r:6.9.4) (q:draft)
kiphu = (t:v) (w:collide/run into each other/stumble against) (d:ki each other with phu push against: knock against one another) (e:khat leh khat ~ kha-in) (b:phu) (r:24.46.12) (q:draft)
kiphu = (t:v) (w:head into/face) (d:with huih wind: of a ship, hold its way against the wind) (e:huih ~ zo nawn lo ahih ciangin) (b:phu) (r:44.27.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiphuakpa = (t:n) (w:one who is named/the man called) (d:kiphuak be named, with pa for a man: the man to whom a name was given) (e:Belteshazzar ci-a a ~ Daniel sam sak in) (b:kiphuak) (r:27.5.12/27.4.8) (q:draft)
kiphuhna = (t:n) (w:settling/resting) (d:kiphuh be set down, with the noun suffix na; a kiphuhna mun, the place where a thing comes to rest, here of the cloud) (e:meii a ~ munah Israel mite in) (b:kiphuh) (r:4.9.17) (q:draft)
kiphukpai = (t:v) (w:be cut down/be felled/be cast down) (d:passive of phukpai cut down) (e:hong bangci ~ ahi hiam) (b:phukpai) (r:23.14.12) (q:draft)
kiphunsanna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (d:kiphunsan grumble against each other, with the noun suffix na) (e:Jew mite kikalah ~ thu hong om hi) (b:kiphunsan) (r:44.6.1/47.12.20) (q:draft)
kiphupai = (t:v) (w:stumble over each other/fall over each other) (d:ki each other with phu push against and pai go: run into one another while fleeing) (e:amaute khat leh khat ~ ding uh hi) (r:3.26.37) (q:draft)
kiphusak = (t:v) (w:smash together/dash against each other) (d:kiphu collide with the causative sak: make people strike against one another) (e:amaute khat leh khat ka ~ ding a) (b:kiphu) (r:24.13.14) (q:draft)
kiphutte = (t:n) (w:settings) (d:kiphut be set in place, with the plural te: the gold settings in which stones are set) (e:a ~’ tungah na bulh ding hi) (b:kiphut) (r:2.28.14) (q:draft)
kipialsak = (t:v) (w:be led astray/be turned aside) (d:pialsak lead astray with ki: lam kipialsak, let oneself be turned off the way) (e:lam ~ kei in) (b:pialsak) (r:18.36.18) (q:draft)
kipilsak = (t:v) (w:be conceited/think oneself wise) (d:pil wise with ki and sak: make oneself out to be wise) (e:~ se kei un) (b:pilsak) (r:45.12.16/44.17.18) (q:draft)
kipoisak = (t:v) (w:be injured/be hurt) (d:passive of poisak injure) (e:a poisak bangin amah ~ ding hi) (b:poisak) (r:3.24.20) (q:draft)
kipsa = (t:adj) (w:established/made firm) (d:kip be established with sa, already: standing firm from before) (e:na tokhom a ~ hi a) (b:kip) (r:19.93.2) (q:draft)
kipsakpa = (t:n) (w:establisher/one who makes firm) (d:kipsak establish, with pa for a male person: he who sets a thing firm, said of God) (e:khuampite a ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:kipsak) (r:19.75.3/23.45.18) (q:draft)
kipuahkik = (t:v) (w:be restored/be repaired again) (d:passive of puahkik renovate; of the sanctuary, where the NIV has be reconsecrated) (e:biakinnpi ~ ding hi) (b:puahkik) (r:27.8.14) (q:draft)
kipuahna = (t:n) (w:beauty treatment/adornment/cosmetics) (d:kipuah make oneself ready with the noun suffix na: something used to prepare and beautify the body) (e:paknamtui tuamtuamte le ~ dangte tawh) (b:kipuah) (r:17.2.12) (q:draft)
kipuahpha = (t:v) (w:reform/mend/put right) (d:puahpha repair well, with ki oneself: put one's own ways right) (e:na gamtat hoih lote uh ~ un) (b:puahpha) (r:24.35.15/47.13.11) (q:draft)
kipuakin = (t:v) (w:being sent/sent) (d:kipuak be sent, with the linking ending in) (e:dal khat ciat ~ tua thu pen) (b:kipuak) (r:17.3.14) (q:draft)
kipuakkhia = (t:v) (w:be carried away/be deported/be sent into exile) (d:passive of puakkhia carry away) (e:hong ~ sal tang mi khempeuhte’ tungah) (b:puakkhia) (r:24.29.4) (q:draft)
kipuakkhiat = (t:v) (w:be carried away/be taken away/be deported) (d:form of kipuakkhia used before endings such as dong and nawn) (e:sal tang dingin a ~ dong) (b:kipuakkhia) (r:24.1.3/24.27.18) (q:draft)
kipuakna = (t:n) (w:being carried off/deportation) (d:kipuak be carried or sent, with the noun suffix na; a kipuakna gam, the land to which people were carried away as captives) (e:galmatin a ~ gamah amaute in) (b:kipuak) (r:14.6.37) (q:draft)
kipuasak = (t:v) (w:be made to carry/be loaded) (d:passive of puasak make carry) (e:sing kitomsakin a lelhpipi-un a ~ hi) (b:puasak) (r:25.5.13) (q:draft)
kipuasehin = (t:v) (w:being cut off/being shut out/banished) (d:kipuaseh be shut out, with the linking ending in; a kipuasehin koih, leave someone in banishment) (e:a hawlkhiatpa a ~ a koih loh nadingin) (b:kipuaseh) (r:10.14.14) (q:draft)
kipukna = (t:n) (w:stumbling block/cause of stumbling) (d:kipuk stumble with the noun suffix na: a thing that makes people fall) (e:Judah mite ading ~ ahi hi) (b:kipuk) (r:46.1.23/45.11.9) (q:draft)
kipuksuk = (t:v) (w:fall on/throw oneself down) (d:puksuk fall down with ki oneself; with sak, let oneself fall on something) (e:a namsau tungah ~ sakin a si hi) (b:puksuk) (r:13.10.5/9.31.5) (q:draft)
kipumpei = (t:v) (w:reel/shake/tremble) (d:of the earth, shake and rock; perhaps pum whole with pei turn) (e:Ama hehna hangin leitung ~ in) (r:19.18.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipung = (t:v) (w:increase/multiply/be fruitful) (d:pung increase with ki; kipung thei lo, nothing can thrive or bear young, said of a barren land) (e:hih gamah ~ thei lo hi) (b:pung) (r:12.2.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipzo = (t:v) (w:be able to stand/stand firm/endure) (d:kip stand firm with zo be able; kipzo lo, cannot stand) (e:tua innkuan ~ lo ding hi) (b:kip) (r:41.3.25/41.3.26) (q:draft)
kisaizaw = (t:v) (w:depend rather on/relate rather to) (d:kisai concern with zaw more, rather: tawh kisaizaw, has to do with this and not with that) (e:Pasian’ hehpihna bek tawh ~ hi) (b:kisai) (r:45.9.16/45.9.11) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpihna = (t:n) (w:pride/boast/thing boasted of) (d:kisaktheihpih take pride in, with the noun suffix na: what one is proud of) (e:a ~ teng uh bei ding hi) (b:kisaktheihpih) (r:26.30.18) (q:draft)
kisamkik = (t:v) (w:be called back/be summoned again) (d:passive of samkik call back) (e:a deih leh a minin ~ hi) (b:samkik) (r:17.2.14/23.54.6) (q:draft)
kisamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/cursing) (d:kisamsiat curse with the noun suffix na: a curse spoken against someone) (e:Thu om lopi-in hong ~ in) (b:kisamsiat) (r:20.26.2) (q:draft)
kisanek = (t:v) (w:eat one another's flesh/devour one another) (d:sa flesh and nek eat, with the reciprocal prefix ki) (e:khat leh khat ~ un) (r:38.11.9) (q:draft)
kisangsakte = (t:n) (w:the lofty/the tall ones/those lifted up) (d:kisangsak with plural te: those that are made high or make themselves high) (e:a ~ a niam-in kikoih ding hi) (b:kisangsak) (r:23.10.33) (q:draft)
kisangtawi = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be highly regarded/be honoured) (d:sang high and tawi hold up, with the prefix ki: be held in high regard) (e:minam khempeuh muhna ah amah ~ hi) (r:14.32.23) (q:draft)
kisapa = (t:n) (w:one who considers himself/one who thinks himself) (d:kisa with pa marking a man; pil a kisapa is the man who thinks himself wise) (e:A pil lo kimlai pil a ~ sangin) (b:kisa) (r:20.26.12) (q:draft)
kisatnen = (t:v) (w:be smashed to bits/be shattered) (d:passive of satnen with the prefix ki) (e:inn neute ~ ding hi) (b:satnen) (r:30.6.11) (q:draft)
kisattan = (t:v) (w:be cut off/be cut down) (d:passive of sattan with the prefix ki; a kisattan ankung is a stalk of grain that has been cut) (e:a ~ ankung bangin keu pah hi) (b:sattan) (r:18.24.24) (q:draft)
kisatvui = (t:v) (w:be smashed to powder/be broken down/be crushed) (d:passive of satvui with the prefix ki) (e:a paknamtui taute uh ~ gawp ding) (b:satvui) (r:26.6.6) (q:draft)
kisatzan = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be pressed/be crushed) (d:passive of satzan with the prefix ki; a kisatzan sathau is oil from beaten olives) (e:an tawh biakna-in a ~ sathau) (b:satzan) (r:4.28.5/2.29.40) (q:draft)
kisatzanin = (t:v) (w:be smashed to pieces/be broken down) (d:kisatzan with the linking ending in: being smashed to pieces, and) (e:inn liante ~ inn neute kisatnen ding hi) (b:kisatzan) (r:30.6.11) (q:draft)
kisau = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:grasshopper) (d:found in kauphe kisau, a kind of locust or grasshopper that may be eaten, the last of the four kinds named in Leviticus 11:22) (e:kauphe ~ nam khempeuh ahi hi) (r:3.11.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawlpa = (t:n) (w:the one sent/messenger) (d:kisawl be sent, with pa marking a man: the man who is sent) (e:a ~ zong a sawl pa sangin) (b:kisawl) (r:43.13.16/43.3.28) (q:draft)
kisawlte = (t:n) (w:those sent/those who are sent) (d:kisawl be sent, with plural te) (e:na kiangah hong ~ zong suang tawh) (b:kisawl) (r:42.13.34/40.23.37) (q:draft)
kisawlzo = (t:v) (w:have been sent/be sent) (d:kisawl be sent, with zo marking the action as done) (e:Minamte lakah kamtai khat ~ a) (b:kisawl) (r:31.1.1/27.10.11) (q:draft)
kisawm = (t:v) (w:be plotted against/be planned against) (d:passive of sawm, intend or plan to do something; in Acts 9:24 of the plan to kill Saul) (e:Saul in amah a ~ lamtak na phawk hi) (b:sawm) (r:44.9.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawm = (t:phrase) (w:ten horns) (d:ki horn and sawm ten written as one word) (e:lutang sagih leh ~ a nei hi) (r:66.12.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisawn = (t:v) (w:be pushed/be thrust) (d:passive of sawn, push, with the prefix ki) (e:nakpi takin hong ~ a) (b:sawn) (r:19.118.13) (q:draft)
kiseekin = (t:v) (w:be hammered out/be beaten out) (d:kiseek with the linking ending in: being hammered out, and) (e:zat dingin kham peek ~ khau-in kizem hi) (b:kiseek) (r:2.39.3) (q:draft)
kiseepsa = (t:adj) (w:winnowed/threshed) (d:said of grain and, as a picture, of a people who have been crushed; paired with kicilsa, trodden out) (e:A kicilsa, a ~ keima’ aa-te aw) (r:23.21.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisehin = (t:v) (w:be set apart/be allotted/be marked out) (d:kiseh with the linking ending in: being set apart, and) (e:a vai tong za nga mah ~) (b:kiseh) (r:26.45.2) (q:draft)
kisehkhenna = (t:n) (w:division/grouping) (d:the way people are divided into groups for a duty; ki, sehkhen divide and assign, with the noun ending na) (e:Kongcingte a ~ hih bang ahi hi) (r:13.26.1/13.26.19) (q:draft)
kisehkhennate = (t:n) (w:divisions/groupings) (e:Aaron’ suante a ~ in hihte ahi hi) (b:kisehkhenna) (r:13.24.1) (q:draft)
kisehtawm = (t:v) (w:appoint oneself/take upon oneself) (d:seh appoint, with the prefix ki and tawm, by oneself) (e:amau utthu tawh a ~ mawk hi lo hi) (r:58.5.4) (q:draft)
kisekin = (t:v) (w:train/exercise/discipline oneself) (d:found in kisekin kisinna, training by exercise; probably sek shape or forge, with the prefix ki and the linking ending in) (e:Pumpi ~ kisinna manpha hi) (r:54.4.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiselsimna = (t:n) (w:hiding/hiding place) (d:the act or place of hiding oneself secretly; a kiselsimna mun is the place where someone hides) (e:a ~ mun khempeuh hong ciamteh un la) (r:9.23.23) (q:draft)
kiselte = (t:n) (w:hidden things/what is hidden) (d:the things that are hidden, with plural te) (e:khuamial sunga ~ thei a) (r:27.2.22/46.4.5) (q:draft)
kisemin = (t:v) (w:be done/be carried on) (d:kisem with the linking ending in: being done, and) (e:hih inn lim takin ~ amau’ makaihna tawh) (b:kisem) (r:15.5.8) (q:draft)
kisemkhia = (t:v) (w:be carried out/be accomplished) (d:passive of semkhia with the prefix ki) (e:Topa’ deihna bangin ~ hi) (b:semkhia) (r:20.16.9) (q:draft)
kisemsa = (t:v) (w:done/have been done) (d:kisem be done, with sa, already: what has been done) (e:a ~ bangin hong kisem kik ding hi) (b:kisem) (r:21.1.9) (q:draft)
kiseng = (t:v) (w:be put in/be deposited/be stored) (d:passive of seng; in Ezra 8:33 of silver, gold and vessels handed over in the temple, where the NIV has weighed out) (e:kham leh um-le-beelte ~ hi) (b:seng) (r:15.8.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisepsak = (t:v) (w:serve one another) (d:sepsak serve, with the reciprocal prefix ki; with khatlekhat, one another) (e:khatlekhat na na ~ un) (b:sepsak) (r:60.5.5) (q:draft)
