koplen = (t:v) (d:said of war horses made ready for an attack; perhaps prance or rear, meaning not confirmed) (e:a sakolte uh hong ~ hi) (r:34.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
koppih = (t:v) (w:side with/support/stand by) (d:be on the side of someone; likely kop pair with the ending pih, do together with) (e:kuamah in hong ~ loin) (b:kop) (r:55.4.16/45.8.31) (q:draft)
korban = (t:n) (w:Corban) (d:loanword from Hebrew: a thing given to God, explained in the text as Pasian a’ ding) (e:hih pen ~) (r:41.7.11) (q:draft)
kosiate = (t:n) (w:slanderers/revilers) (d:kosia slander, revile, with the plural te: those who speak abusively) (e:zukham theite, hangsan ~) (b:kosia) (r:46.6.10/46.5.11) (q:draft)
kuahin = (t:v) (w:strap on/carry/bear) (d:kuah strap on with the linking ending in: carrying shield and sword, and then the next action follows) (e:lum leh namsau ~ thal a tawi) (b:kuah) (r:13.5.18) (q:draft)
kuakin = (t:adv) (w:hollow) (d:kuak hollow with the ending in; a kuakin bawl is make something hollow inside) (e:Singpekte tawh a ~ na bawl ding hi) (b:kuak) (r:2.27.8/2.38.7) (q:draft)
kuakua = (t:pron) (w:whoever/whosoever) (d:kua who doubled; kuakua ahih hangin is whoever he may be) (e:~ ahih hangin ama mawhna dan) (r:48.5.10/45.2.1) (q:draft)
