kuangah = (t:n) (w:in the pouch/in the bowl) (d:kuang bowl with the place marker ah; saili kuangah is in the pouch of a sling) (e:Saili ~ sailungtang khihcip lehang) (b:kuang) (r:20.26.8) (q:draft)
kuangkik = (t:v) (w:burn again/flame up again) (d:kuang burn with kik, again) (e:cikmah hunin ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:kuang) (r:18.18.5) (q:draft)
kuanglekeute = (t:n) (w:vessels/utensils/dishes) (d:household vessels and utensils of all kinds, a pair-word built on kuang, bowl, with plural te) (e:sing tawh kibawl ~ ahihleh) (r:3.15.12/23.22.24) (q:draft)
kuangtuahte = (t:n) (w:sistrums/castanets) (d:a percussion instrument played in worship, listed between timbrels and cymbals; plural te) (e:~ leh daltuahte tumin lungdamin) (r:10.6.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuangzawn = (t:n) (w:trough/watering trough) (d:long trough filled with water for animals to drink from) (e:tuuhonte tui pia dingin ~ dim uh hi) (r:2.2.16) (q:draft)
kuankhiate = (t:n) (w:those who set out/those who go out) (d:kuankhia, set out, with plural te: the people who set out) (e:a ~ bangin na lungdam ding uh hi) (b:kuankhia) (r:23.30.29) (q:draft)
kuankhiatpih = (t:v) (w:lead out/march out with) (d:kuankhiat, set out, with pih, together with: go out to war at the head of others) (e:Israel a ~ leh a ciahpih) (b:kuankhiat) (r:13.11.2) (q:draft)
kuankhop = (t:v) (w:go out together/go along with) (d:kuan, set out for work, with khop, together) (e:ama numeite tawh na ~ hoih mahmah hi) (r:8.2.22) (q:draft)
kuanta = (t:v) (w:be about to/be on the point of) (d:kuan, set out, with ta, now; placed after another verb, the action is just about to happen, as in ni tum kuanta, the sun is about to set) (e:ni tum ~ ahih manin) (b:kuan) (r:44.4.3/42.19.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuante = (t:n) (w:those who march out/those coming to attack) (d:kuan, set out, with plural te; after another verb, as in a si kuante, those who are about to do it, the dying) (e:then nih tawh hong ~) (b:kuan) (r:42.14.31/18.24.12) (q:draft)
kuantoh = (t:v) (w:go up/march up) (d:form of kuanto used before ding) (e:mual dawnah ~ ding amaute in ngaihsun veve) (b:kuanto) (r:4.14.44) (q:draft)
kuavang = (t:n) (w:mouth/opening) (d:the opening of a pit or hole, with vang, opening) (e:in a ~ ka tungah hong) (r:19.69.15) (q:draft)
kuih = (t:v) (w:plow/furrow) (d:form of kui, cut, used before bang: cut furrows in the ground) (e:Lo khote in lei a ~ bangin) (b:kui) (r:19.129.3) (q:draft)
kuikeek = (t:v) (w:gash/tear up/plow up) (d:cut long gashes or furrows in a surface, built on kui, cut) (e:ka nungzang ~ uh a) (r:19.129.3/18.41.30) (q:draft)
kuikham = (t:v) (w:tear/gash/lacerate) (d:cut or tear the flesh, built on kui, cut; stands beside petkham, chew, in the same verse) (e:na nawi na ~ ding hi) (r:26.23.34) (q:draft)
kulhneite = (t:adj) (w:fortified/walled) (d:kulhnei, having a wall, with plural te, which belongs to the whole phrase khuapi kulhnei, fortified cities) (e:Judah khuapi ~ khempeuh ah galkapte koih a) (b:kulhnei) (r:14.17.2) (q:draft)
kultaltui = (t:n) (w:pitch/liquid pitch) (d:kultal, pitch, with tui, liquid) (e:Luitui khempeuh ~ suak ding a) (r:23.34.9) (q:draft)
kumgiat = (t:n) (w:eight years) (d:kum, year, and giat, eight, written as one word) (e:Jerusalem ah ~ sung uk hi) (r:14.21.5/14.21.20) (q:draft)
kumi = (t:intj) (w:koum) (d:Aramaic word meaning get up, quoted in the saying Talitha kumi, Little girl, get up) (r:41.5.41) (q:draft)
kumipa = (t:n) (w:king) (d:spelling of kumpipa, the king, found in two verses of one text, probably a misprint) (e:leh ~’ inn vankoihnate) (r:12.18.15/24.37.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kumkhat = (t:n) (w:one year/a year) (d:kum, year, and khat, one, written as one word; kumkhat a pha is a year old) (e:~ a pha tuuno a pa nga) (r:4.7.41/23.32.10) (q:draft)
kumli = (t:n) (w:four years) (d:kum, year, and li, four, written as one word; kumsawm leh kumli is fourteen years, and kumli a cin’ kum is the fourth year) (e:kumsawm leh ~ khit ciangin) (r:48.2.1/24.25.1) (q:draft)
kumpinute = (t:n) (w:queens) (e:~ pen nang hong khoi na nute) (b:kumpinu) (r:23.49.23) (q:draft)
kumpipate = (t:n) (w:kings) (d:kumpipa with plural te; here te closes a list of several kings) (e:Ivvah ~ koi-ah om ahi hiam) (b:kumpipa) (r:23.37.13) (q:draft)
kumsawm = (t:n) (w:ten years) (d:kum, year, and sawm, ten, written as one word; kumsawm leh kumnga is fifteen years) (e:na nuntakna ~ leh kumnga kong piak) (r:23.38.5/48.2.1) (q:draft)
kumsimin = (t:adv) (w:every year/yearly/year after year) (d:kumsim, yearly, with the adverb ending in) (e:~ Jerusalem-ah pai tawntung ding uh hi) (b:kumsim) (r:38.14.16/42.2.41) (q:draft)
kumza = (t:n) (w:hundred years/a hundred years) (d:kum, year, and za, hundred, written as one word) (e:~ cing loin a site) (r:23.65.20) (q:draft)
kunsa-in = (t:adv) (w:bowing/bowed down/stooping) (d:kun, bow, with sa and the adverb ending in: in a bowed posture) (e:nangma mai-ah ~ hong pai ding uh a) (r:23.60.14) (q:draft)
laate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:donkeys) (d:laa with plural te; gamlak laate is wild donkeys) (e:a khawhsate uh khawmin ~ tungah suanin) (b:laa) (r:16.13.15/24.48.6) (q:draft)
laho = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:nettle) (d:a wild stinging or thorny plant that overgrows ruins, named together with thangling, thistle) (e:~ kung leh thangling kung po ding hi) (r:23.34.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
lahsan = (t:v) (w:shake at/raise against) (d:lah, show, with san, toward: hold up the fist against someone) (e:Pasian langpangin a khuttum a ~) (b:lah) (r:18.15.25) (q:draft)
lahtelnate = (t:n) (w:declarations/explanations) (d:lahtel, show clearly, with na and plural te: things set out plainly) (e:ka ~ na za un) (b:lahtel) (r:18.13.17) (q:draft)
laibawl = (t:v) (w:make a will/draw up a document) (d:lai, writing, with bawl, make; a laibawl pa is the man who made the will) (e:a ~ pa a sih phot ding kisam hi) (b:lai) (r:58.9.16/58.9.17) (q:draft)
laikhakna = (t:n) (w:letter/writing) (d:laikhak, send a letter, with na: the letter sent or the sending of it) (e:hih kong ~ sungah) (b:laikhak) (r:45.15.15/24.29.28) (q:draft)
lailaina = (t:part) (d:lailai, still, with the noun-forming ending na, placed after a verb: the going on doing it, as in gen ngam lailaina, daring to keep on speaking) (e:thu kong gen ngam ~ hong maisak in) (b:lailai) (r:1.18.31) (q:draft)
laimalte = (t:n) (w:letters/writing/inscription) (d:laimal, written letter, with plural te) (e:Bang zah a lian ~ tawh ka khutin) (b:laimal) (r:48.6.11/27.5.24) (q:draft)
lainat = (t:v) (w:have compassion/feel pity/be concerned) (d:feel pain within for someone; nang’ lainat nading is something for you to be troubled about) (e:hehpih lo, ~ lo, it loin ka sisak ding) (r:24.13.14/18.19.4) (q:draft)
lainatna = (t:n) (w:compassion/tenderness/concern) (e:Na lungduaina leh nong ~ kote’ adingin) (b:lainat) (r:23.63.15/18.19.4) (q:draft)
laisim = (t:v) (w:read/study) (d:lai, writing, with sim, read: read a text; laisim ngei lo is never having studied) (e:Hih mi in ~ ngei lo napi-in) (r:43.7.15/44.8.30) (q:draft)
laitaak = (t:v) (w:enclose/have in the middle) (d:lie on both sides of something so that it is in the center) (e:leitang in hihte ~ ding hi) (r:26.48.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
laitat = (t:v) (w:breathe one's last/expire/die) (d:stop breathing at death) (e:nakpitakin Jesuh kiko-in a ~ hi) (r:41.15.37/1.49.33) (q:draft)
lakha = (t:v) (w:take) (d:la, take, with kha, which shows the act as something one ends up doing or should not do) (e:tuate iplahin ka ~ hi) (r:6.7.21/20.22.26) (q:draft)
lakhiasak = (t:v) (w:have brought out/cause to bring out) (d:lakhia, take out, with sak, cause) (e:gam panin sumngo ~ in la) (b:lakhia) (r:19.68.31) (q:draft)
lakhiato = (t:v) (w:bring up/lift out) (d:lakhia, take out, with to, upward) (e:lei thukpi sung panin nong ~ kik ding hi) (b:lakhia) (r:19.71.20) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsa = (t:adj) (w:taken away/taken out) (d:lakkhiat, take out, with sa, already done; before a noun, that which someone has taken away) (e:Pasian in a ~ neihsa khempeuh) (b:lakkhiat) (r:1.31.16) (q:draft)
lakkhiatsakin = (t:v) (w:taking away from/stripping of/removing) (d:lakkhiatsak, take something out or away from someone, with the linking ending in) (e:na suang lungtang uh hong ~ mihing lungtang) (b:lakkhiatsak) (r:26.36.26/26.16.39) (q:draft)
lakkhiatte = (t:n) (d:lakkhiat, take away, with plural te: here the people from whom something is taken away) (e:pan thu a ~ ahi uh hi) (b:lakkhiat) (r:42.8.12/41.4.15) (q:draft)
lakkiksa = (t:adj) (w:taken back/reclaimed) (d:lakkik, take back, with sa, already done) (e:Haman’ tung panin a ~ minthuhna zungbuh) (b:lakkik) (r:17.8.2) (q:draft)
laklak = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after dian’, leap, for the bounding of a deer) (e:thang zuanin a dian’ ~ bangin) (r:20.7.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
lakpan = (t:prep) (w:from among/out of) (d:lak, among, with pan, from) (e:misite ~ Ta upa a suak hi) (r:51.1.18/40.5.19) (q:draft)
laksakte = (t:n) (w:those who take away/those who seize) (d:laksak, take away from, with plural te) (e:a hong ~ tung panin lakik kei un) (b:laksak) (r:42.6.30/24.49.2) (q:draft)
laksate = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured) (d:laksa, taken, with plural te: the people someone has taken) (e:galmatin na ~ that ding na hi hiam) (b:laksa) (r:12.6.22) (q:draft)
lakthuah = (t:v) (w:take in addition/marry also) (d:lak, take, with thuah, in addition: take another wife besides the one already had) (e:zi dang khat a ~ leh) (r:2.21.10/3.20.14) (q:draft)
lalsak = (t:v) (w:move/resettle/cause to migrate) (d:lal, migrate, with sak, cause) (e:hih gamah tua khua panin a ~ hi) (b:lal) (r:44.7.4) (q:draft)
lambehte = (t:n) (w:side rooms/annexes) (d:rooms built on against the wall of a house; plural te) (e:a inn buppi tungah a ~ zomin) (r:11.6.10) (q:draft)
lamdangdang = (t:adj) (w:strange/various strange) (d:lamdang, strange, with its last syllable repeated: strange things of many kinds) (e:a ~ thuhilhna thak zui kei un) (r:58.13.9/20.23.33) (q:draft)
lamding = (t:v) (w:build) (d:lam, build, with ding written as one word: to build, going to build) (e:inn ~ kipan napi-in zozo lo hi) (b:lam) (r:42.14.30/42.14.28) (q:draft)
lametet = (t:v) (w:hope for/expect eagerly/long for) (d:lamet, hope, with its last syllable repeated: keep hoping for over a long time) (e:i ~ David’ suan hi lo ding) (r:40.12.23/50.1.20) (q:draft)
lamethuai = (t:adj) (w:hopeful/worth hoping for) (d:lamet, hope, with huai, worthy of; a lamethuai bangmah om lo is there is nothing to hope for) (e:Mailamah a ~ bangmah a om kei hi) (r:21.11.8/25.2.13) (q:draft)
lametin = (t:adv) (w:as one's hope) (d:lamet, hope, with in; lametin nei is to have as one's hope, put one's hope in) (e:amah bek mah ~ nei ding uh hi) (b:lamet) (r:40.12.21/19.62.10) (q:draft)
lametsakna = (t:n) (w:giving of hope/cause for hope) (d:lamet, hope, with sak, cause, and na: that by which someone is made to hope) (e:Keimah nong ~ ahi na nasempa’) (r:19.119.49) (q:draft)
lamhilh = (t:n) (w:guide) (d:one who shows the way, lam, way, with hilh, teach) (e:kote a dingin ~ nong hi ding hi) (r:4.10.31/40.23.16) (q:draft)
lamhilhte = (t:n) (w:guides) (e:Amau in mittaw ~ ahi uh hi) (b:lamhilh) (r:40.15.14/40.23.16) (q:draft)
