lamkabomte-ah = (t:n) (w:in the public squares/in the streets) (d:lamkabom, public square, with plural te and the place marker ah) (e:kongzing leh ~ a tu dingin) (r:38.8.4) (q:draft)
lamkaih = (t:v) (w:guide/lead) (d:lead along the way, lam, way, with kaih, lead) (e:amaute a hehpihpa in amaute ~ ding a) (r:23.49.10) (q:draft)
lamlahnate = (t:n) (w:instructions/directions/guideposts) (d:lamlahna, guidance, with plural te; on a road, the signs that show the way) (e:hih bang ~ kong piak uh) (b:lamlahna) (r:52.4.2/24.31.21) (q:draft)
lamlakin = (t:v) (w:guiding/directing) (d:lamlak, guide, with the linking ending in) (e:leitung minamte khempeuh ~ makai na hih manin) (b:lamlak) (r:19.67.4/19.105.21) (q:draft)
lamlam = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after kot, circle around, for birds hovering round and round overhead) (e:A kot ~ vasate bangin) (r:23.31.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamnasa = (t:adj) (d:lam, build or set up, with the endings na and sa: where something has been built or pitched; a puanbuk lamnasa leitang is the ground where he had pitched his tent) (e:a puanbuk ~ leitang dangka zakhat tawh) (b:lamna) (r:1.33.19) (q:draft)
lamnawl = (t:n) (w:roadside/side of the road) (d:lam, road, with nawl, edge; lamnawl lam tawnin pai is to pass by along the far side of the road) (e:~ lam tawnin a paisan hi) (r:42.10.31/42.10.32) (q:draft)
lamneu = (t:n) (w:lane/alley/small path) (d:lam, road, with neu, small; set against lamlian, main road) (e:~ ah ahi zongin pai in la) (r:42.14.21/19.77.19) (q:draft)
lamneute = (t:n) (w:lanes/small paths) (e:nangma ~ zong luiliante’ tung mah ahi hi) (b:lamneu) (r:19.77.19/42.14.23) (q:draft)
lampaina = (t:n) (w:marching/journey/way) (d:lampai, walk or travel, with na: the act of walking, or the way someone goes) (e:Lungli kungte’ dawnah ~ kheging na zak ciangin) (b:lampai) (r:10.5.24/16.9.12) (q:draft)
lampangteng = (t:n) (w:whole side/all of the side) (d:lampang, side, with teng, all of: the whole area on that side) (e:nisuahna ~ Gilead gam hi a) (b:lampang) (r:26.47.18) (q:draft)
lamphei-ah = (t:n) (w:on a level path/on level ground) (d:lamphei, a level or even road, with the place marker ah) (e:ka galte hangin ~ hong kha in) (r:19.27.11/19.143.10) (q:draft)
lampialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/mislead) (d:lampial, go astray, with sak, cause) (e:omsak a, Judah mite ~ hi) (b:lampial) (r:14.21.11/23.9.16) (q:draft)
lamsakkik = (t:v) (w:rebuild/have rebuilt) (d:lamsak with kik, again: have something built again, let it be rebuilt) (e:Ama mun ngei mahah a biakinn ~ un) (b:lamsak) (r:15.6.7/15.6.3) (q:draft)
lamzan = (t:v) (w:succeed/prosper) (d:go well on one's way, written with a final apostrophe before theih) (e:hoih takin na ~’ theihna dingin) (r:6.1.7) (q:draft)
lamzin = (t:n) (w:path/way) (d:the road one travels, lam, road, with zin, travel; here set beside lampi) (e:lampi nusia-in, ~ panin pial un la) (r:23.30.11) (q:draft)
langaih = (t:n) (w:melody/music/sweet song) (d:pleasing song, la, song, with ngaih, lovely; langaih sa is to make music) (e:ama tungah ~ sa un) (r:19.149.3/19.98.5) (q:draft)
langgen = (t:v) (w:show partiality/take the side of/favor) (d:lang, side, with gen, speak: speak for one side in a judgment) (e:mizawngte ~ loin, a liante thu zui loin) (r:3.19.15) (q:draft)
langkhiasak = (t:v) (w:display/make known/reveal) (d:cause something to come out into open view) (e:mite lakah nangma vangliatna a ~ khin Pasian) (r:19.77.14) (q:draft)
langnihin = (t:adv) (w:on both sides/both) (d:langnih, both sides, with in; of a sword, double-edged; of feet, both) (e:a ~ a hiam mahmah namsau) (b:langnih) (r:66.2.12/10.9.13) (q:draft)
langpa = (t:n) (w:opponent/other party/adversary) (d:lang, opposing side, with pa, which marks a man: the man on the other side) (e:a ~ in a thuk mateng) (b:lang) (r:20.18.17/10.2.16) (q:draft)
lanlan = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after pai, walk, for the stately walk of a king before his people, beside kuahkuah for the rooster and gangan for the he-goat) (e:a mite mai-ah a pai ~ kumpipa) (r:20.30.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
lanluat = (t:n) (w:lewdness/debauchery/excessive lust) (d:lan, lustful, with luat, too much) (e:kihhuaina le ~ khialhna gamta uh hi) (r:7.20.6/48.5.19) (q:draft)
laphuah = (t:v) (w:compose songs/write poetry) (d:la, song, with phuah, compose; laphuah siampa is a poet, and ama laphuah is the songs he composed) (e:note sung panin ~ siampa khat in) (r:44.17.28/11.4.32) (q:draft)
laptohna = (t:n) (w:lifting up/raising) (d:laptoh, lift up, with na) (e:ka khutte ka ~ pen nitak biak piakna) (r:19.141.2) (q:draft)
lasiam = (t:n) (w:singer/skilled singer) (d:la, song, with siam, skilled: one who is good at singing) (e:la a sa ding ~ numei leh pasal tampi) (r:21.2.8) (q:draft)
lauhlauh = (t:adv) (d:descriptive word placed after tuan, ride, for the jolting and bouncing of a chariot being driven) (e:sakol leeng tuan ~ gingte) (r:34.3.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
lauhuainate = (t:n) (w:terrors/dangers) (e:tui leh mei ~ ka thuak uh hi) (b:lauhuaina) (r:19.66.12) (q:draft)
laulau = (t:v) (w:dread/keep fearing) (d:lau, fear, said twice; ka laulau is the very thing I fear) (e:ka ~ ka tuak ta hi) (r:18.3.25) (q:draft)
laumai = (t:v) (w:look afraid/show fear) (d:lau, fear, with mai, face: of the face, show fear) (e:a mai put uh ~ ding uh hi) (r:26.27.35) (q:draft)
launate = (t:n) (w:terrors/fears) (e:sih ding ~ kei tung hong tung zo hi) (b:launa) (r:19.55.4) (q:draft)
laupih = (t:v) (w:be afraid of/fear) (d:lau, fear, with pih: be afraid on account of someone or something) (e:bang ~ ding ka hi hiam) (b:lau) (r:19.27.1) (q:draft)
lausakgawp = (t:v) (w:terrify/frighten greatly) (d:lausak, frighten, with gawp, severely) (e:Topa in amaute ~ ding a) (b:lausak) (r:36.2.11/26.38.21) (q:draft)
lauzaw = (t:adj) (w:more afraid) (d:lau, afraid, with zaw, more) (e:bangzahin ~ ding i hi hiam) (b:lau) (r:9.23.3) (q:draft)
lawhlawh = (t:v) (w:toss/roll/surge) (d:of waves, heave up again and again) (e:Tuihualte in a ~ hangin zozo lo uh a) (r:24.5.22) (q:draft)
lawhsak = (t:v) (w:rent out/let out) (d:with khawh, farm: let others work a field for a share of the crop) (e:lo kho dangte a khawh ~ ding hi) (r:40.21.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawhsak = (t:v) (w:pass on to/transmit) (d:cause something to spread to others by contact, as holiness passing from the holy offerings to the people) (e:mite a ~ khak loh nading uh ahi hi) (r:26.46.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:buffalo) (d:lawi lokhawhna leeng, the buffalo-drawn implement for working a field, stands for the plow) (e:~ lokhawhna leeng letsan len kawm a) (r:42.9.62) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawi = (t:v) (w:leave/depart from) (d:with a negative, lawi loin, without ever leaving a place) (e:biakna innpi ~ loin a om hi) (r:42.2.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawkgawpna = (t:n) (w:plundering/pillage) (d:being robbed of everything, with gawp, severely, and the noun ending na) (e:~ leh thongkiatna thuak ding uh hi) (r:27.11.33) (q:draft)
lawma = (t:adv) (w:as a friend) (d:lawm friend with the ending a, as: take or win someone as a friend) (e:galte nangawn ~ kaihzawhna ahi hi) (b:lawm) (r:20.16.7/44.12.20) (q:draft)
lawngsim = (t:v) (w:touch secretly/touch) (d:lawng touch with sim, secretly or quietly: touch without being noticed) (e:a puan mongteep a ~ hi) (r:40.9.20/42.8.44) (q:draft)
lawnmang = (t:v) (w:squander/throw away/waste) (d:lawn throw with mang, away and lost) (e:a neihsa teng ~ hi) (r:20.29.3) (q:draft)
lawnthalin = (t:v) (w:overthrowing/throwing down) (d:lawnthal overthrow with the linking ending in, joining it to the verb that follows) (e:migilote ~ a siasak hi) (b:lawnthal) (r:20.21.12) (q:draft)
lawnthang = (t:v) (w:scatter/throw about) (d:lawn throw with thang, spread around) (e:biakna tau kiimah ka ~ gawp ding hi) (r:26.6.5) (q:draft)
lawpluatna = (t:n) (w:over-eagerness/excessive zeal) (d:lawp eager with lua, too much, and the noun suffix na) (e:Thuthei lopi-in ~ hoih lo a) (r:20.19.2) (q:draft)
lawt = (t:v) (w:come out/burst out) (d:come out of its place: ek lawt khia, the bowels empty themselves; mit lawt dongin kap, weep until the eyes give out) (e:tua ciangin a ek ~ khia hi) (r:7.3.22/9.2.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
lee = (t:todo) (q:draft, only in Siria sakhi lee bangin, like a wild gazelle; what lee adds to sakhi deer is not clear)
leek = (t:v) (w:weigh enough/have weight) (d:of something put on a balance: be heavy enough to bring the scale down; leek lo and leek zo kei are too light, found wanting; also written lek) (e:na ~ zo kei hi) (r:27.5.27/19.62.9) (q:draft)
leemin = (t:v) (w:uncovering/lifting back) (d:leem, lift or turn back a covering, with the linking ending in) (e:a khe lam puan ~ lum in) (r:8.3.4) (q:draft)
leenggahzucil = (t:n) (w:wine/strong wine) (d:leenggahzu wine with cil, in the verse the drink poured out to the Lord as a drink offering; what cil adds is not confirmed) (e:~ tawh biakna pen siangtho munah) (r:4.28.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
leengguino = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:young vine/vine seedling) (d:leenggui vine with no, young) (e:Tua ~ hong khangin a hiangpha) (b:leenggui) (r:26.17.6/26.17.5) (q:draft)
leengguipi = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:great vine/large vine) (d:leenggui vine with pi, big: a full-grown spreading vine) (e:a hiangpha ~ hong suak hi) (b:leenggui) (r:26.17.6) (q:draft)
leengmasel = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:mint) (d:a garden herb of which a tenth was given; also written lengmasel) (e:~ leh anis leh meh namkim) (r:42.11.42/40.23.23) (q:draft)
leengthei = (t:v) (w:be able to fly/fly) (d:leeng fly with thei, can: a leengthei vasate, the birds that fly) (e:a ~ vasate nangawn in mu thei lo) (b:leeng) (r:18.28.21/23.30.6) (q:draft)
leenlak = (t:v) (w:swoop on/pounce on) (d:leen fly with lak take: come down on prey or an enemy as an eagle does) (e:muvanlai bangin ka gam a ~ dingin) (r:28.8.1/35.1.8) (q:draft)
leenpih = (t:v) (w:fly away with/carry off flying) (d:leen fly with pih, together with: take something along in flight) (e:Babylon gamah a ~ ding ahi uh hi) (b:leen) (r:38.5.11/38.5.10) (q:draft)
