muhkhit = (t:v) (w:have seen/after seeing) (d:muh see with khit, finished: used before phetin and ciang for after having seen) (e:Paul in maang a ~ phetin) (r:44.16.10/43.20.29) (q:draft)
muhnopna = (t:n) (w:longing to see/desire to see) (d:muhnop want to see with the noun suffix na) (e:Note in kei na hong ~ thu uh) (b:muhnop) (r:47.7.7/52.3.6) (q:draft)
muhpa = (t:n) (w:the one seen/the one found) (d:muh see or find with pa, the man: the man whom someone sees or finds) (e:tua na ~ uh kamsang mawkmawk ciang bek) (b:muh) (r:40.11.9/40.24.46) (q:draft)
muhsaksa = (t:adj) (w:shown/revealed) (d:muhsak show with sa, already: that has been shown, placed before a noun) (e:Topa in kei hong ~ thute khempeuh) (b:muhsak) (r:26.11.25) (q:draft)
muhtel = (t:v) (w:discern/see clearly/understand) (d:muh see with tel clearly; thu muhtel theihna is discernment, intelligence) (e:thu ~ theihna kiseel ding hi) (r:23.29.14) (q:draft)
muhtheihna = (t:n) (w:ability to see/sight/insight) (d:muhtheih be able to see with the noun suffix na; khua muhtheihna is eyesight, thuthuk muhtheihna is insight into deep things) (e:keimah in thuthuk ~ ka nei a) (b:muhtheih) (r:20.8.12/43.9.8) (q:draft)
mumaang = (t:n) (w:vision) (d:mu see with maang vision: something seen in a vision of the night) (e:~ bangin maimang ding a) (r:18.20.8) (q:draft)
mumeika = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:kite/red kite) (d:a bird of prey in the lists of unclean birds, also written mu-meika) (e:mupi, ~, amau nam ciat) (r:5.14.13/3.11.14) (q:draft)
mumu = (t:v) (w:keep seeing/see again and again) (d:mu see doubled to show repeated or continual seeing) (e:~ napi thei lo) (r:44.28.26/23.6.9) (q:draft)
mundai = (t:n) (w:deserted place/desolate place) (d:mun place with dai quiet: a place where no one lives; mundai suak is become deserted) (e:Ama omna ~ suak hen) (r:44.1.20/24.33.10) (q:draft)
mundangah = (t:adv) (w:to another place/elsewhere) (d:mundang another place with the place marker ah) (e:a vaikhak khit ciangin ~ a paikhia hi) (b:mundang) (r:44.12.17/41.5.10) (q:draft)
mungte = (t:n) (w:doorposts/posts) (d:plural; kongkhak mungte is the posts of a door) (e:a zutna kongkhak ~ panin khamte hawkkhia-in) (r:12.18.16) (q:draft)
munphiah = (t:n) (w:broom) (d:a tool for sweeping, compare phiat sweep) (e:siatna ~ tawh ka phiat khia siang ding hi) (r:23.14.23) (q:draft)
munsangte = (t:n) (w:high places) (d:plural of munsang; places on the heights where other gods were worshipped) (e:amau’ ~ tawh amah a sinso nadingin) (r:19.78.58) (q:draft)
musakkik = (t:v) (w:let see again/show again) (d:musak cause to see with kik again; of sight, make the eyes see again) (e:ka mit uh khua hong ~ in) (b:musak) (r:40.20.33/10.15.25) (q:draft)
musan = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:kite) (d:a bird of prey in the list of unclean birds, apparently with san red; the English versions have kite and black kite here) (e:mumeika, ~ nam khempeuh) (r:3.11.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
musuk = (t:v) (w:see down/look down and see) (d:mu see with suk downward: see what is below, as God from heaven) (e:Pasian in hong ~ thei lo ding hi) (b:mu) (r:18.22.14) (q:draft)
mutgawpna = (t:n) (w:blasting/blight) (d:mutgawp blow violently with the noun suffix na; huihpi mutgawpna is the blasting of crops by wind) (e:huihpi ~, leh a nom tawh) (b:mutgawp) (r:5.28.22) (q:draft)
mutkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:blow away) (d:mutkhiat blow away with sak; kong mutkhiatsak is I blew it away from you) (e:kong ~ mang khin hi) (b:mutkhiat) (r:37.1.9) (q:draft)
mutsia = (t:v) (w:wreck by blowing/blow to ruin) (d:mut blow with sia be ruined: of wind, break something up by blowing) (e:tuipi laizangah nang hong ~ hi) (r:26.27.26) (q:draft)
naai = (t:n) (w:slime) (d:in a naai a bei toktol, said where the English has a slug or snail that melts away as it goes; the word may name the slime or the creature itself) (e:a ~ a bei toktol) (r:19.58.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
naang = (t:v) (w:be still alive/hold out) (d:in ka naang lai hi, I am still alive, said by a man mortally wounded; perhaps the same word as nang, withstand) (e:ahi zongin ka ~ lai hi) (r:10.1.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
nadangte = (t:n) (w:other things) (d:na thing with dang other and the plural te) (e:~ khempeuh eek hi ci-in ka ngaihsun hi) (r:50.3.9/44.27.44) (q:draft)
nahpa = (t:n) (w:stubble/chaff) (d:dry stalks or husks that the wind carries off; nahpa keu is dry stubble) (e:huihpi in ~ keu bangin amaute) (r:23.40.24/23.41.2) (q:draft)
nahteh = (t:n) (w:leaves/fallen leaves) (d:nah and teh both mean leaf; nahteh muat is rotten leaves, used where the English has scum and refuse) (e:a kihhuai ~ muat bangin na hong bawl hi) (r:25.3.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
naipuan = (t:n) (w:silk/silk cloth) (d:a costly fine cloth, with puan cloth) (e:~ tungsilh kong silhsak hi) (r:26.16.10/26.16.13) (q:draft)
nakbuhte = (t:n) (w:nose rings) (d:nak nose with buh ring, as in zungbuh finger ring, and the plural te) (e:min gelhna zungbuhte leh ~) (r:23.3.21) (q:draft)
nakgen = (t:v) (w:tell much/talk freely about/keep telling) (d:gen tell with nak before it, strongly, much; nakkham le nakgen is the more he forbade the more they told) (e:Hih thu ~ lua-in kitheithang gawp) (r:41.1.45/41.7.36) (q:draft)
naksiat = (t:v) (w:be badly ruined/be utterly destroyed) (d:siat be ruined with nak before it, strongly, greatly: the ruin was great) (e:Tua inn ~ mahmah hi) (r:40.7.27/42.6.49) (q:draft)
naktoh = (t:n) (w:breath/breathing) (d:nak nose or breathe with toh upward; used in the pair naksuk naktoh, breathing down and up, for breath or the power to breathe) (e:naksuk ~ theihna nei lo uh hi) (b:nak) (r:19.135.17/44.17.25) (q:draft)
nakvangte = (t:n) (w:nostrils) (e:Ama ~ panin meikhu pusuak a) (b:nakvang) (r:19.18.8) (q:draft)
nal = (t:adj) (w:slippery) (d:nal sak is make slippery) (e:lampi uh mial-in ~ sak in) (r:19.35.6/24.23.12) (q:draft)
nalna-ah = (t:adv) (w:on slippery ground/in a slippery place) (d:nal slippery with the noun suffix na and the place marker ah; mun nalna is a slippery place) (e:amaute mun ~ na koih takpi a) (r:19.73.18) (q:draft)
namdangpi = (t:adj) (w:foreign/alien) (d:namdang of another people with pi; mi namdangpi is a foreigner, one whose speech is not understood) (e:kei a dingin mi ~ khat hi ding hi) (b:namdang) (r:46.14.11) (q:draft)
namkimin = (t:adv) (w:of every kind/of all kinds) (d:namkim all kinds with in; a namkimin after a noun is all sorts of) (e:Na a manpha a ~ i sut ding a) (b:namkim) (r:20.1.13) (q:draft)
nampi = (t:adj) (w:noble/excellent) (d:nam kind with pi great: of high kind; said of the holy people where the English has the noble ones) (e:amaute ~ hi a) (b:nam) (r:19.16.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangin = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:nang you with the subject marker in, written as one word) (e:Tua nung ciangin ~ an ne-in) (b:nang) (r:42.17.8) (q:draft)
nangin = (t:conj) (w:in order to/so that) (d:after a verb, for the purpose of; apparently a short form of nadingin) (e:ama dikna thu kilat ~ ahi zongin) (r:45.3.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
nangnawn = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:placed after the word or phrase it stresses; another spelling of nangawn) (e:a inn gei ~-ah pai kha kei un) (r:20.5.8/27.3.22) (q:draft)
nangzote = (t:n) (w:those who persevere/those who withstand) (d:nangzo withstand with the plural te: the ones who stand firm under trial) (e:a ~ a hampha mahmah ahi hi) (b:nangzo) (r:59.1.12) (q:draft)
nanzawh = (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/stand against) (d:nan withstand with zawh be able; the form of nangzo used before ding and nading) (e:eite in bangci ~ ding ihi hiam) (r:12.10.4/3.26.37) (q:draft)
nappa = (t:n) (w:the one kissed) (d:nap kiss with pa, the man: ka nappa is the man I kiss) (e:Ka ~ in Zeisu ahi hi) (b:nap) (r:40.26.48/41.14.44) (q:draft)
nasemnute = (t:n) (w:maidservants/female servants) (e:na nasempate, na ~, na ganhing uh) (b:nasemnu) (r:2.20.10/5.5.14) (q:draft)
nasiasak = (t:v) (w:make severe/make worse/aggravate) (d:nasia severe with sak cause) (e:ka mite’ gimna ~ semsem uh hi) (b:nasia) (r:38.1.15) (q:draft)
nasiazaw = (t:adj) (w:more severe/worse/greater) (d:nasia severe with the comparative zaw) (e:a thuak ding a ~ omlai a) (b:nasia) (r:23.15.9/40.23.14) (q:draft)
nasim = (t:v) (w:regard/respect/esteem) (d:used with lo not: nasim lo is show no respect for, count as nothing; perhaps na thing with sim count) (e:unau khat ahih uh ciangin ~ lo) (r:54.6.2/44.19.27) (q:draft)
natsakna = (t:n) (w:affliction/infliction of pain) (d:nat be ill or in pain with sak cause and the noun suffix na: a making sick or causing of pain) (e:Pasian in ci ~ tawh mihing thuhilh a) (r:18.33.19/5.29.22) (q:draft)
naucing = (t:n) (w:nurse/nursemaid) (d:nau child with cing look after: a woman who nurses and cares for a baby) (e:naupang hong khoisak dingin ~ khat) (r:2.2.7) (q:draft)
naudom = (t:n) (w:midwife) (d:nau child with dom lift up, hold: one who helps at a birth; followed by nu, woman) (e:a gim mahmah laitakin ~ nu in ama kiangah) (r:1.35.17/1.38.28) (q:draft)
naudomnu = (t:n) (w:midwife) (d:naudom with nu, woman) (e:~ in khausan khat la-in a khut tungah) (b:naudom) (r:1.38.28/1.35.17) (q:draft)
naupangpa = (t:n) (w:boy/lad) (d:naupang child with pa, male: a boy, here a young servant) (e:Jonathan in a hiamte a ~ kiangah pia-in) (b:naupang) (r:9.20.40/9.20.38) (q:draft)
nausia = (t:v) (w:miscarry) (d:nau child with sia be spoiled: lose a child before birth; also of the woman to whom it happens) (e:kuamah ~ om lo ding a) (r:2.23.26) (q:draft)
navakna = (t:n) (w:insight/intelligence/keenness) (d:navak quick-witted with the noun suffix na; lungsim navakna is brightness of mind) (e:theihna leh lungsim ~ a nei hi) (b:navak) (r:27.5.11) (q:draft)
nawhkhiat = (t:v) (w:drive out/expel) (d:form of nawhkhia used before khit ciangin and other following words) (e:amaute a ~ khit ciangin) (b:nawhkhia) (r:5.9.4) (q:draft)
nawhkhiatnate = (t:n) (w:things that drive away/acts of driving out) (d:nawhkhiat drive out with the noun suffix na and the plural te: the deeds that drive someone away) (e:a gamla semsemah kei hong ~ en in) (r:26.8.6) (q:draft)
nawhpai = (t:v) (w:hurry/go quickly/speed past) (d:nawh hurry with pai go) (e:Amaute ~ mahmah uh a) (r:42.2.16/18.9.26) (q:draft)
nawhtatna = (t:n) (w:haste/hastiness/hurry) (d:nawhtat hurry with the noun suffix na; mawk nawhtatna is thoughtless haste) (e:mawk ~ in lungkhamna piangsak thei hi) (b:nawhtat) (r:20.19.2) (q:draft)
nawlhui = (t:n) (w:edge/edges) (d:the outer edge of the beard, khamul nawlhui; from nawl edge) (e:amau’ khamul ~ zong kiat loin) (r:3.21.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
nawmvalhna = (t:n) (w:swallowing/swallowing up) (d:nawmvalh swallow with the noun suffix na: the event of the earth swallowing them) (e:amaute a ~ ngaihsun un) (b:nawmvalh) (r:5.11.6) (q:draft)
nawngkaina = (t:n) (w:hindrance/disturbance/trouble) (d:nawngkai be troubled or hindered with the noun suffix na) (e:~ khat beek om loin) (b:nawngkai) (r:44.28.31/44.16.20) (q:draft)
nawngpi = (t:n) (w:marsh/swamp/great marsh) (d:nawng marsh with pi great: wet ground where grass and reeds grow) (e:omna ngei leitang pen ~ suakin) (b:nawng) (r:23.35.7) (q:draft)
nawtsuak = (t:v) (w:press on/go right through/march on) (d:nawt push forward with suak through to the end; mai nawtsuak is march on) (e:Thakhauh takin mai ~ ding) (r:7.5.21/48.5.12) (q:draft)
nawtsuk = (t:v) (w:sweep down/push down into) (d:nawt push forward with suk downward: of flood water, press on down into a land) (e:Judah gam dong hong ~ ding a) (b:nawt) (r:23.8.8) (q:draft)
neelna = (t:n) (w:smoothness) (d:neel smooth with the noun suffix na; a neelna mun is the smooth part, the place where it is smooth) (e:a ~ mun a ngawng sanah silhsak a) (b:neel) (r:1.27.16) (q:draft)
negawp = (t:v) (w:devour/eat up) (d:ne eat with gawp, severely, completely) (e:humpi khat in ~ ding hi) (b:ne) (r:23.15.9/24.50.7) (q:draft)
nehpiksan = (t:v) (w:sneer at/scorn/despise) (d:treat with contempt) (e:amah in ~ lel hi) (r:19.10.5) (q:draft)
neihlai = (t:v) (w:still have) (d:neih, form of nei, have, with lai, still) (e:Gen ding tampi ka ~ hangin) (r:63.1.12/66.3.2) (q:draft)
neihtheihna = (t:n) (d:neihtheih, be able to have, with the noun suffix na; with ding it means so that one may have) (e:lungnopna na ~ dingun hih thu) (b:neihtheih) (r:43.16.33/56.3.8) (q:draft)
neilote = (t:n) (w:those who do not have/those without) (d:neilo, not have, with the plural te; pa neilote is the fatherless) (e:A ~ kiang pan a neihsa) (b:neilo) (r:40.13.12/24.22.3) (q:draft)
neisun = (t:v) (w:have/happen to have) (d:nei, have, with sun; in the verse, should one have any at all) (e:Mavanna khatpeuh ~ leng zong) (r:18.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
neithuah = (t:v) (w:have in addition/have besides/have more) (d:nei, have, with thuah, in addition) (e:tampi tak ka ~ hi) (r:21.2.7/10.19.28) (q:draft)
nekhawmin = (t:v) (w:eating together) (d:nekhawm, eat together, with in, linking to the next verb; an nekhawm renders breaking bread) (e:amaute tawh an ~) (b:nekhawm) (r:44.2.42/44.2.46) (q:draft)
nekin = (t:v) (w:eating/as food) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with in: note’ nekin is as food for you, uang nekin is eating to excess) (e:uang ~ na noptat mahmah uh hi) (b:nek) (r:59.5.5/26.34.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
nekkhak = (t:v) (w:eat by mistake/eat unintentionally/swallow by accident) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with khak, happen to) (e:an khat peuhpeuh a ~ leh) (r:3.22.14/20.23.7) (q:draft)
nekkhop = (t:v) (w:eat together/eat with) (d:form of nekhawm used before ding and ut) (e:note tawh ~ ka ut mahmah hi) (r:42.22.15) (q:draft)
neknekna-in = (t:n) (d:nek, eat or drink, doubled for a repeated action, with the noun suffix na and in: from continually drinking or eating) (e:bawngnawi a ~ a ha pak hi) (r:1.49.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
neksa = (t:v) (w:eaten/have eaten) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with sa, already done: what has been eaten) (e:Na ~ teng na luakhia kik ding a) (b:nek) (r:20.23.8) (q:draft)
nektumsak = (t:v) (w:eat up/devour/consume) (d:nektum, eat up, with sak: eat up what belongs to another, or cause to be eaten up) (e:neihsa teng na ~ uh a) (b:nektum) (r:40.23.14/19.105.35) (q:draft)
nelzaw = (t:adj) (w:smoother/softer) (d:nel, smooth, with zaw, more) (e:thawhbat sangin ~ a) (b:nel) (r:19.55.21) (q:draft)
nengneng = (t:n) (w:equipment/small parts/accessories) (d:the small items that belong to something larger) (e:a ~ teng leh hihte tawh) (r:4.3.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
nengnengte = (t:n) (w:small parts/accessories) (d:nengneng with the plural te: the small items that belong to something larger) (e:a nazatte khempeuh leh a ~ ahi hi) (b:nengneng) (r:4.4.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
nengniampa = (t:n) (w:oppressor) (d:nengniam, oppress, with pa marking a man: the one who oppresses) (e:A ~ om nawn loin) (b:nengniam) (r:23.16.4/23.14.4) (q:draft)
nenniam = (t:v) (w:oppress/subdue/humble) (d:press down, bring low) (e:keimah hong dote ka nuai-ah na ~ hi) (r:19.18.39/9.12.8) (q:draft)
nesim = (t:v) (w:eat secretly) (d:ne, eat, with sim, secretly) (e:amah in tuate ~ ding hi) (r:5.28.57/5.28.56) (q:draft)
neubel = (t:adj) (w:least/smallest) (d:neu, small, with bel, most) (e:a ~ akipan a golbel dongin) (r:58.8.11/46.15.9) (q:draft)
neucik = (t:adj) (w:tiny/very small/little) (e:letsong ~ khat hangin) (r:20.28.21) (q:draft)
neuna = (t:n) (w:smallness/small size) (d:neu, small, with the noun suffix na; a golna leh a neuna is how large or small something is) (e:a golna leh a ~ tawh kizui-in) (b:neu) (r:16.12.44) (q:draft)
neuneu = (t:adj) (w:small/little) (d:neu, small, doubled, said of several small things) (e:biakinn kimkotah inndei ~ om a) (r:26.41.5) (q:draft)
nezo = (t:v) (w:be able to eat/manage to eat) (d:ne, eat, with zo, be able) (e:an nangawn ka ~ kei hi) (b:ne) (r:19.102.4/46.3.2) (q:draft)
ngaam = (t:v) (w:grow weak/waste away) (d:said of the bones in the verse) (e:ka tha kiam a, ka guhte ~ hi) (r:19.31.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngabeng = (t:n) (w:fisherman) (d:nga, fish, with beng, hunt; compare sabeng, hunter) (e:~ tampi ka khah ding a) (r:24.16.16/40.4.18) (q:draft)
ngahkhin = (t:v) (w:have received/have already received) (d:ngah, receive, with khin, already done) (e:nopsakna ~ na hih manun) (b:ngah) (r:42.6.24/44.2.33) (q:draft)
ngahlawh = (t:v) (w:incur/get as a result/bring upon oneself) (d:ngah, receive, with lawh: receive trouble or harm as a consequence) (e:huhau-in siatna a ~ hi) (r:19.106.32/45.11.9) (q:draft)
ngahthuah = (t:v) (w:gain in addition/gain more) (d:ngah, receive, with thuah, in addition) (e:a meet tulnih mah a ~ hi) (r:40.25.17/40.25.16) (q:draft)
ngahthuapna = (t:n) (w:allowance/provision) (d:what a person is regularly given to live on) (e:~ ama tungah kumpipa in pia hi) (r:12.25.30) (q:draft)
ngaihbaangin = (t:adj) (w:lovely/handsome/attractive) (d:ngaihbaang, pleasing to look at, with in, linking to what follows) (e:Tu-in Josef ~ a mel hoih hi) (b:ngaihbaang) (r:1.39.6/20.5.19) (q:draft)
ngaihban'na = (t:n) (w:charm/attractiveness/loveliness) (d:ngaihbaang, lovely, with the noun suffix na) (e:~ in zuaupi hi thei a) (r:20.31.30/20.5.20) (q:draft)
ngaihin = (t:v) (w:heeding/listening to) (d:ngaih with in; ngaihin nei is give heed to, hold dear) (e:zuauthu mah ~ nei hi) (b:ngaih) (r:20.17.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngaihngaih = (t:v) (w:keep listening/listen again and again) (d:ngaih, listen, doubled for a continued action) (e:Thu na ~ uh hangin na tel kei ding) (r:44.28.25/22.4.3) (q:draft)
ngaihsak = (t:v) (w:listen attentively/pay attention to) (d:ngaih, listen, with sak) (e:Amau’ thugente ka ~ a) (b:ngaih) (r:24.8.6) (q:draft)
ngaihsuna = (t:v) (w:thinking of/considering) (d:ngaihsun, think, with the linking a) (e:Ka mangmuhna ~ ka om lai takin) (b:ngaihsun) (r:27.4.13/47.7.12) (q:draft)
ngaihsunsunin = (t:v) (w:pondering/thinking over and over) (d:ngaihsunsun, keep thinking about, with in, linking to the next verb) (e:Ka lupna tungah nangmah hong ~) (b:ngaihsunsun) (r:19.63.5/26.3.15) (q:draft)
