nungto = (t:v) (w:blow up/blow upward) (d:of wind: nung, blow, with to, upward; paired with nungsuk, blow down, and said to the south wind in the verse) (e:khanglam huih aw, hong ~ in) (r:22.4.16) (q:draft)
nungzuih = (t:v) (w:follow/follow after) (d:nung, behind, with zuih, form of zui, follow: go after someone) (e:Peter in zong a kihalin ~ hi) (b:nungzui) (r:42.22.54/41.1.36) (q:draft)
nunna = (t:n) (w:blowing) (d:nun, blow, of wind, with the noun suffix na; huih nunna lam is where the wind blows, huihpi nunna gam a land swept by storms) (e:sehnel gam, huihpi ~ gam sungah) (b:nun) (r:5.32.10/59.1.6) (q:draft)
nuntakdan = (t:n) (w:way of life/conduct/manner of living) (d:nuntak, live, with dan, manner) (e:lungsim kikhat leh ~ kikhat ka pia ding hi) (r:24.32.39/24.32.19) (q:draft)
nuntakkik = (t:v) (w:live again/come back to life) (d:nuntak, live, with kik, again; nuntakkik sak is raise to life again) (e:Ka ~ theih nadingin si ngam) (b:nuntak) (r:43.10.17/44.13.37) (q:draft)
nunungpen = (t:adj) (w:last/very last/lowest) (d:nunung, last, with pen, most; in Luke 22.26 of the follower of lowest rank, the one who serves) (e:a tum ~ pan a kipanin) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.8/42.22.26) (q:draft)
nusiacip = (t:v) (w:abandon/leave behind/forsake) (d:nusia, leave, with cip, firmly: leave and not come back for it) (e:gamah kei nong ~ kei ding a) (b:nusia) (r:44.2.27/26.31.12) (q:draft)
nusiatlai = (t:adj) (w:left behind/remaining/spared) (d:nusiat, leave, with lai, still: describes people or things that someone has left where they were) (e:ka nuntaksak, ka ~ mite a mawhna uh) (r:24.50.20/24.27.19) (q:draft)
nusiatna = (t:n) (w:forsaking/abandonment/desertion) (d:nusiat, forsake, with the noun suffix na; kei hong nusiatna uh is their forsaking me) (e:kei hong ~ uh leh keimah sangin milim) (b:nusiat) (r:26.6.9) (q:draft)
nutate = (t:n) (w:mother and daughter/mother and child) (d:nuta, mother and child, with the plural ending te; in the verse a woman and her mother who are married to one man) (e:tuapa leh a ~, mei tawh kihallum ding hi) (b:nuta) (r:3.20.14) (q:draft)
olna = (t:n) (w:ease/easiness) (d:ol, easy, with the noun suffix na; nuntak olna gam is a land where living is easy, a good land) (e:nuntak ~ gam hiam, haksatna gam hiam) (b:ol) (r:4.13.19) (q:draft)
oltak = (t:adv) (w:easily/at ease) (d:ol, easy, with tak making an adverb; oltak a nuntakna is a life of ease, rest) (e:Hih minamte lakah ~ a nuntakna na mu kei) (b:ol) (r:5.28.65/20.13.11) (q:draft)
omkhawmsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be with/put together with) (d:omkhawm, be together, with sak, cause: make or let someone be in the same place as others) (e:misimtatte tawh a ~ ding hi) (b:omkhawm) (r:40.24.51/43.17.24) (q:draft)
omkhol = (t:v) (w:be ready/be prepared) (d:om, be, with khol, beforehand: be in readiness for what is to be done) (e:sihna nangawn thuak dingin ka ~ hi) (r:44.21.13/44.23.15) (q:draft)
omlo = (t:adj) (w:without/lacking) (d:om, be, with lo, not: where something is not present, as mi omlo, without people, and silngo-omlo, without yeast, unleavened) (e:na inn uh mi ~ gam simthamin kinusia) (b:om) (r:40.23.38/44.12.3) (q:draft)
ommah = (t:v) (w:indeed be/be just so) (d:om, be, with mah for emphasis: a ommah ding is there must indeed be, a ommah bangin is just as one was) (e:kikhenna a ~ ding ahi hi) (b:om) (r:46.11.19/28.2.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
ommawkna = (t:n) (w:idleness/sitting idle/inaction) (d:ommawk, be idle, with the noun suffix na; khutzepin ommawkna is sitting idle with folded hands) (e:khutzepin ~ hangin) (b:ommawk) (r:20.24.33/23.37.26) (q:draft)
omnuam = (t:v) (w:want to be/want to stay) (d:om, be, with nuam, want) (e:Thukham nuai-ah a ~ mite aw) (r:48.4.21) (q:draft)
omnuam = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/agreeable) (d:om, be, with nuam, pleasant: of a person who is pleasant to be with; the English has fine-looking) (e:a ~ mi khat ka mu a) (r:9.16.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
ompi = (t:v) (w:be there/be present) (d:om, be, with pi; in a ompi mahin, even though they were there; what pi adds is not clear) (e:Khaldea mite khuapi kiimah a ~ mahin) (b:om) (r:12.25.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
omsuakin = (t:v) (w:remaining/staying on) (d:omsuak, remain, with in linking it to what follows) (e:ama gam mahah Judah ~) (b:omsuak) (r:6.18.5/22.4.6) (q:draft)
omsung = (t:n) (w:stay/time of staying) (d:om, be, with sung, within or during: the time while someone is in a place; ka omsung khempeuh is all the time I was there) (e:amaute tawh ka ~ khempeuh uh) (r:9.25.16/1.47.9) (q:draft)
omtual = (t:v) (w:stay/dwell/keep to) (d:om, be, with tual; in the verse the wise keep among mourning and fools among pleasure) (e:Mipilte dahna lakah ~ a) (r:21.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
omvat = (t:v) (w:appear suddenly/be there all at once) (d:om, be, with vat, suddenly) (e:Moses le Elijah hong ~ uh a) (r:40.17.3/42.9.30) (q:draft)
otkhai-in = (t:v) (w:shouting after/shouting at) (d:ot, shout, with khai and the linking in; of people who shout as they chase a thief away; what khai adds is not clear) (e:Gutate ~ a kidelh bangin) (r:18.30.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
otsanin = (t:v) (w:shouting to/calling out to) (d:otsan, shout to, with in linking it to the words that are shouted) (e:Amah dingin Israel uliante ~) (b:otsan) (r:9.17.8) (q:draft)
paaikhiasak = (t:v) (w:take out for/remove for) (d:paaikhia, throw out or remove, with sak, do it for another; hong paaikhiasak in is let me take it out for you) (e:a om ninneng tang hong ~ in) (b:paaikhia) (r:40.7.4/42.6.42) (q:draft)
paakin = (t:v) (w:blossoming/blooming) (d:paak, flower, used as a verb, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:~, almond min gah a gah hi) (b:paak) (r:4.17.8) (q:draft)
paam = (t:n) (w:surroundings/neighbourhood) (d:found in the pair kiim and paam, each with its own pronoun: i kiim i paam and ka kiim ka paam, all around us) (e:ka kiim ka ~ uh a mite khempeuh) (r:27.9.16/16.5.17) (q:draft)
paangah = (t:n) (w:in the temple/at the temple) (d:paang, the temple of the head, with ah, at or into) (e:a ~ a khensuk hi) (b:paang) (r:7.4.21/7.4.22) (q:draft)
paatsak = (t:v) (w:wear out/wear down/exhaust) (d:paat, be worn out, with sak, cause) (e:Pasian aw, kei nong ~ ngiingei a) (b:paat) (r:18.16.7) (q:draft)
pahtakbawl = (t:v) (w:speak well of/praise/treat with favour) (d:pahtak, favour or approval, with bawl, do or make: show someone approval) (e:kamsang zuaute a ~ uh hi) (b:pahtak) (r:42.6.26) (q:draft)
pahtawite = (t:n) (w:those who honor) (d:pahtawi, honor, with te, those who) (e:kei hong ~ ka pahtawi ding a) (b:pahtawi) (r:9.2.30) (q:draft)
pahte = (t:adv) (d:pah, at once or readily, after a verb, with te, those who: a zuak pahte, those who sell readily, a mang pahte, those who accept at once) (e:lei nop hun-a a zuak ~ kiphat hi) (b:pah) (r:20.11.26/42.8.13) (q:draft)
paihdak = (t:v) (w:cast away/throw down) (d:paih, throw away, with dak; in the verse of God casting his people into deep darkness; what dak adds is not clear) (e:khuamialpi sungah nong ~ dinga kilawm zahin) (r:19.44.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
paiite = (t:n) (w:goods/valuables/treasures) (d:used together with sum, money, as sum leh paiite and na sum na paiite, money and possessions; compare sumlepai) (e:a neihsa uh sum leh ~) (r:37.2.7/24.15.13) (q:draft)
paikawm = (t:v) (w:while going/while walking) (d:pai, go, with kawm, while: as one goes along, at the same time as another action) (e:Mihaite lampi-ah a ~ nangawnin hai tat uh) (r:21.10.3/44.3.8) (q:draft)
paikhak = (t:v) (w:go near/happen to go/come near) (d:form of paikha used before ciangin) (e:biakinn nai-ah Israel mite a ~ ciangin) (b:paikha) (r:4.8.19) (q:draft)
paikhawmsak = (t:v) (w:send together with/let go with) (d:paikhawm, go together, with sak, make or let) (e:keima nasemte ~ in) (b:paikhawm) (r:11.22.49/44.15.22) (q:draft)
paikhiatnapa = (t:n) (w:man from whom something went out) (d:paikhiatna, going out, with pa marking a man: in the verses the man out of whom the demons had gone) (e:Dawite a ~ in Zeisu tawh) (b:paikhiatna) (r:42.8.38/42.8.35) (q:draft)
paikhiazo = (t:v) (w:have gone out/have come out/have set out) (d:paikhia, go out, with zo marking the action as done) (e:na tanu sung panin dawi a ~ hi) (b:paikhia) (r:41.7.29/24.4.7) (q:draft)
paikhop = (t:v) (w:go together with/come with/accompany) (d:pai, go, with khop, together; form of paikhawm used before ciangin and lai takin) (e:vantungmite tawh hong ~ ciangin) (r:40.25.31/42.12.58) (q:draft)
paikhopna = (t:n) (w:going together/accompanying) (d:paikhop, go together with, with the noun suffix na; nong paikhopna is your going with us) (e:kote tawh nang nong ~ hi lo) (b:paikhop) (r:2.33.16) (q:draft)
paikikna = (t:n) (w:return/coming back/coming again) (d:paikik, return, with the noun suffix na) (e:Zion-ah Topa hong ~ amaute in maitang) (b:paikik) (r:23.52.8/61.1.16) (q:draft)
paikim = (t:v) (w:all come/all go) (d:pai, go or come, with kim, all without exception: come every one of them) (e:a ~ ciat dingin sapna thu) (r:27.3.2) (q:draft)
paipahin = (t:v) (w:going at once/coming straight up) (d:paipah, go at once, with in linking it to the next verb) (e:Judas zong Jesuh kiangah hong ~) (b:paipah) (r:40.26.49/15.5.3) (q:draft)
paiphei = (t:v) (w:go across/run along) (d:pai, go, with phei, crosswise or level; in the verse of a row of rooms running along one level of a building) (e:dawl khat gual ~ suak-ah inndei neu sawmthum) (r:26.41.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
paipihtoh = (t:v) (w:bring up/take up/lead up) (d:form of paipihto used before a kipan and theih) (e:Israel-te ka ~ a kipan tuni dongin) (b:paipihto) (r:13.17.5/13.15.12) (q:draft)
paisakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/send again/let come again) (d:paisak, send or let go, with kik, again or back) (e:kiangah hong ~ inla) (b:paisak) (r:7.13.8/58.13.19) (q:draft)
paisuakpah = (t:v) (w:go straight at once/go directly) (d:pai, go, with suak, right through, and pah, at once: go straight there without delay) (e:Siampipa kiangah ~ inla kivelsak in) (r:42.5.14/41.1.29) (q:draft)
paisuakzawh = (t:v) (w:be able to continue/manage to go on) (d:paisuak, right on or continuing, with zawh, be able; placed after another verb, as thuak paisuakzawh, be able to go on enduring) (e:gimna i thuak ~ leh amah tawh i ukkhawm) (r:55.2.12/46.7.11) (q:draft)
paizaw = (t:v) (w:go rather/go instead) (d:pai, go, with zaw, rather) (e:Israel mite lakah va ~ un) (b:pai) (r:40.10.6/48.1.17) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:be able to come/get in) (d:pai, come or go, with zo, be able) (e:David hong ~ peuhmah lo ding hi) (b:pai) (r:10.5.6) (q:draft)
paizo = (t:v) (w:have come) (d:pai, come, with zo marking the action as done) (e:a susia dingte hong ~ uh hi) (b:pai) (r:24.12.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
pakkualte = (t:n) (w:wreaths/garlands) (d:pakkual, wreath, with the plural ending te) (e:bawngtalte le ~ hong paipih hi) (b:pakkual) (r:44.14.13) (q:draft)
paktatin = (t:v) (w:committing prostitution/acting immorally) (d:paktat, prostitute oneself, with in linking it to the next verb; paktatin gamta is behave as a prostitute) (e:Na monu Tamar ~ gamta hi) (b:paktat) (r:1.38.24/66.18.9) (q:draft)
paktatnate = (t:n) (w:prostitutions/immoral acts) (d:paktatna, prostitution, with the plural ending te; in the verse of Jezebel, where the English has idolatry) (e:~ leh aisannate tua zahin a tam) (b:paktatna) (r:12.9.22) (q:draft)
palhngulhna = (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/adultery) (d:palhngulh, be unfaithful to, with the noun suffix na; in the verse of a people unfaithful to God) (e:gamtatnate tawh ~ a bawl uh hi) (b:palhngulh) (r:19.106.39) (q:draft)
palhte = (t:n) (w:blooms/open flowers) (d:palh, bloom, with the plural ending te; pak palhte is flowers in bloom) (e:nisuh kungte leh pak ~ bawl hi) (b:palh) (r:11.6.29/23.5.24) (q:draft)
palikmangte = (t:n) (w:officers/guard officers) (d:palik, police or guard, with mang, chief or officer, and the plural ending te; biakinncing palikmangte is the officers of the temple guard) (e:siampi liante le biakinncing ~ tawh va kiho) (r:42.22.4/42.22.52) (q:draft)
paltan = (t:v) (w:pass through/go through/cross) (d:go across a land from one side to the other) (e:Amah in Samaria gam ~ a) (r:43.4.4/41.7.31) (q:draft)
pangkhawm = (t:v) (w:side with/stand with/join with) (d:pang, take a side, with khawm, together) (e:amaute zong David tawh ~ uh a) (b:pang) (r:9.22.17/50.1.7) (q:draft)
pangsimin = (t:v) (w:lie in wait/ambush) (d:pangsim, lie in wait for someone, with the linking ending in) (e:hong ~ kei do dingin) (b:pangsim) (r:9.22.13) (q:draft)
pangtatte = (t:n) (w:prostitutes) (d:in numei pangtatte, immoral women; pangtat appears to be another spelling of paktat, with the plural te) (e:mawh mite leh numei ~) (r:23.57.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
pankhia = (t:v) (w:begin/start/set about) (d:pan, begin, with khia, out: start off a work, be the one to begin it) (e:nasep hoih a hong ~ Pasian in) (b:pan) (r:50.1.6/47.8.10) (q:draft)
pankik = (t:v) (w:take up again/declare again) (d:pan, take a stand or begin, with kik, again; teci pankik is testify again, and of a thing given up, take it up again) (e:teci ka ~ inah) (b:pan) (r:48.5.3/48.2.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
panpihin = (t:v) (w:side with/support/favour) (d:panpih, take the part of, with the linking ending in) (e:pawlkhat in Jew mite ~) (b:panpih) (r:44.14.4/18.10.3) (q:draft)
panpihna = (t:n) (w:support/upholding) (d:panpih, take the part of, with the noun suffix na: the taking of someone’s side, upholding of a cause) (e:a thuak mite’ thu a ~) (b:panpih) (r:19.140.12) (q:draft)
pansimna = (t:n) (w:ambush/hiding place) (d:a lying in wait and the place of it; pansim, lie in wait, with the noun suffix na) (e:a ~ panun dingto uh hi) (r:7.9.35/15.8.31) (q:draft)
patauh = (t:v) (w:be alarmed/be dismayed) (d:form of patau used before huai and nading: patauh huai, alarming, shocking) (e:bangmah ~ nading om lo hi) (b:patau) (r:52.5.3/24.5.30) (q:draft)
pataukoh = (t:v) (w:sound the alarm/signal) (d:patau, alarm, with koh, call out: give the alarm call, as with trumpets in war) (e:leh ~ nadingin peengkulte) (r:4.31.6) (q:draft)
patkhaute = (t:n) (w:threads/strings) (d:pat, cotton, with khau, cord, and the plural te: cotton thread, a strand of tow) (e:~ in mei a suk khak ciangin) (r:7.16.9) (q:draft)
patkhiat = (t:v) (w:begin/lead off/start) (d:pat, begin, with khiat, out; form of patkhia used before ding: start off a prayer or song for others to follow) (e:koh thungetna ~ ding a makai Asaf) (b:pat) (r:16.11.17) (q:draft)
patlom = (t:n) (w:tinder/tow) (d:a bunch of cotton or fibre that catches fire easily; pat, cotton, with lom, bundle) (e:mipa pen ~ tawh kibang ding a) (r:23.1.31) (q:draft)
pattahsa = (t:v) (w:reared/brought up) (d:pattah, bring up or nurture a child, with sa marking the action as done: whom one has reared) (e:Ka ~ tapate in kei hong lehdo) (r:23.1.2) (q:draft)
patun = (t:v) (d:pat, begin, with the ending un; found in the pair na pian’ na patun, from birth and beginning, that is by birth) (e:ka pian’ ka ~ Jew mi ka hi) (b:pat) (r:48.2.15/49.2.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
paubanna = (t:n) (w:blemish/defect) (d:pauban, blemish, with the noun suffix na; with om lo, without defect) (e:~ a om lo bawngtal khat) (b:pauban) (r:26.43.23/26.43.25) (q:draft)
paudang = (t:n) (w:foreign language/strange tongue) (d:pau, language, with dang, other) (e:innkuanpihte ~ a zang mite kiang) (r:19.114.1) (q:draft)
paunasate = (t:n) (w:things said/words spoken) (d:pau, speak, with the noun suffix na, sa for what is already done, and the plural te: the things one has said) (e:ka ~ khempeuh hangin ka maizum a) (r:18.42.6) (q:draft)
paupah = (t:v) (w:begin to speak/speak at once) (d:pau, speak, with pah, straight away) (e:zong hong tuto-in hong ~ hi) (r:42.7.15/44.19.6) (q:draft)
paupakna = (t:n) (w:rash talk/hasty speech) (d:speaking out without thought; pau, speak, with pak, hastily, and the noun suffix na) (e:migilote’ ~ in thusia tawh kizom hi) (r:20.15.28) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupaute = (t:n) (d:paupau, keep talking, with te, those who: kihisak-a paupaute, those who talk on proudly) (e:kihisak-a kam ~ buaina ding a zongzong) (b:paupau) (r:20.17.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupeengsak = (t:v) (w:make stubborn/harden) (d:paupeeng, be stubborn or obstinate, with the causative sak) (e:a paupeensak nopte ~ hi) (r:45.9.18/5.2.30) (q:draft)
pautheilote = (t:n) (w:the mute/the dumb) (d:pau thei lo, not able to speak, with the plural te: people who cannot speak) (e:Mi ~ a pau thei uh hi) (r:40.15.31/40.15.30) (q:draft)
pauzaw = (t:v) (w:speak rather/speak instead) (d:pau, speak, with zaw, more or rather: prefer to speak one thing instead of another) (e:kammal nga bek ka ~ ding hi) (b:pau) (r:46.14.19/49.5.4) (q:draft)
pawipuante = (t:n) (w:festal garments/fine robes/sets of clothes) (e:mite tungah a ~ a pia hi) (b:pawipuan) (r:7.14.19/23.3.22) (q:draft)
pawisiim = (t:v) (w:attend a feast/keep a festival) (d:pawi, festival, with siim, go to and take part in) (e:~ dingin note va pai un) (r:43.7.8/25.2.22) (q:draft)
pawisimte = (t:n) (w:wedding guests/guests) (d:those who attend a feast; pawi, feast, with sim, attend, and the plural te) (e:zineipa le ~ a omkhawm laitakin) (r:42.5.34) (q:draft)
pawkhat = (t:det) (w:some/a part of) (d:placed after a noun: some of them, a part of it) (e:Judah minamte’ gamh ngahsa ~ huam hi) (r:6.19.1/14.28.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
pawldang = (t:n) (w:other group/other company) (d:pawl, group, with dang, other) (e:a ko a ~ khat pen) (r:16.12.38/7.9.44) (q:draft)
pawlmat = (t:v) (w:win over/enlist/make an ally of) (d:pawl, group, with mat, catch: get someone onto one’s side, gather people as a party) (e:ahi Blastus a ~ phot uh hi) (r:44.12.20/44.17.5) (q:draft)
pawta = (t:n) (w:measure/quart) (d:a small dry measure for grain) (e:tang ~ thumah hamu man hen) (r:66.6.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
peekin = (t:v) (w:swim) (d:peek, swim, with the linking ending in; tui peekin, by swimming) (e:mi khempeuh tui ~ a taimang ding) (b:peek) (r:44.27.42/44.27.43) (q:draft)
peekkhat = (t:n) (w:one coin/a coin) (d:peek, counter for coins, with khat, one: a single coin, a denarius) (e:~ tek a ngah uh hi) (r:40.20.9/40.17.27) (q:draft)
peeksat = (t:v) (w:break apart/snap/tear apart) (d:break a chain or bond in pieces; also written peksat) (e:kihen ngei hangin sikkhau a ~ a) (r:41.5.4/42.8.29) (q:draft)
peemna = (t:n) (w:lodging/place of stay) (d:peem, live somewhere as an incomer, with the noun suffix na: where or with whom one is staying; ka peemna meigongnu, the widow I am staying with) (e:tawh ka ~ meigongnu’ tung nangawnah) (b:peem) (r:11.17.20) (q:draft)
