suanghum = (t:n) (w:rough rocks/rocky outcrop) (d:in suanghum omna munte, places where there are rough rocks, rugged ground) (e:~ omna munte kizalhtam ding hi) (r:23.40.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
suangkeen = (t:n) (w:rocky crag/rock cliff) (d:suang, rock, with keen, cliff) (e:~ dawnah na teng a) (r:24.49.16/30.6.12) (q:draft)
suangkeente = (t:n) (w:rocks/crags/cliffs) (d:suang stone with keen cliff, a rock face, and the plural te) (e:~ nangawn a cip ding hun) (r:18.14.18) (q:draft)
suangken = (t:n) (w:rocky crag/rock cliff) (d:suang stone with ken, a steep rocky height; suangken lak is among the crags) (e:~ tungah tai thei ngei a) (r:30.6.12/24.49.16) (q:draft)
