sukgawpsa = (t:v) (w:crushed/destroyed/ravaged) (d:sukgawp strike down with sa, already done; placed before the thing or person struck) (e:na ~ mipa lungdamsak in) (b:sukgawp) (r:19.51.8/48.1.23) (q:draft)
sukhawm = (t:v) (w:grind together/pound together) (d:su pound with khawm together; an sukhawm is grind grain together) (e:An a ~ numei nih) (b:su) (r:40.24.41/42.17.35) (q:draft)
sukkhapte = (t:n) (w:broken ones/those broken) (d:sukkhap break with the plural te; the things that someone broke, said of the first stone tablets) (e:suangpeek na ~ tunga thute) (b:sukkhap) (r:5.10.2) (q:draft)
