sukmaisak = (t:v) (w:destroy completely/wipe out) (d:said of destroying a people from top to root) (e:a zung dongin ka ~ hi) (r:30.2.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
suknate = (t:n) (w:presses/vats) (d:plural of sukna, the place where oil or grapes are pressed) (e:sathau le leenggah na ~ uh panin) (b:sukna) (r:2.22.29) (q:draft)
sukniam = (t:v) (w:bring down/topple/humble) (d:su strike with niam low; bring someone down from a high position) (e:panin ~ ding bek amaute in) (r:19.62.4) (q:draft)
suksakna = (t:n) (w:violation/laying hands on) (d:suksak lay hands on with the noun suffix na; in Deuteronomy 22.24 a man's violating of another man's wife) (e:zi a va ~ hangin) (b:suksak) (r:5.22.24) (q:draft)
