Khua = (t:n) (w:town/city/village) (d:khua written with a capital in a title; Shiloh Khua Mi is the man of the town of Shiloh, the Shilonite) (e:le Shiloh ~ Mi Ahijah’ Thugen) (b:khua) (r:14.9.29) (q:draft)
Khualzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khualzin written with a capital in a place name, Khualzin Mite’ Kuam, the valley of the travellers) (e:a om ~ Mite’ Kuam a cihna sungteng) (b:khualzin) (r:26.39.11) (q:draft)
Khualzinzin = (t:v) (w:travel) (d:khualzinzin written with a capital at the start of a sentence; khualzin with the last part doubled, travel about) (e:~ mite tawh kiho ngei lo) (b:khualzinzin) (r:18.21.29) (q:draft)
Khuaniim = (t:n) (w:gloom) (d:khuaniim written with a capital at the start of a sentence) (e:~, khuamial in khuhcip hen) (b:khuaniim) (r:18.3.5) (q:draft)
