Nitumna = (t:n) (c:direction) (w:west) (d:Nitumna Tuipi, the western sea, is the Mediterranean Sea) (e:Judah gam khempeuh ~ Tuipi dong) (b:nitumna) (r:5.34.2) (q:draft)
No = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:second person plural, here the object of the verb) (e:~ kong khiasuk veve ding hi) (b:no) (r:31.1.4) (q:draft)
Nong = (t:pron) (w:you) (d:second person subject acting on the speaker, you to me, placed before the verb) (e:~ thuhilh khit ciangin dah-in ka kun) (b:nong) (r:24.31.19) (q:draft)
Nopna = (t:n) (w:peace/well-being) (d:Nopna lampi is the way of peace) (e:~ lampi ah eite hong kha ding) (b:nopna) (r:42.1.78) (q:draft)
OPA = (t:n) (w:Lord) (d:part of TOPA, the Lord, printed in the text as T OPA with a space) (r:2.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ohah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ohad) (d:a son of Simeon; the text spells the name Ohah) (r:1.46.10) (q:draft)
