Tapil = (t:n) (w:wise son/wise child) (d:ta, child, with pil, wise, written as one word at the start of a proverb; set against tahai, foolish child) (e:~ in a pa lungdamsak a) (r:20.10.1) (q:draft)
Tau = (t:n) (w:tower) (d:first part of tau sangpi, high tower, written apart and capitalised in the name Hananel Tau sangpi, the Tower of Hananel) (e:Hananel ~ sangpi panin nitumna lam) (r:24.31.38) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tausangpi = (t:n) (w:tower/great tower) (d:tausangpi, capitalised in the name Hananel Tausangpi, the Tower of Hananel) (e:Hananel ~ panin khuakulh Kiu Kongpi) (b:tausangpi) (r:24.31.38) (q:draft)
