Thuhilh = (t:v) (w:preach/proclaim/teach) (d:thuhilh, teach or preach, capitalised in Lungdamna Thuhilh, preaching the gospel) (e:Pasian’ Lungdamna ~ na semin) (b:thuhilh) (r:45.15.16) (q:draft)
Thuhoih = (t:n) (w:good news) (d:thuhoih, good word, capitalised in Lungdamna Thuhoih, the good news) (e:kilem nading Lungdamna ~ a hong hilh hi) (b:thuhoih) (r:49.2.17) (q:draft)
Thukhamnate = (t:n) (w:laws/commandments) (d:Thukhamna, law, with the plural te; the commandments of the Law taken together) (e:~ lakah bang thukham lianbel ahi hiam) (b:Thukhamna) (r:40.22.36) (q:draft)
Thulahna = (t:n) (w:counsel/guidance) (d:thulahna, counsel, at the start of a sentence) (e:~ tawh keimah nong makaih a) (b:thulahna) (r:19.73.24) (q:draft)
Thulak = (t:n) (w:counselor) (d:one who gives counsel, with pa for a male person in the title Lamdang Thulak pa, Wonderful Counselor) (e:Lamdang ~ pa, Vanglian Pasian) (r:23.9.6) (q:draft)
Thulakpa = (t:n) (w:counselor) (d:Thulak, counselor, with pa marking a male person; a title of the promised child) (e:Lamdang, ~, Vanglian Pasian, Tawntung Pa) (b:Thulak) (r:23.9.6) (q:draft)
Thum = (t:num) (w:three) (d:thum, three, capitalised in the place name Mangbuk Thum, Three Taverns) (e:kimkhatte in Mangbuk ~ dongin hong pai uh hi) (b:thum) (r:44.28.15) (q:draft)
Thumang-in = (t:adv) (w:obediently/in obedience) (d:thumang, obey, with the suffix in) (e:~ ama pumpi a kiniamsak hi) (r:50.2.8) (q:draft)
Thumanlohna = (t:n) (w:injustice/unrighteousness) (d:thuman, truth or right, with loh, not, and the noun suffix na; in the text it is part of a section heading, Leitungah Thumanlohna, that follows the verse) (r:21.3.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thummin = (t:name) (w:Thummim) (d:the Thummim, used with the Urim by a priest to seek a decision from God) (e:Urim leh ~ aisanna tawh ai) (r:15.2.63) (q:draft)
Thumna = (t:num) (w:third) (d:thumna, third, capitalised in the place name Ansai Thumna, given in the NIV as Three Taverns) (e:pawlkhat in “Ansai ~,” ciang hong ban uh hi) (b:thumna) (r:44.28.15) (q:draft)
Thumute = (t:n) (w:seers) (d:Thumu, seer, with the plural te; in the title of a book of records of the seers) (e:~’ Khang Tangthu sungah kigelh hi) (b:Thumu) (r:14.33.19) (q:draft)
Thunei = (t:n) (w:dispute/case) (d:a matter that someone has against another, brought to be judged; thu, matter, with nei, have) (e:~ khat peuhpeuh a om ciangin) (r:26.44.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
Thupalsat = (t:v) (w:transgress/break the law) (d:thu, word or law, with palsat, transgress; thupalsat mite are transgressors) (e:~ mite tawh amah a kisimkhawm hi) (r:41.15.28) (q:draft)
Thute = (t:n) (w:things/words) (d:thute, words or matters, capitalised for the message that was preached) (e:na zak uh ~ mah kamsangte in) (b:thute) (r:60.1.12) (q:draft)
Thuzuau = (t:n) (w:lie/falsehood) (d:thuzuau, lie, at the start of a clause; thuzuau gen is tell a lie) (e:~ a gen ngei lo Pasian) (b:thuzuau) (r:56.1.1) (q:draft)
Thuzuaute = (t:n) (w:lies/deceit) (d:Thuzuau, lie, with the plural te) (e:~ leh kheemna pawl khempeuh tawh a dim) (b:Thuzuau) (r:44.13.10) (q:draft)
Tomnokhat = (t:n) (w:moment/short time) (d:a very short time; tomnokhat sungin is in a moment) (e:~ sungin minam khat piangkhia ngei) (r:23.66.8) (q:draft)
Top = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Tob) (e:Rehob-a Siria mite, ~ mite, leh Ma-akahte) (r:10.10.8) (q:draft)
Topaz = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:topaz) (d:topaz, a precious stone, capitalised in the text) (e:Ethiopia gam-a piang ~ suangmanphate tawh) (b:topaz) (r:18.28.19) (q:draft)
Tuakna = (t:n) (d:tuak, each or meet, with the noun suffix na; in the text it is part of a section heading, A Kideih Tuakna, apparently the desire of each for the other) (e:Tangval A Kideih ~) (r:22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
Tuiciin = (t:n) (w:flood) (d:tuiciin, flood, capitalised for the flood of Noah) (e:Noah lutin ~ in mi khempeuh) (b:tuiciin) (r:42.17.27) (q:draft)
Tuiduh = (t:adj) (w:thirsty) (d:tuiduh, thirsty, at the start of a sentence; tuiduh mite are the thirsty) (e:~ mite nuntakna ciktui man nei loin) (b:tuiduh) (r:66.21.6) (q:draft)
Tuikulh = (t:n) (w:island) (d:tuikulh, island, capitalised after the name of an island) (e:Krete ~ gam sung tengah) (b:tuikulh) (r:56.1.5) (q:draft)
Tuipeekpa = (t:n) (w:swimmer) (d:tuipeek, swim, with pa marking a male person) (e:~ in tuipeek dingin a khutte) (r:23.25.11) (q:draft)
Tuipite = (t:n) (w:seas/oceans) (d:tuipite, seas, capitalised as the name God gave to the gathered waters) (e:a kikaikhawm tuite pen ~ ci hi) (b:tuipite) (r:1.1.10) (q:draft)
Tuipuak = (t:n) (w:dropsy/swelling) (d:swelling of the body with fluid, in tuipuak natna, the disease of dropsy) (e:~ natna vei khat in) (r:42.14.2) (q:draft)
Tuni-in = (t:adv) (w:today/this day) (d:tuni, today, with the time marker in) (e:~ na Pa ka suak zo hi) (r:58.1.5) (q:draft)
Tutakin = (t:adv) (w:now/at present/just now) (d:tutakin at the start of a sentence) (e:~ anlum mawkmawk ka nei kei hi) (b:tutakin) (r:9.21.4) (q:draft)
Tutung = (t:adv) (w:this time/now) (d:tu, now, with tung; tutung peuhmahin is this time) (e:~ peuhmahin Topa ka hihna thu) (r:24.16.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
Ukpi = (t:n) (w:Prince/ruler/chief) (d:ukpi, chief ruler, capitalised as a title of Jesus) (e:~ le Honpa-in tua Jesuh bawlin) (b:ukpi) (r:44.5.31) (q:draft)
Uliante = (t:n) (w:rulers/princes) (d:uliante, rulers, capitalised where they are addressed) (e:na bil uh ngat un, ~ aw) (b:uliante) (r:7.5.3) (q:draft)
Upa = (t:adj) (w:firstborn/elder) (d:upa, elder, capitalised in ta Upa, the firstborn child, said of the Son) (e:mai-ah zong ta ~ ahi hi) (b:upa) (r:51.1.15) (q:draft)
Upkhialh = (t:n) (w:wrong belief/doubt) (d:up, believe, with khialh, err; upkhialh lungsim is apparently a doubting or mistaken mind) (e:~ lungsim nei kei un) (r:42.12.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
Van = (t:n) (w:heaven/sky) (d:van, heaven, at the start of a clause; van nuai is under heaven) (e:~ nuai leitungah lim ka lak ding hi) (b:van) (r:44.2.19) (q:draft)
Vanleipa = (t:n) (w:buyer) (d:van, goods, with lei, buy, and pa marking a male person; set against vanzuakpa, the seller) (e:~ in vanzuakpa kiangah) (r:20.20.14) (q:draft)
Vantungah = (t:phrase) (w:in heaven) (d:Vantung, heaven, with the place marker ah) (e:~ a om na Pa uh khat bek) (b:Vantung) (r:40.23.9) (q:draft)
Vantungmi = (t:n) (w:angel) (d:vantungmi, angel, capitalised in the title Mi That Vantungmi, the destroying angel) (e:Mi That ~ in Israel mite) (b:vantungmi) (r:58.11.28) (q:draft)
Vasabu = (t:n) (w:nest/bird's nest) (d:vasabu, nest, at the start of a sentence) (e:~ khat, sing tung ahi a) (b:vasabu) (r:5.22.6) (q:draft)
Vom = (t:adj) (w:black) (d:vom, black, capitalised in Mi Vom pa, the Black man, for the byname Niger) (e:Mi ~ pa zong a kici Simon) (b:vom) (r:44.13.1) (q:draft)
Za-anannim = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Zaanannim) (r:6.19.33) (q:draft)
Zado = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zadok) (d:a scribe put in charge of the storerooms by Nehemiah; the name is Zadok in the NIV) (r:16.13.13) (q:draft, spelling without final k may be a misprint)
Zafenath-paneah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zaphenath-Paneah) (d:the name Pharaoh gave to Joseph) (e:Faro in Josef’ min ~ a phuak hi) (r:1.41.45) (q:draft)
Zahin = (t:prep) (w:as much as/as) (d:zahin, as much as, capitalised in a section heading, love is as strong as death) (e:Itna in Sihna ~ Khauh) (b:zahin) (r:22.8.4) (q:draft)
Zan = (t:n) (w:night) (d:zan, night, capitalised as the name God gave to the darkness) (e:khuamial pen ~ ci hi) (b:zan) (r:1.1.5) (q:draft)
Zeba = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zebah) (r:19.83.11) (q:draft)
Zefath-ah = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Zephath) (d:Zefath, Zephath, with the place marker ah, in Zephath) (e:~ a teeng Kanaan mite) (r:7.1.17) (q:draft)
Zefenath-paneah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Zaphenath-Paneah) (d:the name Pharaoh gave to Joseph) (r:1.41.45) (q:draft)
Zubeel = (t:n) (w:wine jar/wineskin) (d:zu, wine or beer, with beel, pot; a vessel for wine) (e:~ khempeuh leenggahzu tawh a kidim ding hi) (r:24.13.12) (q:draft)
Zumna = (t:n) (w:shame) (d:zumna, shame, capitalised in the text) (e:~ a thuak kei ding hi) (b:zumna) (r:60.2.6) (q:draft)
Zung = (t:n) (w:root) (d:zung, root, capitalised in the title David’ Zung, the Root of David) (e:David’ ~, Judah pawl pan Humpinelkai) (b:zung) (r:66.5.5) (q:draft)
aate = (t:n) (w:possessions/property/inheritance) (d:aa, what belongs to someone, with the plural te) (e:amau’ ~ pen a manawh minamte’) (b:aa) (r:4.36.4) (q:draft)
aban = (t:adv) (w:one after another/in turn) (d:in aban banin, one thing after another, step by step) (e:~ banin thu ka phawk khia hi) (r:21.7.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
abat = (t:v) (w:be like/become as) (d:bat, be like, with the prefix a written joined; ciangkhut khat abat is to be as one stick) (e:ciangkhut khat ~ theih nadingin) (b:bat) (r:26.37.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
abei = (t:adj) (w:last/ending) (d:bei, come to an end, with the prefix a written joined; abei ni is the last day) (e:akipat ni-a kipan ~ ni dong) (b:bei) (r:16.8.18) (q:draft)
adangdangte = (t:pron) (w:others/the like) (d:dang, other, repeated, with the prefix a and the plural te; the other such things) (e:zukhamna a kipan ~ ahi hi) (b:dangdangte) (r:48.5.21) (q:draft)
adei = (t:n) (w:room/chamber) (d:dei, room, with the prefix a written joined; adei tungnung is apparently the upper room or court) (b:dei) (r:24.36.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
adiak = (t:adv) (w:especially) (d:diak, especially, with the prefix a; used in adiak diakin, most especially) (e:~ diakin thu-um innkuanpihte tungah) (b:diak) (r:48.6.10) (q:draft)
adik = (t:adj) (w:right/just) (d:dik, right, with the prefix a written joined; adik nate are things that are right) (e:zahtakhuai nate, ~ nate, a siangtho nate) (b:dik) (r:50.4.8) (q:draft)
adingun = (t:prep) (w:for) (d:ading, for, with the plural ending un) (e:na tapate’ ~ na la kei ding uh hi) (b:ading) (r:5.7.3) (q:draft)
agik = (t:n) (w:weight) (d:gik, heavy, with the prefix a written joined: heaviness; agik tehna is the measuring of weight) (e:asau tehna, ~ tehna, atam tehnate) (b:gik) (r:3.19.35) (q:draft)
ahang = (t:n) (w:reason/cause) (d:hang, reason, with the prefix a written joined: its reason; ahang kan is to ask the reason why) (e:kuamah in ~ a kan thei kei hi) (b:hang) (r:27.4.35) (q:draft)
ahau = (t:adj) (w:rich) (d:hau, rich, with the prefix a written joined: the rich; ahau azawng is rich and poor alike) (e:leibate, ~ azawng, a thuakna uh) (b:hau) (r:23.24.2) (q:draft)
ahem = (t:adj) (w:maimed/deformed) (d:hem, deformed, with the prefix a written joined; said of an animal unfit for offering) (e:a gamtang theilo, ~, meima nai a nei) (b:hem) (r:3.22.22) (q:draft)
