ahita = (t:conj) (w:nevertheless/even so) (d:ahi, be, with ta; used in ahita zongin, even so, nevertheless) (e:~ zongin gamdang numeite in amah) (b:ahi) (r:16.13.26) (q:draft)
ahoihin = (t:adv) (w:well/rightly) (d:ahoih, what is good, with the suffix in; ahoihin gamta is do what is right) (e:~ gamta in) (b:ahoih) (r:45.13.3) (q:draft)
ahoihzaw-in = (t:adv) (w:better/even more) (d:hoih, good, with the prefix a, zaw, more, and the suffix in) (e:sangin zong ~ na hih ding) (r:57.1.21) (q:draft)
aikam = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpion) (e:aktui ngen leh, ~ a pia ding) (r:42.11.12) (q:draft)
aikamte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:scorpions) (e:gul gilote leh ~ na sikgawp nading uh) (b:aikam) (r:42.10.19) (q:draft)
aisaanin = (t:v) (w:casting lots) (d:aisaan, cast lots, with the suffix in: by casting lots) (e:lai ~ a puante a hawm uh a) (b:aisaan) (r:40.27.35) (q:draft)
aisannu = (t:n) (w:sorceress/witch) (d:aisan, divination or sorcery, with nu marking a woman) (e:Numei ~ na hing khawi kei ding uh hi) (b:aisan) (r:2.22.18) (q:draft)
aitawi = (t:n) (w:exorcist/sorcerer) (d:one who practises spirit arts; here of Jews who went about driving out evil spirits) (e:Jew mi ~ pawlkhat in zong) (r:44.19.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhang = (t:n) (w:increase/profit) (d:khang, increase, with the prefix a written joined; ameet akhang is interest and profit on a loan) (e:ama tung panin ameet ~ la kei un la) (b:khang) (r:3.25.36) (q:draft)
akhial = (t:adj) (w:wrong/in the wrong) (d:khial, wrong, with the prefix a written joined; akhial min pua is apparently to accept being called wrong) (e:~ min pua nuam lo hi) (b:khial) (r:20.13.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
akhuapi = (t:n) (w:city) (d:khuapi, city, with the prefix a written joined: the city) (e:amaute in ~ bawl uh tawp uh hi) (b:khuapi) (r:1.11.8) (q:draft)
akibawl = (t:v) (w:be made) (d:kibawl, be made, with the prefix a written joined: that which is made) (e:a ngakna sumngo tawh ~ khat zong bawl in) (b:kibawl) (r:2.30.18) (q:draft)
akici = (t:v) (w:be called/so-called) (d:kici, be called, with the prefix a written joined; pasian akici are those that are called gods) (e:leitungah pasian ~ a tampi a om uh hangin) (b:kici) (r:46.8.5) (q:draft)
akihisak = (t:adj) (w:proud/arrogant) (d:kihisak, be proud, with the prefix a written joined; akihisak mite are the proud) (e:Topa in ~ mite mudah a) (b:kihisak) (r:20.16.5) (q:draft)
akiman'na = (t:n) (w:use/worth/benefit) (d:kiman, be of use, with the prefix a and the noun suffix na; bangmah akiman’na om lo is there is nothing of worth in it) (e:kei adingin bangmah ~ om lo hi) (r:21.2.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
akipat = (t:adj) (w:first/beginning) (d:kipat, begin, with the prefix a written joined; akipat ni is the first day) (e:~ ni-a kipan abei ni dong) (b:kipat) (r:16.8.18) (q:draft)
akisa = (t:v) (w:be about to/be ready) (d:with the prefix a written joined; thu dong dinga akisa mite are those who were about to question him) (e:thu dong dinga ~ mite in Paul) (r:44.22.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisak = (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/be about to) (d:the prefix a written together with kisak, a form of kisa get ready; pai dinga akisak lai takin, just as he was getting ready to go) (e:pai dinga ~ lai takin) (b:kisak) (r:44.20.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
akisim = (t:v) (w:be counted/be numbered) (d:the prefix a written together with kisim be counted; those who are counted in the census) (b:kisim) (r:2.30.14) (q:draft)
aksihonpite = (t:n) (w:starry host/multitude of stars) (d:aksi star and honpi great crowd, with the plural te) (r:16.9.6) (q:draft)
alangah = (t:adv) (w:to the side/on the side) (d:a lang side with the place marker ah; the doubled alang alangah means to this side and that, in all directions) (e:alang ~ mihonte kikhin maimai hi) (b:alang) (r:9.14.16) (q:draft)
alipte = (t:n) (w:scales) (d:the prefix a written together with lip scale and the plural te; here the scales of the sea monster) (e:Tua ~ khat leh khat kithuapcip) (b:lipte) (r:18.41.16) (q:draft)
alo = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:aloes) (d:fragrant aloes, a loanword; alo paknamtui, aloes perfume) (e:~ paknamtui leh thalsing namtuite) (r:19.45.8) (q:draft)
aloses = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:aloes) (d:fragrant aloes, a loanword, possibly a misprint of aloes) (e:mirrah leh ~, a namkim om hi) (r:22.4.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
amaan = (t:adj) (w:right/just/true) (d:the prefix a written together with maan right; amaan loin, not rightly, unjustly) (e:~ loin thu khenin) (b:maan) (r:19.82.2) (q:draft)
amahin = (t:pron) (w:he/it) (d:amah he, she or it with the subject marker in) (e:Tua ciangin ~) (b:amah) (r:26.3.24) (q:draft)
amanin = (t:conj) (w:because) (d:ahih manin because it is so, written here as ahih amanin) (e:nusia khin ahih ~ amah mu zo lo) (b:manin) (r:28.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
amanlangin = (t:adv) (w:soon/at once/immediately) (d:the prefix a written together with manlangin quickly) (e:note kiangah ~ kong sawl ding hi) (b:manlangin) (r:50.2.23) (q:draft)
amawkna = (t:adj) (w:vain/worthless/empty) (d:the prefix a written together with mawkna vain; amawkna kamsiate, worthless bad talk) (e:~ kamsiate zong paaikhia un) (b:mawkna) (r:49.5.4) (q:draft)
amawknapi = (t:n) (w:nonsense/vanity/empty thing) (d:amawkna what is vain, with the strengthening suffix pi) (e:~ tawh hehnep nong sawm uh hi) (b:amawkna) (r:18.21.34) (q:draft)
ami = (t:n) (w:person/people) (d:the prefix a written together with mi person; ami' honpi-in is rendered by their divisions, by their hosts) (b:mi) (r:2.6.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
amkhamsakin = (t:v) (w:throw into confusion/confuse) (d:amkhamsak cause to be confused or panic-stricken, with the linking suffix in) (b:amkhamsak) (r:6.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
amnin = (t:conj) (w:because) (d:occurs once in ahih amnin where ahih manin, because it is so, is expected; probably a misprint of manin) (e:pia khin ahih ~ tua thupha hangin) (r:1.27.41) (q:draft, low confidence)
among = (t:n) (w:end) (d:the prefix a written together with mong end; among dongin, to the end) (e:~ dongin ka zui ding hi) (b:mong) (r:19.119.33) (q:draft)
amu = (t:v) (w:see) (d:the prefix a written together with mu see; amu ngeilo, that never sees) (e:~ ngeilo, a pai thei ngeilo) (b:mu) (r:66.9.20) (q:draft)
anam = (t:n) (w:kind/sort) (d:the prefix a written together with nam kind; anam tuamtuam, of various kinds) (e:ngun kuang-uk ~ tuamtuam zali sawmkhat) (b:nam) (r:15.1.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
anduh = (t:v) (w:crave food/hunger for food) (d:an food and duh crave; anduh gilkial lohna, where there is no hunger for food) (e:~ gilkial lohna Egypt gamah) (r:24.42.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
angkawmna = (t:n) (w:adultery) (d:angkawm commit adultery, with the noun suffix na) (e:na ~, na hukna) (b:angkawm) (r:24.13.27) (q:draft)
angkawmsak = (t:v) (w:cause to commit adultery) (d:angkawm commit adultery, with the causative sak) (e:midang tawh a zi ~ a suak hi) (b:angkawm) (r:40.5.32) (q:draft)
angtan'pih = (t:n) (w:pride/glory) (d:what someone is proud of; from angtang be proud, with pih; Jakob' angtan'pih, the pride of Jacob) (r:19.47.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
angtanhuai = (t:adj) (w:honourable/worthy of pride) (d:from angtang be proud, with huai worthy of; a thing that brings honour) (e:nang a dingin ~ mahmah hi) (r:42.14.10) (q:draft)
anhuanna = (t:n) (w:cooking) (d:anhuan cook food, with the noun suffix na; anhuanna beel, a cooking pot) (e:Hih khuapi in ~ beel tawh kibang a) (b:anhuan) (r:26.11.3) (q:draft)
anihin = (t:num) (w:both) (d:the prefix a written together with nih two and in; both of them together) (e:pumpengte ~ ni khat thu-in vat mai hi) (b:nihin) (r:23.9.14) (q:draft)
ankante = (t:n) (w:roasted grain/parched grain) (d:ankan roasted grain, with the plural te) (e:tua pa in ~ tua nu a pia hi) (b:ankan) (r:8.2.14) (q:draft)
ankhamin = (t:v) (w:overeat/be gorged) (d:an food and kham be sated or intoxicated, with the linking suffix in; zukham ankhamin, drunk and gorged) (e:zukham ~ ommawk leh) (r:42.12.45) (q:draft, low confidence)
ankhamvalte = (t:n) (w:leftovers/leftover food) (d:the food left over after eating one's fill: an food, kham be sated, val surplus, with the plural te) (e:a ~ zong la-in a pia hi) (r:8.2.18) (q:draft)
anluite = (t:n) (w:old grain/old crop) (d:an grain and lui old, with the plural te; last year's stored harvest) (e:sauveipi a kikhol ~ ne-in) (b:anlui) (r:3.26.10) (q:draft)
anlumbek = (t:n) (w:cake of bread/loaf) (d:a kind of anlum bread, here one made with oil; the exact kind is not clear from the verse) (e:sathau tawh a kibawl ~ khat) (r:2.29.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
