kikiasuksak = (t:v) (w:throw oneself down) (d:kikiasuk with the causative sak: make oneself fall down) (e:na pumpi ~ in) (b:kikiasuk) (r:40.4.6) (q:draft)
kikilhna = (t:n) (w:nailing/place of nailing) (d:kilh, nail, with the passive ki and the noun suffix na; a kikilhna mate, the wounds where the nails were driven) (e:siktukkilh tawh a ~ mate mu-in) (r:43.20.25) (q:draft)
kikingkalh = (t:todo) (q:draft, describes ornamental work on the temple stands in 1 Kings 7.29, NIV wreaths of hammered work, exact meaning not clear from the verse)
kikip = (t:v) (w:be established/be made firm) (d:kip, be firm, with ki; used with sak, make) (e:leitung ~ sak a) (b:kip) (r:19.93.1) (q:draft)
kikkhui-in = (t:v) (w:embroidering/stitching) (d:of needlework, apparently kik, back, with khui, sew, and the linking suffix in: sewing back and forth) (e:phim tawh ~ a kizem) (r:2.39.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikkikin = (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly) (d:kikkik with the linking suffix in) (e:piaknate pia ~ a ding uh hi) (b:kikkik) (r:58.10.11) (q:draft)
kiknate = (t:n) (d:plural of kikna, the noun form of kik, back or again, joined to a verb: dawn kiknate, answers) (e:a pilna leh a dawn’ ~) (b:kikna) (r:42.2.47) (q:draft)
kikogawp = (t:v) (w:scream/cry out violently) (d:kiko, cry out, with gawp, violently) (e:thakhat thu-in ~ hi) (b:kiko) (r:42.9.39) (q:draft)
kikoh = (t:v) (w:be reported/be informed) (d:passive of koh, report a matter to someone) (e:thu hong ~ ciangin nangma kiangah) (b:koh) (r:44.23.30) (q:draft)
